window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-31"]=[{"id":"news-3009","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"卡塔尔在美国高等教育体系中的足迹","title_en":"Qatar’s Footprint in the American Higher Education System","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会高级研究分析师娜塔莉·埃卡诺向得克萨斯州议会国土安全委员会作证，指出卡塔尔2024年跻身美国高校前五大外国捐助者。自2001年以来，美国高校已接受卡塔尔62.5亿美元资金，但实际支出可能更高，因高校普遍不遵守联邦披露要求。卡塔尔同时资助哈马斯和穆斯林兄弟会等极端组织，通过半岛电视台输出伊斯兰主义意识形态。文章以乔治城大学多哈校区举办会议为例，说明卡塔尔如何借教育投资规避审查并推进敌对意识形态。","summary_en":"Natalie Ecanow, Senior Research Analyst at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, testified before the Texas Legislature House Committee on Homeland Security that Qatar was among the top five foreign donors to American colleges in 2024. U.S. universities have accepted $6.25 billion from Qatar since 2001, though actual spending likely exceeds that due to non-compliance with federal disclosure requirements. Qatar simultaneously sponsors extremist groups including Hamas and the Muslim Brotherhood and exports Islamist ideology via Al Jazeera. The testimony cites a Georgetown University Doha campus conference as an example of Qatar advancing hostile ideologies while avoiding scrutiny.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:41:38.274447+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/04/02/qatars-footprint-in-the-american-higher-education-system/","content":"April 2, 2025\n| Texas Legislature House Committee on Homeland Security, Public Safety & Veterans' Affairs\nQatar’s Footprint in the American Higher Education System\nHome » Gulf States\nNatalie Ecanow\nSenior Research Analyst\nApril 2, 2025\n| Texas Legislature House Committee on Homeland Security, Public Safety & Veterans' Affairs\nQatar’s Footprint in the American Higher Education System\nNatalie Ecanow\nSenior Research Analyst\nOral Testimony April 2, 2025\nWritten Testimony Chairman Hefner, and members of the committee, on behalf of the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, thank you for the opportunity to testify.\nQatar is on a spending spree in the American higher education system. In 2024, Qatar was among the top five foreign donors to American colleges and universities, besting deep-pocketed donors like China and Saudi Arabia.\nWith approximately 11 percent of the world’s natural gas reserves and only 330,000 citizens, Qatar’s has ample wealth to spend on buying prestige and influence. Doha’s wallet is a major source of soft power that it leverages to whitewash its reputation and advance its interests abroad.\nAccording to federal disclosure data, colleges and universities have accepted $6.25 billion from Qatar since 2001. However, Qatar’s total spending likely exceeds that figure. There are two reasons to speculate: first, academic institutions that accept tens or hundreds of millions of dollars from foreign governments routinely fail to comply with their federal disclosure requirements. The previous Trump administration opened investigations into a dozen universities, uncovering $6.5 billion of undisclosed foreign funds, including from Qatar. Compounding this challenge is the historically lax enforcement of reporting requirements.\nSecond, Qatar has often sought to cover its tracks. As Texas legislators might remember, Qatar previously filed a lawsuit to prevent the state of Texas from disclosing funding records for Texas A&M University.  A Texas judge eventually ordered that the funding documents be made public, revealing almost half-a-billion dollars in Qatari grants and contracts.\nQatar enjoys a close bilateral partnership with the United States. But Qatar’s wealth enables it to play both sides. While parading as a friend, Doha has simultaneously sponsored a range of extremist groups, including Hamas and the Muslim Brotherhood. Qatar is a major exporter of Islamist ideology, which it amplifies on the Qatar-owned Al Jazeera network. By pumping money into the American higher education system and across the United States, Qatar avoids scrutiny as it advances hostile ideologies.\nFor example, Georgetown University’s Doha campus hosted a conference on “the future of Gaza” in September 2024 that featured a former Al Jazeera executive who applauded Hamas’s October 7 massacre. He previously delivered a 10-minute eulogy for Yusuf al-Qaradawi, the late Muslim Brotherhood-aligned cleric who famously endorsed suicide bombings against Israelis.\nBy accepting substantial funding from Qatar, colleges and universities are less reliant on traditional alumni donor bases. This reduces the need for schools to engage with their alumni networks. That becomes an acute problem regarding campus antisemitism insofar as school administrators will likely be responsive to Qatar — a country that held Israel solely responsible for the war in Gaza, failed to hold Hamas accountable, and has consistently backed Islamists against the West.\nIssues:\nIssues:\nGulf States\nSanctions and Illicit Finance\nTopics:\nTopics:\nAl Jazeera Media Network\nDoha\nGaza City\nGeorgetown University\nHamas\nIslamism\nIsrael\nIsraelis\nMuslim Brotherhood\nQatar\nSaudi Arabia\nYusuf al-Qaradawi\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年4月2日\n| 得克萨斯州立法机构众议院国土安全、公共安全与退伍军人事务委员会\n卡塔尔在美国高等教育体系中的足迹\n首页 » 海湾国家\nNatalie Ecanow\n高级研究分析师\n2025年4月2日\n| 得克萨斯州立法机构众议院国土安全、公共安全与退伍军人事务委员会\n卡塔尔在美国高等教育体系中的足迹\nNatalie Ecanow\n高级研究分析师\n口头证词 2025年4月2日\n书面证词 赫夫纳主席及委员会各位成员，我谨代表保卫民主基金会，感谢各位给予我作证的机会。\n卡塔尔正在美国高等教育体系中大肆投入资金。2024年，卡塔尔位列向美国学院和大学捐赠的外国捐助方前五名，超过了中国和沙特阿拉伯等资金雄厚的捐助方。\n卡塔尔拥有全球约11%的天然气储量，公民人数却仅有33万，因此拥有充裕的财富来购买声望和影响力。多哈的钱包是软实力的重要来源，它利用这一资源粉饰其声誉，并在海外推进自身利益。\n根据联邦披露数据，自2001年以来，学院和大学已接受来自卡塔尔的62.5亿美元。然而，卡塔尔的总支出很可能超过这一数字。有两个理由可作此推测：第一，接受外国政府数千万或数亿美元资金的学术机构，常常未能遵守联邦披露要求。上届特朗普政府对12所大学展开调查，发现了65亿美元未披露的外国资金，其中包括来自卡塔尔的资金。历史上对报告要求执行宽松，进一步加剧了这一挑战。\n第二，卡塔尔经常试图掩盖其踪迹。得州立法者或许记得，卡塔尔曾提起诉讼，试图阻止得克萨斯州披露得州农工大学的资助记录。最终，一名得州法官下令公开这些资助文件，揭示了近5亿美元的卡塔尔拨款和合同。\n卡塔尔与美国享有密切的双边伙伴关系。但卡塔尔的财富使其能够左右逢源。多哈一边把自己装扮成朋友，一边同时资助包括哈马斯和穆斯林兄弟会在内的一系列极端组织。卡塔尔是伊斯兰主义意识形态的主要输出国，并通过卡塔尔拥有的半岛电视台网络放大这种意识形态。通过向美国高等教育体系以及美国各地注入资金，卡塔尔在推进敌对意识形态的同时避免受到审查。\n例如，乔治城大学多哈校区于2024年9月举办了一场有关“加沙未来”的会议，会议嘉宾包括一名前半岛电视台高管；此人曾赞扬哈马斯10月7日的大屠杀。他此前曾用10分钟发表悼词，悼念已故的优素福·卡拉达维；这位与穆斯林兄弟会结盟的教士以支持针对以色列人的自杀式炸弹袭击而闻名。\n通过接受卡塔尔的大额资助，学院和大学对传统校友捐助基础的依赖降低。这减少了学校与校友网络互动的必要性。在校园反犹主义问题上，这成为一个严重问题，因为学校管理人员很可能会对卡塔尔作出回应——该国将加沙战争的责任完全归咎于以色列，未能追究哈马斯责任，并一贯支持伊斯兰主义者对抗西方。\n问题：\n问题：\n海湾国家\n制裁与非法金融\n主题：\n主题：\n半岛电视台媒体网络\n多哈\n加沙城\n乔治城大学\n哈马斯\n伊斯兰主义\n以色列\n以色列人\n穆斯林兄弟会\n卡塔尔\n沙特阿拉伯\n优素福·卡拉达维\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n保卫民主基金会\n隐私政策\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-04-02T21:05:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3004","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"叙利亚新强人未兑现改革承诺","title_en":"Syria’s new strongman isn’t living up to his promises for reform","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会高级研究分析师艾哈迈德·沙拉维在《国会山报》撰文指出，叙利亚临时总统艾哈迈德·沙拉阿在推翻阿萨德政权前曾承诺建立无人可独断专行的制度，但上任后却掌控政府各部门，安插亲信与家族成员，并于3月中旬强推临时宪法，集行政、立法与司法大权于一身，任期五年，改革承诺落空。","summary_en":"Ahmad Sharawi, a senior research analyst at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, writes in The Hill that Syria's interim president, Ahmad al-Sharaa, once vowed a system where no single ruler makes arbitrary decisions. Yet as interim president he has seized every pillar of government, stacked sensitive posts with loyalists and family, and imposed an interim constitution in mid-March granting him executive, legislative and judicial authority for five years, betraying his reform promises.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:41:04.465613+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/04/06/syrias-new-strongman-isnt-living-up-to-his-promises-for-reform/","content":"April 6, 2025\n| The Hill\nSyria’s new strongman isn’t living up to his promises for reform\nHome » Syria\nAhmad Sharawi\nSenior Research Analyst\nApril 6, 2025\n| The Hill\nSyria’s new strongman isn’t living up to his promises for reform\nAhmad Sharawi\nSenior Research Analyst\nExcerpt\nDays before his troops overthrew the regime of Bashar Assad, Ahmad al-Sharaa declared that Syria deserves a system in which no “single ruler makes arbitrary decisions.” Sharaa, once a feared jihadist and founder of al-Qaeda’s Syrian branch, now vows to abandon vengeance and lead Syria’s reconstruction with moderation and inclusivity.\nBut as interim president, he has seized control of every pillar of government, stacking sensitive posts with loyalists and family. This culminated in mid-March with the imposition of an interim constitution granting him executive, legislative and judicial authority for five years.\nAhmad Sharawi is a research analyst at The Foundation for Defense of Democracies, focusing on Middle East affairs and the Levant.\nRead in The Hill\nIssues:\nIssues:\nAl Qaeda\nSyria\nTopics:\nTopics:\nAhmed al-Sharaa\nAl-Qaeda\nBashar al-Assad\nMiddle East\nSyria\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年4月6日\n| 《国会山报》\n叙利亚的新强人未能兑现其改革承诺\n首页 » 叙利亚\n艾哈迈德·沙拉维\n高级研究分析师\n2025年4月6日\n| 《国会山报》\n叙利亚的新强人未能兑现其改革承诺\n艾哈迈德·沙拉维\n高级研究分析师\n摘录\n在其部队推翻巴沙尔·阿萨德政权前数日，艾哈迈德·沙拉宣称，叙利亚应当拥有一种没有任何“一位统治者任意作出决定”的制度。沙拉曾是一名令人畏惧的圣战分子，也是基地组织叙利亚分支的创始人；如今他承诺放弃报复，并以温和与包容领导叙利亚重建。\n但作为临时总统，他控制了政府的每一根支柱，在敏感职位上安插忠诚者和家族成员。这在3月中旬达到顶点：他强行实施一部临时宪法，在五年内赋予他行政、立法和司法权力。\n艾哈迈德·沙拉维是捍卫民主基金会的研究分析师，专注于中东事务和黎凡特地区。\n在《国会山报》阅读\n议题：\n议题：\n基地组织\n叙利亚\n主题：\n主题：\n艾哈迈德·沙拉\n基地组织\n巴沙尔·阿萨德\n中东\n叙利亚\n版权所有 ©\n2026年\n捍卫民主基金会\n隐私政策\nP.O. Box 33249，华盛顿哥伦比亚特区 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-04-06T22:09:57+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2995","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"关于埃及西奈半岛的十件事","title_en":"10 Things to Know About Egypt’s Sinai Peninsula","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会发布分析文章，梳理西奈半岛的十个关键事实：它是连接非洲与亚洲的战略陆桥，历史上属埃及领土，曾长期被以色列控制，后依《戴维营协议》归还埃及并实现非军事化；该地区长期是圣战武装活动温床，与加沙之间存在走私通道，埃及严格管控拉法口岸，半岛人口稀少，以贝都因部落为主，并多次被提议作为加沙居民安置地。","summary_en":"The Foundation for Defense of Democracies published an analysis listing ten key facts about Egypt's Sinai Peninsula: a strategic land bridge between Africa and Asia, historically Egyptian territory once held by Israel and returned under the Camp David Accords with demilitarization; a long-time hotbed of jihadi militancy with smuggling tunnels into Gaza; tightly controlled Rafah crossing; sparse Bedouin population; and repeatedly proposed as a site for Gazan resettlement.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:39:46.125230+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/04/09/10-things-to-know-about-egypts-sinai-peninsula/","content":"April 9, 2025\n| Insight\n10 Things to Know About Egypt’s Sinai Peninsula\nHome » Arab Politics » Egypt\nApril 9, 2025\n| Insight\n10 Things to Know About Egypt’s Sinai Peninsula\n1. The Sinai Peninsula is a strategic land bridge between Africa and Asia.\nThe Sinai Peninsula, which connects the continents of Africa and Asia, has a landmass of 23,000 square miles, approximately the size of West Virginia. The peninsula is bordered by the vital global shipping artery of the Suez Canal and the Gulf of Suez to the west, the Mediterranean Sea to the north, the Red Sea to the south, and Israel and the Gulf of Aqaba to the east. The peninsula has a diverse landscape, featuring coastal plains along the northern Mediterranean, extensive desert in the center, and rugged mountains in the south.\n2. The Sinai is historically Egyptian territory.\nThe ancient Egyptians controlled the Sinai Peninsula, using it as a source of copper and turquoise. According to the Hebrew Bible, the prophet Moses received the Ten Commandments when he ascended Mount Sinai in the southern part of the peninsula, following the Israelites’ exodus from Egypt’s Nile Delta. The region, along with the rest of Egypt, later came under the control of successive empires, including the Romans, the Byzantines, the Ottomans, and the British. In modern times, the Battles of the Sinai helped secure the nascent State of Israel’s survival in the 1948-1949 Arab-Israeli War. The territory then fell under Israeli control briefly during the Sinai War of 1956 and then for over a decade following the 1967 Six-Day War. Thousands of Israelis subsequently established communities in the Sinai along the Mediterranean coast and the Gulf of Aqaba. Twelve years later, as part of the Camp David Accords mediated by the United States, Israel agreed to remove its citizens and return the area to Egypt in 1982 as part of the peace treaty.\n3. The Sinai has been a hotbed of jihadi militant activity, requiring Egyptian counterterrorism operations.\nThe Sinai has been a focal point of jihadi militant activity, including the 2004 Taba and the 2005 Sharm el-Sheikh hotel bombings, and repeated sabotage attacks on the Egypt-Israel gas pipeline. Since 2014, the most active Islamist group in the region has been the ISIS-affiliated Wilayat Sinai, a Salafi-Jihadi group that has carried out attacks against Egyptian security forces, infrastructure, and civilians. Notable terrorist attacks include the 2015 Russian passenger jet downing that killed 224 people, the 2017 massacre of 305 worshippers at the Sufi al-Rawda Mosque, and the 2017 targeted attacks on Coptic Christians in the northern city of el-Arish. The Egyptian military has launched extensive counterterrorism operations, sometimes with intelligence and air support from Israel. While the counterinsurgency campaign has degraded Wilayat Sinai, elements of the ISIS affiliate continue to pose limited challenges.\n4. Lucrative smuggling takes place from the Sinai into Gaza.\nNorth Sinai shares a nearly nine-mile border with Gaza known as the Philadelphi corridor. As part of an anti-smuggling effort, Egypt has reportedly destroyed more than 3,000 tunnels along the Gaza-Sinai border since 2013. However, following Hamas’s brutal October 2023 massacre launched from Gaza, the Israel Defense Forces (IDF) uncovered hundreds more tunnels leading from Gaza into Sinai used for smuggling weapons, materiel, fuel, drugs, and pharmaceuticals. More recently, smugglers have adapted by using drones. This smuggling economy is estimated to be worth hundreds of millions of dollars annually, with bribes paid to Egyptian officials to allow the tunnel operations to continue. Meanwhile, Hamas collects taxes on smuggled materials and goods.\n5. Egypt tightly regulates movement from Gaza into the Sinai.\nTo prevent Gaza-based militant groups from smuggling weapons and fighters into the Sinai and to limit cross-border attacks, Egypt strictly controls its border with Gaza, especially at the Rafah crossing — the only official border crossing with the territory. Hamas is ideologically aligned with the Muslim Brotherhood, an Islamist movement and political group outlawed in Egypt since 2013. Egypt’s President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, as well as other Arab leaders, considers the Brotherhood a significant threat to regional stability. Since the start of the Gaza conflict, Egypt has rejected the displacement of any Gazans, although more than 100,000 Gazans have bought their way into Egypt since October 2023.\n6. The Sinai was largely demilitarized as part of the Camp David Accords.\nOne of the key provisions of the 1979 Egypt-Israel peace treaty was the demilitarization of the peninsula to ensure long-term stability between the two countries. The agreement established a phased withdrawal of Israeli forces and placed restrictions on the deployment of Egyptian military equipment and personnel. When the United Nations was unable to authorize a peacekeeping mission to monitor compliance, Egypt and Israel agreed to form an independent organization, the Multinational Force and Observers (MFO). This force continues to operate, consisting of approximately 1,000 personnel drawn from 13 nations — the majority from the United States.\n7. Egyptian military forces maintain a limited presence in the Sinai.\nThe 1979 treaty divided the Sinai Peninsula into four security zones, each with different allowances and constraints on the activities of Egyptian and Israeli military forces. Area A near the Suez Canal permits Egyptian tanks, artillery, and mechanized divisions; Area B in central Sinai permits Egyptian police and border guards; Area C near Israel and the Gaza border permits lightly armed Egyptian police and MFO peacekeepers; and Area D is the Israeli side of the border, where Israel maintains a limited military presence. The Agreed Activities Mechanism of the treaty has allowed for modifications, such as Israel agreeing to Egypt’s requests to deploy additional Egyptian forces to Area A in 2011 during the Arab Spring and again in 2012 and 2013 to Area C in response to militant activity.\n8. The Sinai is sparsely populated, mostly by Bedouin tribes.\nAccording to the 2020 Egyptian census, the Sinai’s 600,000 residents are concentrated in the coastal cities and are divided among urban residents, rural dwellers, and nomadic or semi-nomadic Bedouin tribes. Tensions between the Bedouin communities and the Egyptian government have persisted for decades, as many tribes feel marginalized and excluded from economic and political opportunities. Strict security policies, land restrictions, and limited access to state resources have led some Bedouins to engage in smuggling and, in some cases, to align with militant groups.\n9. Israel tightly controls its southern border with the Sinai.\nIsrael has implemented a multi-layered strategy to secure the Israel-Sinai border. Completed in 2013, Israel built a 152-mile barrier to reduce illegal migration, smuggling, and militant attacks. The IDF continuously surveils the border using cameras, drones, motion sensors, and radars, as well as ground and air patrols and unmanned aerial vehicles. Israel and Egypt coordinate and share intelligence to monitor and counter militant groups operating in the Sinai, and Israel restricts civilian movement within Israel near the border to reduce attacks.\n10. The Sinai has been proposed multiple times as a location for Gazan resettlement.\nSince Israel achieved statehood in 1948, the resettlement of Palestinians from Gaza to the Sinai has repeatedly been considered by the United States, Israel, and the United Nations. On several occasions, Egypt blocked the proposal, citing Egyptian sovereignty and rejecting any attempt to shift the “Palestinian issue” onto Egypt. In 2023, Egyptian President Abdel Fattah el-Sisi warned that relocation is a “red line for Egypt” that could both destroy the “Palestinian cause” and destabilize the Sinai. In response, Egypt has reinforced its border with Gaza and strengthened the Rafah border crossing to limit the movement of Gaza’s refugees.\nIssues:\nIssues:\nEgypt\nIsrael\nJihadism\nTopics:\nTopics:\nAbdel Fattah El-Sisi\nAfrica\nArab Spring\nArabs\nArish\nAsia\nBedouin\nByzantine Empire\nCamp David Accords\nCoptic Orthodox Church\nEgypt\nGaza Strip\nHamas\nIslamic State of Iraq and the Levant\nIslamism\nIsrael\nIsrael Defense Forces\nMediterranean Sea\nMuslim Brotherhood\nPalestinians\nRafah\nRed Sea\nSharm el-Sheikh\nSinai Peninsula\nSix-Day War\nSuez Canal\nUnited Kingdom\nUnited Nations\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年4月9日\n| 洞见\n关于埃及西奈半岛须知的10件事\n首页 » 阿拉伯政治 » 埃及\n2025年4月9日\n| 洞见\n关于埃及西奈半岛须知的10件事\n1. 西奈半岛是连接非洲和亚洲的战略陆桥。\n西奈半岛连接非洲和亚洲两大洲，陆地面积为23,000平方英里，大约相当于西弗吉尼亚州的面积。半岛西面毗邻全球重要航运通道苏伊士运河和苏伊士湾，北面濒临地中海，南面濒临红海，东面接壤以色列并毗邻亚喀巴湾。半岛地貌多样，北部地中海沿岸是平原，中部是广袤沙漠，南部则是崎岖山地。\n2. 西奈在历史上属于埃及领土。\n古埃及人控制着西奈半岛，并将其作为铜和绿松石的来源地。根据《希伯来圣经》，先知摩西在以色列人从埃及尼罗河三角洲出走后登上半岛南部的西奈山时，领受了十诫。后来，该地区与埃及其他地区一样，先后受到包括罗马人、拜占庭人、奥斯曼人和英国人在内的多个帝国控制。在现代，西奈战役帮助新生的以色列国在1948年至1949年的阿以战争中得以生存。随后，在1956年的西奈战争期间，该领土一度处于以色列控制之下；在1967年六日战争后，又被以色列控制了十多年。此后，数千名以色列人在西奈地中海沿岸和亚喀巴湾沿岸建立社区。十二年后，作为美国斡旋促成的《戴维营协议》的一部分，以色列同意撤出其公民，并根据和平条约于1982年将该地区归还埃及。\n3. 西奈一直是圣战主义武装活动的温床，因此埃及需要开展反恐行动。\n西奈一直是圣战主义武装活动的焦点，包括2004年塔巴爆炸案和2005年沙姆沙伊赫酒店爆炸案，以及对埃及—以色列天然气管道反复发动的破坏袭击。自2014年以来，该地区最活跃的伊斯兰主义组织一直是与“伊斯兰国”有关联的“西奈省”，这是一个萨拉菲圣战主义组织，曾对埃及安全部队、基础设施和平民发动袭击。值得注意的恐怖袭击包括2015年击落俄罗斯客机、造成224人死亡的事件；2017年在苏菲派拉乌达清真寺屠杀305名礼拜者的事件；以及2017年在北部城市阿里什针对科普特基督徒发动的袭击。埃及军方已开展大规模反恐行动，有时还得到以色列提供的情报和空中支援。尽管反叛乱行动削弱了“西奈省”，但该“伊斯兰国”关联组织的部分成员仍继续构成有限挑战。\n4. 从西奈向加沙进行着获利丰厚的走私活动。\n北西奈与加沙共享一段近9英里的边界，这段边界被称为“费城走廊”。据报道，作为反走私行动的一部分，自2013年以来，埃及已摧毁加沙—西奈边境沿线3,000多条隧道。然而，在哈马斯于2023年10月从加沙发动残酷的大屠杀之后，以色列国防军（IDF）又发现了数百条从加沙通往西奈的隧道，这些隧道被用于走私武器、军需物资、燃料、毒品和药品。最近，走私者开始改用无人机。\n据估计，这一走私经济每年价值数亿美元，并向埃及官员行贿，以允许隧道运营继续进行。与此同时，哈马斯对走私的材料和货物征税。\n5. 埃及严格管控从加沙进入西奈半岛的人员和物资流动。\n为防止总部设在加沙的武装组织将武器和武装人员走私进入西奈半岛，并限制跨境袭击，埃及严格控制其与加沙的边界，尤其是拉法口岸——这是与该地区之间唯一的官方过境点。哈马斯在意识形态上与穆斯林兄弟会一致，该组织是一个伊斯兰主义运动和政治团体，自2013年起在埃及被取缔。埃及总统阿卜杜勒·法塔赫·塞西以及其他阿拉伯领导人认为，穆斯林兄弟会对地区稳定构成重大威胁。自加沙冲突开始以来，埃及一直拒绝任何加沙人被迫迁移，尽管自2023年10月以来，已有超过10万名加沙人通过付费方式进入埃及。\n6. 根据《戴维营协议》，西奈半岛基本实现非军事化。\n1979年埃及—以色列和平条约的关键条款之一，是将该半岛非军事化，以确保两国之间的长期稳定。该协议规定以色列军队分阶段撤出，并限制埃及军事装备和人员的部署。当联合国无法授权维和任务来监督协议执行情况时，埃及和以色列同意成立一个独立组织——多国部队与观察员部队（MFO）。这支部队目前仍在运作，由来自13个国家的约1,000名人员组成，其中大多数来自美国。\n7. 埃及军队在西奈半岛维持有限存在。\n1979年条约将西奈半岛划分为四个安全区，对埃及和以色列军队的活动分别规定了不同的许可范围和限制。苏伊士运河附近的A区允许埃及部署坦克、火炮和机械化师；西奈中部的B区允许埃及警察和边防部队驻扎；以色列和加沙边界附近的C区允许部署轻武装的埃及警察和多国部队与观察员部队维和人员；D区则是边界以色列一侧，以色列在那里维持有限的军事存在。条约中的《商定活动机制》允许对相关安排进行调整，例如，以色列同意埃及的请求，在2011年阿拉伯之春期间向A区增派埃及部队，并于2012年和2013年因应武装分子活动向C区增派部队。\n8. 西奈半岛人口稀少，主要由贝都因部落居住。\n根据2020年埃及人口普查，西奈半岛的60万居民集中在沿海城市，分为城市居民、农村居民以及游牧或半游牧的贝都因部落。贝都因社区与埃及政府之间的紧张关系已持续数十年，许多部落认为自己被边缘化，被排除在经济和政治机会之外。严格的安全政策、土地限制以及对国家资源的有限获取，使一些贝都因人开始从事走私，并在某些情况下与武装组织结盟。\n9. 以色列严格控制其与西奈半岛接壤的南部边界。\n以色列采取了多层次战略来确保以色列—西奈边界的安全。以色列于2013年完成修建一道152英里长的屏障，以减少非法移民、走私和武装袭击。该\n以色列国防军持续使用摄像头、无人机、运动传感器和雷达，以及地面和空中巡逻及无人驾驶飞行器，对边境进行监视。以色列和埃及协调并共享情报，以监控和打击在西奈半岛活动的武装组织；以色列限制边境附近以色列境内的平民活动，以减少袭击。\n10. 西奈半岛曾多次被提议作为加沙人重新安置的地点。\n自以色列于1948年建国以来，美国、以色列和联合国多次考虑将加沙巴勒斯坦人重新安置到西奈半岛。埃及曾多次阻止这一提议，理由是埃及主权，并拒绝任何将“巴勒斯坦问题”转嫁给埃及的企图。2023年，埃及总统阿卜杜勒·法塔赫·塞西警告说，迁移是“埃及的红线”，既可能摧毁“巴勒斯坦事业”，也可能 destabilize 西奈半岛。作为回应，埃及加强了与加沙的边境，并强化拉法口岸，以限制加沙难民的流动。\n问题：\n问题：\n埃及\n以色列\n圣战主义\n主题：\n主题：\n阿卜杜勒·法塔赫·塞西\n非洲\n阿拉伯之春\n阿拉伯人\n阿里什\n亚洲\n贝都因人\n拜占庭帝国\n戴维营协议\n科普特正教会\n埃及\n加沙地带\n哈马斯\n伊拉克和黎凡特伊斯兰国\n伊斯兰主义\n以色列\n以色列国防军\n地中海\n穆斯林兄弟会\n巴勒斯坦人\n拉法\n红海\n沙姆沙伊赫\n西奈半岛\n六日战争\n苏伊士运河\n英国\n联合国\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n民主防卫基金会\n隐私政策\n邮政信箱33249，华盛顿特区20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-04-09T17:17:22+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2715","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"钻地弹：巨型钻地弹（MOP）如何运作","title_en":"Bunker Buster: How the Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) Works","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会发布可视化说明，介绍GBU-57巨型钻地弹（MOP）的运作原理。该武器重约3万磅，采用GPS和惯性导航制导，以高速撞击地表并用特种钢合金外壳“钻”入地下，随后引爆约5000磅弹头，据称可穿透至少200英尺。B-2幽灵轰炸机是目前美军唯一能携带该武器的机型，可挂载两枚，未来的B-21突袭者预计可携带一枚。","summary_en":"The Foundation for Defense of Democracies published a visual explainer on how the GBU-57 Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) works. The roughly 30,000-pound weapon uses GPS and inertial navigation, impacts at high speed, drills through the ground with a specialized steel alloy casing, and detonates a roughly 5,000-pound warhead, reportedly penetrating at least 200 feet. The B-2 Spirit is currently the only U.S. aircraft equipped to carry the MOP, holding two, while the forthcoming B-21 Raider is expected to carry one.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:30:46.861418+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/06/19/bunker-buster-how-the-massive-ordnance-penetrator-mop-works/","content":"June 19, 2025\n| Visual\nBunker Buster: How the Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) Works\nHome » Military and Political Power\nRyan Brobst\nCMPP Deputy Director\nJune 19, 2025\n| Visual\nBunker Buster: How the Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) Works\nRyan Brobst\nCMPP Deputy Director\nThe GBU-57 Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) is a 30,000-pound class weapon designed to strike hardened, deeply buried targets. The MOP guides itself using a combination of GPS and an inertial navigation system, then impacts the surface at high speed while using a specialized steel alloy casing to “drill” through the ground, and finally detonates its roughly 5,000-pound warhead. The MOP can reportedly penetrate at least 200 feet, although newer models may be able to strike even deeper. If a single MOP is unable to reach the target, additional MOPs could be dropped to penetrate deeper underground. The B-2 Spirit is the only aircraft in the U.S. inventory currently equipped to employ the MOP in combat and can carry two of the weapons, while the forthcoming B-21 Raider is expected to carry a single MOP.\nDownload Infographic\nDownload\nBunker Buster: How the Massive Ordnance Penetrator (MOP) Works\nIssues:\nIssues:\nIran Nuclear\nMilitary and Political Power\nTopics:\nTopics:\nNorthrop B-2 Spirit\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年6月19日\n| 视觉资料\n掩体炸弹：大型钻地弹（MOP）如何运作\n首页 » 军事与政治力量\nRyan Brobst\nCMPP副主任\n2025年6月19日\n| 视觉资料\n掩体炸弹：大型钻地弹（MOP）如何运作\nRyan Brobst\nCMPP副主任\nGBU-57大型钻地弹（MOP）是一种3万磅级武器，旨在打击坚固、深埋地下的目标。MOP通过GPS和惯性导航系统的组合进行自主制导，随后以高速撞击地表，利用特制钢合金外壳“钻穿”地面，最后引爆其约5,000磅重的弹头。据报道，MOP至少能够穿透200英尺，尽管更新型号或许能够打击更深的目标。如果单枚MOP无法抵达目标，还可投下额外的MOP，以穿透更深的地下区域。B-2“幽灵”是美国现役库存中目前唯一配备可在实战中使用MOP的飞机，能够携带两枚这种武器；而即将服役的B-21“突袭者”预计将携带一枚MOP。\n下载信息图\n下载\n掩体炸弹：大型钻地弹（MOP）如何运作\n议题：\n议题：\n伊朗核问题\n军事与政治力量\n主题：\n主题：\n诺斯罗普B-2“幽灵”\n版权所有 ©\n2026年\n保卫民主基金会\n隐私政策\nP.O. Box 33249，华盛顿特区 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-06-19T19:14:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2716","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"伊朗及伊朗支持势力针对美国人的袭击（1979年至今）","title_en":"Iranian and Iranian-Backed Attacks Against Americans (1979-Present)","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会发布备忘录，梳理自1979年伊斯兰革命以来伊朗政权及其代理人针对美国人的一系列袭击，包括1979年德黑兰人质事件、1983年贝鲁特军营爆炸、1996年霍巴塔爆炸、2003至2011年伊拉克境内袭击致至少603名美军死亡，以及2023年10月7日哈马斯袭击致至少48名美国人死亡等。文中还引用该基金会2024年报告称伊朗及其代理人在2023年10月至2024年11月间对美军发动逾180次袭击。","summary_en":"The Foundation for Defense of Democracies published a memorandum documenting attacks by Iran and its proxies against Americans since the 1979 Islamic Revolution, including the 1979 Tehran embassy hostage crisis, the 1983 Beirut barracks bombing, the 1996 Khobar Towers bombing, and attacks in Iraq from 2003 to 2011 that killed at least 603 U.S. troops. It also cites an FDD report stating that Iran and its proxies conducted more than 180 attacks on U.S. forces between October 2023 and November 2024.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:30:09.398895+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/06/19/iranian-and-iranian-backed-attacks-against-americans-1979-present/","content":"June 19, 2025\n| Insight\nIranian and Iranian-Backed Attacks Against Americans (1979-Present)\nHome » Iran\nTzvi Kahn\nResearch Fellow and Senior Editor\nJune 19, 2025\n| Insight\nIranian and Iranian-Backed Attacks Against Americans (1979-Present)\nTzvi Kahn\nResearch Fellow and Senior Editor\nSince the 1979 Islamic Revolution, the clerical regime in Tehran and its proxies have committed a range of attacks against Americans. This memorandum provides select documentation of these assaults. While the list is not comprehensive, it demonstrates that Tehran continues to pose a threat to U.S. forces in the Middle East, the American homeland, and Americans residing across the globe.\nNovember 1979-January 1981: Iranian students — with the backing of Tehran — take 66 Americans hostage at the U.S. Embassy in Tehran.\nApril 1983: A suicide car bombing kills 63 people, including 17 Americans, at the U.S. Embassy in Beirut. The Iran-backed terrorist group Islamic Jihad, a precursor and early branch of Hezbollah (not to be confused with Palestinian Islamic Jihad), claims responsibility.\nOctober 1983: Operatives of the Iran-backed Hezbollah drive a truck bomb at a Marine compound in Beirut, killing 220 U.S. Marines and 21 other service personnel.\nDecember 1983: Hezbollah operatives drive an explosives-filled dump truck through the gates of the U.S. Embassy in Kuwait City. No Americans are harmed.\nMarch 1984: Terrorists kidnap CIA station chief William Buckley in Beirut, subsequently torturing and ultimately killing him in 1985. Islamic Jihad claims responsibility.\nDecember 1984: Hezbollah terrorists hijack Kuwait Airways Flight 221 on its way from Kuwait to Pakistan and divert it to Tehran, killing two American officials from the U.S. Agency for International Development.\nJune 1985: Hezbollah terrorists hijack TWA Flight 847 en route from Athens to Rome and kill a U.S. Navy diver.\nJuly 1989: Hezbollah operatives kill U.S. Marine Corps Col. William Higgins after kidnapping him the previous year while on a United Nations peacekeeping mission in southern Lebanon.\nApril 1995: An explosives-laden van crashes into a bus near Kfar Darom in the Gaza Strip, killing one American and seven Israelis. Palestinian Islamic Jihad claims responsibility.\nAugust 1995: A Hamas suicide bomber blows up a bus in the Ramat Eshkol neighborhood of Jerusalem, killing an American and three other passengers and wounding more than 100.\nFebruary 1996: A Hamas suicide bomber blows up a Jerusalem bus, killing three Americans and wounding three other Americans. A total of 26 people die in the attack.\nMarch 1996: A suicide bomber blows up the Dizengoff shopping center in Tel Aviv, wounding two Americans. Twenty people die and 75 others are injured in the attack. Both Hamas and Palestinian Islamic Jihad claim responsibility.\nMay 1996: Gunmen kill an American-Israeli dual citizen in the community of Beit El in the West Bank. Another U.S. citizen and three Israelis are wounded. No group claims responsibility, but Israel suspects Hamas or Palestinian Islamic Jihad.\nJune 1996: A truck carrying 5,000 pounds of explosives blows up the Khobar Towers, a U.S. Air Force housing complex in the Saudi Arabian town of Khobar. Nineteen Americans die and some 500 people are injured. The Iran-backed Hezbollah Al Hijaz, a terrorist group in Saudi Arabia, is deemed responsible.\nSeptember 1997: Three Hamas suicide bombers blow themselves up at the Ben Yehuda shopping mall in Jerusalem, killing a U.S.-Israeli dual citizen and wounding seven other American citizens. Four other people die and nearly 200 are wounded in the attack.\nAugust 1998: With the assistance of Hezbollah, al Qaeda suicide bombers almost simultaneously blow up the U.S. Embassies in Kenya and Tanzania, killing 224 people, including 12 Americans, and wounding thousands. According to the 9/11 Commission Report, al Qaeda developed “the tactical expertise for such attacks months earlier, when some of its operatives — top military committee members and several operatives who were involved with the Kenya cell among them — were sent to Hezbollah training camps in Lebanon.”\nAugust 2001: A Hamas suicide bomber blows up the Sbarro pizzeria in Jerusalem, killing a U.S.-Israeli dual citizen and two other Americans. A total of 15 people die in the attack.\nSeptember 11, 2001: While the 9/11 Commission Report concludes that Iran had no foreknowledge of al Qaeda’s attacks on the World Trade Center, the report indicates that Tehran facilitated the travel of some of the terrorists. “In sum,” the report notes, “there is strong evidence that Iran facilitated the transit of al Qaeda members into and out of Afghanistan before 9/11, and that some of these were future 9/11 hijackers.”\nJanuary 2002: Gunmen affiliated with the Iran-backed al-Aqsa Martyrs’ Brigade kill a U.S.-Israel dual citizen and wound another individual in the West Bank community of Beit Sahur.\nJuly 2002: A bomb planted by a Hamas terrorist kills five Americans at Jerusalem’s Hebrew University, killing five American students, including an American-Israeli dual citizen and an American-French dual citizen. A total of nine people died in the attack.\nJune 2003: An American citizen, along with 16 other people, died when a Hamas terrorist blew himself up on a bus in Jerusalem.\nOctober 2003: Terrorists from the Iran-backed Popular Resistance Committees kill three U.S. diplomatic personnel in a bombing in Gaza.\n2003-2011: Iranian-backed militias kill at least 603 U.S. troops in Iraq, according to the Pentagon. Iranian training and material support for Iraqi militias during the surge greatly increased the difficulty of U.S. forces to combat the insurgency and included some of the deadliest weapons used against American troops, including explosively formed penetrators (EFPs) and improvised explosive devices (IEDs).\nAugust 2003: A Hamas suicide bomber blows up a bus in Jerusalem, killing five Americans and wounding one other American. A total of 24 people died in the attack.\nAugust 2006: Hezbollah fighters kill American citizen Michael Levin, a soldier in the Israel Defense Forces (IDF), during the Second Lebanon War. He is the only American to die in the conflict.\nJanuary 2007: Twelve men affiliated with the Quds Force of Iran’s Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) disguised themselves as U.S. soldiers, entered the Provincial Joint Coordination Center in the Iraqi city of Karbala, killed five U.S. soldiers, and wounded another three. In 2019, the U.S. State Department issued a $15 million bounty for information on an IRGC Quds Force commander who planned the attack and other “assassinations of coalition forces in Iraq.”\nJuly 2014: Hamas terrorists kill two Americans serving in the IDF during fighting between the terrorist group and Israel in Gaza as part of Operation Protective Edge.\nOctober 2015: Hamas terrorists kill an American citizen and his wife, residents of the West Bank community of Neria, in their car in a drive-by shooting.\nDecember 2019: Rockets fired by Kataib Hezbollah, an Iran-backed militia, kills an American security contractor and wounds several U.S. service members and Iraqi personnel at the K1 military base in the Iraqi city of Kirkuk.\nJanuary 2020: A direct Iranian ballistic missile attack against the Ain al-Asad airbase in Iraq causes more than 100 U.S. troops to suffer traumatic brain injuries.\nMarch 2020: The family of former FBI agent Robert Levinson, who disappeared in Iran in 2007, announces that he likely died in an Iranian prison at an unknown date.\nSeptember 2020: U.S. intelligence reports indicate that Iran is weighing a plot to assassinate U.S. Ambassador to South Africa Lana Marks.\nFebruary 2021: An rocket fired by an Iran-backed militia at coalition forces in the Iraqi city of Erbil wounds a U.S. service member and four U.S. civilian contractors.\nJuly 2021: Iranian-backed militias conduct at least three rocket and drone attacks against U.S. forces in 24 hours in Iraq and Syria, wounding two U.S. service members.\nSeptember 2022: An Iranian rocket attack kills an American citizen in Iraqi Kurdistan.\nNovember 2022: A captain in Iran’s IRGC orchestrates the killing of an American citizen living in Baghdad who worked at an English language institute.\nMarch 2023: An Iranian drone kills an American contractor and wounds five service members and another contractor when it strikes a coalition base near the Syrian city of Hasakah.\nOctober 7, 2023: Hamas kills at least 48 Americans and kidnaps at least 12 Americans in a massacre of 1,200 people in southern Israel.\nDecember 2023: A drone attack conducted by an Iranian-backed Iraqi militia against U.S. forces in Erbil wounds three American soldiers, including one critically injured with shrapnel to the head that placed him in a coma.\nJanuary 2024: A drone launched by Kataib Hezbollah kills three U.S. soldiers at a U.S. military base in Jordan and wounded more than 40 other service members.\nOctober 2024: Iran executes German-Iranian national and U.S. permanent resident Jamshid Sharmahd on fraudulent terrorism charges.\nNovember 2024: A report released by the Foundation for Defense of Democracies indicates that Iran and its proxies have conducted more than 180 attacks against U.S. forces in the Middle East between October 17, 2023, and November 19, 2024, resulting in more than 180 wounded and three killed U.S. service members.\nNovember 2024: The U.S. Department of Justice announces charges against an Iranian national and two American accomplices for plotting to assassinate President Trump.\nMarch 2025: A U.S. jury convicts two agents of Iran for plotting to assassinate Iranian-American journalist Masih Alinejad in New York in 2022.\nJune 2025: At least three U.S. bases in Syria and two U.S. bases in Iraq are attacked with missiles or drones, likely by Iranian-backed militias.\nTzvi Kahn is a research fellow and senior editor at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies (FDD). For more analysis from Tzvi and FDD, please subscribe HERE. Follow Tzvi on X @TzviKahn. Follow FDD on X @FDD and @FDD_Iran. FDD is a Washington, DC-based, nonpartisan research institute focusing on foreign policy and national security.\nIssues:\nIssues:\nHezbollah\nIran\nIran Global Threat Network\nIran-backed Terrorism\nU.S. Defense Policy and Strategy\nTopics:\nTopics:\n2006 Lebanon War\n2014 Gaza War\nAl-Aqsa Martyrs' Brigades\nBaghdad\nBeirut\nCentral Intelligence Agency\nDonald Trump\nEnglish\nErbil\nExplosively formed penetrator\nFederal Bureau of Investigation\nFrench\nGaza City\nGaza Strip\nGermany\nHamas\nHasakah\nHebrew University of Jerusalem\nHezbollah\nImprovised explosive device\nIran\nIranian Revolution\nIraq\nIraqi Kurdistan\nIslamic Revolutionary Guard Corps\nIsrael\nIsrael Defense Forces\nJerusalem\nJordan\nKarbala\nKata'ib Hezbollah\nKirkuk\nKuwait\nLebanon\nMiddle East\nNew York\nPakistan\nPalestinian Islamic Jihad\nPopular Resistance Committees\nQuds Force\nRocket\nRome\nSaudi Arabia\nSouth Africa\nSyria\nTehran\nTel Aviv\nTerrorism\nThe U.S. Marine Corps\nUnited Nations\nUnited States Agency for International Development\nUnited States Air Force\nUnited States Department of Justice\nUnited States Department of State\nUnited States Navy\nWashington\nWest Bank\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年6月19日\n| 洞见\n伊朗及伊朗支持的针对美国人的袭击（1979年至今）\n主页 » 伊朗\nTzvi Kahn\n研究员兼高级编辑\n2025年6月19日\n| 洞见\n伊朗及伊朗支持的针对美国人的袭击（1979年至今）\nTzvi Kahn\n研究员兼高级编辑\n自1979年伊斯兰革命以来，德黑兰的教权政权及其代理人对美国人实施了各种袭击。本备忘录提供了这些袭击的部分记录。虽然这份清单并不完整，但它表明，德黑兰继续对中东的美军、美国本土以及居住在全球各地的美国人构成威胁。\n1979年11月至1981年1月：伊朗学生在德黑兰方面的支持下，于美国驻德黑兰大使馆劫持66名美国人为人质。\n1983年4月：一辆自杀式汽车炸弹在美国驻贝鲁特大使馆爆炸，造成63人死亡，其中包括17名美国人。伊朗支持的恐怖组织“伊斯兰圣战组织”宣称对此负责。该组织是后来成为真主党前身及早期分支的组织（不要与巴勒斯坦伊斯兰圣战组织混淆）。\n1983年10月：伊朗支持的真主党武装人员驾驶一辆卡车炸弹冲入贝鲁特一处海军陆战队营地，造成220名美国海军陆战队员和21名其他军职人员死亡。\n1983年12月：真主党武装人员驾驶一辆装满炸药的自卸卡车穿过美国驻科威特城大使馆大门。没有美国人受伤。\n1984年3月：恐怖分子在贝鲁特绑架中央情报局站长威廉·巴克利，随后对其施以酷刑，并最终于1985年将其杀害。伊斯兰圣战组织宣称对此负责。\n1984年12月：真主党恐怖分子劫持从科威特飞往巴基斯坦途中的科威特航空221航班，并将其转飞德黑兰，杀害两名来自美国国际开发署的美国官员。\n1985年6月：真主党恐怖分子劫持从雅典飞往罗马途中的环球航空847航班，并杀害一名美国海军潜水员。\n1989年7月：真主党武装人员杀害美国海军陆战队威廉·希金斯上校。此前一年，他在黎巴嫩南部执行联合国维和任务期间遭到绑架。\n1995年4月：一辆载有炸药的面包车在加沙地带的卡法尔达罗姆附近撞上一辆公共汽车，造成一名美国人和七名以色列人死亡。巴勒斯坦伊斯兰圣战组织宣称对此负责。\n1995年8月：一名哈马斯自杀式炸弹袭击者在耶路撒冷拉马特埃什科尔街区炸毁一辆公共汽车，造成一名美国人和另外三名乘客死亡，并使100多人受伤。\n1996年2月：一名哈马斯自杀式炸弹袭击者炸毁一辆耶路撒冷公共汽车，造成三名美国人死亡、另外三名美国人受伤。这起袭击共造成26人死亡。\n1996年3月：一名自杀式炸弹袭击者炸毁特拉维夫迪岑戈夫购物中心，造成两名美国人受伤。这起袭击造成20人死亡、75人受伤。哈马斯和巴勒斯坦伊斯兰圣战组织均宣称对此负责。\n1996年5月：枪手在约旦河西岸贝特埃尔社区杀害一名拥有美国和以色列双重国籍的人。另一名美国公民和三名以色列人受伤。没有组织宣称对此负责，但以色列怀疑是哈马斯或巴勒斯坦伊斯兰圣战组织所为。\n1996年6月：一辆载有5000磅炸药的卡车炸毁了沙特阿拉伯胡拜尔镇的一处美国空军住宅区——胡拜尔塔。19名美国人死亡，约500人受伤。总部位于沙特阿拉伯、受伊朗支持的恐怖组织汉志真主党被认定对此负责。\n1997年9月：三名哈马斯自杀式炸弹袭击者在耶路撒冷本耶胡达购物中心引爆炸弹，炸死一名美以双重\n一名美国公民，并使另外七名美国公民受伤。袭击中另有四人死亡，近200人受伤。\n1998年8月：在真主党的协助下，“基地”组织自杀式炸弹袭击者几乎同时炸毁美国驻肯尼亚和坦桑尼亚大使馆，造成224人死亡，其中包括12名美国人，并使数千人受伤。根据《9·11委员会报告》，几个月前，“基地”组织就已为此类袭击发展出“战术专长，当时其一些行动人员——包括高级军事委员会成员以及几名参与肯尼亚小组的行动人员——被派往黎巴嫩的真主党训练营”。\n2001年8月：一名哈马斯自杀式炸弹袭击者炸毁耶路撒冷的萨巴罗披萨店，造成一名美国-以色列双重国籍者和另外两名美国人死亡。袭击共造成15人死亡。\n2001年9月11日：尽管《9·11委员会报告》 concluyó 伊朗事先并不知道“基地”组织对世界贸易中心的袭击，但报告显示，德黑兰协助了部分恐怖分子的旅行。报告指出：“总而言之，有强有力的证据表明，9·11之前，伊朗协助‘基地’组织成员进出阿富汗，其中一些人后来成为9·11劫机者。”\n2002年1月：与伊朗支持的阿克萨烈士旅有关联的枪手在约旦河西岸的拜特萨胡尔社区杀死一名美以双重国籍者，并使另一人受伤。\n2002年7月：一名哈马斯恐怖分子安放的炸弹在耶路撒冷希伯来大学杀死五名美国人，其中包括一名美以双重国籍者和一名美法双重国籍者。袭击共造成9人死亡。\n2003年6月：一名美国公民与另外16人在耶路撒冷一辆公交车上被哈马斯恐怖分子引爆自身炸死。\n2003年10月：伊朗支持的人民抵抗委员会恐怖分子在加沙的一次爆炸中杀死三名美国外交人员。\n2003年至2011年：据五角大楼称，伊朗支持的民兵在伊拉克杀死至少603名美国军人。增兵期间，伊朗对伊拉克民兵的训练和物资支持大大增加了美军打击叛乱的难度，其中包括一些用于对付美军的最致命武器，如爆炸成型穿甲弹（EFP）和简易爆炸装置（IED）。\n2003年8月：一名哈马斯自杀式炸弹袭击者在耶路撒冷炸毁一辆公交车，造成五名美国人死亡、另一名美国人受伤。袭击共造成24人死亡。\n2006年8月：第二次黎巴嫩战争期间，真主党武装分子杀死了美国公民迈克尔·莱文；他是以色列国防军（IDF）的一名士兵。他是冲突中唯一死亡的美国人。\n2007年1月：12名与伊朗伊斯兰革命卫队圣城军有关联的男子伪装成美国士兵，进入伊拉克城市卡尔巴拉的省联合协调中心，杀死5名美国士兵，并使另外3人受伤。2019年，美国国务院悬赏1500万美元，征集有关一名伊斯兰革命卫队圣城军指挥官的信息；此人策划了这次袭击以及其他“在伊拉克对联军实施的暗杀”。\n2014年7月：作为“护刃行动”的一部分，在该恐怖组织与以色列于加沙的战斗中，哈马斯恐怖分子杀死两名在以色列国防军服役的美国人。\n2015年10月：哈马斯恐怖分子在驾车经过时开枪射击，杀死了美国公民及其妻子；两人是约旦河西岸内里亚社区的居民。\n2019年12月：伊朗支持的民兵组织真主党旅发射火箭弹，造成一名美国安全承包商死亡，并在伊拉克城市基尔库克的K1军事基地打伤数名美国军人和伊拉克人员。\n2020年1月：伊朗直接向伊拉克艾因·阿萨德空军基地发动弹道导弹袭击，导致100多名美军士兵遭受创伤性脑损伤。\n2020年3月：前联邦调查局探员罗伯特·莱文森的家人宣布，他很可能已于不明日期死于伊朗一所监狱。莱文森于2007年在伊朗失踪。\n2020年9月：美国情报报告显示，伊朗正在考虑策划暗杀美国驻南非大使拉娜·马克斯。\n2021年2月：伊朗支持的民兵向伊拉克城市埃尔比勒的联军发射火箭弹，打伤一名美国军人和四名美国文职承包商。\n2021年7月：伊朗支持的民兵在24小时内对驻伊拉克和叙利亚的美军发动至少三次火箭弹和无人机袭击，打伤两名美国军人。\n2022年9月：伊朗发动的火箭弹袭击在伊拉克库尔德斯坦杀死一名美国公民。\n2022年11月：伊朗伊斯兰革命卫队一名上尉策划杀害一名居住在巴格达、在一家英语语言学院工作的美国公民。\n2023年3月：一架伊朗无人机袭击叙利亚城市哈塞克附近的联军基地，造成一名美国承包商死亡、五名军人和另一名承包商受伤。\n2023年10月7日：哈马斯在以色列南部一场造成1,200人死亡的大屠杀中杀害至少48名美国人，并绑架至少12名美国人。\n2023年12月：伊朗支持的伊拉克民兵对埃尔比勒的美军发动无人机袭击，打伤三名美国士兵，其中一人头部被弹片击中，重伤昏迷。\n2024年1月：真主党旅发射的无人机在约旦一个美国军事基地杀死三名美国士兵，并打伤另外40多名军人。\n2024年10月：伊朗以虚假的恐怖主义指控处决德国—伊朗籍人士、美国永久居民沙姆希德·沙尔马赫德。\n2024年11月：民主保卫基金会发布的一份报告显示，在2023年10月17日至2024年11月19日期间，伊朗及其代理人对中东美军发动了180多次袭击，造成180多名美国军人受伤、三人死亡。\n2024年11月：美国司法部宣布起诉一名伊朗公民及两名美国同谋，他们被指控密谋暗杀特朗普总统。\n2025年3月：美国一个陪审团裁定两名伊朗特工有罪，他们曾密谋于2022年在纽约暗杀伊朗裔美国记者马西赫·阿丽内贾德。\n2025年6月：叙利亚至少三个美国基地和伊拉克两个美国基地遭到导弹或无人机袭击，袭击者很可能是伊朗支持的民兵。\nTzvi Kahn是民主保卫基金会（FDD）的研究员兼高级编辑。如需阅读Tzvi和FDD的更多分析，请点击此处订阅。请在X上关注Tzvi：@TzviKahn。请在X上关注FDD：@FDD和@FDD_Iran。FDD是一家总部位于华盛顿特区、无党派的研究机构，专注于外交政策和国家安全。\n议题：\n议题：\n真主党\n伊朗\n伊朗全球威胁网络\n伊朗支持的恐怖主义\n美国国防政策与战略\n主题：\n主题：\n2006年黎巴嫩战争\n2014年加沙战争\n阿克萨烈士旅\n巴格达\n贝鲁特\n中央情报局\n唐纳德·特朗普\n英语\n埃尔比勒\n爆炸成形穿甲弹\n联邦\n调查局\n法语\n加沙市\n加沙地带\n德国\n哈马斯\n哈塞克\n耶路撒冷希伯来大学\n真主党\n简易爆炸装置\n伊朗\n伊朗革命\n伊拉克\n伊拉克库尔德斯坦\n伊斯兰革命卫队\n以色列\n以色列国防军\n耶路撒冷\n约旦\n卡尔巴拉\n真主党旅\n基尔库克\n科威特\n黎巴嫩\n中东\n纽约\n巴基斯坦\n巴勒斯坦伊斯兰圣战组织\n人民抵抗委员会\n圣城旅\n火箭\n罗马\n沙特阿拉伯\n南非\n叙利亚\n德黑兰\n特拉维夫\n恐怖主义\n美国海军陆战队\n联合国\n美国国际开发署\n美国空军\n美国司法部\n美国国务院\n美国海军\n华盛顿\n约旦河西岸\n显示更多\n版权 ©\n2026\n民主保卫基金会\n隐私政策\n邮政信箱33249，华盛顿特区20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-06-19T16:28:37+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2690","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“与神为敌”：伊朗以涉嫌为以色列从事间谍活动为由逮捕数百人并处决3人","title_en":"‘Enmity Against God’: Iran Arrests Hundreds and Executes 3 for Allegedly Spying for Israel","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会发布快讯称，自6月13日与以色列冲突爆发以来，伊朗当局已逮捕700多人，官方媒体称其为“以色列雇佣兵”。6月25日，伊朗以“与神为敌”和“人间腐败”罪名处决三名库尔德男子，指控其与敌对外国合作支持以色列。伊朗人权组织称审判缺乏正当程序，另有至少六名被控为以色列从事间谍活动者等待处决。","summary_en":"FDD reports that Iran has arrested over 700 people since its conflict with Israel began on June 13, with state media calling them Israeli mercenaries. On June 25, Tehran executed three Kurdish men on charges of moharebeh and corruption on earth for allegedly collaborating with enemy states in favor of Israel. Iran Human Rights says the trials lacked due process, and at least six other detainees face execution on espionage charges.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:27:10.887367+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/06/25/enmity-against-god-iran-arrests-hundreds-and-executes-3-for-allegedly-spying-for-israel/","content":"June 25, 2025\n| Flash Brief\n‘Enmity Against God’: Iran Arrests Hundreds and Executes 3 for Allegedly Spying for Israel\nHome » Iran\nJune 25, 2025\n| Flash Brief\n‘Enmity Against God’: Iran Arrests Hundreds and Executes 3 for Allegedly Spying for Israel\nLatest Developments\nMass Detentions Unfold: The Iranian authorities have arrested more than 700 people since the conflict with Israel began on June 13, Iranian state media reported this week. The Fars News Agency called the detainees “Israeli mercenaries” who “were mainly operating within espionage and sabotage networks” and were “identified and arrested based on tip-offs and intelligence operations.” Tehran has not announced formal charges against the prisoners or provided evidence for its allegations.\nTehran Hangs 3: The Islamic Republic executed three Kurdish men — Edris Ali, Azad Shojaei, and Rasoul Ahmad Rasoul — on June 25 on charges of spying for Israel, the Norway-based nonprofit Iran Human Rights (IHR) reported. Iran alleged that the three men had committed “moharebeh (enmity against god) and efsad-fil-arz (corruption on earth) through collaboration with enemy foreign states in favor of the Zionist regime.” According to IHR, the trio endured unfair trials devoid of due process after the regime extracted false confessions through torture.\nMore Executions May Follow: IHR stated that at least six other detainees are waiting on death row on charges of espionage for Israel: Ahmadreza Djalali, Afshin Ghorbani Meishani, Rouzbeh Vadi, Naser Bekrzadeh, Shahin Vasaf, and Shahin Basami. Djalali, a Swedish-Iranian dual national, may be the most prominent defendant. First arrested in 2016, the physician crisis manager researcher had traveled from Sweden to Iran at the invitations of the Universities of Tehran and Shiraz when the regime arrested him. Djalali has spent more than nine years on death row as European efforts to secure his release have failed thus far.\nFDD Expert Response\n“The regime convicts and imposes the death penalty based on trumped-up charges to spread terror among the Iranians. Meanwhile, Israel’s Operation Rising Lion has helped the public realize that the Iranian regime is a paper tiger that is weaker than ever.” — Saeed Ghasseminejad, Senior Iran and Financial Economics Advisor\n“Surges in arrests and executions in Iran consistently reflect the regime’s deep-rooted fear of its own people. Even after Israeli strikes eliminated senior officials, the Islamic Republic remained fixated on repression, terrorizing civilians with checkpoints. When the regime turns inward to punish its people, maximum support from Washington for the people must follow.” — Janatan Sayeh, Research Analyst\nFDD Background and Analysis\n“Iran Executes Alleged Israeli Spy as Regime’s Internet Blackout Persists,” FDD Flash Brief\n“5 Oppressive Iranian Institutions Israel has Targeted,” by Janatan Sayeh\n“Israel cannot settle for a temporary military win, it must topple the Islamic regime,” by Saeed Ghasseminejad\n“Weakened Tehran Regime Hangs Innocent Man on Espionage Charges in Attempt to Show Strength,” by Tzvi Kahn\nSubscribe to FDD Flash Briefs\nSubmit\nIssues:\nIssues:\nIran\nIran Human Rights\nIsrael\nIsrael at War\nTopics:\nTopics:\nFars News Agency\nGod\nIran\nIslam\nIslamic republic\nIsrael\nKurds\nNorway\nShiraz\nSweden\nTehran\nZionism\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年6月25日\n| 快讯\n“与真主为敌”：伊朗以涉嫌为以色列从事间谍活动为由逮捕数百人并处决3人\n首页 » 伊朗\n2025年6月25日\n| 快讯\n“与真主为敌”：伊朗以涉嫌为以色列从事间谍活动为由逮捕数百人并处决3人\n最新动态\n大规模拘捕展开：伊朗国家媒体本周报道称，自6月13日与以色列的冲突开始以来，伊朗当局已逮捕700多人。法尔斯通讯社称，被拘留者是“以色列雇佣兵”，他们“主要在间谍和破坏网络中活动”，并且是“根据举报和情报行动被识别和逮捕的”。德黑兰尚未宣布对囚犯的正式指控，也未为其指控提供证据。\n德黑兰绞死3人：总部设在挪威的非营利组织伊朗人权组织（IHR）报道，伊斯兰共和国于6月25日以为以色列从事间谍活动的罪名处决了三名库尔德男子——Edris Ali、Azad Shojaei和Rasoul Ahmad Rasoul。伊朗指控三人“通过与敌对外国国家合作、为犹太复国主义政权效力，犯下‘moharebeh（与真主为敌）和efsad-fil-arz（地上腐败）’罪”。据IHR称，政权通过酷刑逼取虚假供词后，三人经历了缺乏正当程序的不公正审判。\n可能还有更多处决：IHR表示，至少还有六名被拘留者因被控为以色列从事间谍活动而在死囚牢房等待：Ahmadreza Djalali、Afshin Ghorbani Meishani、Rouzbeh Vadi、Naser Bekrzadeh、Shahin Vasaf和Shahin Basami。拥有瑞典和伊朗双重国籍的Djalali可能是最受瞩目的被告。该危机管理医师研究员于2016年首次被捕；当时他应德黑兰大学和设拉子大学邀请从瑞典前往伊朗，随后被政权逮捕。由于欧洲为争取其获释的努力迄今未果，Djalali已在死囚牢房度过九年多。\nFDD专家回应\n“该政权基于捏造的指控定罪并判处死刑，以在伊朗人中散播恐惧。与此同时，以色列的‘雄狮崛起’行动帮助公众认识到，伊朗政权是一只比以往任何时候都更虚弱的纸老虎。”——Saeed Ghasseminejad，伊朗与金融经济学高级顾问\n“伊朗逮捕和处决人数的激增，一贯反映出该政权对本国人民根深蒂固的恐惧。即使以色列的打击消灭了高级官员，伊斯兰共和国仍执迷于镇压，通过检查站恐吓平民。当政权转而向内惩罚其人民时，华盛顿也必须最大限度地支持人民。”——Janatan Sayeh，研究分析师\nFDD背景与分析\n“政权网络封锁持续之际，伊朗处决被指控的以色列间谍”，FDD快讯\n“以色列已打击的5个压迫性伊朗机构”，Janatan Sayeh著\n“以色列不能满足于暂时的军事胜利，必须推翻伊斯兰政权”，Saeed Ghasseminejad著\n“虚弱的德黑兰政权以间谍罪绞死无辜男子，试图展示力量”，Tzvi Kahn著\n订阅FDD快讯\n提交\n议题：\n议题：\n伊朗\n伊朗人权组织\n以色列\n战争中的以色列\n主题：\n主题：\n法尔斯通讯社\n真主\n伊朗\n伊斯兰教\n伊斯兰共和国\n以色列\n库尔德人\n挪威\n设拉子\n瑞典\n德黑兰\n犹太复国主义\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n捍卫民主基金会\n隐私政策\nP.O. Box 33249，华盛顿哥伦比亚特区20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-06-25T20:19:58+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2609","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"南非拒绝与伊斯兰国有关联的政党注册","title_en":"South Africa Rejects ISIS-Linked Political Party","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会研究人员David May撰文称，南非选举委员会7月12日拒绝由美国认定的恐怖分子Farhad Hoomer领导的“非洲伊斯兰国党”参加选举，理由包括未达到签名门槛、未公开宣布参选以及该党主张以伊斯兰教法为治国原则。文章指出，选举委员会在拒绝时未提及Hoomer与伊斯兰国的关联，该党有30天时间上诉。文章认为此案显示南非应对本土恐怖主义存在困难。","summary_en":"FDD research manager David May writes that South Africa's Electoral Commission on July 12 denied ballot access to the Islamic State of Africa party led by U.S.-designated terrorist Farhad Hoomer, citing insufficient signatures, failure to publicly announce candidacy, and the party's commitment to Sharia law. The commission did not mention Hoomer's ISIS ties in its denial, and the party has 30 days to appeal. The case, May argues, demonstrates South Africa's difficulties in dealing with homegrown terrorism.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:17:12.092166+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/07/17/south-africa-rejects-isis-linked-political-party/","content":"July 17, 2025\n| The National Interest\nSouth Africa Rejects ISIS-Linked Political Party\nThe case of Farhad Hoomer has demonstrated South Africa’s difficulties in dealing with homegrown terrorism.\nHome » Jihadism » Islamic State\nDavid May\nResearch Manager and Senior Research Analyst\nJuly 17, 2025\n| The National Interest\nSouth Africa Rejects ISIS-Linked Political Party\nThe case of Farhad Hoomer has demonstrated South Africa’s difficulties in dealing with homegrown terrorism.\nDavid May\nResearch Manager and Senior Research Analyst\nExcerpt\nThe Islamic State’s South African cell got its nose bloodied on July 12 when South Africa’s Electoral Commission denied it access to the ballot box.\nLed by Farhad Hoomer, a US-designated terrorist, the Islamic State of Africa party did not meet the threshold of signatures it needed from registered voters and failed to announce its candidacy publicly, having only announced it in a local newspaper in Durban. The commission also noted the party’s commitment to Sharia law as a disqualifying factor. The party has 30 days to appeal.\nHoomer hopes to “bring back Sharia law” as the law of the land in a country with a Muslim community comprising less than 2 percent of the population. He has been open about his anti-democratic views, stating, “All of mankind has been enslaved by democracy and capitalism.”\nPrior to the party’s rejection, a member of parliament lodged a formal complaint that the “specific choice of this name could indicate affiliation with Islamic State and its affiliates.” But the electoral commission did not mention Hoomer’s connection to ISIS when it denied the Islamic State of Africa’s application.\nDavid May is a research manager and senior research analyst at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies (FDD). For more analysis from the author and FDD, please subscribe HERE. Follow David on X @DavidSamuelMay. Follow FDD on X @FDD. FDD is a Washington, DC-based, nonpartisan research institute focusing on national security and foreign policy.\nRead in The National Interest\nIssues:\nIssues:\nIslamic State\nJihadism\nSanctions and Illicit Finance\nSouth Africa\nTopics:\nTopics:\nDemocratic Republic of the Congo\nDurban\nFinancial Action Task Force\nIslam\nIslamic State of Iraq and the Levant\nPretoria\nShia Islam\nSouth Africa\nTanzania\nUnited States Department of the Treasury\nWashington\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年7月17日\n|《国家利益》\n南非拒绝与“伊斯兰国”有关联的政党\n法尔哈德·胡默尔一案显示出南非应对本土恐怖主义的困难。\n主页 » 圣战主义 » 伊斯兰国\n大卫·梅\n研究经理兼高级研究分析师\n2025年7月17日\n|《国家利益》\n南非拒绝与“伊斯兰国”有关联的政党\n法尔哈德·胡默尔一案显示出南非应对本土恐怖主义的困难。\n大卫·梅\n研究经理兼高级研究分析师\n摘录\n7月12日，当南非选举委员会拒绝让其进入投票箱时，“伊斯兰国”在南非的分支遭受了挫败。\n由美国认定的恐怖分子法尔哈德·胡默尔领导的“非洲伊斯兰国”党未达到所需的注册选民签名门槛，也未公开宣布参选，只是在德班的一份地方报纸上宣布。委员会还指出，该党对沙里亚法的承诺是取消其资格的因素。该党有30天时间提出上诉。\n胡默尔希望在这个穆斯林社区人口占比不足2%的国家“恢复沙里亚法”，使其成为国家法律。他一直公开表达反民主观点，称：“全人类都被民主和资本主义奴役了。”\n在该党遭拒之前，一名国会议员提出正式投诉，称“选择这个特定名称可能表明其与‘伊斯兰国’及其附属组织有关联。”但选举委员会拒绝“非洲伊斯兰国”的申请时，没有提到胡默尔与ISIS的联系。\n大卫·梅是民主防御基金会（FDD）的研究经理兼高级研究分析师。如需阅读作者和FDD的更多分析，请在此处订阅。请在X上关注大卫@DavidSamuelMay。在X上关注FDD@FDD。FDD是一家总部位于华盛顿特区、专注于国家安全和外交政策的无党派研究机构。\n在《国家利益》上阅读\n议题：\n议题：\n伊斯兰国\n圣战主义\n制裁与非法金融\n南非\n主题：\n主题：\n刚果民主共和国\n德班\n金融行动特别工作组\n伊斯兰教\n伊拉克和黎凡特伊斯兰国\n比勒陀利亚\n什叶派伊斯兰教\n南非\n坦桑尼亚\n美国财政部\n华盛顿\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n民主防御基金会\n隐私政策\n邮政信箱33249，华盛顿特区20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-07-17T15:27:39+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2570","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"叙利亚总统能控制他的部队吗？","title_en":"Can Syria’s President Control His Troops?","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会高级研究分析师艾哈迈德·沙拉维在《华尔街日报》撰文指出，特朗普政府对新任叙利亚总统艾哈迈德·沙拉阿寄予厚望，但其迅速夺取大马士革后，政府军近期两起针对平民的屠杀暴露出他对军队控制有限。文章称沙拉阿低估了建设国家、组建统一安全架构并确保各族群代表性的难度，援引前美国驻大马士革大使克罗克的观点，呼吁美国施压其改革叙利亚军队。","summary_en":"Ahmad Sharawi, a senior research analyst at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, writes in The Wall Street Journal that the Trump administration has placed significant trust in Syria's new president, Ahmed al-Sharaa, but recent massacres of civilians by government forces have exposed the limits of his control over the military. The article argues al-Sharaa underestimated the complexity of building a state, forming a unified security structure, and ensuring representation for all segments of the population, citing former U.S. ambassador to Damascus Ryan Crocker, and calls on Washington to pressure him to reform the Syrian military.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:13:23.819529+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/07/29/can-syrias-president-control-his-troops/","content":"July 29, 2025\n| The Wall Street Journal\nCan Syria’s President Control His Troops?\nAfter two massacres by government forces, the U.S. should turn up the heat.\nHome » Syria\nAhmad Sharawi\nSenior Research Analyst\nJuly 29, 2025\n| The Wall Street Journal\nCan Syria’s President Control His Troops?\nAfter two massacres by government forces, the U.S. should turn up the heat.\nAhmad Sharawi\nSenior Research Analyst\nExcerpt\nThe Trump administration has placed significant trust in Syria’s new president, Ahmed al-Sharaa, and he appeared strong when he seized Damascus swiftly in December. But recent massacres of civilians by government forces have exposed the limits of Mr. Sharaa’s control. The U.S. must pressure him to reform the Syrian military.\nAfter toppling the Bashar al-Assad regime in under two weeks, Mr. Sharaa emerged from his Idlib enclave as Syria’s de facto ruler. He managed to unify multiple armed factions, and his allies formally declared him interim president in January. Bringing stability to Syria after a 14-year civil war was always going to be a daunting challenge. Now it’s become clear that Mr. Sharaa underestimated the complexity of building a state, forming a unified security structure, and ensuring representation for all segments of the population. “There is a big difference between managing one province in Syria, Idlib in the north, and managing an entire country with all its diverse ethnic and sectarian groups,” said Ryan Crocker, a former U.S. ambassador to Damascus.\nMr. Sharawi is a research analyst at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies.\nRead in The Wall Street Journal\nIssues:\nIssues:\nKurds\nSyria\nTopics:\nTopics:\nAhmed al-Sharaa\nBashar al-Assad\nDamascus\nDonald Trump\nIdlib\nRyan Crocker\nSyria\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年7月29日\n|《华尔街日报》\n叙利亚总统能控制他的部队吗？\n在政府军制造两起大屠杀后，美国应加大施压。\n主页 » 叙利亚\n艾哈迈德·沙拉维\n高级研究分析师\n2025年7月29日\n|《华尔街日报》\n叙利亚总统能控制他的部队吗？\n在政府军制造两起大屠杀后，美国应加大施压。\n艾哈迈德·沙拉维\n高级研究分析师\n摘录\n特朗普政府对叙利亚新总统艾哈迈德·沙拉阿寄予了很大信任；去年12月他迅速夺取大马士革时，表现得很强势。但政府军最近对平民实施的大屠杀暴露了沙拉阿控制力的局限。美国必须施压，要求他改革叙利亚军队。\n在不到两周内推翻巴沙尔·阿萨德政权后，沙拉阿从其伊德利卜飞地走出，成为叙利亚事实上的统治者。他设法统一了多个武装派别，其盟友于1月正式宣布他为临时总统。在经历14年内战后为叙利亚带来稳定，一直会是艰巨挑战。现在已经清楚，沙拉阿低估了建立国家、组建统一安全体系以及确保各个社会群体获得代表权的复杂性。“管理叙利亚北部的一个省份伊德利卜，与管理一个拥有多元民族和宗派群体的完整国家之间存在巨大差异，”美国前驻大马士革大使瑞安·克罗克说。\n沙拉维先生是民主防卫基金会的研究分析师。\n在《华尔街日报》阅读\n议题：\n议题：\n库尔德人\n叙利亚\n主题：\n主题：\n艾哈迈德·沙拉阿\n巴沙尔·阿萨德\n大马士革\n唐纳德·特朗普\n伊德利卜\n瑞安·克罗克\n叙利亚\n版权所有©\n2026\n民主防卫基金会\n隐私政策\n华盛顿特区邮政信箱33249，邮编20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-07-29T22:30:51+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2539","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"俄罗斯诱骗拉美年轻移民女性制造无人机","title_en":"Russia Lures Young Migrant Women from Latin America to Build Drones","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会政策简报称，其发现俄罗斯Alabuga Start项目正从委内瑞拉、巴西、墨西哥等国招募年轻女性，以教育和工作为名从事低成本无人机生产，包括仿制伊朗Shahed-136的Geran-2。文章建议美国国务院与拉美政府合作，通过宣传、技术追踪和替代就业阻断招募网络。","summary_en":"An FDD policy brief says it found Russia's Alabuga Start program recruiting young women from Venezuela, Brazil, Mexico and elsewhere under promises of education and work, channeling them into low-cost drone production including the Geran-2, a copy of Iran's Shahed-136. It urges the State Department to work with Latin American governments on messaging, tracking recruitment networks and alternative opportunities.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:10:11.557614+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/08/06/russia-lures-young-migrant-women-from-latin-america-to-build-drones/","content":"August 6, 2025\n| Policy Brief\nRussia Lures Young Migrant Women from Latin America to Build Drones\nHome » Cyber\nMax Lesser\nCCTI Senior Analyst on Emerging Threats\nMaria Riofrio\nResearch Assistant\nAugust 6, 2025\n| Policy Brief\nRussia Lures Young Migrant Women from Latin America to Build Drones\nMax Lesser\nCCTI Senior Analyst on Emerging Threats\nMaria Riofrio\nResearch Assistant\nThe Foundation for Defense of Democracies (FDD) has discovered Russian efforts to recruit young migrant women from Latin America to build drones to sustain its war of aggression in Ukraine.\nThe Alabuga Start program, originally focused on recruiting African women, is now targeting Latin American youth — luring them with promises of education, paid work, and cultural exchange. The program allegedly functions as a recruitment funnel for low-cost labor that sustains Russia’s drone production and exposes women to exploitative conditions.\nThe Alabuga Bait and Switch\nThe Alabuga Start program markets itself as a career accelerator for young migrant women, offering free travel, housing, Russian language courses, and vocational training at the Special Economic Zone (SEZ) in Alabuga. However, the Associated Press (AP) and the Institute for Science and International Security revealed the program’s true purpose: providing low-cost labor for Russia’s defense manufacturing sector.\nThe program lures recruits, initially promised education and training, into low-cost drone production in the SEZ Alabuga, home to Russia’s main factory for the Geran-2, the Russian-made version of Iran’s Shahed-136 long-range one-way attack drone. Satellite imagery from July 2025 reveals significant construction efforts to expand the facility, with newly built warehouses and dormitories, likely to accommodate a growing influx of foreign labor. Russian production of these drones has risen exponentially since it began in 2023.\nThe AP reported that African women recruited by the program experienced grueling shifts, constant surveillance, and exposure to hazardous materials. Although some reporting has noted the program’s intent to expand into Latin America and other regions, media coverage continues to focus primarily on its recruitment in Africa.\nAlabuga’s Recruitment Efforts Increasingly Target Latin America\nFDD has observed multiple efforts to promote Alabuga Start across Latin America, targeting countries including Venezuela, Brazil, Mexico, Ecuador, Panama, and Bolivia.\nIn Venezuela, the pro-Chavista Telegram channel @antiescualidos incentivized Venezuelan youth to join the program, framing Russia as a lucrative alternative to the “broken promises of the West.” The post links to Alabuga Start’s Telegram channel and includes an AI-generated video promoting the program. The same post appeared on Pravda Español, which is part of a known Russian influence operation, showing direct state-backed efforts to expand outreach.\nFDD found other accounts sharing the same post across different online platforms. For example, influencer Liu Shivaya, a Spanish-language commentator flagged for spreading Kremlin-aligned narratives, shared it with her 140,000 Telegram subscribers.\nBrazilian influencers on TikTok and Instagram, with a combined following exceeding 15 million, have also posted content promoting the program. The content ranges from promotional clips describing the program as a life-changing opportunity to vlog-style videos where influencers allegedly travel to Russia for the program.\nAlabuga Start’s own social media accounts reflect this regional shift. The official X account for SEZ Alabuga ramped up Spanish-language content promoting the program in May 2025. An Instagram account dedicated to the program’s outreach efforts in Latin America started posting promotional content in late March, highlighting official partnerships with the Ecuadorian national soccer team to increase recruitment.\nThe U.S. Should Actively Disrupt Russia’s Recruitment and Exploitation Efforts\nThe U.S. Treasury Department sanctioned SEZ Alabuga in February 2024, noting its key role in bolstering domestic production of Iran-designed drones. The statement also notes that the region “exploited underage students from an affiliated polytechnic university” to build the drones.\nWhile sanctions were a good start, Washington must take further action to disrupt Russia’s efforts to recruit and exploit young migrant women. The State Department — particularly the Bureau of Cyberspace and Digital Policy and the Bureau of Democracy, Human Rights, and Labor — should lead a coordinated effort with Latin American governments and regional bodies like the Inter-American Commission on Human Rights to counter Alabuga Start’s outreach.\nThis effort should include joint messaging campaigns to expose the program’s true purpose, technical cooperation to track and block recruitment networks online, and support for local governments to provide alternative employment and educational opportunities for at-risk youth.\nMax Lesser is a senior analyst on emerging threats at FDD’s Center on Cyber and Technology Innovation (CCTI). Maria Riofrio is an intern at FDD. For more analysis from the authors and FDD, please subscribe HERE. Follow FDD on X @FDD and @FDD_CCTI. FDD is a Washington, DC-based, nonpartisan research institute focusing on foreign policy and national security.\nIssues:\nIssues:\nCyber\nInformation Warfare\nRussia\nTopics:\nTopics:\nAssociated Press\nBolivia\nBrazil\nEcuador\nHESA Shahed 136\nInstagram\nInstitute for Science and International Security\nIran\nKremlin\nLatin America\nMexico\nPanama\nRussia\nRussian\nSpanish\nTarget Corporation\nTikTok\nUkraine\nUnited States Department of State\nUnited States Department of the Treasury\nVenezuela\nWashington\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年8月6日\n| 政策简报\n俄罗斯从拉丁美洲招募年轻移民女性制造无人机\n主页 » 网络安全\nMax Lesser\nCCTI新兴威胁高级分析师\nMaria Riofrio\n研究助理\n2025年8月6日\n| 政策简报\n俄罗斯从拉丁美洲招募年轻移民女性制造无人机\nMax Lesser\nCCTI新兴威胁高级分析师\nMaria Riofrio\n研究助理\n民主保卫基金会（FDD）发现，俄罗斯正努力招募来自拉丁美洲的年轻移民女性制造无人机，以维持其在乌克兰的侵略战争。\nAlabuga Start项目最初专注于招募非洲女性，如今正将目标转向拉丁美洲青年——以教育、有偿工作和文化交流的承诺吸引她们。该项目据称充当廉价劳动力的招募渠道，为俄罗斯的无人机生产提供支持，并使女性暴露于剥削性环境之中。\nAlabuga的诱饵与调包\nAlabuga Start项目将自身宣传为面向年轻移民女性的职业加速器，在Alabuga经济特区（SEZ）提供免费旅行、住宿、俄语课程和职业培训。然而，美联社（AP）和科学与国际安全研究所揭示了该项目的真实目的：为俄罗斯国防制造业提供廉价劳动力。\n该项目诱骗最初被承诺接受教育和培训的招募者，在Alabuga经济特区从事低成本无人机生产。这里是俄罗斯生产Geran-2的主要工厂所在地；Geran-2是俄罗斯制造的伊朗Shahed-136远程单向攻击无人机版本。2025年7月的卫星图像显示，该设施正在进行大规模扩建，新建了仓库和宿舍，可能是为了容纳不断增加的外国劳动力。自2023年开始生产以来，俄罗斯这类无人机的产量呈指数级增长。\n美联社报道，被该项目招募的非洲女性经历了艰苦的轮班、持续监视，并暴露于危险材料之中。尽管一些报道指出该项目有意扩展到拉丁美洲和其他地区，但媒体报道仍主要聚焦于其在非洲的招募活动。\nAlabuga的招募工作日益瞄准拉丁美洲\nFDD观察到，Alabuga Start在拉丁美洲开展了多项推广活动，目标国家包括委内瑞拉、巴西、墨西哥、厄瓜多尔、巴拿马和玻利维亚。\n在委内瑞拉，亲查韦斯的Telegram频道@antiescualidos鼓励委内瑞拉青年加入该项目，将俄罗斯描述为“西方破碎承诺”之外的有利可图的选择。该帖子链接到Alabuga Start的Telegram频道，并包含一段宣传该项目的人工智能生成视频。同一帖子还出现在Pravda Español上；该网站属于一个已知的俄罗斯影响力行动，显示出国家支持的直接扩大宣传覆盖面的努力。\nFDD发现，其他账号也在不同网络平台上分享了同一帖子。例如，被标记为传播亲克里姆林宫叙事的西班牙语评论员、网红Liu Shivaya，将其分享给了自己14万名Telegram订阅者。\nTikTok和Instagram上的巴西网红，其合计粉丝数超过1500万，也发布了宣传该项目的内容。这些内容包括将该项目描述为改变人生机会的宣传短片，以及网红据称因该项目前往俄罗斯的博客式视频。\nAlabuga Start自身的\n社交媒体账号反映了这一地区性转变。2025年5月，阿拉布加经济特区（SEZ Alabuga）的官方X账号增加了推广该项目的西班牙语内容。一个专门负责该项目在拉丁美洲推广工作的Instagram账号于3月底开始发布宣传内容，突出展示与厄瓜多尔国家足球队的官方合作，以扩大招募规模。\n美国应积极破坏俄罗斯的招募和剥削行动\n美国财政部于2024年2月制裁了阿拉布加经济特区，并指出其在加强伊朗设计无人机的国内生产方面发挥了关键作用。声明还指出，该地区“利用一所附属理工大学的未成年学生”制造无人机。\n虽然制裁是一个良好的开端，但华盛顿必须采取进一步行动，破坏俄罗斯招募和剥削年轻移民女性的努力。国务院——尤其是网络空间与数字政策局以及民主、人权和劳工局——应与拉丁美洲各国政府及美洲人权委员会等地区机构开展协调行动，遏制阿拉布加Start项目的推广活动。\n这项行动应包括联合宣传活动，以揭露该项目的真实目的；开展技术合作，在线追踪并阻断招募网络；支持地方政府为面临风险的青年提供替代性的就业和教育机会。\nMax Lesser是民主防卫基金会（FDD）网络与技术创新中心（CCTI）的新兴威胁高级分析师。Maria Riofrio是FDD的实习生。如需阅读作者和FDD的更多分析，请点击此处订阅。在X上关注FDD：@FDD和@FDD_CCTI。FDD是一家总部位于华盛顿特区、无党派的研究机构，专注于外交政策和国家安全。\n议题：\n议题：\n网络\n信息战\n俄罗斯\n主题：\n主题：\n美联社\n玻利维亚\n巴西\n厄瓜多尔\nHESA Shahed 136\nInstagram\n科学与国际安全研究所\n伊朗\n克里姆林宫\n拉丁美洲\n墨西哥\n巴拿马\n俄罗斯\n俄罗斯的\n西班牙语\n塔吉特公司\nTikTok\n乌克兰\n美国国务院\n美国财政部\n委内瑞拉\n华盛顿\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n民主防卫基金会\n隐私政策\n邮政信箱33249，华盛顿特区20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-08-06T22:36:50+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2533","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"特朗普政府未能阻止伊朗石油出口","title_en":"Trump Administration Fails to Halt Iran’s Oil Exports","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会政策简报援引TankerTrackers数据称，特朗普政府未能兑现将伊朗石油出口压至每日10万桶的承诺，2025年2至7月伊朗日均出口约180万桶，与拜登时期相近，其中95%流向中国。文章建议美国制裁相关高管，并加强海军拦截与秘密行动以打击伊朗石油贸易。","summary_en":"An FDD policy brief, citing TankerTrackers data, says the Trump administration has failed to deliver on cutting Iran's oil exports to 100,000 barrels per day; February-July 2025 exports averaged about 1.8 mbpd, similar to the Biden era, with 95 percent going to China. It urges sanctioning executives and tougher naval interdiction and covert action against Iran's oil trade.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:09:10.533338+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/08/07/trump-administration-fails-to-halt-irans-oil-exports/","content":"August 7, 2025\n| Policy Brief\nTrump Administration Fails to Halt Iran’s Oil Exports\nHome » Iran\nSaeed Ghasseminejad\nNUFDI\nAugust 7, 2025\n| Policy Brief\nTrump Administration Fails to Halt Iran’s Oil Exports\nSaeed Ghasseminejad\nNUFDI\nThe Trump administration came into power promising to reduce Iran’s oil exports to 100,000 barrels per day. It has so far failed to deliver on that promise. Early data by TankerTrackers indicate that during the second Trump administration, Iran’s oil exports, the government’s largest source of hard currency, have not diverged significantly from the same period in the last year of the Biden administration.\nThe data show that Tehran managed to export 1.65 mbpd of crude, condensate, and fuel oil in July 2025 — almost identical to the July 2024 exports number. In total, between February and July 2025, Iran exported an average of 1.8 mbpd of crude, condensate, and fuel oil. For the same period in 2024, under the Biden administration, Iran exported an average of 1.85 mbpd.\nIran’s Oil Exports Benefit Primarily China\nNinety-five percent of the exports in July 2025 went to China, according to TankerTrackers. The other 5 percent went to the United Arab Emirates. Ports such as Ningbo in China and Fujairah and Jebel Ali in the United Arab Emirates were on the receiving end of the Iranian crude, condensate, and fuel oil. Forty-four percent of the total volume was transferred through 15 vessels with Iranian flags. Vessels from 11 other countries, such as Guyana and Brazil, have been involved in transferring the rest of the oil.\nIran’s Oil Exports in 2024 Reached a New High\nAccording to the Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), Tehran’s oil export income in 2024 reached its highest level since 2019. In 2024, Tehran exported $46.7 billion worth of crude oil, $5.6 billion more than in 2023. The number is in line with, but slightly higher than, our estimate at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, $41 billion to 45.5 billion, which considers the discount that Tehran has been reportedly offering to its main customer, China, to incentivize Beijing to buy its sanctioned oil. We estimate that so far in 2025, Tehran has exported up to $27 billion of oil.\nCongressional Efforts to Enforce Sanctions\nThe Biden administration’s inability or unwillingness to enforce U.S. sanctions against Tehran’s oil export operation was a source of tensions between the White House and the U.S. Congress. In an attempt to force Biden’s hand, the House in 2023 passed the Stop Harboring Iranian Petroleum Act (SHIP) Act, which would both expand the administration’s punitive tools to enforce sanctions and introduce mandatory reporting to increase Congress’s visibility into the administration’s enforcement efforts.\nWashington Should Sharpen Its Sanctions\nIran uses the money it gains from oil exports to fund repression at home and aggression abroad. If the exports continue, Iran will have the money it needs to rebuild and expand its nuclear program, missile arsenal, and proxy groups.\nTo effectively cripple Iran’s illicit oil trade, the United States must change its approach. The current sanctions are too timid, avoiding major banks and ports in places like China and the United Arab Emirates, which are known hubs for this activity. A tougher stance is needed, starting with sanctioning not just the companies involved but also the people who run them, from the C-suite to the board of directors.\nAt the same time, the United States should move beyond sanctions alone and use its military and intelligence capabilities more forcefully. This means increasing the U.S. Navy’s interception of Iranian oil tankers and running clandestine operations against top offenders to send a clear message: The cost of helping Iran has skyrocketed.\nSaeed Ghasseminejad is a senior Iran and financial economics advisor at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies (FDD). For more analysis from the authors and FDD, please subscribe HERE. Follow Saeed on X @SGhasseminejad. Follow FDD on X @FDD and @FDD_Iran. FDD is a Washington, DC-based, nonpartisan research institute focusing on foreign policy and national security.\nIssues:\nIssues:\nChina\nEnergy\nIran\nIran Politics and Economy\nTopics:\nTopics:\nBeijing\nBrazil\nChina\nDonald Trump\nGuyana\nIran\nJoe Biden\nOPEC\nTehran\nUnited Arab Emirates\nUnited States Congress\nUnited States Navy\nUnited States Senate\nWashington\nShow More\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年8月7日\n| 政策简报\n特朗普政府未能阻止伊朗石油出口\n首页 » 伊朗\nSaeed Ghasseminejad\nNUFDI\n2025年8月7日\n| 政策简报\n特朗普政府未能阻止伊朗石油出口\nSaeed Ghasseminejad\nNUFDI\n特朗普政府上台时承诺将伊朗石油出口减少到每天10万桶。到目前为止，它未能兑现这一承诺。TankerTrackers的早期数据显示，在特朗普第二任政府时期，伊朗石油出口——该国政府最大的硬通货来源——与拜登政府最后一年同期相比并无显著差异。\n数据显示，2025年7月，德黑兰出口了165万桶/日的原油、凝析油和燃料油——几乎与2024年7月的出口量完全相同。总体而言，2025年2月至7月期间，伊朗原油、凝析油和燃料油的平均出口量为180万桶/日。2024年同期，在拜登政府执政期间，伊朗平均出口185万桶/日。\n伊朗石油出口主要惠及中国\n据TankerTrackers称，2025年7月出口量的95%流向中国，其余5%流向阿拉伯联合酋长国。中国的宁波，以及阿拉伯联合酋长国的富查伊拉和杰贝阿里等港口接收了伊朗的原油、凝析油和燃料油。总量的44%通过15艘悬挂伊朗国旗的船只转运。来自其他11个国家的船只，如圭亚那和巴西，也参与了其余石油的转运。\n2024年伊朗石油出口创下新高\n根据石油输出国组织（OPEC）的数据，德黑兰2024年的石油出口收入达到2019年以来的最高水平。2024年，德黑安出口了价值467亿美元的原油，比2023年多56亿美元。这一数字与我们在民主防卫基金会的估算相符，但略高于我们的估算——410亿至455亿美元；该估算考虑了据报道德黑兰为鼓励其主要客户中国购买受制裁石油而提供的折扣。我们估计，截至目前，2025年德黑兰已出口价值最高达270亿美元的石油。\n国会为执行制裁所作的努力\n拜登政府无力或不愿执行美国针对德黑兰石油出口业务的制裁，是白宫与美国国会之间紧张关系的一个根源。为迫使拜登采取行动，众议院于2023年通过了《停止窝藏伊朗石油法》（SHIP法案），该法案既将扩大政府执行制裁的惩罚工具，也将引入强制性报告制度，以提高国会对政府执行制裁努力的了解程度。\n华盛顿应加强制裁\n伊朗利用石油出口所得资金资助国内镇压和海外侵略。如果出口继续，伊朗将拥有重建和扩充其核计划、导弹武库及代理组织所需的资金。\n为了有效打击伊朗的非法石油贸易，美国必须改变做法。当前的制裁过于软弱，避开了中国和阿拉伯联合酋长国等地已知的相关活动枢纽中的大型银行和港口。需要采取更强硬的立场，首先不仅要制裁涉事公司，还要制裁管理这些公司的人员，从高管层到董事会。\n与此同时，美国应\n超越单靠制裁的做法，更有力地运用其军事和情报能力。这意味着增加美国海军对伊朗油轮的拦截，并针对顶级违规者开展秘密行动，以传递一个明确的信息：帮助伊朗的代价已大幅飙升。\n\nSaeed Ghasseminejad 是民主防卫基金会（FDD）的伊朗事务和金融经济学高级顾问。欲获取作者和FDD的更多分析，请点击此处订阅。请在X上关注Saeed：@SGhasseminejad。在X上关注FDD：@FDD 和 @FDD_Iran。FDD是一家总部位于华盛顿特区、专注于外交政策和国家安全的无党派研究机构。\n\n议题：\n议题：\n中国\n能源\n伊朗\n伊朗政治与经济\n主题：\n主题：\n北京\n巴西\n中国\n唐纳德·特朗普\n圭亚那\n伊朗\n乔·拜登\n石油输出国组织（OPEC）\n德黑兰\n阿拉伯联合酋长国\n美国国会\n美国海军\n美国参议院\n华盛顿\n显示更多\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n民主防卫基金会\n隐私政策\n邮政信箱 33249，华盛顿特区 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-08-07T21:07:01+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2429","ktid":1001350,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001350","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"中国洗钱者正在为美国的芬太尼危机提供资金","title_en":"China’s money launderers are bankrolling America’s fentanyl epidemic","summary_cn":"保卫民主基金会经济与金融权力中心研究人员在《国会山报》撰文指出，中国洗钱网络正通过美国金融体系清洗墨西哥贩毒集团的资金，助长美国芬太尼危机。文章援引财政部金融犯罪执法网络8月28日发布的警告，称中国洗钱网络是美国金融体系面临的最重大洗钱威胁之一，呼吁政府采取更多行动予以打击。","summary_en":"Researchers from FDD's Center on Economic and Financial Power argue in The Hill that Chinese money laundering networks are scrubbing Mexican cartel cash through the U.S. financial system, fueling America's fentanyl crisis. They cite a FinCEN advisory warning that Chinese money laundering networks represent one of the most significant threats to the U.S. financial system, and call for stronger government action to shut them down.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:00:12.128572+00:00","url":"https://www.fdd.org/analysis/2025/09/08/chinas-money-launderers-are-bankrolling-americas-fentanyl-epidemic/","content":"September 8, 2025\n| The Hill\nChina’s money launderers are bankrolling America’s fentanyl epidemic\nHome » China\nMax Meizlish\nCEFP Research Fellow\nElaine K. Dezenski\nCEFP Senior Director and Head\nSeptember 8, 2025\n| The Hill\nChina’s money launderers are bankrolling America’s fentanyl epidemic\nMax Meizlish\nCEFP Research Fellow\nElaine K. Dezenski\nCEFP Senior Director and Head\nExcerpt\nMoney laundering isn’t new — and neither is China’s role in it. Millennia ago, Chinese merchants developed schemes to “clean” the profits of commercial trade and avoid taxation. Today, their successors are doing much the same. Only now, they’re laundering billions through the U.S. financial system and fueling one of the deadliest fentanyl-fueled drug crises in American history.\nIn a step in the right direction, the Treasury Department’s Financial Crimes Enforcement Network (known as FinCEN) issued a sweeping advisory on Aug. 28 warning that Chinese money laundering networks now represent “one of the most significant money laundering threat actors facing the U.S. financial system.” Few Americans have heard of these Chinese networks, but they are using our local, regional and national banks to scrub Mexican cartel cash clean.\nThe government must do more to shut them down.\nMax Meizlish, who previously worked in the U.S. Treasury’s Office of Foreign Assets Control, is a senior research analyst for the Foundation for Defense of Democracies‘ Center on Economic and Financial Power, where Elaine Dezenski is senior director. Dezenski is also a former deputy and acting assistant secretary of Homeland Security.\nRead in The Hill\nIssues:\nIssues:\nChina\nSanctions and Illicit Finance\nTrade\nTopics:\nTopics:\nChina\nChinese\nElaine Dezenski\nFinancial Crimes Enforcement Network\nOffice of Foreign Assets Control\nU.S. Department of Homeland Security\nUnited States Department of the Treasury\nCopyright ©\n2026\nFoundation for Defense of Democracies\nPrivacy Policy\nP.O. Box 33249, Washington D.C. 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\nSubscribe\nMedia Center","content_cn":"2025年9月8日\n| The Hill\n中国洗钱者正在为美国芬太尼流行病提供资金\n首页 » 中国\nMax Meizlish\nCEFP 研究员\nElaine K. Dezenski\nCEFP 高级主任兼负责人\n2025年9月8日\n| The Hill\n中国洗钱者正在为美国芬太尼流行病提供资金\nMax Meizlish\nCEFP 研究员\nElaine K. Dezenski\nCEFP 高级主任兼负责人\n摘录\n洗钱并不新鲜——中国在其中扮演的角色也不新鲜。数千年前，中国商人就开发出将商业贸易利润“洗白”并逃避税收的方案。如今，他们的继承者所做的大致相同。只是现在，他们正通过美国金融体系洗白数十亿美元，并助长美国历史上最致命的、由芬太尼驱动的毒品危机之一。\n朝着正确方向迈出的一步是，财政部金融犯罪执法网络（称为 FinCEN）于8月28日发布了一份范围广泛的咨询公告，警告中国洗钱网络如今构成“美国金融体系面临的最重大洗钱威胁行为体之一”。很少有美国人听说过这些中国网络，但它们正利用我们的地方性、区域性和全国性银行来洗白墨西哥贩毒集团的现金。\n政府必须采取更多措施来关闭这些网络。\nMax Meizlish 曾在美国财政部外国资产控制办公室任职，现为保卫民主基金会经济与金融力量中心的高级研究分析师；Elaine Dezenski 在该中心担任高级主任。Dezenski 还曾任国土安全部副助理部长及代理助理部长。\n在 The Hill 阅读\n议题：\n议题：\n中国\n制裁与非法金融\n贸易\n主题：\n主题：\n中国\n中国人\nElaine Dezenski\n金融犯罪执法网络\n外国资产控制办公室\n美国国土安全部\n美国财政部\n版权所有 ©\n2026\n保卫民主基金会\n隐私政策\nP.O. Box 33249，华盛顿特区 20033\n202-207-0190\n[email protected]\n订阅\n媒体中心","publish_source":"fdd.org","publish_time":"2025-09-08T20:20:49+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3656","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CISA发布安全远程办公实践指南","title_en":"CISA Releases Guide on Safe Teleworking Practices — FEDagent","summary_cn":"随着大量联邦雇员转为远程办公，网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）发布了一份长期安全远程办公指南，面向管理层、IT专业人员和普通员工三部分提出建议。指南要求高管更新组织政策、开展网络安全培训并评估远程资产风险；IT人员应更新软硬件、评估安全架构、强制多因素认证、维护协作工具清单、定期备份并部署DMARC验证；员工则需确保家庭网络安全、谨慎处理敏感数据并报告可疑活动。","summary_en":"With many federal employees now teleworking, the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) released a guide to help individuals and organizations telework safely for the long term. The guide is divided into three parts for executives, IT professionals and everyday employees. Executives are urged to update policies, provide cybersecurity training and assess risks of remote assets; IT staff should update hardware and software, evaluate security architecture, enforce multifactor authentication, maintain approved collaboration tools, perform backups and implement DMARC validation; employees should secure home networks, handle sensitive data carefully and report suspicious activity.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:40:26.704764+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/cisa-releases-guide-on-safe-teleworking-practices","content":"CISA Releases Guide on Safe Teleworking Practices\nNews\nOct 8\nWritten By FEDagent\nWith many federal employees now teleworking, the importance of working from home securely and safely is high. In response to both new and old cybersecurity risks, the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) released a guide to help individuals and organizations safely telework for the long-term. The guide is divided into three primary parts for bosses, security professionals, and everyday employees. The guide states, “An organization’s executive leaders, IT professionals, and teleworkers all have roles to play in the shift from temporary to long-term or permanent telework strategies.” The following four focus areas are suggested for executive leaders:Update organizational policies and procedures for a stronger cyber security infrastructure and communicate applicable changes with employees.Implement cyber security training for employees to better educate them for the cyber workspace.Determine cybersecurity risks when moving organizational assets such as printing from home and using a personal computer. Include security configurations for all employees.Create a hybrid culture of remote employees, on premise employees, and both. Address the basics of cyber hygiene with employees.The next six focus areas are suggested for IT professionals, who have a large responsibility when it comes to cybersecurity:Update hardware and software to manage and assess vulnerability risks. Consider using automatic software updates. Evaluate the current security architecture and ensure that it is properly protecting—and providing visibility into—remote sites and endpoints, including employees who may use public WiFi. Enforce multifactor authentication for employee remote access.Use of multifactor authentication.Maintain a list of organizationally approved products for collaboration and ensure these are secure. Provide users guidance on these tools.Perform frequent backups and reboots of the organization’s systems and important files, verifying them regularly, and storing them securely.Implement a Domain-Based Message Authentication, Reporting and Conformance (DMARC) validation system to address increased risk of phishing and business email compromise while teleworking.The final focus areas are suggested for remote employees:Ensure your home network is properly configured and secure.Follow secure practices and organizational policies for handling all sensitive data.Exercise caution when opening email attachments and clicking links in email in case of phishing attacks or malware risks.Report suspicious activity to organization’s IT security team immediately. Know the procedures for doing so.The CISA guide also includes specific resources that readers can access for additional information on any of the recommendations.CISA explains on their website, “The Telework Essentials Toolkit is designed to assist business leaders, IT staff, and end users in their transition to a secure, permanent telework environment through simple, actionable recommendations.” CISA has released various telework tools since the onset of the pandemic. On their website, they have a variety of resources that user can access including a cyber-security assessment, tips for cyber safety, detection and prevention, and cyber incident response.\nteleworkremote workcybersecurityCISACybersecurity and Infrastucture Security Agency\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nFederal Judge Orders Presidential Law Enforcement Commission to Halt Work\nNext\nNext\nSafeguarding Your Vote: A Joint Message on Election Security","content_cn":"CISA发布安全远程办公实践指南\n新闻\n10月8日\n撰稿：FEDagent\n目前许多联邦雇员都在远程办公，因此安全可靠地在家工作的重要性很高。为应对新的和旧的网络安全风险，网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）发布了一份指南，帮助个人和组织长期安全地开展远程办公。该指南分为三个主要部分，分别面向管理者、安全专业人员和普通员工。指南称：“组织的高管领导者、IT专业人员和远程办公人员，在从临时远程办公战略转向长期或永久远程办公战略的过程中，都承担着应有的职责。”\n建议高管领导者关注以下四个领域：\n更新组织政策和流程，以建立更强的网络安全基础设施，并将适用的变更告知员工。\n实施员工网络安全培训，更好地帮助他们适应网络工作环境。\n在将打印等组织资产转移到家庭使用并使用个人电脑时，确定网络安全风险。为所有员工纳入安全配置。\n建立由远程员工、现场员工以及两者组成的混合文化。向员工讲解网络卫生基础知识。\n\n接下来建议IT专业人员关注六个领域；在网络安全方面，他们承担着重大责任：\n更新硬件和软件，以管理和评估漏洞风险。考虑使用自动软件更新。\n评估当前的安全架构，确保其能够妥善保护远程站点和终端，并提供对这些站点和终端的可见性，包括可能使用公共WiFi的员工。\n强制员工远程访问使用多因素身份验证。\n使用多因素身份验证。\n维护一份组织批准用于协作的产品清单，并确保这些产品安全。向用户提供这些工具的使用指导。\n定期备份和重启组织系统及重要文件，定期验证备份，并安全存储。\n实施基于域的消息认证、报告和一致性（DMARC）验证系统，以应对远程办公期间网络钓鱼和商业电子邮件入侵风险增加的问题。\n\n最后，建议远程员工关注以下领域：\n确保家庭网络配置正确且安全。\n在处理所有敏感数据时，遵循安全实践和组织政策。\n打开电子邮件附件和点击邮件中的链接时保持谨慎，以防网络钓鱼攻击或恶意软件风险。\n立即向组织的IT安全团队报告可疑活动。了解报告程序。\n\nCISA指南还包括具体资源，读者可以访问这些资源，以获取有关任何建议的更多信息。\nCISA在其网站上解释说：“远程办公必备工具包旨在通过简单、可操作的建议，帮助企业领导者、IT员工和最终用户过渡到安全、永久的远程办公环境。”自疫情开始以来，CISA已发布各种远程办公工具。在其网站上，用户可以访问多种资源，包括网络安全评估、网络安全提示、检测与预防以及网络事件响应。\n\n远程办公\n远程工作\n网络安全\nCISA\n网络安全与基础设施安全局\nFEDagent\n上一页\n上一页\n联邦法官命令总统执法委员会停止工作\n下一页\n下一页\n保障你的选票：关于选举安全的联合信息","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2020-10-08T18:07:43-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3652","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CISA与华盛顿指挥官队在NFL赛季前举行安全演练","title_en":"CISA, Washington Commanders Hold Safety Exercise Ahead of NFL Season — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）近日与华盛顿指挥官队、FedEx球场工作人员及马里兰州和地方急救人员举行桌面演练，模拟真实事件，重点演练事件前后信息共享及应急响应与恢复。CISA官员强调信息共享和伙伴关系的重要性。此类演练CISA每年与体育联盟、场馆等举办逾150次。","summary_en":"The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) recently held a tabletop exercise with the Washington Commanders, FedEx Field staff and Maryland state and local first responders, simulating a real incident. The four-hour drill focused on information sharing and emergency response and recovery. CISA officials stressed the importance of trusted partnerships. CISA conducts over 150 such exercises yearly with sports leagues and venues.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:49:44.903448+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/cisa-washington-commanders-hold-safety-exercise-ahead-of-nfl-season","content":"CISA, Washington Commanders Hold Safety Exercise Ahead of NFL Season\nNews\nJul 27\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe NFL season is right around the corner and that means law enforcement personnel will be charged with keeping athletes, fans, and employees safe at stadiums around the country. To make sure everyone is prepared, the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Agency (CISA) recently held a tabletop training exercise with the Washington Commanders, FedEx Field staff, and Maryland state and local first responders, simulating a real incident. The exercise was for training purposes and was not in response to a real threat. The four-hour exercise prioritized information sharing before and during the incident, as well as emergency response and immediate recovery operations. CISA Executive Assistant Director for Infrastructure Security David Mussington explained that information sharing is critical. “If a real-world emergency happens, no single agency is going to respond alone. Now more than ever, we need strong, trusted, reliable relationships with partners who know how to communicate and work together effectively,” said Mussington. After the exercise, participants shared best practices to keep everyone safe during highly attended events. “Tabletop exercises, in partnership with CISA, are crucial in reinforcing our preparedness for safety incidents and updating our approaches to response and recovery plans in a rapidly evolving environment,” said Washington Commanders Senior Vice President of Operations and Guest Experience Trista Langdon. CISA reminds the public to follow state and local guidance, remain vigilant, and report any suspicious activity to personnel or law enforcement. The Commanders’ exercise was one of over 150 that CISA conducts each year with sports leagues, stadiums, arenas, and other large venues around the country. \"This exercise was just one of the many examples of the planning and coordination that takes place long before game days to keep fans and athletes safe,” said CISA Regional Director Bill Ryan.Agency staff also advises venues on how to improve their security and resiliency.  More information on CISA’s physical security programs can be found on the CISA website.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nNavigating The Mental Health Landscape Of Gen Z: An Interview With Dr. Katie Finn\nNext\nNext\nBills to Boost Border Patrol Pay, CBP Hiring, Wildland Firefighter Pay Advance","content_cn":"CISA与华盛顿指挥官队在NFL赛季前举行安全演练\n新闻\n7月27日\nFEDagent撰写\nNFL赛季即将开始，这意味着执法人员将负责保障全国各地体育场内运动员、球迷和员工的安全。为确保所有人做好准备，网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）最近与华盛顿指挥官队、FedEx Field工作人员以及马里兰州和地方的首批响应人员举行了一次桌面推演，模拟真实事件。此次演练仅用于培训，并非应对真实威胁。为期四小时的演练重点是在事件发生前和期间共享信息，以及应急响应和即时恢复行动。CISA基础设施安全执行助理局长David Mussington解释说，信息共享至关重要。“如果现实世界发生紧急情况，不会有任何一个机构单独响应。现在比以往任何时候都更需要与了解如何有效沟通和协作的合作伙伴建立强大、可信赖、可靠的关系，”Mussington说。演练结束后，参与者分享了在高人流活动期间保障所有人安全的最佳做法。“与CISA合作开展桌面演练，对于强化我们应对安全事件的准备，并在快速变化的环境中更新响应和恢复计划的方法至关重要，”华盛顿指挥官队运营与宾客体验高级副总裁Trista Langdon说。CISA提醒公众遵循州和地方指导，保持警惕，并向工作人员或执法部门报告任何可疑活动。指挥官队的演练是CISA每年与全国各地的体育联盟、体育场、竞技场和其他大型场所开展的150多次演练之一。“这次演练只是众多例子之一，体现了比赛日之前很久就开始进行的规划与协调，以保障球迷和运动员的安全，”CISA区域主任Bill Ryan说。该机构工作人员还就如何改善场所的安全和韧性向场所提供建议。有关CISA实体安全项目的更多信息，可在CISA网站上找到。\nFEDagent\n上一页\n上一页\n探索Z世代心理健康领域：采访Katie Finn博士\n下一页\n下一页\n提高边境巡逻薪酬、增加海关与边境保护局招聘及提高野地消防员薪酬的法案获推进","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2023-07-27T10:34:18-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1770","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部将在拨款法案中获得逾640亿美元资金","title_en":"Department of Homeland Security Slated to Receive Over $64 Billion in Funding Bill — FEDagent","summary_cn":"众议院正推进国土安全部2026财年拨款法案，总额644亿美元，其中海关与边境保护局获183亿，移民与海关执法局获100亿。法案包含拘留资金上限、为ICE和CBP人员提供降级培训等条款。民主党领导层对法案存在分歧，部分人认为改革力度不足，部分人担忧否决将影响TSA、FEMA和海岸警卫队。","summary_en":"The House is advancing the Department of Homeland Security funding bill for fiscal year 2026, totaling $64.4 billion, with $18.3 billion for Customs and Border Protection and $10 billion for Immigration and Customs Enforcement. The bill includes detention funding caps and de-escalation training for ICE and CBP officers. Democratic leaders are divided, with some saying reforms are insufficient and others warning a lapse would affect TSA, FEMA, and the Coast Guard.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:41:02.829129+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/department-of-homeland-security-slated-to-receive-over-64-billion-in-funding-bill","content":"Department of Homeland Security Slated to Receive Over $64 Billion in Funding Bill\nNews\nJan 22\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe House is moving toward passing the funding bill for the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) as it looks to wrap up all 12 spending bills for fiscal year (FY) 2026 and avoid a partial government shutdown on January 30.  The DHS bill is shaping up to be the most controversial of the FY26 spending package. Democratic leaders say they cannot support the bipartisan-negotiated bill, arguing it fails to sufficiently limit President Trump’s use of Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) officers. Republican leaders counter that the bill strikes a balance between border security, enforcement, and accountability.What’s in the BillThe bill funds the Department of Homeland Security with $64.4 billion for FY 26. The legislation allocates $18.3 billion to U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP). And it allocates $10 billion to ICE, which is flat from the prior year. Some of the provisions for ICE including the following:$3.8 billion for detainment and deportation operations (a drop of $115 million)$2.6 billion for Homeland Security Investigations $20 million for body camerasDHS ordered to standardize uniforms for domestic law enforcement except when officers are working undercoverDetention funding cappedImproves transparency around DHS’s use of funds from the One Big Beautiful Bill In addition, DHS is ordered to provide additional de-escalation training for ICE and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) officers, and training on the public’s right to record interactions with federal agents. The bill puts Democrats in a tough spot. Democratic Appropriations Committee Ranking Member Rosa DeLauro (D-CT) says the bill is a step toward reining in ICE, and that denying funding would affect other DHS agencies. “The Homeland Security funding bill is more than just ICE. If we allow a lapse in funding, TSA agents will be forced to work without pay, FEMA assistance could be delayed, and the U.S. Coast Guard will be adversely affected,” said Rep. DeLauro. But other Democrats say the bill is a non-starter. “These reforms aren’t enough. [ICE’s] lawlessness has to stop. And they’re only doing this because they can,” said Democratic Caucus Chairman Pete Aguilar (D-CA). Other Provisions in the Funding BillBeyond ICE, the legislation allocates $5.7 billion to FEMA, $873 million above current levels. It includes language restricting pauses in FEMA’s non-grant funding and includes new public reporting requirements on FEMA’s review of state reimbursement requests. The Secret Service would be funded with $3.3 billion, including $44 million for planning and coordination of security around major events, like the 2026 FIFA World Cup.The Transportation Security Administration (TSA) would receive $11.8 billion, including $6 billion for the frontline screening workforce. The U.S. Coast Guard is on track to get $13.9 billion, “reflecting enhancement of resources to modernize the Coast Guard and support surge operations to safeguard our border and promote national security.”\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nRetired DEA Agent Sentenced to Five Years for Protecting Drug Traffickers\nNext\nNext\nVA Watchdog Flags Patient Safety Risks from AI Use in Veterans Health Care","content_cn":"国土安全部将在拨款法案中获得超过640亿美元的资金\n新闻\n1月22日\n撰稿：FEDagent\n众议院正准备通过国土安全部（DHS）拨款法案，同时力争完成2026财年（FY）全部12项拨款法案，并避免1月30日部分政府停摆。DHS法案正逐渐成为2026财年拨款方案中争议最大的一项。民主党领导人表示无法支持这项两党协商达成的法案，认为其未能充分限制特朗普总统对移民与海关执法局（ICE）官员的使用。共和党领导人则反驳说，该法案在边境安全、执法和问责之间取得了平衡。\n法案内容\n该法案为国土安全部2026财年提供644亿美元资金。立法向美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）拨款183亿美元，并向ICE拨款100亿美元，与上一年度持平。法案中有关ICE的部分条款包括：\n38亿美元用于拘留和驱逐行动（减少1.15亿美元）\n26亿美元用于国土安全调查\n2000万美元用于随身摄像机\n要求DHS为国内执法人员统一制服，但官员执行卧底任务时除外\n设定拘留资金上限\n提高DHS使用《一项伟大而美丽的法案》资金的透明度\n此外，DHS被要求为ICE和海关与边境保护局（CBP）官员提供额外的降级冲突培训，以及关于公众有权记录与联邦特工互动的培训。\n该法案让民主党陷入两难。民主党拨款委员会首席成员Rosa DeLauro（康涅狄格州民主党人）表示，该法案是约束ICE的一步，拒绝拨款将影响DHS的其他机构。DeLauro众议员说：“国土安全拨款法案不仅仅涉及ICE。如果拨款中断，运输安全管理局（TSA）特工将被迫无薪工作，联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）的援助可能被延误，美国海岸警卫队也将受到不利影响。”\n但其他民主党人表示，该法案不可接受。民主党党团主席Pete Aguilar（加利福尼亚州民主党人）说：“这些改革还不够。[ICE的]违法行为必须停止。而他们之所以这样做，只是因为他们做得到。”\n拨款法案中的其他条款\n除ICE外，法案还向FEMA拨款57亿美元，比当前水平增加8.73亿美元。法案包括限制暂停FEMA非拨款资金的条款，并新增要求公开报告FEMA审核各州报销申请的规定。特勤局将获得33亿美元，其中包括4400万美元，用于规划和协调2026年国际足联世界杯等重大活动的安保工作。\n运输安全管理局（TSA）将获得118亿美元，其中60亿美元用于一线安检工作人员。美国海岸警卫队预计将获得139亿美元，“反映出增加资源以实现海岸警卫队现代化、支持激增行动、保障边境安全并促进国家安全”。\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n退休缉毒局特工因保护毒贩被判五年监禁\n下一篇\n下一篇\n退伍军人事务部监察机构警告人工智能用于退伍军人医疗保健存在患者安全风险","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-01-22T12:22:58-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3148","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部裁员波及FEMA和CISA，部长诺姆下令测谎","title_en":"DHS Firings Hit FEMA, CISA as Secretary Noem Orders Lie Detector Tests — FEDagent","summary_cn":"据FEDagent报道，美国国土安全部（DHS）解雇了400名试用期员工，其中联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）约200人、网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）130人、美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）50人。DHS称此举可为纳税人节省约5000万美元。此外，部长克里斯蒂·诺姆下令所有测谎测试须包含关于未经授权与媒体和非营利组织沟通的问题，并准备解雇数百名高级领导人。","summary_en":"FEDagent reports that the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) fired 400 probationary employees, including about 200 at FEMA, 130 at CISA, and 50 at USCIS, claiming roughly $50 million in taxpayer savings. DHS Secretary Kristi Noem also ordered that all polygraph tests include a question about unauthorized communications with media and nonprofit organizations, and the department is preparing to fire hundreds of senior leaders to align with the administration's goals.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:04:27.622380+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-firings-hit-fema-cisa-as-secretary-noem-orders-lie-detector-tests","content":"DHS Firings Hit FEMA, CISA as Secretary Noem Orders Lie Detector Tests\nNews\nFeb 20\nWritten By FEDagent\nAcross the board federal agencies are firing employees on probation, following President Trump's orders. The Department of Homeland Security (DHS) fired 400 employees, with promises to remove more. The employees were on probationary status and were said to be in non-critical positions. “Today’s Department of Homeland Security personnel action will result in roughly $50 million in savings for American taxpayers and incalculable value toward accountability and cutting red tape,” said a DHS spokesperson in a statement. DHS also promised further reductions noting that it is “actively identifying other wasteful positions and offices that do not fulfill DHS’ mission.” FEMA FiringsThe biggest cuts were at the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA), where approximately 200 employees on probation were fired. The Washington Post reports that latency officials estimate they’ll be short about 1,000 employees because of the terminations and the deferred resignation program. While Democrats worry it will hurt the agency’s ability to respond to disasters (FEMA is currently responding to about 100 across the nation), Republicans say change is needed. “The federal government’s labyrinthine disaster response and recovery programs have not been subject to the scrutiny needed to assess whether it is achieving its goals or whether its funding would be better spent with limited strings attached at the state and local levels,” wrote Senator James Lankford (R-OK).The firing of Chief Financial Officer Mary Comans is said to be particularly unsettling to FEMA employees. According to CNN, Comans is being made the scapegoat for sending money to state and local programs that were used to help undocumented immigrants. Earlier, DHS Secretary Kristi Noem ordered all such payments to stop, but did not specify the ending of payments to state and local governments for such purposes. Other FiringsThe cuts include 130 positions at the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA), which plays a role in helping the private sector prepare for cyberattacks, as well as physical risks. 50 employees at U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) were let go. Senior Leaders on the Chopping BlockMeanwhile, NBC News reports that the DHS is preparing to fire hundreds of senior leaders as soon as this week, to align leadership more with the administration’s goals. The administration reportedly has a “centralized plan” and a list of people in high-level positions across every component of DHS slated for firing. Lie Detector Tests OrderedAnd DHS Secretary Kristi Noem told employees that polygraph tests will be used to catch leaks that are foiling immigration enforcement plants. As reported by Bloomberg, Secretary Noem ordered that all DHS polygraphs administered must include a question about unauthorized communications with media and nonprofit organizations.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nImmigration Judges Canned by Administration as ICE Falls Behind Arrest Goals\nNext\nNext\nPolice Arrest Leader of Alleged “Cultlike” Group with Ties to Murder of Border Patrol Agent","content_cn":"DHS裁员波及FEMA和CISA，部长诺姆下令进行测谎测试\n新闻\n2月20日\n作者：FEDagent\n联邦机构正在全面解雇处于试用期的员工，此举遵循特朗普总统的命令。国土安全部（DHS）解雇了400名员工，并承诺还将进一步裁员。这些员工处于试用期，据称担任非关键职位。DHS发言人在声明中说：“今天国土安全部的人事行动将为美国纳税人节省约5000万美元，并为问责和减少繁文缛节带来不可估量的价值。”DHS还承诺进一步削减人员，并指出其“正在积极识别其他浪费性职位和办公室，这些职位和办公室未能履行DHS的使命”。\nFEMA裁员\n最大规模的削减发生在联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA），约200名处于试用期的员工被解雇。《华盛顿邮报》报道称，机构官员估计，由于这些解雇和延期辞职计划，他们将短缺约1000名员工。民主党人担心这会损害该机构应对灾害的能力（FEMA目前正在全国应对约100起灾害），而共和党人则表示需要改革。俄克拉荷马州共和党参议员詹姆斯·兰克福特写道：“联邦政府错综复杂的灾害响应和恢复项目一直没有接受必要的审查，以评估其是否实现了目标，或者其资金是否更适合在州和地方层面、附带较少限制的情况下使用。”\n据称，解雇首席财务官玛丽·科曼斯尤其令FEMA员工不安。据CNN报道，科曼斯被当作替罪羊，因为她向州和地方项目拨款，而这些项目曾被用于帮助无证移民。此前，DHS部长克里斯蒂·诺姆下令停止所有此类付款，但没有明确说明是否停止向州和地方政府提供用于此类目的的资金。\n其他裁员\n此次削减包括网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）的130个职位，该机构负责帮助私营部门为网络攻击及实体风险做好准备。美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）有50名员工被解雇。\n高级领导层面临裁撤\n与此同时，NBC新闻报道称，DHS正准备最早于本周解雇数百名高级领导，以使领导层更加符合本届政府的目标。据报道，本届政府制定了一个“集中化计划”，并列出DHS各组成部门所有高级职位中计划被解雇的人员名单。\n下令进行测谎测试\nDHS部长克里斯蒂·诺姆告诉员工，将使用测谎测试来抓出破坏移民执法计划的泄密行为。据彭博社报道，诺姆部长下令，所有进行的DHS测谎测试必须包含一个关于未经授权与媒体和非营利组织沟通的问题。\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n政府解雇移民法官，ICE未达到逮捕目标\n下一篇\n警方逮捕涉嫌“邪教式”团体领导人，该团体与谋杀边境巡逻队员有关","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-02-20T12:55:52-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3623","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"GAO：国土安全部需要更好的流程来招聘优先岗位人员","title_en":"DHS Needs Better Processes to Hire Priority Staff: GAO — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国政府问责局（GAO）审查了国土安全部（DHS）优先岗位的招聘时间，包括边境巡逻人员、移民服务官员和网络防御事件响应人员。GAO发现，DHS在2022财年13个优先岗位中有9个未达到平均招聘时间目标。招聘缓慢的原因之一是审查流程，部分岗位需要体检、药检和背景调查。GAO还发现DHS各机构跟踪和报告招聘时间的方式不同，且互惠跟踪系统存在问题。GAO提出四项建议，DHS全部同意。","summary_en":"The U.S. Government Accountability Office (GAO) reviewed hiring timelines for priority positions at the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), including border patrol agents, immigration services officers and cyber defense incident responders. GAO found that DHS did not meet its average time-to-hire targets in fiscal year 2022 for nine of the 13 priority positions. One reason for slower hiring is vetting, as some positions require medical exams, drug testing and background checks. GAO also found that DHS agencies track and report time-to-hire differently and that its reciprocity tracking system has issues. GAO made four recommendations, all of which DHS concurred with.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:15:10.467298+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-needs-better-processes-to-hire-priority-staff-gao","content":"DHS Needs Better Processes to Hire Priority Staff: GAO\nNews\nJun 20\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe Government Accountability Office reviewed hiring timelines for priority positions at the Department of Homeland Security (DHS). Priority positions include border patrol agents, immigration services officers, and cyber defense incident responders. GAO found that DHS did not meet its average time-to-hire targets in fiscal year (FY) 2022 for nine of the 13 priority positions.In its report, GAO notes that DHS’s ability to hire quickly is hampered in part because the department has a variety data and vetting practices in its various subagencies. “Having more accurate information could help provide additional clarity on DHS’s hiring and vetting efforts, including whether DHS is making timely hiring decisions so that it does not result in DHS losing out on otherwise qualified candidates,” noted the report. VettingOne of the reasons for slower hiring is vetting. Some DHS positions require significant vetting processes, including medical exams, drug testing, and background checks. DHS noted that ensuring that the vetting is done properly slows the process. GAO also noted that DHS does not include personnel responsible for implementing hiring and vetting in its two working groups on expediting hiring decisions. “By ensuring that DHS and component personnel tasked with implementing hiring and vetting processes are included in existing working groups and other forums, DHS could better leverage practices across components to make faster hiring decisions,” the report notes. Discrepancies in Hiring Timelines GAO also found that it’s difficult to give an accurate assessment on how long it takes to hire, because various DHS agencies track and report time to hire differently. Some of them track when applications are received, others track from the first job posting.Department officials told GAO this is because some component agencies mass hire or post job announcements with indefinite application deadlines. While the discrepancy is acceptable to the Office of Personnel Management (OPM), GAO notes that DHS did not disclose the variability of tracked-to-hire data, which prevents HR leaders from properly analyzing the data to speed up hiring times. In addition, GAO pointed out issues with the DHS system for tracking reciprocity, or when an agency accepts an existing background investigation or trust determination from another agency. GAO found that a certain position could have multiple names and different spellings, making it hard to determine exactly who is eligible for reciprocity. DHS is set to start using a new reciprocity tracking system in 2026, and GAO told the agency to ensure that it standardizes position titles. GAO made four recommendations. DHS concurred with all four. DHS Hiring EventThis comes as DHS makes a continued push to staff up in critical positions. The agency is holding a career expo at the Dulles Expo Center in Chantilly, Virginia, June 27 and 28. Panels include “A Day in the Life of DHS Law Enforcement,” “DHS Women (Leadership) in Law Enforcement,” and “CBP Career Opportunities.”\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nDHS Not Properly Vetting Foreign Nationals: Watchdog\nNext\nNext\nDHS Releases Groundbreaking Strategic Plan","content_cn":"国土安全部需要更好的流程来招聘优先岗位人员：政府问责局\n新闻\n6月20日\n作者：FEDagent\n政府问责局审查了国土安全部（DHS）优先岗位的招聘时间线。优先岗位包括边境巡逻特工、移民服务官员和网络防御事件响应人员。政府问责局发现，国土安全部在2022财年（FY）的13个优先岗位中，有9个未达到平均招聘用时目标。\n\n政府问责局在报告中指出，国土安全部快速招聘的能力在一定程度上受到该部门各下属机构采用不同数据和审查做法的阻碍。报告指出：“拥有更准确的信息，可能有助于进一步厘清国土安全部的招聘和审查工作，包括国土安全部是否及时作出招聘决定，从而避免其失去原本合格的候选人。”\n\n审查\n招聘较慢的原因之一是审查。一些国土安全部职位需要重要的审查流程，包括体检、药物检测和背景调查。国土安全部指出，确保审查工作正确完成会减缓流程。政府问责局还指出，国土安全部没有将负责落实招聘和审查工作的人员纳入其两个旨在加快招聘决定的工作组。报告指出：“通过确保将负责落实招聘和审查流程的国土安全部及其组成机构人员纳入现有工作组和其他论坛，国土安全部可以更好地利用各组成机构的做法，更快地作出招聘决定。”\n\n招聘时间线的差异\n政府问责局还发现，由于国土安全部各机构以不同方式跟踪和报告招聘用时，因此很难准确评估招聘需要多长时间。其中一些机构从收到申请时开始跟踪，另一些则从首次发布职位公告时开始跟踪。\n\n部门官员告诉政府问责局，这是因为一些组成机构会大规模招聘，或发布申请截止日期不确定的职位公告。尽管这种差异为人事管理办公室（OPM）所接受，政府问责局指出，国土安全部没有披露所跟踪招聘数据的差异性，这妨碍了人力资源负责人恰当分析数据以缩短招聘时间。此外，政府问责局还指出，国土安全部用于跟踪互认的系统存在问题；互认是指一个机构接受另一机构已有的背景调查或信任认定。政府问责局发现，某一职位可能有多个名称和不同拼写，因此很难准确确定谁符合互认资格。国土安全部计划于2026年开始使用新的互认跟踪系统，政府问责局要求该机构确保职位名称标准化。政府问责局提出了四项建议。国土安全部同意全部四项。\n\n国土安全部招聘活动\n与此同时，国土安全部持续推动为关键岗位增员。该机构将于6月27日和28日在弗吉尼亚州尚蒂利的杜勒斯博览中心举办职业博览会。专题讨论包括“国土安全部执法人员的一天”、“国土安全部执法部门女性（领导力）”和“美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）职业机会”。\n\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n国土安全部未适当审查外国国民：监察机构\n下一篇\n下一篇\n国土安全部发布开创性战略计划","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2024-06-20T12:19:58-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1205","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长提出从庇护城市机场撤走CBP官员；DHS员工将收到工资","title_en":"DHS Secretary Floats Pulling CBP Officers From Sanctuary City Airports; DHS Workers to Receive Paychecks — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长Markwayne Mullin表示，可能减少或撤走限制与联邦移民执法合作的庇护城市机场的海关与边境保护局（CBP）官员，此举或影响纽约肯尼迪、旧金山、洛杉矶和芝加哥奥黑尔等繁忙国际机场。移民政策专家对此表示担忧，认为按政府自身定义这将终止约58%国际航空客流。与此同时，DHS因拨款中断仍处于停摆状态，员工将于4月10日起收到补发工资，国会复会前快速达成拨款协议的前景不明。","summary_en":"Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin suggested he may remove or limit U.S. Customs and Border Protection officers at airports in sanctuary cities that restrict cooperation with federal immigration enforcement, potentially disrupting international travel at busy airports such as New York's JFK, San Francisco, Los Angeles and Chicago O'Hare. Immigration policy experts expressed concern, noting that by the administration's own definitions this would end about 58 percent of international air traffic. Meanwhile, DHS remains shut down amid a funding lapse, with employees set to receive backpay starting April 10, while prospects for a quick congressional funding deal remain dim.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:07:05.742081+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-secretary-floats-pulling-cbp-officers-from-sanctuary-city-airports-dhs-workers-to-receive-paychecks","content":"DHS Secretary Floats Pulling CBP Officers From Sanctuary City Airports; DHS Workers to Receive Paychecks\nNews\nApr 9\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nNew Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin suggested he may remove or limit U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) officers at airports in cities that restrict cooperation between local law enforcement and federal immigration authorities. “If they're a sanctuary city and they're receiving international flights, and we're asking them to partner with us at the airport, but once they walk out of the airport, they're not going to enforce immigration policy — maybe we need to have a really hard look at that,\" Secretary Mullin told Fox News. Should that happen international travel could be disrupted at some of the busiest airports in the world including New York’s JFK Airport, San Francisco International, Los Angeles International, and Chicago O’Hare. Secretary Mullin said DHS would prioritize working with cities and counties that cooperate with federal immigration enforcement officers. \"I am not going outside the policies that Congress passed for me, and we're not trying to push those, but we're saying you've got to partner with us,\" said Secretary Mullin. Immigration policy experts expressed concern, even as they said such a move is not likely to happen. “I did some research. By administration’s own definitions this would end international air travel at US airports where about 58 percent of international traffic happens,” Todd Schulte, president of the pro-immigration political advocacy organization FWD, wrote on X, “so would crash economy (hence won’t happen). [But] it’s very bad it even gets floated!”Paychecks Coming as Shutdown Continues The comments come as DHS remains shut down and Congress is in recess until the week of April 13. DHS employees will start receiving paychecks for backpay on Friday, April 10, with all checks expected to be delivered by Thursday, April 16. Furloughed and excepted employees will be paid their full salaries covering the start of the shutdown on February 14 through April 4, the end of the last full pay period. The paychecks come after President Trump issued a memo ordering DHS and the Office of Management and Budget (OMB) to find a way to make the payments. Prospects for Quick Congressional Deal DimBefore the recess, the Senate twice passed a bill funding DHS minus Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and CBP, sending it to the House for consideration.After resisting the first time, Speaker Mike Johnson (R-LA) supported the legislation. But some more conservative members are demanding that funding for ICE and CBP be taken care of before moving forward. \"We cannot leave ICE and CBP hanging with nothing but hopes and prayers that reconciliation 2.0 comes together,\" the House Freedom Caucus wrote. \"That’s why we must use reconciliation to fully fund all of the Department of Homeland Security.\"\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nFederal Law Enforcement to See Hiring Boost in Proposed Budget\nNext\nNext\nCyber Scams Impersonating U.S. Officials Nearly Double in 2025: FBI","content_cn":"国土安全部长提出从“庇护城市”机场撤出海关与边境保护局官员；国土安全部工作人员将收到工资\n新闻\n4月9日\n撰稿：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n新任国土安全部长马克韦恩·穆林暗示，他可能会从限制地方执法部门与联邦移民当局合作的城市机场撤走或限制美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）官员。“如果他们是庇护城市，并且接收国际航班，而我们要求他们在机场与我们合作，但一走出机场，他们就不执行移民政策——也许我们需要认真审视这一点，”穆林部长告诉福克斯新闻。如果发生这种情况，世界上一些最繁忙机场的国际旅行可能会受到干扰，包括纽约肯尼迪机场、旧金山国际机场、洛杉矶国际机场和芝加哥奥黑尔机场。穆林部长表示，国土安全部将优先与那些配合联邦移民执法官员的城市和县合作。“我没有超出国会为我制定的政策，我们也不是要推动这些政策，但我们是在说，你们必须与我们合作，”穆林部长说。移民政策专家对此表示担忧，尽管他们认为这种举措不太可能发生。“我做了一些研究。按照本届政府自己的定义，这将终结美国机场的国际航空旅行，而美国约58%的国际客流发生在这些机场，”支持移民的政治倡议组织FWD主席托德·舒尔特在X上写道，“所以会摧毁经济（因此不会发生）。但即使有人提出这种想法，也非常糟糕！”\n政府停摆持续，工资即将发放\n上述言论发表之际，国土安全部仍处于停摆状态，国会休会至4月13日当周。国土安全部员工将于4月10日星期五开始收到补发工资，预计所有支票将在4月16日星期四前送达。被迫休假员工和例外员工将获得全额工资，涵盖2月14日停摆开始日至4月4日最后一个完整发薪期结束日。总统特朗普发布备忘录，要求国土安全部和管理与预算办公室（OMB）设法支付这些款项后，工资支票才得以发放。\n国会迅速达成协议的前景黯淡\n休会前，参议院两次通过一项为国土安全部提供资金的法案，但不包括移民与海关执法局（ICE）和海关与边境保护局（CBP）的资金，并将其提交众议院审议。众议院议长迈克·约翰逊（共和党，路易斯安那州）起初反对，但后来支持该法案。不过，一些更保守的议员要求先解决ICE和CBP的资金问题再继续推进。“我们不能让ICE和CBP悬而未决，只能寄希望于‘第二轮预算协调’能够达成，”众议院自由党团写道。“因此，我们必须利用预算协调程序，为国土安全部的全部部门提供充分资金。”\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一篇\n上一篇\n拟议预算将增加联邦执法部门招聘\n下一篇\n下一篇\n2025年冒充美国官员的网络诈骗几乎翻倍：联邦调查局","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-04-09T12:57:05-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2119","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部招聘激增，司法部面临招聘危机","title_en":"DHS Sees Record Recruitment Surge as DOJ Faces Hiring Crisis — FEDagent","summary_cn":"国土安全部报告称ICE收到逾20万份职位申请，并提供最高5万美元签约奖金等激励措施，目标是将执法人员规模翻倍。USCIS的Homeland Defender职位也收到创纪录的3.5万份申请。与此同时，司法部自特朗普上任以来流失约半数律师，约5500人离职，招聘合格候选人面临困难，新入职者更多具有政治背景。","summary_en":"DHS reports over 200,000 applications for ICE positions, offering incentives such as signing bonuses up to $50,000, aiming to double its workforce. USCIS also received a record 35,000 applications for Homeland Defender roles. Meanwhile, DOJ has lost about half its attorneys since Trump took office, roughly 5,500 departures, and is struggling to find qualified candidates, with new hires more likely to have political backgrounds.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:15:13.395799+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-sees-record-recruitment-surge-as-doj-faces-hiring-crisis","content":"DHS Sees Record Recruitment Surge as DOJ Faces Hiring Crisis\nNov 13\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe Department of Homeland Security (DHS) is reporting record recruitment numbers for certain agencies while the Department of Justice (DOJ) is reportedly having trouble filling positions. First to DHS, which says it received more than 200,000 applications for positions at Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE). ICE has been aggressively recruiting as President Trump has made removing illegal migrants a priority of his administration. The One Big Beautiful Bill also provided the agency with a $30 billion cash infusion. The administration wants to double the size of the workforce and have 10,000 deportation officers on the job by January.  To attract workers, ICE is offering benefits including:·       A maximum $50,000 signing bonus·       Student loan repayment and forgiveness options·       25% Law Enforcement Availability Pay (LEAP) for HSI Special Agents·       Administratively Uncontrollable Overtime for Enforcement Removal Operations (ERO) Deportation Officers·       Enhanced retirement benefitsThere are also reports that with the election of Democrat Zohran Mamdani as New York City mayor, ICE is targeting officers with the NYPD for recruitment. However, as we reported earlier at FEDagent, not all is going well with the rush to hire, with questions mounting on whether some were fully vetted before being placed into training programs. USCIS Record Applicants U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services (USCIS) says it received a record 35,000 applications for its Homeland Defender positions. “I’m pleased to announce that in addition to seeing a historic number of applications, we are starting to bring on applicants at a rapid pace,” said USCIS Director Joseph Edlow. USCIS has made hundreds of job offers and is starting to bring new personnel on board. Among those receiving offers are former law enforcement personnel and U.S. military veterans. The Homeland Defender position is an entry-level role with a signing bonus of up to $50,000. Homeland Defenders are responsible for interviewing applicants, reviewing immigration benefits requests, and identifying individuals who may be ineligible under federal law.DOJ Recruiting TroublesIt’s a different story at the Department of Justice. The Washington Post reports that DOJ is struggling with recruitment, as the agency has lost about half of its attorneys since President Trump took office. Advocacy group Justice Connection estimates that around 5,500 people have left this year. Last year, roughly 10,000 attorneys worked across DOJ. The Post says the department has had difficulty finding qualified candidates for open slots, and that interest in working for DOJ among recent law school grads has “plummeted.” “What we are seeing is a total drop in who is applying,” said William Treanor, the former dean of Georgetown University Law Center. “It’s very, very dramatic. It’s gone from a good amount of our graduating class to virtually no one applying for jobs at the Justice Department.”The Post notes that prospective DOJ hires are now more likely to have political backgrounds, with many coming from Republican congressional offices and advocacy groups. But DOJ defended its hiring practices. “The Department of Justice is committed to ensuring taxpayer dollars are used efficiently by hiring the best and most qualified individuals to serve the American people — with emphasis on hiring those fulfilling critical law enforcement and public safety missions,” DOJ said in a statement.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nTech Glitch at VA Leaves Thousands Without Education Payments\nNext\nNext\nFederal Workers Return, Paychecks to Start as Record Breaking Shutdown Ends","content_cn":"国土安全部招聘人数创纪录增长，司法部面临招聘危机\n11月13日\n作者：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n国土安全部（DHS）报告称，某些机构的招聘人数创下纪录，而据报道，司法部（DOJ）正难以填补职位空缺。先说国土安全部：该部门称，已收到超过20万份移民与海关执法局（ICE）职位申请。由于特朗普总统将遣返非法移民列为其政府的优先事项，ICE一直在积极招聘。《一项伟大而美丽的法案》还向该机构注入了300亿美元资金。政府希望将劳动力规模扩大一倍，并在1月前让1万名遣返官员上岗。\n为吸引员工，ICE提供的福利包括：\n· 最高5万美元的签约奖金\n· 学生贷款偿还和豁免选项\n· 国土安全调查局（HSI）特别探员可获得25%的执法可用性薪酬（LEAP）\n· 执法与遣返行动（ERO）遣返官员可获得行政上不可控的加班费\n· 增强的退休福利\n另有报道称，随着民主党人佐赫兰·马姆达尼当选纽约市市长，ICE正瞄准纽约警察局（NYPD）的警员进行招募。\n然而，正如我们此前在FEDagent报道的那样，招聘热潮并非一切顺利；越来越多人质疑，部分人员在被安排进入培训项目之前是否经过了充分审查。\n\nUSCIS申请人数创纪录\n美国公民及移民服务局（USCIS）称，其“国土捍卫者”职位收到了创纪录的3.5万份申请。\nUSCIS局长约瑟夫·埃德洛表示：“我很高兴地宣布，除了看到创纪录数量的申请外，我们也开始以快速节奏录用申请人。”\nUSCIS已发出数百份工作邀约，并开始让新员工入职。收到邀约者中包括前执法人员和美国退伍军人。\n“国土捍卫者”职位属于入门级岗位，签约奖金最高可达5万美元。国土捍卫者负责面试申请人、审查移民福利申请，并识别可能根据联邦法律不具资格的个人。\n\n司法部招聘困境\n司法部的情况则不同。《华盛顿邮报》报道称，司法部正艰难招聘；自特朗普总统上任以来，该机构约有一半律师流失。\n倡导组织Justice Connection估计，今年约有5,500人离职。去年，约有1万名律师在整个司法部任职。\n《邮报》称，该部门难以为职位空缺找到合格候选人，近期法学院毕业生对在司法部工作的兴趣已“骤降”。乔治城大学法律中心前院长威廉·特里纳表示：“我们看到的是申请人数全面下降。这非常、非常显著。原本我们毕业班中有相当一部分人申请司法部的职位，如今几乎没有人申请。”\n《邮报》指出，司法部的潜在雇员如今更可能具有政治背景，许多人来自共和党国会办公室和倡导团体。\n但司法部为其招聘做法辩护。司法部在一份声明中表示：“司法部致力于通过聘用最优秀、最合格的人员为美国人民服务，确保纳税人的钱得到高效使用——重点是聘用履行关键执法和公共安全任务的人员。”\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一篇\n上一篇\n退伍军人事务部技术故障导致数千人未获得教育款项\n下一篇\n下一篇\n创纪录的停摆结束，联邦工作人员返岗，薪水将开始发放","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-11-13T11:53:48-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1231","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI称局长卡什·帕特尔个人邮箱遭黑客入侵，无政府数据泄露","title_en":"FBI Says Director Kash Patel’s Personal Email Hacked, No Government Data Compromised — FEDagent","summary_cn":"FBI证实局长卡什·帕特尔的个人Gmail账户遭黑客入侵，部分个人信息被访问。FBI称被访问信息属历史性质，不涉及政府信息，并已采取缓解措施。与伊朗有关联的黑客组织Handala HackTeam宣称对此负责，称系报复司法部查封其相关域名。事件发生之际，CISA约60%员工因拨款中断被迫休假，网络安全人才流失引发担忧。","summary_en":"The FBI confirmed that Director Kash Patel's personal Gmail account was hacked and some personal information was accessed. The FBI said the information is historical and involves no government information, and that it has taken steps to mitigate risks. An Iranian-linked hacking group, Handala HackTeam, claimed responsibility, calling it retaliation for the DOJ seizing its domains. The incident comes as about 60 percent of CISA employees are furloughed amid the DHS shutdown, raising cybersecurity concerns.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:34:47.032820+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-shutdown-deal-remains-elusive-with-recess-looming-xrjx2-rcb7r","content":"FBI Says Director Kash Patel’s Personal Email Hacked, No Government Data Compromised\nNews\nApr 2\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) confirmed that FBI Director Kash Patel’s personal Gmail account was hacked and that some personal information was accessed. In a statement, the FBI said it’s \"aware of malicious actors targeting\" Director Patel's personal email information and it has \"taken all necessary steps to mitigate potential risks associated with this activity.\" The FBI said information accessed \"is historical in nature and involves no government information.\" An Iranian-linked hacking group known as Handala HackTeam claimed responsibility for the breach. It comes shortly after the Department of Justice (DOJ) seized four domains connected to Handala as part of an ongoing operation to target cybercrimes coming from Iran. The hacking group noted the seizures on its website and said it breached Director Patel’s accounts in retaliation.In March, Handala also claimed responsibility for a cyberattack against U.S. medical-device company Stryker. The federal government is offering a $10 million reward for information about hacking groups from Iran, including Handala. Cyber Concerns MountThe incident comes amid broader concerns about U.S. cybersecurity readiness, particularly as the military conflict with Iran continues and staffing shortages affect key cyber agencies during the DHS shutdown.\"Diminishing of resources here on cybersecurity at this particular juncture is absolutely dangerous,\" Dr. Frederic Lemieux, Georgetown University professor of cybersecurity risk management told ABC News. \"In a conflict with a known enemy that uses cyber weapons to, you know, like to inflict damage on its opponents, I think that it will be tested, that's for sure.”About 60 percent of the employees at the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) are currently on furlough due to the lapse in appropriations.CISA Acting Director Nick Andersen told the House Homeland Security Committee that the agency is also losing workers. “In a single day, just a couple of weeks ago, we received six resignation notices from the highly technical subject matter experts we have in places like our threat [hunting team],” said Acting Director Andersen. “That’s not a sustainable model going forward.”\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nGOP Unveils Two-Track DHS Plan as Shutdown Drags On and Pay Pressure Builds\nNext\nNext\nFEMA Restarts BRIC Disaster Grant Program after Federal Court Order","content_cn":"FBI称局长Kash Patel的个人电子邮箱遭黑客入侵，未泄露政府数据\n新闻\n4月2日\n作者：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n美国联邦调查局（FBI）确认，FBI局长Kash Patel的个人Gmail账户遭到黑客入侵，部分个人信息被访问。FBI在一份声明中称，其“知悉恶意行为者正针对”Patel局长的个人电子邮件信息，并且已“采取一切必要措施，以减轻与该活动相关的潜在风险”。FBI称，被访问的信息“具有历史性质，且不涉及任何政府信息”。\n\n一个名为Handala HackTeam、与伊朗有关联的黑客组织声称对此次入侵负责。此前不久，司法部（DOJ）作为持续打击来自伊朗的网络犯罪行动的一部分，查封了与Handala有关的四个域名。该黑客组织在其网站上提及了这些查封行动，并称其是出于报复而入侵Patel局长的账户。3月，Handala还声称对针对美国医疗器械公司Stryker的一次网络攻击负责。\n\n联邦政府正悬赏1,000万美元，以获取有关来自伊朗的黑客组织、包括Handala在内的信息。\n\n网络安全担忧加剧\n\n该事件发生之际，美国网络安全准备状况受到更广泛的担忧，尤其是在与伊朗的军事冲突持续、且国土安全部停摆期间人员短缺影响主要网络机构之时。\n\n“在这个特定关头削减网络安全资源绝对是危险的，”乔治城大学网络安全风险管理教授Frederic Lemieux博士告诉ABC News。“在与一个使用网络武器、你知道的、喜欢对其对手造成损害的已知敌人的冲突中，我认为这肯定会受到考验。”\n\n由于拨款中断，网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）目前约60%的员工被强制休假。\n\nCISA代理局长Nick Andersen告诉众议院国土安全委员会，该机构也正在流失员工。\n\n代理局长Andersen说：“仅仅几周前的一天，我们就收到6份辞职通知，来自我们在诸如威胁[搜寻团队]等岗位上的高技术主题专家。这不是一个可持续的发展模式。”\n\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n\n上一篇\n上一篇\n随着停摆持续和薪酬压力加大，共和党公布两轨国土安全部计划\n\n下一篇\n下一篇\n联邦法院下令后，FEMA重启BRIC灾害补助计划","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-04-02T13:11:16-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3653","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部公布首个部门级随身摄像头政策","title_en":"DHS Unveils First Department-Wide Policy on Body-Worn Cameras — FEDagent","summary_cn":"国土安全部宣布首个覆盖全部九个执法机构、约8万名执法人员的部门级随身摄像头政策，落实拜登2022年警务行政令。政策规定在响应紧急呼叫、预定逮捕或执行搜查令时须佩戴并开启摄像头，禁止仅为记录第一修正案活动而使用。各机构须在180天内制定或更新符合或超过该指南的政策，部分人员将待资金到位后配备。","summary_en":"DHS announced its first department-wide body-worn camera policy, covering about 80,000 law enforcement officers across nine agencies, implementing Biden's 2022 policing executive order. Officers must wear and activate cameras when responding to emergency calls, making pre-planned arrests, or executing warrants, and cameras may not be used solely to record First Amendment activity. Agencies have 180 days to issue or update compliant policies, with some officers awaiting funding.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:16:27.827219+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/dhs-unveils-first-department-wide-policy-on-body-worn-cameras","content":"DHS Unveils First Department-Wide Policy on Body-Worn Cameras\nNews\nMay 25\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe Department of Homeland Security (DHS) announced its first department-wide policy on body-worn cameras (BWCs). It applies to all the department’s 80,000 law enforcement officers across its nine operational law enforcement agencies. The policy update is required under President Biden’s May 2022 Executive Order on Advancing Effective, Accountable Policing and Criminal Justice Practices to Enhance Public Trust and Public Safety. That order, issued on the two-year anniversary of George Floyd’s murder, called for cameras to be activated in all appropriate circumstances. DHS agencies and offices have 180 days to draft, issue, or update their own BWC policies that meet or exceed DHS guidelines. “Requiring the use of body-worn cameras by our law enforcement officers and agents is another important step DHS is making to bring our law enforcement workforce to the forefront of innovation, and to further build public trust and confidence in the thousands of dedicated and professional law enforcement officers at DHS,” said Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro N. Mayorkas. GuidelinesThe policy states that DHS law enforcement officers are to wear and activate body-worn cameras “in response to emergency calls, pre-planned arrests, or during execution of a search or seizure warrant or order.”There are restrictions on the recordings including that BWCs are “not be used for the sole purpose of recording individuals engaged in First Amendment activity.”In addition, agencies are responsible for ensuring that programs comply and that law enforcement personnel are properly trained. The DHS Office of Strategy, Policy and Plans will be developing metrics to track each agency’s compliance. Law enforcement officers themselves are deemed responsible for “proper use of BWC equipment, including activation and deactivation, and storage and care of BWC data in their possession.”Phased-In ApproachNot all DHS law enforcement officers will get the BWCs immediately. Some officers will not get BWCs until funding becomes available, which DHS says it is working to obtain.  Some officers in other agencies including U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) and U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) have been using the cameras on a trial basis since 2021. The CBP program started in August 2021 at Border Patrol locations across the southwest and northern borders. The department-wide policy was developed through the DHS Law Enforcement Coordination Council and brings DHS into alignment with the Department of Justice (DOJ) policy on BWCs. The BWC policy is supported by federal law enforcement organizations including the Federal Law Enforcement Officers Association (FLEOA), as long as it bolsters trust between the public and law enforcement. FLEOA President Larry Cosme told GovExec, “As DHS components issue and update their policies, we will be looking to ensure offices maintain officer privacy and properly regulate the public disclosure of footage.”\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nNew OPM Guide Aims to Help Employees Navigate Retirement Process\nNext\nNext\n35th Annual Candlelight Vigil | National Police Week 2023","content_cn":"国土安全部公布首项全部门佩戴式摄像机政策\n新闻\n5月25日\n作者：FEDagent\n国土安全部（DHS）宣布了其首项全部门佩戴式摄像机（BWC）政策。该政策适用于该部门九个业务执法机构的8万名执法人员。此次政策更新是根据拜登总统2022年5月发布的《关于推进有效、负责的警务和刑事司法实践以增强公众信任与公共安全的行政命令》制定的。该命令发布于乔治·弗洛伊德遇害两周年之际，要求在所有适当情况下启用摄像机。国土安全部各机构和办公室有180天时间起草、发布或更新各自的BWC政策，使其达到或超过国土安全部的指导方针。“要求我们的执法人员和特工使用佩戴式摄像机，是国土安全部为使我们的执法队伍站在创新前沿、进一步建立公众对国土安全部数千名敬业且专业的执法人员的信任和信心而采取的又一重要举措，”国土安全部长 Alejandro N. Mayorkas 说。\n\n指导方针\n政策规定，国土安全部执法人员应“在接到紧急呼叫、执行预先计划的逮捕行动，或执行搜查或扣押令状或命令期间”佩戴并启用佩戴式摄像机。录像受到一些限制，包括BWC“不得仅为记录参与第一修正案活动的个人而使用”。此外，各机构负责确保相关项目合规，并确保执法人员接受适当培训。国土安全部战略、政策与计划办公室将制定指标，以跟踪各机构的合规情况。执法人员本人被认定负责“正确使用BWC设备，包括启用和停用，以及对其掌握的BWC数据进行存储和保管”。\n\n分阶段实施\n并非所有国土安全部执法人员都会立即获得BWC。一些人员要等到资金到位后才能获得BWC，国土安全部表示正在努力争取资金。其他机构的一些人员，包括美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）和美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）的人员，自2021年以来一直在试用这些摄像机。CBP项目于2021年8月在西南部和北部边境各地的边境巡逻站点启动。该全部门政策由国土安全部执法协调委员会制定，使国土安全部与司法部（DOJ）的BWC政策保持一致。包括联邦执法人员协会（FLEOA）在内的联邦执法组织支持这项BWC政策，前提是它能够加强公众与执法部门之间的信任。FLEOA主席 Larry Cosme 对 GovExec 表示：“随着国土安全部各组成部门发布和更新政策，我们将关注各办公室是否维护警员隐私，并妥善规范录像的公开披露。”\n\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n新的 OPM 指南旨在帮助员工办理退休流程\n下一篇\n下一篇\n第35届年度烛光守夜活动｜2023年全国警察周","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2023-05-25T15:28:43-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2988","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长帕特尔被免去ATF职务，陆军部长接任","title_en":"FBI Director Patel Out at ATF as Army Secretary Takes Charge — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国司法部人事变动引发关注：联邦调查局（FBI）局长Kash Patel被免去烟酒枪炮及爆炸物管理局（ATF）代理负责人职务，据《华盛顿邮报》报道其早在2月即被免职，但直至近日才公开，连ATF高层都不知情。Patel将继续担任参议院确认的FBI局长，陆军部长Dan Driscoll以代理身份接掌ATF，成为首位监管ATF的五角大楼官员。白宫称此为等待参议院确认期间的常规短期安排，未说明更换原因。ATF未来仍存疑，副司法部长曾提议将其与DEA合并。","summary_en":"Personnel moves at the Department of Justice are drawing attention: FBI Director Kash Patel was removed as interim leader of the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives, a move the Washington Post reports occurred in February but only became public now, with even senior ATF officials unaware. Patel remains Senate-confirmed FBI Director, while Army Secretary Dan Driscoll takes over ATF on an acting basis, the first Pentagon official to oversee the agency. The White House called it a standard short-term designation pending Senate confirmations and did not explain the replacement. ATF's future remains uncertain, with a proposal to merge it with the DEA.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:15:45.776654+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-director-patel-out-at-atf-as-army-secretary-takes-charge","content":"FBI Director Patel Out at ATF as Army Secretary Takes Charge\nNews\nApr 10\nWritten By FEDagent\nPersonnel moves at the Department of Justice (DOJ) continue to raise eyebrows among the federal law enforcement community. Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) Director Kash Patel was removed as interim leader of the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives (ATF). In fact, the Washington Post reports that Patel was removed in February, shortly after his appointment at ATF was announced. However, it’s just becoming public now and the paper says that even senior ATF officials were unaware of the move.Director Patel, who will remain in his Senate-confirmed position as FBI Director, is replaced at ATF on an acting basis by Secretary of the Army Dan Driscoll. Secretary Driscoll will now do double duty as both Army Secretary and interim leader of ATF. “Director Kash Patel was briefly designated ATF Director while awaiting Senate confirmations — a standard, short-term move,” said White House spokesman Harrison Fields. “Dozens of similar re-designations have occurred across the federal government. Director Patel is now excelling in his role at the FBI and delivering outstanding results.”The White House did not say why Secretary Driscoll was selected as his replacement. It will be the first time that a Pentagon official oversees the ATF. ATF’s FutureThe personnel moves come as the agency’s future remains in doubt. The 5,000 strong agency is responsible for regulating the sales and licensing of firearms and helps local law enforcement solve gun crimes. It also investigates illegal sales of explosives, alcoholic beverages, and tobacco products.But President Trump has not said whether he’ll nominate a permanent ATF director, and Deputy Attorney General Todd Blanche has proposed merging ATF with the Drug Enforcement Administration (DEA) amid a wider push to cut the size of government. Multiple Jobs Questioned The appointment of Secretary Driscoll to lead ATF continues a pattern in the Trump Administration of using officials for multiple jobs. The president also previously tapped Department of Veterans Affairs (VA) Secretary Doug Collins as interim leader of the Office of Special Counsel (OSC). Critics say it could lead to confusion about responsibilities and could distract appointees from their significant duties. And Secretary Driscoll faces a long to-do list as Secretary of the Army as he takes on the ATF role. The secretary is currently reviewing overseas troop numbers. The Army is also working to cut eight percent of its budget and reinvest in the Pentagon’s new priorities.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nJob Cuts Coming to DHS as Employees Offered Resignation Options\nNext\nNext\nSending Aircraft Parts to Russia Lands Two Men to Federal Prison","content_cn":"FBI 局长 Patel 不再担任 ATF 负责人，陆军部长接管\n新闻\n4月10日\n作者：FEDagent\n司法部（DOJ）的人事变动持续引起联邦执法界的关注。联邦调查局（FBI）局长 Kash Patel 被免去酒精、烟草、火器和爆炸物局（ATF）临时负责人的职务。事实上，《华盛顿邮报》报道称，Patel 在其 ATF 任命宣布后不久的 2 月即被免职。然而，此事直到现在才公开；该报称，甚至 ATF 的高级官员也不知道这一变动。\n\nPatel 局长将继续担任经参议院确认的 FBI 局长职务；他在 ATF 的职务由陆军部长 Dan Driscoll 以代理身份接替。Driscoll 部长现在将同时担任陆军部长和 ATF 临时负责人。\n\n白宫发言人 Harrison Fields 表示：“Kash Patel 局长在等待参议院确认期间被短暂指定为 ATF 局长——这是常规的短期安排。联邦政府各部门已发生数十起类似的重新指定。Patel 局长如今在 FBI 的岗位上表现出色，并取得了卓越成果。”\n\n白宫没有说明为何选择 Driscoll 部长作为其继任者。这将是首次由五角大楼官员监管 ATF。\n\nATF 的未来\n\n在人们对该机构未来仍存疑之际，人事变动随之而来。\n\n该机构拥有 5,000 名员工，负责监管枪支销售和许可，并协助地方执法部门侦破枪支犯罪。它还调查爆炸物、酒类和烟草产品的非法销售。\n\n但特朗普总统尚未表示是否会提名一位常任 ATF 局长；司法部副部长 Todd Blanche 则提议将 ATF 与缉毒局（DEA）合并，这是更广泛削减政府规模行动的一部分。\n\n多项职务受到质疑\n\n任命 Driscoll 部长领导 ATF 延续了特朗普政府让官员兼任多项职务的做法。\n\n总统此前还任命退伍军人事务部（VA）部长 Doug Collins 担任特别检察官办公室（OSC）的临时负责人。\n\n批评者表示，这可能导致职责混乱，并可能使被任命者分心，无法专注于其重要职责。\n\n随着 Driscoll 部长接任 ATF 职务，他作为陆军部长也面临一长串待办事项。该部长目前正在审查海外驻军人数。陆军还在努力削减其预算的 8%，并将资金再投资于五角大楼的新优先事项。\n\nFEDagent\n上一条\n上一条\n国土安全部将裁员，员工获提供辞职选项\n下一条\n下一条\n向俄罗斯运送飞机零部件导致两名男子被判入联邦监狱","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-04-10T12:08:11-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3277","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"报告：FBI在1月6日事件前遗漏步骤，26名线人出现在人群中","title_en":"FBI Missed Steps in Runup to January 6 Events, 26 Informants Were in Crowd: Reports — FEDagent","summary_cn":"司法部监察长报告指出，FBI在2021年1月6日国会山事件前未对55个外勤办公室进行排查，副局长称这是遗漏的“基本步骤”。报告称FBI没有卧底探员在人群中，但有26名线人在华盛顿特区，其中部分进入国会大厦或限制区域。报告还指出FBI向国会所作陈述并非故意不准确，而是沟通混乱所致。","summary_en":"A DOJ Inspector General report found the FBI failed to canvass its 55 field offices before the January 6, 2021 Capitol attack, which the deputy director called a missed basic step. The report said no undercover agents were in the crowd, but 26 informants were in Washington, D.C., some entering the Capitol or restricted areas. It also found the FBI's statements to Congress were not intentionally inaccurate but resulted from confusion and poor coordination.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:40:32.785261+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-missed-steps-in-runup-to-january-6-events-26-informants-were-in-crowd-reports","content":"FBI Missed Steps in Runup to January 6 Events, 26 Informants Were in Crowd: Reports\nNews\nDec 19\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) missed a “basic step” in the runup to the January 6, 2021, attack on the U.S. Capitol but had no undercover agents in the crowd nor did it instruct any of its informants to participate in the riot or break the law.  That’s according to a new report from Department of Justice (DOJ) Inspector General Michael Horowitz.The report found that the FBI only played a supporting role in the runup to the January 6, 2021, certification of the 2020 presidential election, and “recognized the potential for violence and took significant and appropriate steps to prepare for this supporting role.”What Was MissedA black mark for the FBI was that it failed to canvass its 55 field offices ahead of the January 6 events. The report suggested that if the FBI spoke to confidential human sources (CHSs) it may have helped the agency with preparations for the day. “FBI Deputy Director Paul Abbate described the lack of a canvass prior to January 6 as a ‘basic step that was missed,’ and told the OIG that he would have expected a formal canvassing of sources to have occurred,” noted the report. To top it off, the FBI told Congress that it had indeed canvassed field offices ahead of January 6. The IG report blamed confusion for that mistake. “We found that the FBI’s statements to Congress were not intentionally inaccurate, and that confusion and lack of coordinated communications contributed to the inaccurate reporting,” stated the report.The report also noted the FBI failed to conduct a comprehensive threat assessment. Undercover Sources in the CrowdThe IG report noted there were no undercover FBI employes in the crowd. However, there were 26 FBI CHSs or informants in Washington, DC, on that day. Three of those were tasked with the FBI on reporting on domestic terrorism case subjects who were thought to be in the crowd on January 6. Out of those three, one entered the U.S. Capitol while the other two entered a restricted area. The 23 additional FBI informants were attending the events on their own initiative and were not asked by the FBI to attend the events. Out of those, three entered the Capitol during the riot and an additional 11 entered a restricted area. “Many of these 26 CHSs had provided information relevant to the January 6 Electoral Certification before the event and that a few CHSs also provided information about the riot as it occurred,” noted the report. The relevant information included tips on actions of the Oath Keepers and the Proud Boys, two of the far right-wing groups that were present on that day. The IG made one recommendation to the FBI to assess the policies and procedures it uses to prepare for events that it determines present potential domestic security issues. The FBI concurred with the recommendation.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nPresident Biden Set to Sign Legislation to Improve Security at Federal Buildings\nNext\nNext\nFourth Suspect Sentenced in Ohio Drug Case with Tie’s to Sinaloa Cartel","content_cn":"FBI在1月6日事件前夕漏掉步骤，报告称人群中有26名线人\n新闻\n12月19日\n作者：FEDagent\n\n美国联邦调查局（FBI）在2021年1月6日袭击美国国会大厦前夕漏掉了一个“基本步骤”，但人群中没有FBI卧底特工，FBI也没有指示其任何线人参与骚乱或违法。这是司法部（DOJ）监察长迈克尔·霍罗威茨的一份新报告所述内容。\n\n报告发现，在2021年1月6日认证2020年总统选举结果前夕，FBI只发挥了支援作用，并且“认识到发生暴力的可能性，并采取了重大且适当的措施，为这一支援角色做好准备”。\n\n遗漏了什么\n\nFBI的一大污点是，在1月6日事件前未对其55个外地办事处进行摸排。报告称，如果FBI与机密人类情报来源（CHS）交谈，可能会帮助该机构为当天做好准备。报告指出：“FBI副局长保罗·阿巴特将1月6日前未进行摸排描述为‘漏掉的基本步骤’，并告诉监察长办公室，他原本预计应对情报来源进行正式摸排。”\n\n更糟糕的是，FBI告诉国会，它确实在1月6日前对外地办事处进行了摸排。监察长报告将这一错误归咎于混乱。报告称：“我们发现，FBI向国会作出的陈述并非有意不准确，混乱和缺乏协调一致的沟通导致了不准确的报告。”\n\n报告还指出，FBI未进行全面的威胁评估。\n\n人群中的卧底线人\n\n监察长报告指出，人群中没有FBI卧底雇员。然而，当天华盛顿特区有26名FBI机密人类情报来源或线人。其中3人受FBI指派，负责报告被认为会在1月6日人群中的国内恐怖主义案件涉案人员情况。在这3人中，1人进入了美国国会大厦，另外2人进入了限制区域。\n\n其余23名FBI线人是自行决定参加活动的，FBI没有要求他们参加活动。在这些人中，3人在骚乱期间进入了国会大厦，另有11人进入了限制区域。\n\n报告指出：“这26名CHS中有许多人在活动前提供了与1月6日选举认证有关的信息，另有少数CHS也提供了骚乱发生期间的相关信息。”相关信息包括关于“守誓者”和“骄傲男孩”行动的线索，这两个团体是当天到场的两个极右翼组织。\n\n监察长向FBI提出了一项建议，要求其评估用于准备那些被认定可能涉及国内安全问题的事件的政策和程序。FBI同意了该建议。\n\nFEDagent\n\n上一篇\n上一篇\n拜登总统将签署改善联邦建筑安全的立法\n\n下一篇\n下一篇\n俄亥俄州毒品案件中的第四名嫌疑人被判刑，该案与锡那罗亚贩毒集团有关","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2024-12-19T14:52:28-05:00"}},{"id":"news-2493","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI任命第二位副局长，更多高级特工被解雇","title_en":"FBI Names Second Deputy Director as More Top Agents Are Let Go — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）罕见地增设第二位副局长，由密苏里州总检察长安德鲁·贝利与现任副局长丹·邦吉诺共同担任，两人职责分工尚不明确。此举正值邦吉诺因爱泼斯坦文件发布问题与司法部长邦迪产生分歧之际。同时，FBI多名高级特工被解雇，包括曾代理局长的布赖恩·德里斯科尔和华盛顿外勤办公室主管史蒂夫·詹森，FBI特工协会和参议员德宾对此表示担忧。","summary_en":"The FBI is bringing on a second deputy director, with Missouri Attorney General Andrew Bailey serving alongside current Deputy Director Dan Bongino, though how they will split duties remains unclear. The move comes amid a rift between Bongino and Attorney General Bondi over the release of Jeffrey Epstein files. Meanwhile, senior FBI agents including Brian Driscoll and Steve Jensen have been fired, prompting concern from the FBI Agents Association and Senator Dick Durbin, who asked the DOJ inspector general to investigate the purge.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:56:21.008107+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-names-second-deputy-director-as-more-top-agents-are-let-go","content":"FBI Names Second Deputy Director as More Top Agents Are Let Go\nNews\nAug 21\nWritten By FEDagent\nIn an unusual move, the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is bringing on a second deputy director to serve alongside current Deputy Director Dan Bongino. U.S. Attorney General Pam Bondi and FBI Director Kash Patel announced that Missouri Attorney General Andrew Bailey will serve as co-deputy director of the FBI. The deputy director historically manages the bureau’s day-to-day operations. It is not immediately clear how Bongino and Bailey will split the duties. “(Andrew Bailey’s) leadership and commitment to country will be a tremendous asset as we work together to advance President Trump’s mission,” said Attorney General Bondi. \"My life has been defined by a call to service, and I am once again answering that call, this time at the national level,\" wrote Bailey. Bailey’s hiring comes after a rift developed between Attorney General Bondi and Deputy Director Bongino over the release of the Jeffrey Epstein files, with Bongino protesting the AG’s decision not to release additional files. Deputy Director Bongino, formerly a Fox News pundit and right-wing podcaster, has also taken to the airwaves to complain about the position. “People ask me all the time, ‘Do you like it?’ I say, ‘No, I don’t,” stated Deputy Director Bongino. For his part, Bailey is no stranger to the Trump team. He interviewed for the Attorney General job during the Trump transition. As Missouri Attorney General he worked to advance cases aligned with President Trump’s interest such as filing a long-shot petition with the U.S. Supreme Court seeking to lift the gag order against the president and delay his New York sentencing. FBI FiringsThe turmoil at the top of the agency comes as senior FBI agents are fired. Among those let go is Brian Driscoll, who briefly served as acting director after President Trump took over. Driscoll made news when he resisted a Department of Justice directive to turn over a list of agents who had worked on cases tied to the January 6, 2021, riots. Also let go was Steve Jensen, assistant director in charge of the Washington field office, who also played a key role in January 6 investigations. In a statement, the FBI Agents Association (FBIAA) expressed dismay over the dozens of firings of top FBI agents since President Trump took power. “If these Agents are fired without due process, it makes the American people less safe. Agents need to be focused on their work and not on potentially being illegally fired based on their assignments,” said FBIAA in a statement. Meanwhile, Senate Judiciary Committee Ranking Member Dick Durbin (D-IL) asked the DOJ Acting Inspector General to investigate the purge of senior FBI executives, special agents in charge, and other supervisory agents, and the disparate impact on personnel who are women or persons of color. “These shortsighted and politically motivated personnel decisions have significantly destabilized the Bureau, harmed our public safety apparatus, and made Americans less safe,” wrote Senator Durbin.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nBill to Simplify Federal Criminal Code and Force Agencies to Count Crimes Advances\nNext\nNext\nDOJ Seizes Nearly $3 Million in Cryptocurrency after Ransomware Attacks","content_cn":"FBI任命第二名副局长，更多高层特工被解雇\n新闻\n8月21日\n作者：FEDagent\n联邦调查局（FBI）采取了一项不寻常的举措，任命第二名副局长，与现任副局长丹·邦吉诺共同任职。美国司法部长帕姆·邦迪和FBI局长卡什·帕特尔宣布，密苏里州总检察长安德鲁·贝利将担任FBI联合副局长。副局长历来负责管理该机构的日常运营。目前尚不清楚邦吉诺和贝利将如何分工。\n司法部长邦迪说：“（安德鲁·贝利的）领导力和对国家的承诺，将在我们共同推进特朗普总统使命的过程中成为巨大资产。”\n贝利写道：“我的一生都由服务召唤所定义，而我再次响应这一召唤，这一次是在国家层面。”\n贝利的任命发生在司法部长邦迪与副局长邦吉诺就公布杰弗里·爱泼斯坦文件产生裂痕之后，邦吉诺抗议司法部长决定不再公布更多文件。曾是福克斯新闻评论员和右翼播客主持人的副局长邦吉诺也开始通过媒体抱怨这份工作。\n副局长邦吉诺说：“人们总是问我，‘你喜欢这份工作吗？’我说，‘不，我不喜欢。’”\n至于贝利，他并不陌生于特朗普团队。他曾在特朗普过渡期间接受司法部长职位的面试。作为密苏里州总检察长，他推动了符合特朗普总统利益的案件，例如向美国最高法院提交一份胜算渺茫的请愿书，要求解除针对总统的禁言令，并推迟其在纽约的判刑。\nFBI解雇事件\n该机构高层的动荡发生之际，多名FBI高级特工遭到解雇。其中包括布莱恩·德里斯科尔，他曾在特朗普总统接管后短暂担任代理局长。德里斯科尔因抵制司法部要求提供参与调查与2021年1月6日骚乱有关案件的特工名单的指令而受到关注。\n史蒂夫·詹森也被解雇；他曾担任华盛顿外勤办公室负责人助理局长，并在1月6日调查中发挥了关键作用。\nFBI特工协会（FBIAA）在一份声明中对特朗普总统执政以来数十名FBI高级特工被解雇表示震惊。FBIAA在声明中说：“如果这些特工未经正当程序就被解雇，美国人民的安全就会受到更大威胁。特工需要专注于工作，而不是担心可能因所负责的任务而被非法解雇。”\n与此同时，参议院司法委员会排名成员迪克·德宾（D-IL）要求司法部代理监察长调查对FBI高级主管、负责特工和其他主管特工的清洗，以及对女性或有色人种人员造成的不成比例影响。\n迪克·德宾参议员写道：“这些目光短浅且出于政治动机的人事决定，严重破坏了该局的稳定，损害了我们的公共安全体系，并使美国人更加不安全。”\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n《简化联邦刑法并强制各机构统计犯罪数量的法案》获推进\n下一篇\n下一篇\n勒索软件攻击后，司法部查扣近300万美元加密货币","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-08-21T11:58:10-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1307","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI恢复购买商业数据，无证监控争议再起","title_en":"FBI Resumes Buying Commercial Data Renewing Debate Over Warrantless Surveillance — FEDagent","summary_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院情报委员会作证时表示，FBI已恢复购买美国公民的商业可用数据用于调查，称其符合宪法及《电子通信隐私法》。FBI声明称帕特尔未提及位置数据。此举与2023年前局长雷的表态形成转变。参议员怀登批评这是绕过第四修正案，主席科顿则为其辩护。两党议员提出《政府监控改革法》更新版，拟禁止无证购买美国人数据。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel testified before the Senate Intelligence Committee that the FBI has resumed purchasing commercially available data on Americans for investigations, saying it is consistent with the Constitution and the Electronic Communications Privacy Act. The FBI said Patel made no reference to location data. The shift contrasts with 2023 statements by former Director Wray. Senator Wyden criticized the practice as an end run around the Fourth Amendment, while Chairman Cotton defended it. Bipartisan lawmakers introduced an updated Government Surveillance Reform Act to ban warrantless data purchases.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:37:08.429753+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-resumes-buying-commercial-data-renewing-debate-over-warrantless-surveillance","content":"FBI Resumes Buying Commercial Data Renewing Debate Over Warrantless Surveillance\nNews\nMar 26\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) has resumed purchasing commercially available data on American citizens for use in investigations, according to testimony from FBI Director Kash Patel before the Senate Select Committee on Intelligence.In a response to a question from Senator Ron Wyden (D-OR) on whether the FBI resumed the practice of purchasing data without a warrant, Director Patel stated, “We do purchase commercially available information that is consistent with the Constitution and the laws under the Electronic Communications Privacy Act — and it has led to some valuable intelligence for us.” However, the FBI noted in a statement that neither Director Patel nor the FBI made any reference to location data in the answer. Nevertheless, it marks a shift from 2023 when then-FBI Director Christopher Wray told Senator Wyden that the FBI wasn't buying location data any longer, but that it had previously.Senator Wyden criticized the practice saying, “Doing that without a warrant is an outrageous end run around the Fourth Amendment, it’s particularly dangerous given the use of artificial intelligence to comb through massive amounts of private information.”However, Committee Chairman Tom Cotton (R-AR) defended buying the data.  “I would observe about commercially available data that the key words are commercially available,” said Senator Cotton. “If any other person can buy it and the FBI can buy it and it helps them locate a depraved child molester or savage cartel leader, I certainly hope the FBI is doing anything they can to keep Americans safe.” Government Surveillance Reform ActThis comes as Senator Wyden and other lawmakers introduced an updated version of the Government Surveillance Reform Act in both houses of Congress. The bipartisan legislation would close the data broker loophole by banning the federal government from buying Americans’ data without a warrant.It would also require the federal government to get a warrant to access Americans’ private communications gathered under Section 702 of the Foreign Intelligence Surveillance Act (FISA), with some emergency exceptions. President Trump meanwhile called for an 18-month extension of Section 702, currently set to sunset on April 20, 2026. “With the ongoing successful Military activities against the Terrorist Iranian Regime, it is more important than ever that we remain vigilant, PROTECT our Homeland, Troops, and Diplomats stationed abroad, and maintain our ability to quickly stop bad actors seeking to cause harm to our People and our Country,” the president wrote on Truth Social.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nICE in Support Role at Airports as Security Lines Persist\nNext\nNext\nDEA Announces Major Arizona Drug Seizure, Results of Phase II of Operation Fentanyl Free America","content_cn":"联邦调查局恢复购买商业数据，无证监控争议再起\n新闻\n3月26日\n作者：Shaw Bransford & Roth律师事务所\n据联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔在参议院特别情报委员会作证时透露，FBI已恢复购买市场上可获得的美国公民数据，用于调查。\n\n在回答参议员罗恩·怀登（俄勒冈州民主党）关于FBI是否恢复无搜查令购买数据这一做法的问题时，帕特尔局长表示：“我们确实购买符合宪法以及《电子通信隐私法》规定的商业可得信息——这些信息为我们带来了一些有价值的情报。”然而，FBI在一份声明中指出，帕特尔局长和FBI在回答中都没有提到位置数据。\n\n尽管如此，这标志着与2023年的情况相比发生了变化。当时，时任FBI局长克里斯托弗·雷告诉参议员怀登，FBI已不再购买位置数据，但过去曾这样做。\n\n怀登参议员批评了这一做法，他说：“在没有搜查令的情况下这样做，是对第四修正案的公然规避；鉴于利用人工智能梳理海量私人信息，这尤其危险。”\n\n然而，委员会主席汤姆·科顿（阿肯色州共和党）为购买这些数据辩护。“关于商业可得数据，我要指出，关键词是‘商业可得’，”科顿参议员说。“如果其他任何人可以买到，FBI也可以买到，而且这能帮助他们找到堕落的儿童猥亵者或凶残的贩毒集团头目，我当然希望FBI采取一切可能的行动来保护美国人的安全。”\n\n《政府监控改革法》\n\n就在此时，怀登参议员和其他议员在国会两院提出了《政府监控改革法》的更新版本。这项两党法案将通过禁止联邦政府在没有搜查令的情况下购买美国人的数据，堵住数据经纪商漏洞。\n\n该法案还将要求联邦政府取得搜查令，才能访问根据《外国情报监视法》（FISA）第702条收集的美国人私人通信，但存在一些紧急例外。\n\n与此同时，特朗普总统呼吁将第702条延长18个月。该条款目前定于2026年4月20日到期。“鉴于针对恐怖主义的伊朗政权正在进行的军事行动取得持续成功，我们比以往任何时候都更有必要保持警惕，保护我们的国土、部队以及驻外外交官，并保持我们迅速制止企图伤害我国人民和国家的恶意行为者的能力，”总统在Truth Social上写道。\n\nShaw Bransford & Roth律师事务所\n上一篇\n上一篇\n机场安保队伍持续，移民与海关执法局担任支援角色\n下一篇\n下一篇\n缉毒局宣布亚利桑那州大规模缉毒行动，并公布“无芬太尼美国行动”第二阶段结果","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-03-26T12:32:49-04:00"}},{"id":"news-136","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI在新网络战略中聚焦招聘与合作伙伴关系","title_en":"FBI Targets Hiring, Partnerships in New Cyber Strategy — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）发布了首个机构范围的未分类网络战略，呼吁“争夺并留住全国最优秀的网络人才”。该战略基于四大支柱：调查、瓦解网络对手并使其付出代价；支持受害者；通过伙伴关系扩大影响；增强FBI自身网络能力。战略还计划统一56个外勤办公室以应对日益增长的网络威胁，并优先招聘特工、情报分析师、计算机科学家等关键岗位人员。","summary_en":"The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) released its first agency-wide unclassified cyber strategy, calling for the bureau to \"compete for and retain the best cyber talent in the nation.\" The strategy rests on four pillars: investigating, disrupting and imposing costs on cyber adversaries; supporting victims; increasing impact through partnerships; and enhancing the FBI's own cyber capabilities. It also aims to unify the bureau's 56 field offices to counter growing cyber threats, with priority hiring for special agents, intelligence analysts, computer scientists and other key roles.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:31:55.549340+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-targets-hiring-partnerships-in-new-cyber-strategy","content":"FBI Targets Hiring, Partnerships in New Cyber Strategy\nNews\nSep 17\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) released its first agency-wide unclassified cyber strategy and it calls for the FBI to “compete for and retain the best cyber talent in the nation.”The strategy is based on four pillars: investigating, disrupting and imposing costs on cyber adversaries; supporting victims; increasing “impact” through partnerships; and enhancing the FBI’s own cyber capabilities. It also intends to unify the bureau’s 56 field offices to counter growing cyber threats. “Our strategy is really focused on moving beyond the ad-hoc way that we do [disruptions] right now … to do it in a more steady state,” said FBI Cyber Division Assistant Director Brett Leatherman at the Billington Cybersecurity Summit. Hiring GoalsThe FBI says it will prioritize the hiring, development, and retention of employees in key roles. These include special agents, intelligence analysts, computer scientists, data scientists, malware analysts, cryptocurrency specialists, technical operators, and field cyber leaders.The strategy says the FBI will draw from the private sector, academia, government, and military to “draw from the broadest possible talent base.”There are plans to offer training, mentorship, and professional development opportunities for both leaders and technical experts, with the FBI’s Cyber Education and Training Unit spearheading that work through classroom instruction and hands-on training. The strategy also calls for the FBI workforce to implement new tools and techniques to stay ahead of cyber adversaries. That includes using artificial intelligence (AI) in specific cases where it can improve speed, scale, accuracy, and operational decision making, under FBI authorities.Cooperation with Private SectorAnother pillar of the strategy is working with the private sector. That includes improving intelligence sharing on threats and cyberattacks. Assistant Director Brett Leatherman says that in the past, the private sector has been hesitant to alert the FBI to potential cybersecurity concerns. He says the FBI is “trying to be very vocal” about its obligation to protect information provided by cyber incident victims. The FBI will also share more timely and actionable cyber threat intelligence with private industry.Investigative PivotsAnd on the investigation front, the strategy calls for teams focusing on specific threats including Russia and China, to develop their own customized plans. Tailored strategies will also be developed for teams on specific types of operations, including offensive hacking and investigating operational technology breaches.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nFederal Judge: Plan to Cut FEMA Workforce in Half Was Unlawful\nNext\nNext\nAir Traffic Controllers Still Waiting on Much of Pay Raise While FAA Defends Withholding","content_cn":"联邦调查局在新网络战略中瞄准招聘与合作\n新闻\n9月17日\n撰稿：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n联邦调查局（FBI）发布了首份全机构范围的非机密网络战略，提出联邦调查局要“争取并留住全国最优秀的网络人才”。该战略基于四大支柱：调查、扰乱网络对手并施加代价；支持受害者；通过合作伙伴关系提高“影响力”；以及增强联邦调查局自身的网络能力。该战略还旨在统一该局56个外勤办公室的行动，以应对日益严重的网络威胁。“我们的战略真正关注的是，摆脱我们目前以临时方式开展[扰乱行动]的做法……转而以更加稳定的常态开展行动，”联邦调查局网络部门助理局长布雷特·利瑟曼在比灵顿网络安全峰会上说。\n招聘目标\n联邦调查局表示，将优先招聘、培养和留任关键岗位员工。这些岗位包括特别探员、情报分析师、计算机科学家、数据科学家、恶意软件分析师、加密货币专家、技术操作员和外勤网络负责人。该战略称，联邦调查局将从私营部门、学术界、政府和军方吸纳人才，以“从尽可能广泛的人才基础中选拔”。计划为领导人员和技术专家提供培训、导师指导及职业发展机会，联邦调查局网络教育与培训部门将通过课堂教学和实践培训牵头开展相关工作。该战略还要求联邦调查局工作人员实施新工具和新技术，以保持领先于网络对手。这包括在联邦调查局授权范围内，在能够提升速度、规模、准确性和运营决策能力的特定情况下使用人工智能（AI）。\n与私营部门合作\n该战略的另一大支柱是与私营部门合作，包括改善有关威胁和网络攻击的信息共享。助理局长布雷特·利瑟曼表示，过去私营部门一直不愿向联邦调查局报告潜在的网络安全问题。他说，联邦调查局“正努力明确表达”其保护网络事件受害者所提供信息的义务。联邦调查局还将向私营企业更及时地分享可采取行动的网络威胁情报。\n调查方向调整\n在调查方面，该战略要求专注于俄罗斯和中国等特定威胁的团队制定各自定制的计划。针对特定类型的行动，包括进攻性黑客攻击和调查运营技术遭入侵，也将为相关团队制定量身定制的战略。\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一篇\n上一篇\n联邦法官：将联邦紧急事务管理局人员削减一半的计划违法\n下一篇\n下一篇\n联邦航空局为扣留加薪辩护之际，空中交通管制员仍在等待大部分加薪","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-09-17T10:32:11-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2459","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI将降低招聘标准，取消大学学历要求并缩短培训时间","title_en":"FBI to Lower Recruiting Standards, Cut College Degree Requirement and Training Time — FEDagent","summary_cn":"据报道，美国联邦调查局（FBI）计划降低招聘标准，以应对9月约5000名员工因特朗普政府离职补偿和提前退休方案而离开的局面。在局长卡什·帕特尔和副局长丹·邦吉诺推动下，FBI将取消新员工大学学历要求，培训期从18周缩短至8周，并可从移民和海关执法局、烟酒枪炮及爆炸物管理局等机构招募人员。前特工警告此举可能削弱FBI处理金融欺诈、公共腐败和国家安全等复杂案件的能力。","summary_en":"The FBI is reportedly planning to lower recruitment standards as it prepares for the departure of some 5,000 employees in September due to Trump administration severance and early retirement packages. Under a plan pushed by Director Kash Patel and Deputy Director Dan Bongino, the FBI will eliminate the college degree requirement for recruits and cut training from 18 weeks to eight weeks, drawing from agencies such as ICE and ATF. Former agents warn the move could weaken the FBI's ability to handle complex cases involving financial fraud, public corruption, and national security.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:50:46.280627+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-to-lower-recruiting-standards-cut-college-degree-requirement-and-training-time","content":"FBI to Lower Recruiting Standards, Cut College Degree Requirement and Training Time\nNews\nAug 28\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is reportedly planning to lower its recruitment standards as the agency prepares for the departure of some 5,000 employees in September due to the Trump Administration's severance and early retirement packages. The New York Times reports that under a plan pushed by FBI Director Kash Patel and Deputy Director Dan Bongino, the FBI will eliminate the requirement that new recruits hold a college degree. The FBI training period will also reportedly be cut from 18 weeks to eight weeks. The move will allow the FBI to draw from other federal law enforcement agencies, such as Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms & Explosives (ATF), including criminal investors who are classified as 1811s. Current and former agents tell the Times that the plan appears to shift the FBI’s focus to street crime and being more of a police force, instead of taking on complicated cases involving financial fraud, public corruption, and national security. “When you lower the standards, your mission effectiveness goes down with that, because not only does the capability of each individual agent decline, but your reputation, both domestically and globally, takes a hit,” said Chris O’Leary, a former FBI agent and senior counterterrorism official.Adding to the changes is the recent hiring of Andrew Bailey as co-deputy director, serving alongside Deputy Director Bongino. O’Leary noted that the confusion in top leadership and the cut in training standards may show that the FBI will “do the bidding of the administration, no matter what it is.”The news comes as law enforcement at both the federal and state and local levels, is lowering recruitment standards to get more recruits in the door. Amidst its own staffing push, ICE recently removed age limits and dropped requirements for recruits to take Spanish courses.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nFunding Shortfall Impacts Federal Public Defenders, Advocates Warn of Consequences\nNext\nNext\nFederal Prosecutors Threatened: Updates on Two Cases","content_cn":"FBI将降低招募标准，取消大学学位要求并缩短培训时间\n新闻\n8月28日\n作者：FEDagent\n据报道，随着特朗普政府的离职补偿和提前退休方案导致约5,000名员工将在9月离职，联邦调查局（FBI）正计划降低招募标准。《纽约时报》报道，根据由FBI局长卡什·帕特尔和副局长丹·邦吉诺推动的一项计划，FBI将取消新招募人员须持有大学学位的要求。据报道，FBI培训期也将从18周缩短至8周。\n\n此举将使FBI能够从其他联邦执法机构招募人员，例如移民与海关执法局（ICE）和烟酒枪炮及爆炸物管理局（ATF），其中包括被归类为1811的刑事调查员。\n\n现任和前任探员向《纽约时报》表示，该计划似乎将FBI的重心转向街头犯罪，使其更像一支警察力量，而不是处理涉及金融欺诈、公共腐败和国家安全的复杂案件。\n\n“当你降低标准时，任务效能也会随之下降，因为不仅每名探员的能力会下降，你在国内和全球的声誉也会受损，”前FBI探员兼高级反恐官员克里斯·奥利里说。\n\n近期安德鲁·贝利被聘为共同副局长、与副局长邦吉诺一同任职，也增加了这些变化。奥利里指出，高层领导的混乱以及培训标准的削减，可能表明FBI将“无论政府要求什么，都会照办”。\n\n这一消息传出之际，联邦、州和地方各级执法部门都在降低招募标准，以吸引更多新招募人员。ICE在自身扩招期间，最近取消了年龄限制，并取消了要求新招募人员修读西班牙语课程的规定。\n\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n资金短缺影响联邦公设辩护人，倡导者警告后果\n下一篇\n下一篇\n联邦检察官受到威胁：两起案件的最新进展","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-08-28T12:46:16-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2835","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI将1500名员工迁出华盛顿地区，总部搬迁仍悬而未决","title_en":"FBI to Move 1,500 Employees Out of DC Region as HQ Move Remains in Limbo — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）计划将1500名员工迁出华盛顿特区地区，并打算离开市中心的J·埃德加·胡佛大楼。目前约1.1万名FBI员工在华盛顿地区工作，约占其总员工数的三分之一。约1000名员工将前往全国各地，另有500人前往阿拉巴马州亨茨维尔的雷德斯通阿森纳设施，搬迁将在未来三至九个月内进行。FBI总部搬迁计划仍不明朗，原定马里兰州格林贝尔特新址因监察长报告批评选址过程而受阻。","summary_en":"The FBI is moving 1,500 employees out of the Washington, DC area and plans to leave its current headquarters at the J. Edgar Hoover building. About 11,000 FBI employees currently work in the DC area, roughly one-third of the total workforce. About 1,000 workers will head to various parts of the country, with an additional 500 going to the FBI's Redstone Arsenal facility in Huntsville, Alabama, over the next three to nine months. The FBI's headquarters relocation remains uncertain after an inspector general report faulted the Greenbelt, Maryland selection process.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:33:54.060473+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/fbi-to-move-1500-employees-out-of-dc-region-as-hq-move-remains-in-limbo","content":"FBI to Move 1,500 Employees Out of DC Region as HQ Move Remains in Limbo\nNews\nMay 22\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is moving 1,500 employees out of the Washington, DC area, and plans to leave its current headquarters at the J. Edgar Hoover FBI building in downtown DC.  About 11,000 FBI employees currently work in the DC area, roughly one-third of the total FBI workforce. “A third of the crime doesn’t happen here, so we’re taking 1,500 of those folks and moving them out,” said FBI Director Kash Patel. “Every state is getting a plus up.”About 1,000 FBI workers will be headed to various parts of the country, with the director indicating that every state will see a personnel boost. An additional 500 employees are headed to the FBI’s facility at the Redstone Arsenal in Huntsville, Alabama.  The personnel moves are slated to take place over the next three to nine months. Director Patel was recently in Huntsville, calling the facility one of the “crown jewels of the FBI,” noting that the agency built five new buildings, a cyber training facility, and a long-range facility. It’s also equipped with a Terrorist Explosive Device Analytical Center (TEDAC) and a Ballistic Research Facility (BRF). “Because we have had new buildings and new structures already there, we need our outdated facilities and personnel to move to Huntsville, where the training has been set up for them, and fill those seats,” said Director Patel.“The FBI’s operations on Redstone Arsenal are at the forefront of 21st-century innovation and training needed to combat the threats of the future, and I am confident Redstone will be instrumental in fulfilling the FBI’s core mission for decades to come,” said Senator Katie Britt (R-AL) who accompanied Director Patel on his visit. Headquarters FutureUp in the air are the FBI’s plans for relocating its headquarters. The one thing that is clear however, is that the Trump Administration wants out of the current Hoover building. \"This FBI is leaving the Hoover building because this building is unsafe for our workforce and we want… the American men and women to know, if you're going to come work at the premier law enforcement agency in the world, we're going to give you a building that's commensurate with that, and that's not this place,” said Director Patel. The FBI had planned to build a new headquarters in Greenbelt, Maryland. However, an inspector general report faulted the selection process, which passed over a rival site in Springfield, Virginia. President Trump then said he planned to stop the move to Greenbelt and urged construction of a new headquarters in DC.  But lawmakers in Maryland say Greenbelt is the way to go. “This site was selected based on a thorough, objective process examining cost, construction timeline, transportation access, community impact, and the FBI's mission requirements,” wrote members of Congress from Maryland. \"Team Maryland remains committed to providing the world's premier law enforcement agency with the world's premier law enforcement facility. If the ​Trump Administration truly shares that goal, it will work with us to proceed on this project.\"\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nLEOSA, Officer Benefits, Wellness Among the Law Enforcement Bills Advancing During National Police Week\nNext\nNext\nFBI: Palm Springs Bombing an Act of Terrorism, Agents Focus on Subject’s Anti-Life Views","content_cn":"FBI将在总部搬迁悬而未决之际将1,500名员工调离华盛顿特区地区\n新闻\n5月22日\n作者：FEDagent\n联邦调查局（FBI）正将1,500名员工调离华盛顿特区地区，并计划离开位于华盛顿特区市中心的现有J. Edgar Hoover FBI大楼总部。目前约有11,000名FBI员工在华盛顿特区地区工作，约占FBI员工总数的三分之一。FBI局长Kash Patel表示：“三分之一的犯罪并不发生在这里，因此我们会将其中1,500人调离。每个州都将获得人员增加。”约1,000名FBI工作人员将前往全国各地，局长表示每个州的人员都会增加。另有500名员工将前往位于阿拉巴马州亨茨维尔红石兵工厂的FBI设施。人员调动计划将在未来三至九个月内进行。\nPatel局长近日到访亨茨维尔，称该设施是“FBI的皇冠明珠”之一，并指出该机构已建造五栋新建筑、一座网络培训设施和一座远程设施。那里还配备恐怖主义爆炸装置分析中心（TEDAC）和弹道研究设施（BRF）。Patel局长表示：“由于那里已经有新的建筑和新设施，我们需要将过时设施中的人员调到亨茨维尔，那里已为他们配备培训，并填补这些岗位。”\n陪同Patel局长访问的阿拉巴马州共和党参议员Katie Britt表示：“FBI在红石兵工厂的行动处于应对未来威胁所需的21世纪创新和培训的前沿，我相信红石将在未来数十年中成为完成FBI核心任务的重要力量。”\n总部未来\nFBI总部迁址计划仍悬而未决。但有一点很明确：特朗普政府希望离开目前的Hoover大楼。Patel局长表示：“本届FBI将离开Hoover大楼，因为这栋建筑对我们的员工并不安全；我们希望……美国男女民众知道，如果你来到世界顶尖执法机构工作，我们将为你提供与之相称的建筑，而这里不是。”\nFBI原计划在马里兰州Greenbelt建设新总部。然而，一份监察长报告批评了选址程序；该程序没有选择位于弗吉尼亚州Springfield的竞争地点。随后，特朗普总统表示，他计划停止迁往Greenbelt，并敦促在华盛顿特区建设新总部。\n但马里兰州议员表示，Greenbelt才是正确选择。马里兰州国会议员写道：“该地点是基于一项全面、客观的程序选定的，该程序考察了成本、建设时间表、交通可达性、社区影响以及FBI的任务要求。马里兰团队仍致力于为世界顶尖执法机构提供世界顶尖执法设施。如果特朗普政府确实认同这一目标，它将与我们合作推进该项目。”\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n全国警察周期间推进的执法法案中包括LEOSA、警官福利与健康议题\n下一篇\nFBI：棕榈泉爆炸案为恐怖主义行为，探员聚焦嫌疑人的反生命观点","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2025-05-22T03:43:10-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1462","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"伊朗冲突引发网络安全担忧，DHS停摆与CISA动荡持续","title_en":"Iran Conflict Raises Cybersecurity Concerns as DHS Shutdown, CISA Turmoil Continue — FEDagent","summary_cn":"伊朗冲突使联邦网络防御受到更多关注，而美国国土安全部（DHS）因拨款中断处于停摆，网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）也面临领导层动荡。专家警告伊朗可能对美国企业和基础设施发动网站篡改、分布式拒绝服务等低级别攻击。CISA自特朗普上任以来流失约三分之一员工，代理局长Madhu Gottumukkala被调离，由Nick Andersen代理，首席信息官Robert Costello离职，常任局长提名人Sean Plankey尚未获参议院表决。","summary_en":"The conflict in Iran is drawing added attention to federal cyber defenses while the Department of Homeland Security is shut down due to a funding lapse and the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency faces leadership turmoil. Experts warn Iran could launch a barrage of low-level attacks such as website defacements and distributed denial-of-service attacks against U.S. companies and infrastructure. CISA has lost about one-third of its workforce since President Trump took office; acting director Madhu Gottumukkala was reassigned, replaced by Nick Andersen, while CIO Robert Costello is leaving and permanent director nominee Sean Plankey has yet to receive a Senate vote.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:12:20.559149+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/iran-conflict-raises-cybersecurity-concerns-as-dhs-shutdown-cisa-turmoil-continue","content":"Iran Conflict Raises Cybersecurity Concerns as DHS Shutdown, CISA Turmoil Continue\nNews\nMar 5\nWritten By FEDagent\nThe conflict in Iran is putting additional focus on federal cyber defenses at a time when the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) is shut down due to a funding lapse, and there is leadership turmoil within the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA). Iran has been known to respond to overseas threats with cyber attacks and experts warn that American companies and infrastructure could see a “barrage” of low-level attacks like website defacements and distributed denial-of-service attacks.“This is a bad time for Washington’s cyber agency to be operating with limited staff,” said Annie Fixler, director of the Center on Cyber and Technology Innovation at the Foundation for Defense of Democracies, a national security think tank. “Iran might also see some limited success against targets that do not have proper cyber hygiene — exposed edge devices with default passwords, for example.”That position was echoed by other cyber experts. “Threat hunters should be working overtime right now. By combining disruptive attacks with psychological operations, Iran will seek to erode public trust in government institutions and project domestic strength during periods of heightened conflict,” said former CISA official Brian Harrell.Turmoil at CISACISA lost about one-third of its workforce since President Trump took office. The agency is also dealing with leadership turmoil. Madhu Gottumukkala was recently removed as acting director to become director of strategic implementation at DHS. He was replaced by Nick Andersen on an acting basis. Andersen was serving as CISA’s executive director for cybersecurity.     Gottumukkala– who worked with DHS Secretary Kristi Noem as Chief Information Officer for the state of South Dakota— had a rocky tenure. He faced increased scrutiny after reports that he failed a polygraph test and uploaded sensitive documents to a public version of ChatGPT.Also leaving the agency is CISA Chief Information Officer (CIO) Robert Costello, who was in the position for five years. Costello had reportedly clashed with Gottumukkala, who tried to force him out and transfer him to a different DHS position. Costello is instead leaving federal service. President Trump’s choice for a permanent CISA Director– Sean Plankey– has yet to receive a Senate vote. Plankey recently left his position with the U.S. Coast Guard but is expected to remain the CISA Director nominee. “[CISA] needs Senate-confirmed leadership immediately,” said Foundation for Defense of Democracies senior fellow Mark Montgomery. “Whether he’s the perfect guy for every administration, I don’t know. He’s the perfect guy for this administration.”\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nHouse Moves to End DHS Shutdown as 100,000 Employees Work Without Pay\nNext\nNext\nNavy Launches Department-Wide Review That Could Cut Up to 20 Percent of Civilian Jobs","content_cn":"伊朗冲突加剧网络安全担忧，国土安全部停摆、CISA动荡持续\n新闻\n3月5日\n作者：FEDagent\n伊朗冲突使人们更加关注联邦网络防御，而此时国土安全部（DHS）因资金中断而停摆，网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）内部也存在领导层动荡。伊朗向来会以网络攻击回应海外威胁，专家警告，美国企业和基础设施可能遭遇一连串低级别攻击，例如网站篡改和分布式拒绝服务攻击。\n民主防御基金会网络与技术创新中心主任Annie Fixler表示：“华盛顿的网络机构在人员有限的情况下运作，现在是一个糟糕的时机。”该基金会是一家国家安全智库。“伊朗也可能对网络卫生措施不当的目标取得一些有限成功——例如，使用默认密码的暴露边缘设备。”\n其他网络专家也赞同这一观点。前CISA官员Brian Harrell表示：“威胁猎手现在应该加班工作。通过将破坏性攻击与心理行动相结合，伊朗将试图削弱公众对政府机构的信任，并在冲突加剧时期展示其国内实力。”\nCISA的动荡\n自特朗普总统上任以来，CISA失去了约三分之一的员工。该机构还面临领导层动荡。Madhu Gottumukkala最近被免去代理局长职务，转任DHS战略实施主任。他由Nick Andersen代理接任。Andersen此前担任CISA网络安全执行主任。\n曾与DHS部长Kristi Noem在南达科他州共事、担任该州首席信息官的Gottumukkala，其任期并不顺利。有报道称，他未通过测谎测试，并将敏感文件上传至公开版本的ChatGPT，此后他面临更严格的审查。\nCISA首席信息官（CIO）Robert Costello也将离开该机构，他已在该职位任职五年。据报道，Costello曾与Gottumukkala发生冲突；后者试图迫使他离职并将其调往DHS的另一职位。Costello将离开联邦政府工作。特朗普总统提名的CISA常任局长人选Sean Plankey尚未获得参议院表决。Plankey最近离开了其在美国海岸警卫队的职位，但预计仍将作为CISA局长提名人留任。民主防御基金会高级研究员Mark Montgomery表示：“[CISA]需要立即拥有经参议院确认的领导层。”“我不知道他是否是每届政府的完美人选。他是本届政府的完美人选。”\nFEDagent\n上一篇\n上一篇\n众议院采取行动结束DHS停摆，10万名员工无薪工作\n下一篇\n下一篇\n海军启动全部门审查，可能削减多达20%的文职岗位","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-03-05T12:04:42-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3662","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"饮酒之夜导致FBI主管的格洛克手枪和劳力士被盗","title_en":"Night of Drinking led to Theft of FBI Supervisor’s Glock, Rolex — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）反恐部门一名主管因饮酒后枪支、劳力士手表和现金在酒店房间被盗而接受内部调查。据文件和政府官员称，FBI国际恐怖主义部门主管罗伯特·曼森在夏洛特威斯汀酒店住宿期间，其格洛克.40口径手枪、价值6000美元的劳力士手表和60美元现金被盗。曼森与其他高级特工在夏洛特参加培训时与自称异国舞者的女性外出饮酒。目前无人被捕，警方尚未找回武器。","summary_en":"A supervisor in the FBI's counterterrorism unit is under internal investigation after a night of drinking led to the theft of his gun, Rolex watch, and cash from his hotel room. According to documents and government officials, Robert Manson, a unit chief in the FBI's international terrorism section, was staying at a Westin hotel in Charlotte, North Carolina, when his Glock .40-caliber handgun, a $6,000 Rolex watch, and $60 in cash were stolen. Manson and other senior agents were in Charlotte for training when they went out drinking with women they said were exotic dancers. No arrests have been made and the weapon has not been recovered.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:31:52.547885+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/night-of-drinking-led-to-theft-of-fbi-supervisors-glock-rolex","content":"Night of Drinking led to Theft of FBI Supervisor’s Glock, Rolex\nThe Takedown\nNov 9\nWritten By FEDagent\nA supervisor in FBI’s counterterrorism unit is the subject of an internal investigation after a night of drinking led to the theft of his gun, his Rolex, and cash from his hotel room.According to documents and government officials, Robert Manson, a unit chief in the FBI’s international terrorism section, was staying at a Westin hotel in Charlotte, N.C. this summer when his Glock .40-caliber handgun was stolen, a $6,000 Rolex watch and $60 in cash, according to a police report.Manson and other senior agents were in Charlotte for training when they went out drinking with women who they said were exotic dancers, reports the New York Times.“Investigators determined that the victim, Robert Manson, met a woman in the hotel bar the prior night and took her back to his hotel room,” Robert Tufano, a spokesman for the Charlotte-Mecklenburg Police Department, said in a statement.According to the Times, Manson was incapacitated from drinking alcohol and a fellow agent, Kevin Thurman, reported the theft to the police. In the police report, the theft is noted as occurring sometime between 2 a.m. and 5 a.m. since the hotel bar closes at 2 p.m.In the police report, the gun was identified as a Glock 27, a compact model that is easy to conceal. While agents are allowed to carry concealed weapons while off duty, this permission does not apply when agents are intoxicated.No arrests have been made and police officers have not recovered the weapon.Image: \"FBI\" by Steven Isaacson. Used under CC BY-SA 2.0, cropped, edited from original.\nFEDagent\nPrevious\nPrevious\nThis Week on FEDtalk: When Gov Gets Modern\nNext\nNext\nGet Your 2018 Custom Jeep Wrangler JL Raffle Ticket","content_cn":"酗酒之夜导致FBI主管的格洛克手枪和劳力士被盗 《缉捕行动》 11月9日 撰稿：FEDagent FBI反恐部门一名主管在一夜饮酒后，其枪支、劳力士手表和酒店房间内的现金被盗，目前正接受内部调查。 根据文件和政府官员的说法，FBI国际恐怖主义部门的一名组长罗伯特·曼森今年夏天入住北卡罗来纳州夏洛特市的一家威斯汀酒店时，一把格洛克0.40口径手枪、一块价值6000美元的劳力士手表和60美元现金被盗，警方报告记录了这一情况。 据《纽约时报》报道，曼森和其他高级特工当时在夏洛特接受培训，期间他们与几名自称脱衣舞娘的女性外出饮酒。 夏洛特-梅克伦堡警察局发言人罗伯特·图法诺在一份声明中说：“调查人员确定，受害者罗伯特·曼森前一晚在酒店酒吧认识了一名女子，并带她回到自己的酒店房间。” 据《纽约时报》报道，曼森因饮酒而失去行动能力，另一名特工凯文·瑟曼向警方报告了盗窃案。警方报告称，盗窃发生在凌晨2点至5点之间，因为酒店酒吧下午2点关闭。 警方报告称，被盗枪支为格洛克27，一款便于隐藏的紧凑型型号。特工下班后获准携带隐蔽武器，但特工醉酒时不适用这一许可。 尚未有人被捕，警察也没有找回枪支。 图片：“FBI”，作者Steven Isaacson。依据CC BY-SA 2.0使用，从原图裁剪并编辑。 FEDagent 上一篇 上一篇 本周FEDtalk：政府现代化 下一篇 下一篇 获取你的2018款定制Jeep Wrangler JL抽奖券","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2017-11-09T13:50:00-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1063","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"史上最长停摆接近结束，众议院通过DHS拨款法案","title_en":"Record-Long Shutdown Nears End as House Passes DHS Funding Bill — FEDagent","summary_cn":"美国史上最长政府停摆的大部分有望结束，众议院以口头表决通过参议院提出的国土安全部拨款法案，该法案不包括移民与海关执法局及海关与边境保护局。法案将全面重启海岸警卫队、特勤局、联邦应急管理局和运输安全管理局等DHS机构，待总统特朗普签署。众议院另以215比211通过参议院财政蓝图，为ICE和CBP的约700亿美元移民执法拨款铺路。","summary_en":"The bulk of the longest government shutdown in U.S. history is set to end after the House passed the Senate's bill funding the Department of Homeland Security, excluding ICE and CBP. The measure, which twice passed the Senate, was approved by voice vote and will fully reopen DHS agencies including the Coast Guard, Secret Service, FEMA and TSA once signed by President Trump. Separately, the House approved the Senate's fiscal blueprint 215-211, unlocking a reconciliation package with about $70 billion for immigration enforcement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:27:46.178356+00:00","url":"https://www.fedagent.com/news/record-long-shutdown-nears-end-as-house-passes-dhs-funding-bill","content":"Record-Long Shutdown Nears End as House Passes DHS Funding Bill\nNews\nApr 30\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe bulk of the longest government shutdown in U.S. history is on track to be over soon, after the House passed the Senate’s bill funding the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), excluding Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP). The bill, which twice passed the Senate, was approved by voice vote in the House. The measure will fully reopen all DHS agencies, including the US Coast Guard, Secret Service, Federal Emergency Management Agency, and Transportation Security Administration, once signed into law by President Trump. Speaker Mike Johnson said earlier in the week that he wanted significant changes to the bill. But that all changed. The speaker cited progress in immigration funding efforts. The White House and Senate Republicans were also putting pressure on the House since the shooting at the White House Correspondents Association Dinner on Saturday and the fact that DHS said it would run out of emergency money for paychecks come May. Reconciliation Bill Moving Forward TooSeparately, the House approved the Senate’s fiscal blueprint funding ICE and CBP, unlocking the ability for Republicans to pass a party-line reconciliation package. The 215-211 vote was along party lines. With both chambers passing the blueprint, lawmakers can work on a filibuster-proof reconciliation bill to provide about $70 billion in funding for immigration enforcement. The Senate Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs and Judiciary committees will take the lead on writing the legislation. Senate leaders hope to have the bill on the floor by the week of May 11. Democrats continue to demand reforms to immigration enforcement.Rep. Jamie Raskin (D-MD) says the bill funds ICE and CBP “with basically no strings attached.”\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nThe Use of a Geofence Warrant in Argument before the Supreme Court\nNext\nNext\nScrutiny Grows After WHCD Attack; Secret Service Defends Security Posture","content_cn":"《创纪录的长期停摆即将结束：众议院通过国土安全部拨款法案》\n新闻\n4月30日\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.撰写\n美国历史上持续时间最长的政府停摆，其主体部分即将结束。此前，众议院通过了参议院提出的国土安全部（DHS）拨款法案，但不包括移民与海关执法局（ICE）和美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）的拨款。该法案此前曾两次在参议院通过，此次在众议院以口头表决方式获批。总统特朗普签署成为法律后，该措施将全面重新开放国土安全部所有机构，包括美国海岸警卫队、特勤局、联邦紧急事务管理局和运输安全管理局。本周早些时候，众议院议长迈克·约翰逊表示，他希望对该法案作出重大修改。但后来情况完全改变。议长提到了移民拨款工作取得的进展。自周六白宫记者协会晚宴发生枪击事件以来，以及国土安全部表示到5月发放工资时将用完应急资金，白宫和参议院共和党人也一直向众议院施压。\n和解法案也在推进\n另外，众议院批准了参议院提出的财政蓝图，为ICE和CBP提供资金，从而解锁了共和党以党派路线通过和解方案的能力。215票对211票的表决按照党派立场进行。随着两院都通过该蓝图，议员们可以制定一项不受阻挠议事影响的和解法案，为移民执法提供约700亿美元资金。参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会和司法委员会将牵头起草该法案。参议院领导人希望在5月11日当周将法案提交全院审议。民主党人继续要求改革移民执法。众议员杰米·拉斯金（马里兰州民主党）表示，该法案为ICE和CBP提供资金，“基本上没有任何附加条件”。\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一篇\n上一篇\n最高法院辩论中使用地理围栏搜查令\n下一篇\n下一篇\n白宫记者协会晚宴袭击事件后审查加剧；特勤局为安保部署辩护","publish_source":"fedagent.com","publish_time":"2026-04-30T11:50:50-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3070","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部将终止运输安全官员的集体谈判权","title_en":"DHS to End Collective Bargaining for Transportation Security Officers — FEDmanager","summary_cn":"国土安全部计划终止运输安全管理局运输安全官员的集体谈判权，称其工会美国联邦政府雇员联合会未能保护员工并阻碍绩效认可。该工会2023年与TSA签署七年集体谈判协议，代表约4.7万名TSO。工会主席凯利称这是斗争的开始，众议员汤普森批评此举将降低士气。此举是特朗普政府削弱联邦工会影响力的更广泛行动的一部分。","summary_en":"DHS plans to end collective bargaining rights for Transportation Security Officers at TSA, saying their union AFGE failed to protect them and hindered merit-based recognition. AFGE signed a seven-year agreement in 2023 and represents about 47,000 TSOs. Union president Kelley called it the beginning of the fight, and Rep. Thompson criticized the move as harmful to morale. It is part of the Trump administration's broader effort to curb federal labor groups.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:59:51.791330+00:00","url":"https://www.fedmanager.com/news/dhs-to-end-collective-bargaining-for-transportation-security-officers","content":"DHS to End Collective Bargaining for Transportation Security Officers\nMar 11\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe Department of Homeland Security (DHS) plans to end collective bargaining rights for Transportation Security Officers (TSOs) at the Transportation Security Administration (TSA). DHS says the group’s union, the American Federal of Government Employees (AFGE), did not protect TSOs and “hindered merit-based performance recognition and advancement.”In a statement, DHS says nearly 200 TSOs were working full-time on union activities instead of safeguarding the flying public. It also blamed the union for helping a “select few poor performers” exploit gaps in benefit programs, placing a greater burden on TSOs at the “expense of American travelers and taxpayers.”DHS notes that “By eliminating the collective bargaining agreement, Transportation Security Officers will now have opportunities based on their performance, not longevity or union membership.”AFGE RespondsTSA and the American Federal of Government Employees (AFGE) signed a seven-year collective bargaining agreement in May 2023. AFGE played an important role in helping to secure a pay increase for TSOs that brought them in line with general schedule employees and currently represents about 47,000 TSOs. “Let’s be clear: this is the beginning, not the end, of the fight for Americans’ fundamental rights to join a union,” said AFGE National President Everett Kelley. “AFGE will not rest until the basic dignity and rights of the workers at TSA are acknowledged by the government once again.”That position was echoed by Representative Bennie Thompson (D-MS), ranking Democrat on the House Homeland Security Committee, and a key figure in the fight for equal pay for TSOs. “Attempting to negate their legally binding collective bargaining agreement now makes zero sense — it will only reduce morale and hamper the workforce,” said Representative Thompson. In addition, AFGE pointed out all federal employees who join a union do so voluntarily, and that TSOs who volunteer as union representatives account for less than half a percent of all work hours performed at TSA. Administration Takes Aim at Organized LaborThis is part of broader action that the Trump Administration has taken to cut down on the influence of federal labor groups. Shortly after taking office the President issued an executive order that would eliminate any CBAs struck in the 30 days prior to the inauguration of a new president. In that order, President Trump expressed his annoyance that the Department of Education signed a new CBA three days before he took office. Agencies were also ordered to report on union activities in fiscal year 2024, by March 14. That includes time spent on union duties, the number of employees in the union, expenses agencies paid for union activities, and the “amounts of time used for each purpose of taxpayer-funded union time.”Agencies were also told to report employee data such as salary, position, and other information for any employee who used taxpayer funded union time in FY 2024.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nBuyouts Offered at HHS; DOD Starts Firings as Large-Scale Layoff Plans Due\nNext\nNext\nMembers of Congress Demand Clarity on Looming VA Job Cuts","content_cn":"国土安全部将终止运输安全官员的集体谈判\n3月11日\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C. 撰写\n国土安全部（DHS）计划终止运输安全管理局（TSA）运输安全官员（TSO）的集体谈判权。DHS称，该群体的工会——美国联邦政府雇员联合会（AFGE）没有保护TSO，并且“阻碍了基于绩效的认可和晋升”。DHS在一份声明中表示，近200名TSO全职从事工会活动，而不是保障乘客安全。DHS还指责该工会帮助“一小撮表现不佳者”利用福利计划漏洞，使其他TSO承担更大负担，“代价由美国旅客和纳税人承担”。DHS指出：“通过取消集体谈判协议，运输安全官员今后的机会将取决于其绩效，而不是工龄或工会会员身份。”\n\nAFGE回应\n\nTSA与美国联邦政府雇员联合会（AFGE）于2023年5月签署了一份为期七年的集体谈判协议。AFGE在帮助争取提高TSO薪资方面发挥了重要作用，使其薪资与通用薪级雇员相当；目前该工会约代表47,000名TSO。\n“需要明确的是：这不是美国人捍卫加入工会这一基本权利的斗争的结束，而是开始，”AFGE全国主席Everett Kelley表示。“在政府再次承认TSA工人的基本尊严和权利之前，AFGE不会停歇。”\n密西西比州民主党众议员Bennie Thompson也表达了同样立场。他是众议院国土安全委员会民主党首席成员，也是争取TSO同工同酬斗争中的关键人物。“现在试图否定这份具有法律约束力的集体谈判协议毫无道理——这只会降低士气并妨碍劳动力队伍，”Thompson众议员说。此外，AFGE指出，所有加入工会的联邦雇员都是自愿加入；在TSA，志愿担任工会代表的TSO所占工作时间不到全部工时的0.5%。\n\n政府瞄准有组织劳工\n\n这是特朗普政府为削弱联邦劳工团体影响力而采取的更广泛行动的一部分。总统上任后不久签署了一项行政命令，将取消新总统就职前30天内签订的任何集体谈判协议。在该命令中，特朗普总统表达了对教育部在其上任前三天签署新集体谈判协议的不满。\n各机构还被命令在3月14日前报告2024财年的工会活动情况。这包括用于工会职责的时间、工会成员人数、各机构为工会活动支付的费用，以及“纳税人资助的工会时间用于各项目的的时长”。\n各机构还被要求报告任何在2024财年使用纳税人资助的工会时间的雇员数据，例如薪资、职位及其他信息。\n\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n\n上一篇\n上一篇\n卫生与公众服务部提供买断方案；国防部开始解雇，大规模裁员计划即将到期\n\n下一篇\n下一篇\n国会议员要求澄清即将到来的退伍军人事务部岗位削减","publish_source":"fedmanager.com","publish_time":"2025-03-11T11:28:02-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3422","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"团体“盯上”监视名单上的雇员后，联邦团体与国土安全部作出回应","title_en":"Federal Groups, DHS Respond, After Group “Targets” Employees on “Watch List” — FEDmanager","summary_cn":"右翼非营利组织美国问责基金会发布“国土安全部官僚监视名单”，公开部分雇员的姓名、照片、薪资及财务信息，称其为在移民问题上不可信的“激进左派”。国土安全部联系受影响雇员并提供安全支持，部长马约卡斯谴责骚扰恐吓行为。工会AFGE称此举为麦卡锡主义，学者莫伊尼汉指出名单未区分政治任命者与职业公务员。","summary_en":"The far-right nonprofit American Accountability Foundation released a \"DHS Bureaucrat Watch List,\" posting employees' names, photos, salaries, and financial details, calling them untrustworthy \"radical leftists\" on immigration. DHS contacted affected employees and offered security support, with Secretary Mayorkas condemning harassment. AFGE called it McCarthyism, and professor Moynihan noted the list fails to distinguish political appointees from career civil servants.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:26:22.653671+00:00","url":"https://www.fedmanager.com/news/federal-groups-dhs-respond-after-group-targets-employees-on-watch-list","content":"Federal Groups, DHS Respond, After Group “Targets” Employees on “Watch List”\nNov 5\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nImagine your name, picture, salary, and financial situation posted online in one place for all to see, simply because you are doing your job. That’s the situation some federal employees find themselves in today, after the far-right nonprofit American Accountability Foundation released a \"DHS Bureaucrat Watch List” to “target” and remove so-called “subversive bureaucrats” from government. American Accountability Foundation is funded by the Heritage Foundation and the Conservative Partnership Institute.According to the group, the “watch list” identifies “radical leftists” who are working in or with the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), particularly on immigration issues. The conservative group claims these civil servants cannot be trusted to secure the border.   “We created DHSWatchlist.com to shine a light on the swamp’s darkest corners. No longer will these radicals be able to hide in anonymity,” said American Accountability Foundation president Thomas Jones, a former Republican senate staffer. Jones said he created the site to expose “long-standing and deep bias” on immigration policy.The site posts the name of the civil servant, picture, salary, employment history, and even if they have credit card debt. Some employees are cited because they donated as little as $10 to Democratic campaigns. Others are cited because they made a social media support in support of diversity, equity, accessibility, inclusion topics or Democrats. “Obviously this is designed to intimidate career government officials who are civil servants trying to fulfill the mission of the department and do it across administrations and do it with integrity,” said one anonymous employee on the list to the Washington Post. DHS contacted the affected employees and offered security and support. “We condemn in the strongest terms any effort to harass or intimidate our public servants,” DHS Secretary Alejandro N. Mayorkas said in a statement.Employees named also work at the Department of Justice (DOJ) and the Office of Management and Budget (OMB). The threats prompted calls for action from unions and federal employee groups. The American Federation of Government Employees (AFGE) called it McCarthyism. \"Creating watchlists of so-called subversives inside government is a tactic straight out of the McCarthy era, plain in its intent to terrorize individual civil servants and frighten other Americans away from getting involved in politics and public service,” said AFGE National President Everett Kelly. \"Far from doing anything to improve government, this shameful, un-American behavior makes it more difficult to attract top talent to important government positions, hurting the entire country in the process.\"And in a post called “Can We Still Govern” on Substack, University of Michigan Public Policy Professor Don Moynihan wrote about the increasing conditions of “terror” that federal officials have to work and live under. Moynihan also noted that the American Accountability Foundation did not make it clear that some people on the list are political employees, and not career civil servants.“It is completely misleading to present them as “career bureaucrats are that implement their orders” as AAF does,” wrote Moynihan.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nOPM Issues Guidance on Implementing Civil Service Protections\nNext\nNext\nSecretary Blinken Applauds Workforce Rebuilding Progress, Warns of Challenges","content_cn":"联邦团体、国土安全部回应团体在“名单”上“针对”员工\n11月5日\n作者：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n想象一下，仅仅因为你在履行工作职责，你的姓名、照片、薪资和财务状况就被集中发布到网上，供所有人查看。这正是一些联邦雇员如今面临的情况，此前右翼非营利组织美国问责基金会发布了“国土安全部官僚观察名单”，以“针对”并清除政府中的所谓“颠覆性官僚”。美国问责基金会由传统基金会和保守派伙伴关系研究所资助。根据该组织的说法，这份“观察名单”列出了在国土安全部（DHS）任职或与其合作的“激进左翼人士”，尤其是处理移民问题的人士。该保守派组织声称，这些公务员不值得信任，无法保障边境安全。“我们创建DHSWatchlist.com，是为了照亮沼泽最黑暗的角落。这些激进分子将不再能够匿名隐藏，”美国问责基金会主席、前共和党参议院工作人员托马斯·琼斯说。琼斯表示，他创建该网站是为了揭露移民政策上“长期存在且根深蒂固的偏见”。该网站发布公务员的姓名、照片、薪资、工作经历，甚至是否有信用卡债务。有些员工仅仅因为向民主党竞选活动捐赠了10美元，就被列入其中。另一些人则因为在社交媒体上发表支持多元、公平、无障碍、包容议题或民主党的内容而被列出。“显然，这是为了恐吓那些职业政府官员——他们是公务员，努力履行部门使命，无论政府如何更迭都坚持这样做，并以诚信履职，”名单上的一名匿名员工对《华盛顿邮报》说。国土安全部联系了受影响的员工，并提供安全保障和支持。“我们最强烈地谴责任何骚扰或恐吓公职人员的企图，”国土安全部部长亚历杭德罗·N·马约卡斯在一份声明中说。被点名的员工还在司法部（DOJ）和管理与预算办公室（OMB）任职。这些威胁促使工会和联邦雇员团体呼吁采取行动。美国政府雇员联合会（AFGE）称这是麦卡锡主义。“在政府内部创建所谓颠覆分子的观察名单，是直接出自麦卡锡时代的手段，其意图显然是恐吓个别公务员，并吓阻其他美国人参与政治和公共服务，”AFGE全国主席埃弗里特·凯利说。“这种可耻且不符合美国精神的行为非但没有改善政府，反而使重要政府职位更难吸引顶尖人才，最终损害整个国家。”密歇根大学公共政策教授唐·莫伊尼汉在Substack上发表题为《我们还能治理吗》的文章，谈到了联邦官员不得不在其中工作和生活的日益加剧的“恐怖”环境。莫伊尼汉还指出，美国问责基金会没有明确说明，名单上的一些人是政治任命人员，而不是职业公务员。“AAF把他们描述成‘执行上级命令的职业官僚’，这是完全具有误导性的，”莫伊尼汉写道。\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一页\n上一页\n人事管理局发布实施公务员保护措施的指导意见\n下一页\n下一页\n布林肯部长赞扬重建劳动力取得进展，并警告面临的挑战","publish_source":"fedmanager.com","publish_time":"2024-11-05T13:16:53-05:00"}},{"id":"news-1090","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"结束DHS停摆压力加大，参众两院分歧加深","title_en":"House, Senate Divide Grows Amid Pressure to End DHS Shutdown — FEDmanager","summary_cn":"随着参众两院共和党人分歧加深，国会重新寻求结束国土安全部停摆。DHS警告工资资金数日内将耗尽，白宫记者协会晚宴枪击事件后压力进一步上升。众议长约翰逊称将提出新版本法案，不希望ICE和CBP成为“孤儿”。参议院多数党领袖图恩表示只做技术性修改。参议院另在推进为ICE和CBP提供700亿至800亿美元资金的独立和解法案。","summary_en":"Congress is returning to the drawing board to end the DHS shutdown as the divide grows between House and Senate Republicans. DHS warns paycheck money will dry up within days, and pressure mounts after the shooting at the White House Correspondents Association dinner. Speaker Johnson said the House will propose a new version, not wanting ICE and CBP to become 'orphans.' Majority Leader Thune said he would make only technical changes. The Senate is also working on a separate reconciliation bill funding ICE and CBP with $70-80 billion.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:29:51.276501+00:00","url":"https://www.fedmanager.com/news/house-senate-divide-grows-amid-pressure-to-end-dhs-shutdown","content":"House, Senate Divide Grows Amid Pressure to End DHS Shutdown\nFrom the Hill\nApr 28\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nCongress is heading back to the drawing board to end the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) shutdown, as the divide grows between House and Senate Republicans.This as DHS warns that money for paychecks will dry up within days. And pressure mounts to end the shutdown following the shooting at the White House Correspondents Association dinner, with the shooter apparently targeting President Trump and other administration officials. In the latest twist: House Speaker Mike Johnson (R-LA) says the House Republican conference will propose a new version of a bill that was twice passed by the Senate, funding most DHS agencies. He says the Senate version funding everything except for Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) must change, saying he doesn’t want ICE and CBP to become “orphans.” “It has some problematic language because it was haphazardly drafted,” said Speaker Johnson. “We have a modified version that I think is going to be much better for both chambers.”Senate Majority Leader John Thune (R-SD) said he’ll make technical changes to the bill to get it over the finish line, but anything beyond that is a “real problem.” Senators also noted the importance of funding DHS as soon as possible, noting that Secret Service agents are among those who will be going without paychecks when the current funding runs dry. “For 72 days they have gone without their mission being funded. That’s a problem. That’s absolutely a problem,” said Senator Katie Britt (R-AL), chair of the Homeland Security Appropriations Subcommittee. If the House passes a new bill putting in language funding ICE and CBP, the Senate will then have to pass it a third time. That could be problematic, with Democrats demanding restrictions on federal immigration enforcement. Still, Democrats say Republicans have the power to end the shutdown. “I think the standoff is now between the two Republican leaders in the House and Senate,” said Senate Minority Whip Dick Durbin (D-IL). The Senate meanwhile is continuing to work on a separate reconciliation bill funding ICE and CBP. It would allocate an additional $70 to $80 billion to those agencies through 2029. “Our work in terms of the funding process is well underway here, and hopefully that will be enough to get the House in a comfortable position,” said Senate Majority Leader Thune.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nOPM, GSA to Share HQ Space in Federal Real Estate Overhaul; USDA Moving Workers\nNext\nNext\nSpending Fight, Staffing Shakeups Dominate Budget Hearings","content_cn":"众议院、参议院分歧加深，结束国土安全部停摆的压力增大\n来自国会山\n4月28日\n作者：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n随着众议院和参议院共和党人之间的分歧加深，国会正重新研究结束国土安全部（DHS）停摆的方案。\n与此同时，国土安全部警告称，发工资的钱将在几天内耗尽。在白宫记者协会晚宴发生枪击事件后，结束停摆的压力也在增加；枪手似乎以特朗普总统和其他政府官员为目标。\n最新进展是：众议院议长Mike Johnson（路易斯安那州共和党人）表示，众议院共和党党团将提出一份新版本法案。该法案此前已获参议院两次通过，为国土安全部大多数机构提供资金。他说，参议院版本中除移民及海关执法局（ICE）和海关与边境保护局（CBP）外为所有机构提供资金的安排必须改变，因为他不希望ICE和CBP成为“孤儿”。\n“其中有一些有问题的措辞，因为起草得很仓促。”议长Johnson说，“我们有一个修改后的版本，我认为这对两院都会好得多。”\n参议院多数党领袖John Thune（南达科他州共和党人）说，他将对法案作出技术性修改，以推动其最终通过，但除此之外的任何改动都会是“真正的问题”。\n参议员们还指出，尽快为国土安全部提供资金非常重要，并指出特勤局特工也将成为当前拨款耗尽后拿不到工资的人之一。\n“72天来，他们的任务一直没有得到资金支持。这是个问题，绝对是个问题。”国土安全拨款小组委员会主席、参议员Katie Britt（阿拉巴马州共和党人）说。\n如果众议院通过一项加入ICE和CBP拨款条款的新法案，参议院随后将不得不第三次通过该法案。这可能会带来问题，因为民主党人要求限制联邦移民执法。\n不过，民主党人表示，共和党人有能力结束停摆。\n“我认为，目前的僵局存在于众议院和参议院的两位共和党领导人之间。”参议院少数党党鞭Dick Durbin（伊利诺伊州民主党人）说。\n与此同时，参议院正在继续推动另一项和解法案，为ICE和CBP提供资金。该法案将在2029年前向这两个机构额外拨款700亿至800亿美元。\n“我们在拨款流程方面的工作已经在这里全面展开，希望这足以让众议院处于一个较为舒适的位置。”参议院多数党领袖Thune说。\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一页\n上一页\nOPM、GSA将在联邦房地产改革中共享总部空间；USDA调动工作人员\n下一页\n下一页\n支出之争与人员调整主导预算听证会","publish_source":"fedmanager.com","publish_time":"2026-04-28T12:36:36-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3513","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"参议院听证会：若Schedule F回归，国家安全与国土安全将受损","title_en":"National, Homeland Security Would Be Compromised if Schedule F Returns: Senate Hearing — FEDmanager","summary_cn":"美国参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会举行听证会，前国防部代理副部长彼得·莱文和前国土安全部代理副部长伊莱恩·杜克等证人警告，若Schedule F行政令回归，将把大量公务员转为随意雇佣制，削弱国家安全与执法机构能力，影响灾害应对、边境巡逻和军事技术保障。杜克称国土安全任务所需职业培训需数年，人才流失将侵蚀机构知识。参议员彼得斯指出，新增至少5万个政治任命职位将导致更多空缺。特朗普已誓言若当选将恢复该令。","summary_en":"A Senate Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs Committee hearing examined the potential return of Schedule F, the Trump-era executive order that would reclassify large swaths of the civil service as at-will employees. Witnesses including former DHS Acting and Deputy Secretary Elaine Duke and former DOD Acting Under Secretary Peter Levine warned it would erode national and homeland security missions, from disaster response to border patrol and military technology. Duke said many homeland security career paths take years to train. Chairman Gary Peters said adding at least 50,000 political positions would increase vacancies. Trump has vowed to reinstate Schedule F if he wins the November election.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:31:14.331216+00:00","url":"https://www.fedmanager.com/news/national-homeland-security-would-be-compromised-if-schedule-f-returns-senate-hearing","content":"National, Homeland Security Would Be Compromised if Schedule F Returns: Senate Hearing\nFrom the Hill\nSep 24\nWritten By Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nThe impact of the potential return of Schedule F on national security and law enforcement agencies was the topic of a recent hearing on Capitol Hill. Witnesses told senators that it could impact everything from disaster response to patrolling the border to securing technology for the nation’s military. The hearing was held by the Senate Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs Committee. However, no Republicans questioned witnesses at the hearing. Schedule F is the Trump-era executive order that would allow a president to reclassify large swathes of the civil service to at-will employees, making them easier to remove. President Biden rescinded that order and has been working to codify protections for the civil service. At the hearing, Chairman Gary Peters (D-MI) noted that a return of Schedule F would “weaken our national security and make us vulnerable to serious threats that continually face our nation.”Concerns Span the National Security CommunityWitnesses including former Department of Defense (DOD) Acting Under Secretary for Personnel and Readiness Peter Levine and former Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Acting and Deputy Secretary Elaine Duke agreed with the chairman’s comments. Former Under Secretary Levine noted that civilian employees touch nearly all aspects of defense and that their ability to provide advice is unmeasurable. “The ability of career civil servants to provide open and candid advice without losing their jobs enables political appointees like me to benefit from their knowledge and expertise,” said Levine. “The risk that political appointees will fail to listen to the informed views of career civil servants is far greater than the risk that civil servants will fail to carry out a directive from a political appointee once it has been made.” Former Acting Secretary Duke noted it would harm the mission. “The ability to carry out the mission would be eroded by not having enough people doing the mission and not having that institutional knowledge. Many of the career paths in the Homeland Security mission take years to train and develop,” stated Duke.  Also testifying was Government Accountability Project Legal Director Tom Devine who noted that Schedule F would erase the merit systems’ check on abuses of power in the Executive Branch, no matter which party holds the White House.  “We have seen the Schedule F playbook, and it is a recipe for corruption and abuse that will harm not only millions of federal employees, but the public they serve,” said Devine. In addition, lawmakers questioned how agencies could continue to function, if at least 50,000 career federal positions can be converted into political roles. Currently, just 4,000 positions require a political appointment, and many of those get held up in the confirmation process. “Adding at least 50,000 more political positions, as proposed by the advocates of Schedule F, I believe would undoubtedly result in a higher number of vacant positions at these agencies,” said Senator Peters. President Trump has vowed to reinstate Schedule F if he wins the November election.\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\nPrevious\nPrevious\nHouse, Senate Pass Workforce Bills; Some Bipartisan, Some Contentious\nNext\nNext\nFighting Fraud Front and Center on Capitol Hill","content_cn":"国内事务\n如果“F计划”回归，国家安全和国土安全将受到损害：参议院听证会\n来自《国会山报》\n9月24日\n撰稿：Shaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n“F计划”可能回归对国家安全和执法机构的影响，是国会山近期一次听证会的主题。证人告诉参议员，这可能影响从灾害响应、边境巡逻到保障国家军队技术安全的方方面面。听证会由参议院国土安全与政府事务委员会举行。不过，听证会上没有共和党人向证人提问。“F计划”是特朗普时期的一项行政命令，允许总统将大批公务员重新分类为任意雇用员工，从而更容易将其解雇。拜登总统撤销了该命令，并一直推动将公务员保护措施编入法律。在听证会上，委员会主席加里·彼得斯（密歇根州民主党）指出，恢复“F计划”将“削弱我们的国家安全，使我们容易受到持续威胁我国的严重威胁”。\n\n国家安全界的担忧\n包括前国防部（DOD）负责人员与战备事务的代理副部长彼得·莱文和前国土安全部（DHS）代理部长兼副部长伊莱恩·杜克在内的证人，都同意主席的看法。前副部长莱文指出，文职雇员参与国防几乎所有方面，他们提供建议的能力无法估量。“职业公务员能够提供公开、坦率的建议而不必担心失去工作，这让像我这样的政治任命官员能够受益于他们的知识和专业能力，”莱文说。“政治任命官员不听取职业公务员知情意见的风险，远大于公务员在政治任命官员作出指示后无法执行该指示的风险。”前代理部长杜克指出，这会损害任务执行。“由于没有足够人员执行任务，也没有相应的机构知识，完成任务的能力将受到削弱。国土安全任务中的许多职业道路都需要数年培训和培养，”杜克表示。政府问责项目法律主任汤姆·德文也出席作证。他指出，无论哪一党掌控白宫，“F计划”都会抹去功绩制度对行政部门滥用权力的制衡。“我们已经看到了‘F计划’的剧本，它是腐败和滥用的配方，不仅会伤害数百万联邦雇员，也会伤害他们所服务的公众，”德文说。此外，议员们质问，如果至少50,000个职业联邦职位可以转变为政治职位，各机构如何继续运作。目前，只有4,000个职位需要政治任命，其中许多还会在确认程序中被搁置。“按照‘F计划’倡导者的提议，再增加至少50,000个政治职位，我相信无疑会导致这些机构出现更多空缺职位，”彼得斯参议员说。特朗普总统曾承诺，如果赢得11月大选，将恢复“F计划”。\nShaw Bransford & Roth P.C.\n上一篇\n上一篇\n众议院、参议院通过劳动力法案；部分获两党支持，部分争议激烈\n下一篇\n下一篇\n打击欺诈成为国会山的首要任务","publish_source":"fedmanager.com","publish_time":"2024-09-24T11:01:57-04:00"}},{"id":"news-3307","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FIA WEC与勒芒24小时耐力赛宣布与CrowdStrike达成全球合作","title_en":"FIA WEC and 24 Hours of Le Mans announce global partnership with CrowdStrike","summary_cn":"FIA世界耐力锦标赛（WEC）与由西方汽车俱乐部主办的勒芒24小时耐力赛宣布与全球网络安全企业CrowdStrike建立战略合作，CrowdStrike成为该赛事的优质合作伙伴。文章称耐力赛与网络安全在压力、不可预测性和快速决策方面具有共通性，CrowdStrike以AI驱动的网络安全能力为赛事提供技术支持，双方在创新、可靠性和极端条件下的表现方面理念一致。","summary_en":"The FIA World Endurance Championship (WEC) and the 24 Hours of Le Mans, organised by the Automobile Club de l'Ouest, announced a strategic partnership with global cybersecurity leader CrowdStrike, which joins as a premium partner. The article says endurance racing and cybersecurity share foundations of pressure, unpredictability and rapid decision-making, and that CrowdStrike provides AI-driven cybersecurity expertise to raise the technological threshold of modern endurance racing, uniting two organisations driven by innovation, reliability and performance under extreme conditions.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:35:31.911215+00:00","url":"https://www.fiawec.com/en/news/fia-wec-and-24-hours-of-le-mans-announce-global-partnership-with-crowdstrike/11929","content":"Back\nFIA WEC and 24 Hours of Le Mans announce global partnership with CrowdStrike\nThe FIA World Endurance Championship (WEC) and the 24 Hours of Le Mans, organised by the Automobile Club de l'Ouest (ACO), are pleased to announce a strategic partnership with global cybersecurity leader CrowdStrike, which joins the championship as a premium partner.\nCrowdStrike\n27/02/2026\nWith 14 manufacturers committed across Hypercar and LMGT3, an unparalleled grid in international motorsport, FIA WEC continues to expand its competitive depth and worldwide visibility.Founded in 1923, the 24 Hours of Le Mans stands as one of the sport’s most prestigious Triple Crown events, alongside the Formula One World Championship and the Indianapolis 500. It remains the cornerstone of FIA WEC, which competes on a global stage with rounds in Qatar, Belgium, Italy, Brazil, the USA, Japan and Bahrain.A natural synergy: endurance challenges & cybersecurity excellenceEndurance racing and cybersecurity share the same foundations: pressure, unpredictability and rapid decision-making. CrowdStrike secures the critical systems teams rely on in real time, operating with the same speed and precision demanded of teams, manufacturers and race control throughout long-distance races. As FIA WEC seeks trusted partners capable of raising the technological threshold of modern endurance racing, CrowdStrike delivers advanced expertise in AI-driven cybersecurity that’s essential to meeting the sport’s most complex challenges. The partnership unites two organisations driven by innovation, reliability and performance under extreme conditions.\nQatar 1812km\n6 Heures d'Imola\nTotalEnergies 6 Heures de Spa-Francorchamps\n24 Heures du Mans\nROLEX 6 Heures de São Paulo\nLone Star Le Mans\n6 Heures de Fuji\nBapco Energies 8 Heures du Bahreïn\nHypercar\nLMGT3\nShare\nNext article\nLatest news\nBroadcast\nHow to Watch the 6 Hours of Fuji 2026: Preview and Guide\nFuji\nSights set on the summit: Teams aim to tame Fuji Speedway\nMichelin\nMichelin prepared for unique Fuji challenge\n6 Hours of\nFuji\nSeptember 25, 2026\nRace info\nTickets\nCOUNTDOWN TO Free Practice 1\n0\ndays\n:\n4\nhours\n:\n39\nmin\n:\n29\nsec\n14 Manufacturers","content_cn":"返回\nFIA世界耐力锦标赛（WEC）与勒芒24小时耐力赛宣布与CrowdStrike建立全球合作伙伴关系\nFIA世界耐力锦标赛（WEC）和由西部汽车俱乐部（ACO）组织的勒芒24小时耐力赛，很高兴宣布与全球网络安全领导者CrowdStrike达成战略合作伙伴关系。CrowdStrike将作为高级合作伙伴加入该锦标赛。\nCrowdStrike\n2026年2月27日\n凭借在Hypercar和LMGT3组别中共有14家制造商参赛，FIA WEC拥有国际赛车运动中无与伦比的发车阵容，并持续扩大其竞争深度和全球影响力。勒芒24小时耐力赛创办于1923年，是这项运动最负盛名的“三冠王”赛事之一，与一级方程式世界锦标赛和印第安纳波利斯500并列。它仍是FIA WEC的基石；FIA WEC在全球舞台上进行比赛，赛站遍布卡塔尔、比利时、意大利、巴西、美国、日本和巴林。\n天然协同：耐力挑战与网络安全卓越性\n耐力赛与网络安全拥有相同基础：压力、不可预测性和快速决策。CrowdStrike实时保护车队所依赖的关键系统，以长距离比赛期间车队、制造商和比赛控制所要求的同等速度与精确度运行。随着FIA WEC寻求能够提升现代耐力赛技术门槛的可信合作伙伴，CrowdStrike提供由人工智能驱动的先进网络安全专业能力，这对于应对这项运动最复杂的挑战至关重要。该合作将两个在极端条件下以创新、可靠性和性能为驱动力的组织联合起来。\n卡塔尔1812公里\n伊莫拉6小时耐力赛\nTotalEnergies斯帕-弗朗科尔尚6小时耐力赛\n勒芒24小时耐力赛\nROLEX圣保罗6小时耐力赛\n孤星勒芒\n富士6小时耐力赛\nBapco Energies巴林8小时耐力赛\nHypercar\nLMGT3\n分享\n下一篇文章\n最新消息\n转播\n如何观看2026年富士6小时耐力赛：预览与指南\n富士\n目标瞄准巅峰：车队力图征服富士赛道\n米其林\n米其林为独特的富士挑战做好准备\n富士6小时耐力赛\n2026年9月25日\n比赛信息\n门票\n距离第一次自由练习开始倒计时\n0\n天\n：\n4\n小时\n：\n39\n分钟\n：\n29\n秒\n14家制造商","publish_source":"fiawec.com","publish_time":"2024-12-12T09:48:24+01:00"}},{"id":"news-1488","ktid":1056514,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056514","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"亚当斯离开摩根大通转投富国银行","title_en":"Adams swaps JP Morgan for Wells Fargo - The DESK - The leading source of information for bond traders","summary_cn":"查尔斯·亚当斯在摩根大通工作近15年后，加入富国银行担任欧洲利率证券交易高级主管，常驻伦敦，负责构建超国家机构、主权及机构类（SSA）及相关利率证券的做市平台。他2011年以分析师身份加入摩根大通，后担任美国国债交易员、回购交易员，并于2024年被任命为EMEA地区SSA与信用回购交易主管，2025年6月离职。富国银行2025年第四季度企业与投资银行部门FICC收入为12亿美元，同比下降1%，环比下降14%。","summary_en":"Charles Adams has joined Wells Fargo as a senior lead for European rates securities trading after almost 15 years at JP Morgan. Based in London, he will build out a market-making platform for supranationals, sovereigns and agencies (SSA) and related rates securities. Adams began at JP Morgan as an analyst in 2011, later becoming a US Treasuries trader, a repo trader, and head of EMEA SSA and credit repo trading in 2024. He left the bank in June 2025. Wells Fargo reported US$1.2 billion in FICC revenues for Q4 2025, down 1% year-on-year and 14% quarter-on-quarter.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:43:39.528860+00:00","url":"https://www.fi-desk.com/adams-swaps-jp-morgan-for-wells-fargo/","content":"Adams swaps JP Morgan for Wells Fargo\nBy Lucy Carter - March 2, 20261767\nShareTweetShareCharles Adams has joined Wells Fargo as a senior lead for European rates securities trading after almost 15 years at JP Morgan.\nBased in London, he is responsible for trading and building out a market making platform for supranationals, sovereigns and agencies (SSA) and related rates securities.\nWells Fargo reported US$1.2 billion in FICC revenues for Q4 2025 within its corporate and investment banking segment, down 1% year-on-year and down 14% quarter-on-quarter.\nAdams began his career as an analyst at JP Morgan in 2011, later becoming a US Treasuries trader, a repo trader, and being named head of EMEA SSA and credit repo trading in 2024. He left the bank in June 2025.\n©Markets Media Europe 2026TOP OF PAGEShareTweetShare\nTAGSJP MorganWells FargoCharles Adams\nPrevious articleTokenisation booms in repo marketsNext articleThis Week from Trader TV: Sweta Singh, City Different Investments Lucy Carter","content_cn":"亚当斯离开摩根大通加盟富国银行\n作者：露西·卡特——2026年3月2日1767\n分享 推文 分享\n查尔斯·亚当斯在摩根大通工作近15年后，已加入富国银行，担任欧洲利率证券交易高级负责人。\n他常驻伦敦，负责交易并搭建超国家机构、主权机构及政府支持机构（SSA）以及相关利率证券的做市平台。\n富国银行报告称，其公司和投资银行部门2025年第四季度的固定收益、货币和大宗商品（FICC）收入为12亿美元，同比下降1%，环比下降14%。\n亚当斯于2011年在摩根大通以分析师身份开始职业生涯，后来担任美国国债交易员、回购交易员，并于2024年被任命为欧洲、中东及非洲地区 SSA 和信用回购交易主管。他于2025年6月离开该行。\n©Markets Media Europe 2026页面顶部分享 推文 分享\n标签\n摩根大通 富国银行 查尔斯·亚当斯\n上一篇文章：代币化在回购市场蓬勃发展 下一篇文章：本周 Trader TV：斯韦塔·辛格，City Different Investments 露西·卡特","publish_source":"fi-desk.com","publish_time":"2026-03-02T10:25:16+00:00"}},{"id":"news-933","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FIRE诉国土安全部：ICE数据库《信息自由法》诉讼","title_en":"FIRE v. Department of Homeland Security: ICE Database FOIA Litigation","summary_cn":"FIRE就有关ICE抗议者数据库的《信息自由法》请求起诉国土安全部与移民及海关执法局。2026年初DHS部署大量ICE探员开展移民执法，引发全国抗议；边境事务负责人霍曼公开称将建立抗议者数据库并通知其雇主，缅因州一名ICE探员也对合法拍摄的“ICE观察者”发出类似威胁。FIRE提交三份FOIA请求，DHS未在20天法定期限内回应，遂提起诉讼以迫使披露相关文件。","summary_en":"FIRE is suing the Department of Homeland Security and Immigration and Customs Enforcement over Freedom of Information Act requests concerning an alleged ICE database of protesters. After DHS deployed thousands of ICE agents in early 2026, protests erupted and Border Czar Tom Homan publicly said DHS would create such a database and inform employers, while an ICE agent in Maine made a similar threat to a lawful recorder. DHS failed to respond within the FOIA's 20-day window, prompting the suit to compel disclosure.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:24:37.090871+00:00","url":"https://www.fire.org/cases/fire-v-department-homeland-security-ice-database-foia-litigation","content":"Home\nCases\nShare\nShare with Email\nShare on Bluesky\nShare on Twitter\nShare on Facebook\nPrint\nFIRE v. Department of Homeland Security: ICE Database FOIA Litigation\nCases\nSearch all Cases\nCase Overview\nCase OverviewOriginal Court\nU.S. District Court for the District of Columbia\nCurrent Court\nU.S. District Court for the District of Columbia\nDate FiledMay 19, 2026Case Status\nActive\nCase NewsFilings/RulingsOriginal Court\nU.S. District Court for the District of Columbia\nCurrent Court\nU.S. District Court for the District of Columbia\nDate FiledMay 19, 2026Case Status\nActive\nCase Overview\nFIRE is suing the Department of Homeland Security and Immigration and Customs Enforcement over Freedom of Information Act requests about an ICE database of protesters DHS failed to respond to. In early 2026, DHS deployed thousands of ICE agents to carry out large-scale immigration enforcement operations. In response, people across the country organized protests and monitoring of immigration enforcement. As protests intensified, Trump administration “Border Czar” Tom Homan publicly claimed DHS would “create a database” of ICE protesters, “make them famous,” and inform their employers. At the same time, an ICE agent in Maine told an “ICE watcher” — a woman lawfully recording law enforcement activity — that he would “put her face” in such a database.Because the potential existence of this system would be deeply at odds with the free speech principles FIRE advocates for, FIRE filed three FOIA requests asking about the alleged database. However, DHS failed to respond during the FOIA’s required 20-day window. FIRE now challenges the agency’s failure to respond with the aim of compelling disclosure of responsive documents about the database. Whether this database exists is of great consequences because its existence would raise serious First Amendment concerns about chilling effects and retaliation for protected speech. If people believe they may be tracked for protesting ICE or lawfully filming agents, they may not choose to engage in those protected activities at all.\nCase Team\nAdam Steinbaugh\nSenior Attorney\nJacob Gaba\nLegal Fellow\nLitigation\nPolice Encounters\nPublic Records\n© 2026 Foundation for Individual Rights and ExpressionP.O. Box 40128Philadelphia, PA 19106fire@fire.org215-717-FIREFoundation for Individual Rights and Expression, FIRE, the flame logo, and Free Speech Makes Free People are registered trademarks of the Foundation for Individual Rights and Expression. All rights reserved.\nAbout UsContact UsCareersSubmit a CasePrivacy StatementTerms and Conditions\nFacebookTwitterInstagramYouTubeTikTok\nDonate\nShare\nShare this selection on Twitter\nShare this selection via email","content_cn":"主页\n案件\n分享\n通过电子邮件分享\n在Bluesky上分享\n在Twitter上分享\n在Facebook上分享\n打印\n\nFIRE诉国土安全部：ICE数据库《信息自由法》诉讼\n\n案件\n搜索所有案件\n\n案件概览\n\n案件概览\n原审法院\n美国哥伦比亚特区地区法院\n现审法院\n美国哥伦比亚特区地区法院\n立案日期：2026年5月19日\n案件状态\n审理中\n\n案件新闻\n文件/裁定\n原审法院\n美国哥伦比亚特区地区法院\n现审法院\n美国哥伦比亚特区地区法院\n立案日期：2026年5月19日\n案件状态\n审理中\n\n案件概览\n\nFIRE正在起诉国土安全部和移民及海关执法局（ICE），涉及其就一个ICE抗议者数据库提出的信息自由法请求；国土安全部未对这些请求作出回应。2026年初，国土安全部部署数千名ICE特工，开展大规模移民执法行动。作为回应，全国各地的人们组织了抗议活动，并监测移民执法。\n\n随着抗议活动升级，特朗普政府的“边境事务主管”Tom Homan公开声称，国土安全部将“建立一个数据库”记录ICE抗议者，“让他们出名”，并通知他们的雇主。与此同时，缅因州一名ICE特工告诉一名“ICE观察员”——一名依法记录执法活动的女性——他会把“她的脸”放入这样的数据库。\n\n由于这一系统可能存在，与FIRE所倡导的言论自由原则严重背离，FIRE提出了三项信息自由法请求，询问有关该数据库的情况。然而，国土安全部未能在《信息自由法》规定的20天期限内作出回应。FIRE现在就该机构未作出回应提出异议，目的是迫使其披露与该数据库有关的应答文件。\n\n该数据库是否存在具有重大影响，因为它的存在将引发有关寒蝉效应以及对受保护言论进行报复的严重第一修正案问题。如果人们认为自己可能因抗议ICE或合法拍摄特工而被跟踪，他们可能根本不会选择参与这些受保护的活动。\n\n案件团队\nAdam Steinbaugh\n高级律师\nJacob Gaba\n法律研究员\n\n诉讼\n警察接触\n公共记录\n\n© 2026个人权利与表达基金会\nP.O. Box 40128\nPhiladelphia, PA 19106\nfire@fire.org\n215-717-FIRE\n\n个人权利与表达基金会、FIRE、火焰标志以及“言论自由让人民自由”均为个人权利与表达基金会的注册商标。保留所有权利。\n\n关于我们\n联系我们\n招聘\n提交案件\n隐私声明\n条款与条件\n\nFacebook\nTwitter\nInstagram\nYouTube\nTikTok\n\n捐赠\n\n在Twitter上分享此内容\n通过电子邮件分享此内容","publish_source":"fire.org","publish_time":"2026-05-19T12:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3125","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部人员现身利伯蒂后，警探因发布移民权利梗图被解雇","title_en":"Detective fired for posting meme on immigration rights after Homeland Security seen in Liberty","summary_cn":"密苏里州克莱县警长办公室警探汤姆·布特科维奇因在Facebook评论中发布涉及移民权利的梗图被解雇。该评论出现在关于国土安全调查局（HSI）探员在利伯蒂El Potro墨西哥餐厅现身、多人被拘留的帖子下。梗图显示疑似特朗普持枪指向车外，配文暗示拉美裔美国人应感到恐惧。警长办公室认定其违反行为准则及成员言论、表达和社交网络政策，经专业标准调查后于2025年2月25日终止其雇佣关系。HSI未回应媒体询问。","summary_en":"Clay County Sheriff's Office detective Tom Butkovich was fired after posting a meme about immigration rights in a Facebook comment. The comment appeared under a post about Homeland Security Investigations (HSI) agents seen at El Potro Mexican Restaurant in Liberty, Missouri, where multiple people were taken into custody. The meme showed what appeared to be President Trump pointing a firearm from a vehicle, with text suggesting Hispanic Americans should be fearful. The sheriff's office found he violated conduct and social media policies and terminated his employment on Feb. 25, 2025, after a professional standards investigation. HSI did not respond to inquiries.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:03:30.341411+00:00","url":"https://www.firstalert4.com/2025/02/25/detective-fired-posting-meme-immigration-rights-after-homeland-security-seen-liberty","content":"Detective fired for posting meme on immigration rights after Homeland Security seen in LibertyFILE-- Clay County Sheriff's Office(Clay County Sheriff's Office)By Zoë ShrinerPublished: Feb. 25, 2025 at 1:01 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleKANSAS CITY, Mo. (KCTV) - Just over two weeks after a sheriff’s deputy was placed on leave for his alleged online conduct, it was announced that his employment has been terminated for violating employee standards agreements.According to the Clay County Sheriff’s Office, Deputy Tom Butkovich “violated [the office’s] Conduct and Member Speech, Expression and Social Networking policies” on Feb. 7, 2025, when he left a meme regarding immigration rights in a Facebook comment. The meme was a photo of what appeared to be President Donald Trump pointing a firearm out of a vehicle’s window. The text overlaying the photo indicated that Hispanic Americans should be fearful.The Member Speech, Expression and Social Networking policy the sheriff’s office cited explains that members of the department are “held to a higher standard than general members of the public.”“Members are cautioned that speech on or off-duty, made pursuant to their official duties, is not protected under the First Amendment,” the policy says in part.Butkovich’s meme was left on another user’s Facebook post regarding an incident earlier that day in Liberty, Missouri when Homeland Security Investigations (HSI) agents were seen at El Potro Mexican Restaurant. The restaurant’s manager said multiple people were taken into custody. HSI has not responded to either of KCTV5′s inquiries asking to confirm this information.After the incident at El Potro, photos and videos were circulated widely online, gaining hundreds of reshares and comments. Users began to point out that one of the commenters appeared to be Butkovich, as the profile had his name and headshot as its profile photo, and said the meme he used was not appropriate.PREVIOUS COVERAGE: Deputy on leave for alleged comment posted after Homeland Security seen in LibertySheriff Will Akin responded online stating that Butkovich had been placed on administrative leave and the next day, the Clay County Sheriff’s Office issued the following statement:“Our professional standards (some other agencies call them internal affairs) investigators will gather evidence and conduct interviews with the goal of determining whether the employee violated any of our policies or procedures. In this case, they will be looking at our Conduct policy and our Member Speech, Expression and Social Media policy. Their investigation could always lead them in other directions, too. Investigators also will work to determine whether it was actually the deputy who posted it or if someone happened to clone his account and do so.”Just over two weeks later, on Feb. 25, 2025, the sheriff’s office responded with the findings of their investigation, confirming that Butkovich’s employment was terminated.“The Professional Standards investigation into a meme posted on social media by a Clay County Sheriff’s Office detective on Feb. 7 has now concluded. The investigation found the detective violated our Conduct and Member Speech, Expression and Social Networking policies. Therefore, the detective’s employment has been terminated. As this is a personnel matter, no further information will be released.”ALSO READ: Kansas City federal employee speaks on anxiety, confusion at VACopyright 2025 KCTV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"因在“自由”事件后发布移民权利表情包而被解雇的侦探——克莱县警长办公室（克莱县警长办公室）\n作者：Zoë Shriner\n发布时间：2025年2月25日下午1:01（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n\n密苏里州堪萨斯城（KCTV）——一名警长副手因涉嫌网络行为被停职后仅两周多，现宣布其因违反员工标准协议而被解雇。\n\n据克莱县警长办公室称，副手Tom Butkovich于2025年2月7日在Facebook评论中留下了一张涉及移民权利的表情包，违反了该办公室的“行为规范”和“成员言论、表达及社交网络政策”。这张表情包是一张照片，照片中似乎是总统Donald Trump从一辆车的车窗伸出枪械。照片上的文字表明，西裔美国人应当感到害怕。\n\n警长办公室引用的“成员言论、表达及社交网络政策”解释说，部门成员“被要求达到高于普通公众成员的标准”。\n\n该政策部分内容写道：“成员须注意，在职或非在职期间，因履行其官方职责而发表的言论，不受第一修正案保护。”\n\nButkovich是在另一名用户的Facebook帖子下发布这张表情包的。该帖子涉及当天早些时候在密苏里州利伯蒂发生的一起事件，当时有人看到国土安全调查局（HSI）特工出现在El Potro墨西哥餐厅。餐厅经理表示，多人被拘留。HSI尚未回应KCTV5要求确认这一信息的两次询问。\n\nEl Potro事件发生后，照片和视频在网上广泛传播，获得数百次转发和评论。用户开始指出，其中一名评论者似乎是Butkovich，因为该个人资料使用了他的姓名和头像，并表示他使用的表情包并不恰当。\n\n此前报道：国土安全部门在利伯蒂出现后，副手因涉嫌发表评论而休假\n\n警长Will Akin在网上回应称，Butkovich已被行政停职。次日，克莱县警长办公室发表以下声明：\n\n“我们的专业标准（一些其他机构称之为内部事务）调查人员将收集证据并进行访谈，目标是确定该员工是否违反了我们的任何政策或程序。在本案中，他们将审查我们的行为规范以及成员言论、表达和社交媒体政策。他们的调查也可能将他们引向其他方向。调查人员还将努力确定，是否确实是这名副手发布了该内容，或者是否有人克隆了他的账户并进行了发布。”\n\n两周多后的2025年2月25日，警长办公室公布调查结果，确认Butkovich已被解雇。\n\n“关于克莱县警长办公室一名侦探于2月7日在社交媒体上发布表情包的专业标准调查现已结束。调查发现，该侦探违反了我们的行为规范以及成员言论、表达和社交网络政策。因此，该侦探已被解雇。由于这是人事事务，将不再发布更多信息。”\n\n另请阅读：堪萨斯城联邦雇员谈及在VA的焦虑与困惑\n\n版权2025 KCTV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"firstalert4.com","publish_time":"2025-02-25T19:01:20.899000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2068","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔会见圣路易斯执法部门","title_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel meets with St. Louis law enforcement","summary_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔在圣路易斯与联邦探员及地方执法领导人举行闭门会议，会后未接受媒体采访。参议员埃里克·施密特与FBI联合副局长安德鲁·贝利向记者介绍打击暴力犯罪的努力，称圣路易斯获得全国人均最多的常驻探员增派。官员公布“夏季高温”行动逮捕276人，并称FY25暴力犯罪项目逮捕545人，同比增71%。市长斯宾塞与警察局长特雷西受邀参会。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel met with federal agents and local law enforcement leaders in a closed-door session in St. Louis, and did not speak to media afterward. Senator Eric Schmitt and FBI Co-Deputy Director Andrew Bailey briefed reporters on combating violent crime, saying St. Louis is receiving the largest per capita increase of permanent agents in the country. Officials cited 276 arrests under Operation Summer Heat and 545 arrests in the FY25 violent crime program, up 71% year over year. Mayor Spencer and Police Chief Tracy attended.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:47:49.172947+00:00","url":"https://www.firstalert4.com/2025/11/22/fbi-director-kash-patel-meets-with-st-louis-law-enforcement","content":"FBI Director Kash Patel meets with St. Louis law enforcement By Lauren TragerPublished: Nov. 21, 2025 at 6:26 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleST. LOUIS, Mo. (First Alert 4) -FBI Director Kash Patel met with federal agents and local law enforcement leaders Friday in a closed-door session, but officials provided few details about what was discussed during the hours-long meeting.Patel did not speak to media after the session. Instead, two former Missouri attorneys general, U.S. Senator Eric Schmitt and FBI Co-Deputy Director Andrew Bailey, briefly addressed reporters about combating violent crime in St. Louis.“This is personal for me. This is my hometown. It’s where I still live. I want St. Louis to do well. I want people to feel safe,” Schmitt said.Schmitt said he was “really gratified that Director Kash Patel, who was here, gave a great briefing.”“We had an all-hands meeting. We met with local law enforcement,” Schmitt said.Over the summer, Schmitt announced a surge of new FBI agents to the St. Louis region, though officials have declined to specify exact numbers or locations.“Because of the commitment from this administration, St. Louis is receiving the largest per capita increase of permanent agents anywhere in the country,” Schmitt said.When asked to quantify how many agents are in the region and whether they are new or transferred from other areas, Bailey said they are “brand new agents that have come here and that continues.”“So not all of them are actually here yet, but it’s a kind of a continuing flow to move resources to St. Louis, which is a good thing,” Bailey said.Officials displayed statistics from an ongoing FBI campaign called Summer Heat, showing 276 arrests. However, they provided no details on how many resulted in charges or for what specific crimes.Bailey said the arrests were for “all violent crime.”In a release, Senator Schmitt’s office provided the following stats:545 arrests were made by FBI St. Louis as part of its Violent Crime program in FY25, a 71% increase from FY24.208 firearms were confiscated by FBI St. Louis in FY25, a 23% increase from FY24.As part of Operation Summer Heat, 2.6 kilograms of fentanyl, 848 grams of Methamphetamine, and 684 grams of cocaine were seized by FBI St. Louis, including smaller amounts of heroin, marijuana, ecstasy, and other illicit narcotics.Mayor Cara Spencer attended the meeting with Patel Friday. A spokesperson said it was “a roundtable discussion with law enforcement from around the region” and that Spencer “was pleased to share a St. Louisan perspective.”St. Louis Police Chief Robert Tracy was also invited to join regional law enforcement leaders for the meeting to “discuss a variety of topics,” according to a department spokesperson.“The St. Louis Metropolitan Police Department remains committed to working alongside local, state, and federal agencies to address violent crime and strengthen public safety across the region,” the spokesperson said.Bailey was also asked about his role regarding the release of the Epstein files. He said it had not come across his desk and could not comment otherwise.Copyright 2025 KMOV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"FBI局长Kash Patel会见圣路易斯执法部门\n作者：Lauren Trager\n发布时间：2025年11月21日下午6:26（中部标准时间）\n分享\n在Google上添加我们\n在Google上添加为首选来源\n密苏里州圣路易斯（First Alert 4）——FBI局长Kash Patel周五与联邦探员及地方执法部门领导人举行了闭门会议，但官员们没有透露这场持续数小时的会议讨论了什么细节。\n会议结束后，Patel没有向媒体发表讲话。相反，密苏里州两名前总检察长、美国参议员Eric Schmitt和FBI副局长Andrew Bailey短暂向记者介绍了打击圣路易斯暴力犯罪的情况。\nSchmitt说：“这对我来说是个人的事。这是我的家乡。我现在仍然住在那里。我希望圣路易斯发展良好。我希望人们感到安全。”\nSchmitt说，他“非常欣慰Patel局长来到这里并作了很好的简报”。\nSchmitt说：“我们召开了全员会议。我们会见了地方执法部门。”\n今年夏天，Schmitt宣布向圣路易斯地区增派FBI探员，但官员们拒绝说明确切人数或地点。\nSchmitt说：“由于本届政府的承诺，圣路易斯获得了全国任何地方人均规模最大的常驻探员增幅。”\n当被问及该地区有多少探员，以及他们是新招募的还是从其他地区调来的时，Bailey说，他们是“来到这里的全新探员，而且这一过程仍在继续”。\nBailey说：“所以他们并非全部已经到位，但这是一个持续向圣路易斯调配资源的过程，这是一件好事。”\n官员们展示了FBI一项名为“夏季热浪”的持续行动统计数据，显示已逮捕276人。然而，他们没有说明其中有多少人被提出指控，或涉及哪些具体罪行。\nBailey说，这些逮捕涉及“所有暴力犯罪”。\nSchmitt参议员办公室在一份新闻稿中提供了以下数据：\nFBI圣路易斯分局在2025财年作为其暴力犯罪项目的一部分逮捕545人，比2024财年增加71%。\nFBI圣路易斯分局在2025财年缴获208支枪械，比2024财年增加23%。\n作为“夏季热浪行动”的一部分，FBI圣路易斯分局缴获了2.6千克芬太尼、848克甲基苯丙胺和684克可卡因，此外还缴获少量海洛因、大麻、摇头丸和其他非法麻醉品。\n市长Cara Spencer周五参加了与Patel的会议。一名发言人称，这是“与该地区各地执法部门举行的圆桌讨论”，Spencer“很高兴分享圣路易斯人的观点”。\n据警察局发言人介绍，圣路易斯警察局长Robert Tracy也受邀与地区执法部门领导人一起参加会议，以“讨论各种议题”。\n该发言人说：“圣路易斯大都会警察局仍致力于与地方、州和联邦机构合作，处理暴力犯罪并加强整个地区的公共安全。”\nBailey还被问及其在公布爱泼斯坦档案方面的作用。他说，这件事尚未提交到他的办公桌上，因此无法发表评论。\n版权所有2025 KMOV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"firstalert4.com","publish_time":"2025-11-22T00:26:44.599000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1980","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部长承诺审查当地祖母案件","title_en":"Homeland Security secretary commits to reviewing local grandmother’s case","summary_cn":"国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在国会听证会上承诺审查密苏里州特洛伊市合法永久居民唐娜·休斯·布朗的案件。布朗自7月在芝加哥被ICE拘留后一直关押在肯塔基州监狱，其丈夫、退伍军人吉姆·布朗发起释放呼吁。民主党众议员马加齐纳质询称布朗仅十余年前有两项开空头支票的轻罪记录，诺姆最终同意审查该案及受移民执法影响的其他退伍军人相关案件。","summary_en":"Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem committed at a congressional hearing to reviewing the case of Donna Hughes Brown, a lawful permanent resident from Troy, Missouri, detained by ICE since July and held in a Kentucky jail. Her husband, combat veteran Jim Brown, campaigned for her release. Democratic Rep. Magaziner pressed Noem, noting Brown's only criminal history was two misdemeanor bad-check convictions over a decade ago. Noem agreed to review the case and other veterans' cases affected by immigration enforcement.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:54:50.766722+00:00","url":"https://www.firstalert4.com/2025/12/12/homeland-security-secretary-commits-reviewing-local-grandmothers-case","content":"Homeland Security secretary commits to reviewing local grandmother’s case By Lauren TragerPublished: Dec. 11, 2025 at 6:55 PM CSTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleWASHINGTON, Mo. (First Alert 4) -Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem committed Thursday to reviewing the case of Donna Hughes Brown, a local woman who has been detained by ICE since July despite being a legal resident.Brown, a Troy, Missouri resident, came to the United States nearly 50 years ago when she was 11 years old. She is a legal permanent resident but not a U.S. citizen.The case gained national attention after her husband Jim Brown, a combat veteran, launched a campaign for her release. Brown has been held at a jail in Kentucky since her July detention in Chicago.During a congressional hearing Thursday, Rhode Island Democratic Rep. Seth Magaziner confronted Noem about the case.“Because of you, Jim’s wife Donna has been in prison for the last 4 months,” Magaziner said.Magaziner pressed Noem on why Brown remains detained, noting her only criminal history consists of two misdemeanor convictions for writing bad checks more than 10 years ago.“Now what possible explanation can there be for locking up his wife for 4 months when she has committed no crime other than writing a couple of bad checks for $80?” Magaziner asked.Noem initially defended the enforcement action, saying it was not her job to “pick and choose which laws in this country get enforced.”But when Magaziner asked her to commit to reviewing the case, Noem agreed.“I will review the case,” Noem said.Noem also committed to reviewing cases of other U.S. veterans impacted by immigration enforcement at Magaziner’s request.“There are many problems with your leadership, but the biggest problem is this, you don’t know how to tell the difference between the good guys and the bad guys,” Magaziner said.ICE has previously stated that people in the country lawfully who have not committed crimes have no reason to fear enforcement actions.Brown is scheduled for another hearing next week. Homeland Security has not yet responded to requests about how the case review will be conducted.Copyright 2025 KMOV. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部部长承诺审查当地祖母的案件\n作者：Lauren Trager\n发布时间：2025年12月11日美国中部标准时间下午6:55\n分享\n在 Google 上添加我们\n在 Google 上将其添加为首选来源\n\n密苏里州华盛顿市（First Alert 4）——国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆周四承诺，将审查当地女性唐娜·休斯·布朗的案件。布朗自7月以来一直被美国移民和海关执法局（ICE）拘留，尽管她是合法居民。\n\n来自密苏里州特洛伊的布朗近50年前、11岁时来到美国。她是合法永久居民，但不是美国公民。\n\n在其身为退伍军人的丈夫吉姆·布朗发起要求释放她的行动后，该案获得全国关注。布朗自7月在芝加哥被拘留后，一直被关押在肯塔基州的一所监狱。\n\n在周四的国会听证会上，罗得岛州民主党众议员塞思·马加齐纳就此案质问诺姆。\n\n“因为你，吉姆的妻子唐娜在过去4个月里一直被关在监狱里，”马加齐纳说。\n\n马加齐纳追问诺姆，为何布朗仍被拘留，并指出她唯一的犯罪记录是10多年前因开空头支票而被判两项轻罪。\n\n“当她除了开了几张80美元的空头支票以外没有犯过任何罪时，把他的妻子关押4个月，究竟有什么可能的解释？”马加齐纳问道。\n\n诺姆起初为执法行动辩护，称“选择性决定执行本国哪些法律”不是她的职责。\n\n但当马加齐纳要求她承诺审查此案时，诺姆同意了。\n\n“我会审查此案，”诺姆说。\n\n应马加齐纳要求，诺姆还承诺审查其他受移民执法影响的美国退伍军人的案件。\n\n“你的领导力存在许多问题，但最大的问题是：你不知道如何区分好人和坏人，”马加齐纳说。\n\nICE此前曾表示，合法在美且未犯罪的人无需害怕执法行动。\n\n布朗定于下周再次出庭。国土安全部尚未回应有关将如何开展案件审查的问询。\n\n版权所有 © 2025 KMOV。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"firstalert4.com","publish_time":"2025-12-12T00:55:09.143000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3282","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI寻找可能途经佛罗里达的逃犯夫妇下落","title_en":"FBI seeking whereabouts of fugitive couple who may travel to or through Florida | firstcoastnews.com","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局堪萨斯城分局宣布，正在寻找一对夫妇瓦西里·萨瓦和奥尼塔·罗斯塔斯的下落。两人于2024年1月31日在堪萨斯州联邦地区法院被控共谋跨州运输被盗财产，涉嫌以分散注意力手法盗窃多家珠宝店。调查人员认为他们可能使用多个化名，活动范围或涉及加州、得州、佛州、马里兰州和弗吉尼亚州。","summary_en":"The FBI's Kansas City Division announced it is seeking the whereabouts of Vasile Sava and Onita Rostas, a married couple charged in the U.S. District Court for the District of Kansas on Jan. 31, 2024, with conspiracy to commit interstate transportation of stolen property. They are alleged to have targeted jewelry businesses using distraction thefts. Investigators believe they may use aliases and operate in California, Texas, Florida, Maryland and Virginia.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:33:20.509282+00:00","url":"https://www.firstcoastnews.com/article/news/regional/florida/fbi-seeking-the-whereabouts-of-fugitive-couple-who-may-travel-to-or-through-florida/77-a3013363-886b-43d1-9505-3ee89f05d363","content":"Florida\nFBI seeking whereabouts of 2 fugitives 'who may travel to or through Florida'\nThe FBI says arrest warrants have been issued for the couple, charging them with \"conspiracy to commit interstate transportation of stolen property.\"\nCredit: Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation is seeking the whereabouts of Onita Rostas (left) and Vasile Sava (right).\nAuthor: Malcolm Harvey, First Coast News (On Your Side)\nPublished: 1:40 PM EST December 19, 2024\nUpdated: 2:05 PM EST December 19, 2024\nJACKSONVILLE, Fla. — The Federal Bureau of Investigation's (FBI) Kansas City Division announced Thursday it is seeking the whereabouts of a married couple who the agency says are \"two wanted fugitives.\"\nThe FBI has identified the two individuals as Vasile Sava and Onita Rostas, according to a news release. Authorities say arrest warrants were issued for them in the United States District Court, District of Kansas on Jan. 31, 2024, as both \"were charged with conspiracy to commit interstate transportation of stolen property.\"\nThe release states it is alleged that Sava and Rostas, among others known and unknown, targeted multiple jewelry businesses.\n\"During these targeted robberies, it is alleged that the individuals entered the respective jewelry store in groups of two or more, distracted and/or separated the assisting employee or employees, while one or more of the other individuals would remove, conceal, ultimately exit the business with items of jewelry that were displayed for purchase in a practice known as a slight-of-hand distraction theft,\" the release says.\nInvestigators believe Sava and Rostas may be using a variety of aliases and may be living and/or operating in \"various areas\" across the country including California, Texas, Florida, Maryland and Virginia.\nCredit: Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)\nThe Federal Bureau of Investigation is seeking the whereabouts of Onita Rostas (left) and Vasile Sava (right).\nClose Ad\nTo stream FCN on your phone, you need the FCN app.\nDownload the FCN app\nMore Videos\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nNext up in 5\nExample video title will go here for this video\nIn Other News\nOne in custody after shots fired at Miami International Airport\nBefore You Leave, Check This Out","content_cn":"佛罗里达州\nFBI寻找两名“可能前往或途经佛罗里达州”的逃犯的下落\nFBI表示，已对这对夫妇签发逮捕令，指控他们“共谋实施州际运输赃物罪”。\n图片来源：联邦调查局（FBI）\n联邦调查局正在寻找Onita Rostas（左）和Vasile Sava（右）的下落。\n作者：Malcolm Harvey，First Coast News（为您服务）\n发布时间：2024年12月19日美国东部时间下午1:40\n更新时间：2024年12月19日美国东部时间下午2:05\n佛罗里达州杰克逊维尔——联邦调查局（FBI）堪萨斯城分局周四宣布，正在寻找一对已婚夫妇的下落；该机构称两人为“两名被通缉的逃犯”。\n根据新闻稿，FBI确认这两人为Vasile Sava和Onita Rostas。有关部门表示，美国堪萨斯州联邦地区法院于2024年1月31日对他们签发逮捕令，两人均被控“共谋实施州际运输赃物罪”。\n新闻稿称，据称Sava和Rostas与其他身份已知或未知人员，曾以多家珠宝企业为目标。\n新闻稿称：“据称，在这些有针对性的盗窃中，涉案人员以两人或以上的团体进入相应珠宝店，分散和／或支开提供协助的一名或多名员工；与此同时，其他一名或多名人员会取走、藏匿，最终带着陈列待售的珠宝离开商店。这种做法被称为‘障眼法分散注意力盗窃’。”\n调查人员认为，Sava和Rostas可能使用多种化名，并可能在全国“多个地区”居住和／或活动，包括加利福尼亚州、得克萨斯州、佛罗里达州、马里兰州和弗吉尼亚州。\n图片来源：联邦调查局（FBI）\n联邦调查局正在寻找Onita Rostas（左）和Vasile Sava（右）的下落。\n关闭广告\n要在手机上观看FCN，您需要FCN应用程序。\n下载FCN应用程序\n更多视频\n5秒后播放\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n5秒后播放\n此视频的示例视频标题将显示在这里\n其他新闻\n迈阿密国际机场发生枪击事件后，一人被拘留\n离开前，看看这些内容","publish_source":"firstcoastnews.com","publish_time":"2024-12-19T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3030","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"印度教价值观如何塑造FBI局长卡什·帕特尔的历程","title_en":"How Hindu values have shaped FBI chief Kash Patel’s journey","summary_cn":"文章介绍美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔如何展现其印度教价值观。帕特尔分享了一篇关于其印度教成长背景的文章，称父母教导的勤奋、尊重和教育等价值观影响其世界观。他宣誓就职时使用《薄伽梵歌》，在参议院确认听证会上向父母行触足礼并问候“Jai Shri Krishna”。","summary_en":"The article examines how FBI Director Kash Patel has displayed his Hindu values. Patel shared an article about his Hindu upbringing, saying values of hard work, respect and education shaped his worldview. He took his oath of office on the Bhagavad Gita, touched his parents' feet during his Senate confirmation hearing and greeted them with 'Jai Shri Krishna.'","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:17:45.987359+00:00","url":"https://www.firstpost.com/explainers/kash-patel-fbi-director-hindu-values-13874313.html","content":"How Hindu values have shaped FBI chief Kash Patel’s journeyWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionLifestyleBusinessTechWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionLifestyleBusinessTechTrendingTata Sons shakeupTrump plane switchKaroline Leavitt resignsAir India pilot dope rowLindsay Clancy murder trialAdvertisement First AI HomeLive TVFirst AISectionsWorldEntertainmentExplainersCricketSportsOpinionIndiaTechAutoLifestyleHealthBusinessVideosImpact ShortsWeb StoriesShowsVantageFirstpost AmericaFirstpost AfricaFirst SportsSpotlightLive TVEventsFIFA World CupUnion BudgetIndependence DayDelhi Elections 2025How Hindu values have shaped FBI chief Kash Patel’s journeyFBI Director Kash Patel has time and again displayed his Hindu values and discussed their influence on his leadership. Now, the Indian-American has shared an article about his personal background, which states that he was raised in a traditional Hindu household, where these teachings shaped his perspective on life and work AdvertisementThe FBI director shared an article which discusses his Hindu upbringing. Reuters/File Photo\nFP Explainers|Mar 25, 2025, 15:04:42 ISTKash Patel has not been one to shy away from displaying his Hindu values time and again.The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) director recently shared an article on social media which discusses his Hindu upbringing and its influence on his leadership approach.ALSO READ | Oath on Bhagavad Gita, ‘Jai Shri Krishna’ greetings: How FBI chief Kash Patel embraces his Indian rootsThe article, which explores his personal beliefs, has since gone viral, particularly within Indian-American communities.Earlier, Patel made headlines when he took his oath as FBI Director on the Bhagavad Gita, a sacred Hindu scripture, and touched his parents’ feet during his US Senate confirmation hearing.AdvertisementBut what was the latest article about? How has the FBI Director displayed his Hindu values in the past?We will take a look:What did the article say?The article, titled \"FBI Director Kash Patel: A Hindu Warrior in Washington’s Political Battlefield,\" was published by the Chicago-based news website India Tribune.It opens with: “Kashyap ‘Kash’ Patel, 45, a Hindu and the son of Indian immigrants, now holds the most powerful law enforcement position in the United States: Director of the FBI.”More from Explainers<em>Earlier, Patel made headlines when he took his oath as FBI Director on the Bhagavad Gita. Reuters/File Photo</em>The article delves into Patel’s personal background and traces his family’s journey. His father, Pramod Patel, fled Uganda in 1972 during Idi Amin’s brutal regime. After spending some time in India, he eventually settled in the United States. Meanwhile, Patel’s mother, Anjana Patel, was Tanzanian.According to the article, Patel was raised in a traditional Hindu household, and these teachings shaped his perspective and approach to both life and work.“Kash’s upbringing was rooted in the values of Hinduism - hard work, respect, and education - values that have influenced his worldview. His parents taught him to respect all religions, embodying the message of universal tolerance famously delivered by Swami Vivekananda in his 1893 speech at the World Parliament of Religions in Chicago,\" it read.AdvertisementThe FBI director discussed the significance of dharma (righteous duty), karma (action with accountability), and seva (selfless service), principles that guide his role in public service.Patel has pledged to “restore justice and fairness, aiming to fix an FBI that has been criticised for its role in an American criminal justice system,” the article added.Earlier in the day, Patel gave his first television interview as FBI Director. Speaking to Fox News, he addressed several key issues, including rising violent crime and the fentanyl crisis in the United States.He expressed concern that violent crime is “out of control” and added that the FBI must take stronger action to tackle the problem.He also criticised the previous administration for failing to address these challenges and stated that the FBI now has new priorities to confront them. Patel assured that the agency is fully committed to adopting a more proactive approach.How Kash Patel embraces his Indian rootsFrom greeting people with Jai Shri Krishna to seeking his parents’ blessings, Kashyap ‘Kash’ Patel has consistently embraced his Indian heritage.AdvertisementWhen Patel was sworn in as FBI Director, he took his oath on the Bhagavad Gita, instead of the Bible. Attorney General Pam Bondi administered the oath using the Bhagavad Gita.Patel’s girlfriend, Alexis Wilkins, held the scripture as he took the oath in the Indian Treaty Room at the Eisenhower Executive Office Building, with his family present.Following the ceremony, Patel spoke about fulfilling the American dream, stating that a “first-generation Indian is about to lead the law enforcement agency of the greatest nation on earth.”During his US Senate confirmation hearing, Patel introduced his parents before the Senate Judiciary Committee and greeted them with ‘Jai Shri Krishna’.A viral video captured the moment he bowed to touch his parents’ feet before the proceedings commenced. Patel expressed deep gratitude to his family for travelling from India to attend the hearing.“I like to welcome my father and my mother Anjana who are sitting here today. They travelled to get here from India. My sister is also here. She also travelled the oceans just to be with me here today. It means the world that you guys are here. Jai Shri Krishna,” he said.Kash Patel’s connection to IndiaPatel was born on February 25, 1980, in Garden City, New York, to Gujarati parents.According to him, his mother is originally from Tanzania and pursued her studies in India, as did his father. The couple married in India before eventually settling in New York, where Patel was born.<em>Kashyap ‘Kash’ Patel has consistently embraced his Indian heritage. Reuters/File Photo</em>He completed his undergraduate studies at the University of Richmond before obtaining a Juris Doctor from Pace University School of Law.Although he was born and raised in the United States, Patel has frequently spoken about his Indian heritage and its influence on his values and professional path.While he has ancestral roots in India, his career has been primarily centred on US national security, intelligence, and law enforcement.With inputs from agenciesHandpicked stories, in your inboxGlobal stories. Indian perspective. Zero noise.Subscribe NowNo Spam. Unsubscribe Any Time.TagsFBIFirst Published:Mar 25, 2025, 15:04:42 ISTHomeExplainerskash patel fbi director hindu valuesAdvertisementAdvertisementTrending StoriesWhat are the disputed Kuril Islands that Putin visited, triggering Japan's protest?Russian President Vladimir Putin’s visit to the disputed Kuril Islands has triggered a sharp protest from Japan, reviving a decades-old territorial dispute. His appearance on Iturup comes amid growing Russian militarisation, strained Tokyo-Moscow ties and shifting security alignments involving China and North Korea11 min readIs India’s data centre boom coming at the cost of the environment?India is building data centres rapidly to support cloud computing, digital services, and AI. The spurt in such facilities is driving up demand for electricity, water, and land. The ecological impact will depend on where facilities are built, how they are powered and how they are cooled 7 min readKaroline Leavitt to leave White House Press Secretary role: Who could replace her?Karoline Leavitt is set to leave her role as White House Press Secretary at the end of August, just months before the 2026 US midterm elections. Trump said she will become an outside adviser. Potential successors include Anna Kelly, Steven Cheung, Tricia McLaughlin, Jason Miller and Alina Habba8 min readWho is Gautam Rangarajan, the ex-BBC employee hired by UK PM Andy Burnham as expert adviser?UK PM Andy Burnham has appointed Indian-origin strategist Gautam Rangarajan to the newly created role of Expert Adviser on Structure and Process. The British PM is looking to use Rangarajan’s 30 years of experience at the BBC to bring about transformation in the government3 min readJournalist says Imran Khan is dead, then Pak Army issues a rare response. What’s going on?Pakistan’s military has denied viral rumours that jailed former Prime Minister Imran Khan died in Rawalpindi’s Adiala Jail. The remark came after an explosive claim by Pakistani journalist Wajahat Saeed Khan, who later walked back on it4 min readAdvertisementAdvertisementUp NextAbout FirstpostLatest NewsX open-sources its ranking algorithm, lets users check account-level impactsUK hits 38.1°C, its hottest day of 2026 as extreme heat grips EuropeUttarakhand tunnel accident: 3 workers feared trapped, 16 rescued after water, debris flood Pipalkoti sitePassenger train derails near UK’s Lewes, rescue operation onGoogle launches Gemini 3.7 Flash with stronger coding and agent capabilitiesUS can maintain Iran naval blockade ‘indefinitely’, Hegseth says as war drags onUkraine proposes Black Sea truce with Russia as attacks threaten grain exports, global food suppliesJaishankar holds 'productive conversation' with Liberian FM Nyanti, congratulates her on opening of new embassy in IndiaCategoriesWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionSportsCricketTechnologyEntertainmentPhotostoriesLifestyleAutoBusinessVideosWebstoriesNETWORK18 SITESNews18Money ControlCNBC TV18Forbes IndiaAdvertise with usSitemapContact Us Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Terms Of Use Copyright @ 2026. Firstpost - All Rights Reserved.HomeVideosFirst AIQuick ReadsShorts","content_cn":"印度教价值观如何塑造了联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔的人生历程世界印度解读观点生活方式商业科技世界印度解读观点生活方式商业科技热门话题塔塔集团重组特朗普专机更换卡罗琳·莱维特辞职印度航空飞行员涉毒争议林赛·克兰西谋杀案审判广告 首个AI首页直播电视首个AI栏目世界娱乐解读板球体育观点印度科技汽车生活方式健康商业视频影响力短片网络故事节目VantageFirstpost AmericaFirstpost AfricaFirst SportsSpotlight直播电视活动国际足联世界杯联邦预算独立日德里选举2025印度教价值观如何塑造了联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔的人生历程联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔一次又一次地展现他的印度教价值观，并讨论这些价值观对其领导方式的影响。如今，这位印度裔美国人分享了一篇关于其个人背景的文章，文章称他在一个传统的印度教家庭中长大，这些教诲塑造了他对生活和工作的看法 广告联邦调查局局长分享了一篇讨论其印度教成长经历的文章。路透社/资料照片\nFP解读|2025年3月25日15:04:42（印度标准时间）卡什·帕特尔从未回避一次又一次地展现自己的印度教价值观。联邦调查局（FBI）局长近日在社交媒体上分享了一篇文章，讨论他的印度教成长经历及其对其领导方式的影响。另请阅读 | 以《博伽梵歌》宣誓、“Jai Shri Krishna”问候：联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔如何拥抱印度根源这篇探讨其个人信仰的文章此后在社交媒体上走红，尤其是在印度裔美国人社区中。此前，帕特尔在联邦调查局局长宣誓时手按《博伽梵歌》——印度教神圣经典，并在美国参议院确认听证会上触摸父母的脚，因此登上头条。广告但这篇最新文章讲了什么？联邦调查局局长过去如何展现他的印度教价值观？我们来看看：文章说了什么？这篇题为《联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔：华盛顿政治战场上的印度教战士》的文章由总部位于芝加哥的新闻网站《印度论坛报》发表。文章开头写道：“45岁的卡夏普·‘卡什’·帕特尔是一名印度教徒，也是印度移民的儿子，如今担任美国最具权力的执法职位：联邦调查局局长。”更多解读<em>此前，帕特尔在联邦调查局局长宣誓时手按《博伽梵歌》。路透社/资料照片</em>文章深入介绍了帕特尔的个人背景，并追溯了其家族的经历。他的父亲普拉莫德·帕特尔于1972年在伊迪·阿明残暴统治期间逃离乌干达。在印度度过一段时间后，他最终定居美国。与此同时，帕特尔的母亲安贾娜·帕特尔来自坦桑尼亚。文章称，帕特尔在一个传统的印度教家庭中长大，这些教诲塑造了他对生活和工作的看法与方式。“卡什的成长根植于印度教的价值观——勤奋、尊重和教育——这些价值观影响了他的世界观。他的父母教导他尊重所有宗教，体现了斯瓦米·维韦卡南达在1893年芝加哥世界宗教议会演讲中著名宣扬的普遍宽容理念，”文章写道。广告联邦调查局局长谈到了达摩（正义的职责）、业（对行为负责）和奉献服务（无私服务）的重要意义，这些原则指导着他在公共服务中的角色。帕特尔承诺“恢复正义与公平，旨在\n“修复一个因其在美国刑事司法体系中的作用而受到批评的联邦调查局（FBI）”，文章补充道。\n\n当天早些时候，帕特尔接受了担任FBI局长以来的首次电视采访。他在接受福克斯新闻采访时谈到了几个关键问题，包括美国日益严重的暴力犯罪和芬太尼危机。\n\n他表示担忧，称暴力犯罪已经“失控”，并补充说，FBI必须采取更有力的行动来解决这一问题。\n\n他还批评前任政府未能应对这些挑战，并表示FBI如今有了新的优先事项来处理这些问题。帕特尔保证，该机构完全致力于采取更加积极主动的方式。\n\n卡什·帕特尔如何拥抱自己的印度根源\n\n从用“Jai Shri Krishna”（胜利属于奎师那）向人们问候，到寻求父母的祝福，卡什亚普·“卡什”·帕特尔始终拥抱自己的印度传统。\n\n广告\n\n帕特尔宣誓就任FBI局长时，没有以《圣经》而是以《博伽梵歌》作为宣誓依据。司法部长帕姆·邦迪使用《博伽梵歌》主持了宣誓仪式。\n\n帕特尔的女友亚历克西斯·威尔金斯在他于艾森豪威尔行政办公大楼的印度条约室宣誓时，手捧这部经文，他的家人也在场。\n\n仪式结束后，帕特尔谈到实现美国梦，并表示，“一个印度第一代移民即将领导这个地球上最伟大国家的执法机构。”\n\n在美国参议院确认听证会上，帕特尔向参议院司法委员会介绍了他的父母，并用“Jai Shri Krishna”向他们问候。\n\n一段走红网络的视频记录下了他在程序开始前俯身触摸父母双脚的瞬间。帕特尔对家人从印度赶来参加听证会表达了深深的感激。\n\n“我想欢迎我的父亲和母亲安贾娜，他们今天坐在这里。他们从印度长途跋涉来到这里。我的姐姐也在这里。她也跨越海洋，只为今天陪在我身边。你们能来到这里，对我来说意义重大。Jai Shri Krishna。”他说。\n\n卡什·帕特尔与印度的联系\n\n帕特尔于1980年2月25日出生于纽约州加登城，父母是古吉拉特人。\n\n据他介绍，他的母亲原籍坦桑尼亚，后来像他的父亲一样在印度求学。两人在印度结婚，最终定居纽约，帕特尔便出生在那里。\n\n<em>卡什亚普·“卡什”·帕特尔始终拥抱自己的印度传统。路透社/档案照片</em>\n\n他在里士满大学完成本科课程，随后获得佩斯大学法学院法学博士学位。\n\n尽管出生并成长于美国，帕特尔经常谈论自己的印度传统，以及它对其价值观和职业道路的影响。\n\n虽然他的祖先根源在印度，但他的职业生涯主要集中于美国国家安全、情报和执法领域。\n\n据通讯社报道\n\n精心挑选的故事，送到你的收件箱\n\n全球故事。印度视角。零噪音。\n\n立即订阅\n\n无垃圾邮件。随时取消订阅\n\n标签\n\nFBI\n\n首次发布：2025年3月25日，印度标准时间15:04:42\n\n首页\n\n解释\n\n卡什·帕特尔 FBI 局长 印度教价值观\n\n广告\n\n广告\n\n热门故事\n\n什么是普京到访并引发日本抗议的有争议的千岛群岛？\n\n俄罗斯总统弗拉基米尔·普京访问有争议的千岛群岛，引发日本强烈抗议，使这场持续数十年的领土争端重新浮出水面。他现身伊图鲁普岛之际，俄罗斯军事化程度不断加深，关系日益紧张。\n东京—莫斯科关系及涉及中国和朝鲜的不断变化的安全结盟\n11分钟阅读\n印度的数据中心热潮是否正以环境为代价？\n印度正在迅速建设数据中心，以支持云计算、数字服务和人工智能。这类设施的激增推高了对电力、水和土地的需求。生态影响将取决于设施建在哪里、如何供电以及如何冷却\n7分钟阅读\n卡罗琳·莱维特将离任白宫新闻秘书：谁可能接替她？\n卡罗琳·莱维特预计将在8月底离开白宫新闻秘书一职，距离2026年美国中期选举仅数月。特朗普称她将成为外部顾问。潜在继任者包括安娜·凯利、史蒂文·张、特里西娅·麦克劳克林、杰森·米勒和阿丽娜·哈巴\n8分钟阅读\n谁是高塔姆·兰加拉詹？这名前BBC员工被英国首相安迪·伯纳姆聘为专家顾问\n英国首相安迪·伯纳姆任命印度裔战略顾问高塔姆·兰加拉詹担任新设立的结构与流程专家顾问一职。这位英国首相希望利用兰加拉詹在BBC积累的30年经验，推动政府转型\n3分钟阅读\n记者称伊姆兰·汗已死亡，随后巴基斯坦军方罕见回应。究竟发生了什么？\n巴基斯坦军方否认了有关被监禁的前总理伊姆兰·汗在拉瓦尔品第阿迪亚拉监狱死亡的网络传言。此前，巴基斯坦记者瓦贾哈特·赛义德·汗提出了这一爆炸性说法，后来又收回了这一说法\n4分钟阅读\n广告\n广告\n接下来\n关于Firstpost\n最新消息\nX开放其排名算法，允许用户查看对账户层面的影响\n英国气温达到38.1°C，成为2026年最热的一天，极端高温席卷欧洲\n北阿坎德邦隧道事故：洪水、碎石冲入皮帕尔科蒂现场后，3名工人恐被困，16人获救\n客运列车在英国刘易斯附近脱轨，救援行动正在进行\n谷歌推出Gemini 3.7 Flash，编码和智能体能力更强\n赫格塞思称，随着战争拖延，美国可以“无限期”维持对伊朗的海上封锁\n乌克兰提议与俄罗斯在黑海停火，袭击威胁谷物出口和全球粮食供应\nJaishankar与利比里亚外交部长Nyanti进行了“富有成效的交谈”，祝贺她在印度开设新使馆\n类别\n世界\n印度\n解释\n观点\n体育\n板球\n科技\n娱乐\n图片故事\n生活方式\n汽车\n商业\n视频\n网络故事\nNETWORK18网站\nNews18\nMoney Control\nCNBC TV18\n福布斯印度\n与我们刊登广告\n网站地图\n联系我们\n隐私政策\nCookie政策\n使用条款\n版权@2026。Firstpost—保留所有权利。\n首页\n视频\nFirst AI\n快速阅读\nShorts","publish_source":"firstpost.com","publish_time":"2025-03-25T15:04:42+05:30"}},{"id":"news-3397","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI突袭选举博彩平台Polymarket首席执行官住所并查扣设备","title_en":"FBI raids house of election betting platform Polymarket's CEO Shayne Coplan, seizes devices","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局突袭了选举博彩平台Polymarket首席执行官Shayne Coplan的住所，查扣其手机等电子设备。报道称，FBI与纽约南区联邦检察官办公室正就Coplan是否违反2022年和解协议展开刑事调查，该协议要求Polymarket停止向美国用户提供博彩服务并缴纳140万美元罚款。Coplan在X上回应称此举是政治报复，强调平台保持无党派立场。","summary_en":"The FBI raided the home of Polymarket CEO Shayne Coplan and seized electronic devices including his cell phone. The New York Times reported the raid relates to a criminal investigation into whether Coplan violated a 2022 settlement requiring Polymarket to stop offering betting services to US users and pay a $1.4 million fine. Coplan called the raid a political vendetta on X, saying Polymarket remains committed to being non-partisan.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:41:05.369473+00:00","url":"https://www.firstpost.com/world/fbi-raids-house-of-election-betting-platform-polymarkets-ceo-shayne-coplan-seizes-devices-13835116.html","content":"FBI raids house of election betting platform Polymarket's CEO Shayne Coplan, seizes devicesWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionLifestyleBusinessFlauntWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionLifestyleBusinessFlauntTrendingNepal flash floodsPM Modi in Central AsiaLake Ontario rowChaTTJBMohan Bhagwat in NYCAdvertisement First AI HomeLive TVFirst AISectionsWorldEntertainmentExplainersCricketSportsOpinionIndiaTechAutoLifestyleHealthBusinessVideosImpact ShortsShowsVantageFirstpost AmericaFirstpost AfricaFirst SportsSpotlightThe SpendPlanet PulseLive TVEventsFIFA World CupUnion BudgetIndependence DayDelhi Elections 2025FBI raids house of election betting platform Polymarket's CEO Shayne Coplan, seizes devicesThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) is investigating whether election betting platform Polymarket violated a 2022 settlement by allowing betting for US users AdvertisementThe FBI is investigating the alleged involvement of Indian nationals in the assassination case of a US national. (Photo: Reuters)FP Staff|Nov 14, 2024, 15:16:37 ISTThe Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) on Wednesday raided the house of betting platform Polymarket's CEO Shayne Coplan.In the run-up to the Election Day, Polymarket predicted Republican nominee Donald Trump's victory over Vice President Kamala Harris.The FBI seized electronic devices from Coplan's home, including his cell phone, according to The New York Times.While the FBI has not formally commented on the case so far, The Times reported sources as saying that the raid was related to an alleged violation of agreement that Coplan had signed in 2022 to disallow political betting in the United States.Meanwhile, Coplan has dubbed the raid a political vendetta. In a post on X (formerly Twitter), he said the raid was a \"last-ditch effort\" to go after opponent's supporters.AdvertisementWhat is case against Polymarket CEO Shayne Coplan?The FBI and US attorney's office for the South District of New York are pursuing a criminal investigation into Coplan's alleged violation of a 2022 agreement, according to The Times.In 2022, Polymarket agreed to stop providing betting services to US users and paid a $1.4 million fine. Now, Polymarket appears in violation of the pact.The ongoing investigation appears to be focussed on whether Coplan ran Polymarket as an unlicensed commodities exchange, allowing users in the United States to place bets in violation of a settlement with the US government, according to The Times.More from WorldHowever, users can access betting via virtual private networks (VPNs)'It's disgusting'In a post on X, Coplan projected himself as a victim of a plot by political opponents.Coplain said, \"It’s discouraging that the current administration would seek a last-ditch effort to go after companies they deem to be associated with political opponents.\"Coplan further said that Polymarket has been, and will forever be, committed to being non-partisan.\"We are deeply committed to being non-partisan, and today is no different, but the incumbts should do some self-reflecting and recognize that taking a more pro-business, pro-startup approach may be what would have changed their fate this election,\" said Coplain.AdvertisementHandpicked stories, in your inboxGlobal stories. Indian perspective. Zero noise.Subscribe NowNo Spam. Unsubscribe Any Time.TagsUnited States of AmericaFirst Published:Nov 14, 2024, 15:14:26 ISTHomeWorldfbi raids house of election betting platform polymarkets ceo shayne coplan seizes devicesAdvertisementAdvertisementTrending StoriesNepal floods: 149 Indian nationals rescued as death toll rises to 788, over 2,500 missingIndia has rescued 149 nationals from flood-hit Nepal as the death toll climbed to 788, with more than 2,500 people still missing on the fifth day of the devastating disaster.1 min readRussia submits bid for India’s ₹ 50,000-crore deal to buy 5 more S-400 squadrons: ReportThe move comes months after Operation Sindoor, during which the Russian-made system proved highly effective against Pakistani aerial threats.2 min read‘Pretty reclusive, doesn’t go out’: Why Barron Trump keeps low profile amid Iran-linked threatDonald Trump’s youngest son, Barron Trump, has been keeping a low profile amid heightened security concerns, with a report describing the 20-year-old as “pretty reclusive” as threats against the US president and his family continue.3 min readUkraine’s new defence chief seeks early EU loan to plug $27 billion war budget gapDefence Minister Yevhenii Khmara said Kyiv will present allies with a clear war plan and seek early access to part of an EU loan as Ukraine faces mounting military funding needs.\n2 min readNasa launches $4.3 billion Roman Space Telescope to explore universe’s biggest mysteriesSpaceX launched Nasa's $4.3 billion Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope on Sunday aboard a Falcon Heavy rocket from the Kennedy Space Center in Florida2 min readAdvertisementAdvertisementUp NextAbout FirstpostLatest NewsNepal floods: 149 Indian nationals rescued as death toll rises to 788, over 2,500 missingPM Modi arrives in Kyrgyzstan for SCO summit, set to meet Putin, ZhaparovApple watch series 12 and ultra 4 could get these new health features: ReportRussia submits bid for India’s ₹ 50,000-crore deal to buy 5 more S-400 squadrons: Report‘Pretty reclusive, doesn’t go out’: Why Barron Trump keeps low profile amid Iran-linked threatUkraine’s new defence chief seeks early EU loan to plug $27 billion war budget gapWhy Tesla cars keep driving into train paths at Railway crossings, FSD users raise concernsNasa launches $4.3 billion Roman Space Telescope to explore universe’s biggest mysteriesCategoriesWorldIndiaExplainersOpinionSportsCricketTechnologyEntertainmentPhotostoriesLifestyleAutoBusinessVideosWebstoriesNETWORK18 SITESNews18Money ControlCNBC TV18Forbes IndiaAdvertise with usSitemapContact Us Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Terms Of Use Copyright @ 2026. Firstpost - All Rights Reserved.HomeVideosFirst AIQuick ReadsShorts","content_cn":"FBI突袭选举博彩平台Polymarket首席执行官Shayne Coplan的住宅，扣押电子设备\n世界 印度 解释 观点 生活方式 商业 Flaunt 世界 印度 解释 观点 生活方式 商业 Flaunt\n热门\n尼泊尔突发洪水\n莫迪总理访问中亚\n安大略湖划船\nChaTTJBMohan Bhagwat在纽约\n广告\n首个AI主页\n电视直播\n首个AI\n栏目\n世界\n娱乐\n解释\n板球\n体育\n观点\n印度\n科技\n汽车\n生活方式\n健康\n商业\n视频\nImpact Shorts\n节目\nVantage\nFirstpost America\nFirstpost Africa\nFirst Sports\nSpotlight\nThe Spend\nPlanet Pulse\n电视直播\n活动\n国际足联世界杯\n联邦预算\n独立日\n德里选举2025\n\nFBI突袭选举博彩平台Polymarket首席执行官Shayne Coplan的住宅，扣押电子设备\n联邦调查局（FBI）正在调查选举博彩平台Polymarket是否违反了2022年的和解协议，因为该平台允许美国用户下注\n\n广告\n（照片：路透社）\nFP Staff|2024年11月14日15:16:37（印度标准时间）\n\n联邦调查局（FBI）周三突袭了博彩平台Polymarket首席执行官Shayne Coplan的住宅。\n\n在选举日临近之际，Polymarket预测共和党候选人唐纳德·特朗普将击败副总统卡玛拉·哈里斯。\n\n据《纽约时报》报道，FBI从Coplan的家中扣押了包括其手机在内的电子设备。\n\n截至目前，FBI尚未正式对此案发表评论，但《纽约时报》援引消息人士称，这次突袭与一项涉嫌违反协议的行为有关；Coplan于2022年签署该协议，同意不允许在美国进行政治博彩。\n\n与此同时，Coplan将这次突袭称为政治报复。他在X（前身为Twitter）上发帖称，这次突袭是针对对手支持者的“最后一搏”。\n\n广告\n\n针对Polymarket首席执行官Shayne Coplan的案件是什么？\n\n据《纽约时报》报道，FBI和纽约南区联邦检察官办公室正在对Coplan涉嫌违反2022年协议展开刑事调查。\n\n2022年，Polymarket同意停止向美国用户提供博彩服务，并支付140万美元罚款。如今，Polymarket似乎违反了这项协议。\n\n据《纽约时报》报道，目前的调查似乎集中于Coplan是否将Polymarket作为一家无牌商品交易所运营，允许美国用户下注，从而违反与美国政府达成的和解协议。\n\n更多世界新闻\n\n然而，用户可以通过虚拟专用网络（VPN）访问博彩服务\n\n“令人作呕”\n\nCoplan在X上发帖，将自己描述为政治对手阴谋的受害者。\n\nCoplain说：“令人沮丧的是，现任政府会采取最后一搏的行动，去打击他们认为与政治对手有关联的公司。”\n\nCoplan进一步表示，Polymarket过去一直、今后也将永远致力于保持非党派立场。\n\nCoplain说：“我们一直坚定致力于保持非党派立场，今天也没有不同，但现任者应该进行自我反思，并认识到，采取更加亲商业、亲初创企业的方式，或许会改变他们在这次选举中的命运。”\n\n广告\n\n精选故事，送到你的收件箱\n全球故事。印度视角。零噪音。\n立即订阅\n无垃圾邮件。随时取消订阅\n\n标签\n美利坚合众国\n\n首次发布：2024年11月14日15:14:26（印度标准时间）\n\n首页\n世界\nfbi突袭选举博彩平台polymarkets首席执行官shayne coplan扣押\n设备广告广告\n热门故事\n尼泊尔洪灾：149名印度公民获救，死亡人数升至788人，超过2,500人失踪\n印度已从遭受洪灾的尼泊尔救出149名公民。灾难进入第五天，死亡人数升至788人，仍有超过2,500人失踪。\n1分钟阅读\n俄罗斯提交竞标，欲承接印度₹ 50,000 crore卢比的订单，再购买5个S-400中队：报道\n此举发生在“辛杜尔行动”数月后。在该行动期间，这套俄罗斯制造的系统被证明能非常有效地应对巴基斯坦的空中威胁。\n2分钟阅读\n“相当隐居，不出门”：为何伊朗相关威胁下巴伦·特朗普保持低调\n美国总统唐纳德·特朗普最小的儿子巴伦·特朗普在安全担忧加剧之际一直保持低调。一篇报道称，随着针对美国总统及其家人的威胁持续，这名20岁的年轻人“相当隐居”。\n3分钟阅读\n乌克兰新任国防部长寻求欧盟提前贷款，以填补270亿美元战争预算缺口\n国防部长叶夫根尼·赫马拉表示，基辅将向盟友提交明确的战争计划，并寻求提前获得欧盟贷款的一部分，因为乌克兰面临日益增加的军事资金需求。\n2分钟阅读\n美国国家航空航天局发射价值43亿美元的罗曼太空望远镜，探索宇宙最大奥秘\nSpaceX于周日从佛罗里达州肯尼迪航天中心搭载“猎鹰重型”火箭发射了美国国家航空航天局价值43亿美元的南希·格雷斯·罗曼太空望远镜\n2分钟阅读\n广告广告\n接下来\n关于Firstpost\n最新消息\n尼泊尔洪灾：149名印度公民获救，死亡人数升至788人，超过2,500人失踪\n印度总理莫迪抵达吉尔吉斯斯坦参加上海合作组织峰会，将与普京、扎帕罗夫会面\nApple Watch Series 12和Ultra 4或将获得这些新健康功能：报道\n俄罗斯提交竞标，欲承接印度₹ 50,000 crore卢比的订单，再购买5个S-400中队：报道\n“相当隐居，不出门”：为何伊朗相关威胁下巴伦·特朗普保持低调\n乌克兰新任国防部长寻求欧盟提前贷款，以填补270亿美元战争预算缺口\n为何特斯拉汽车不断驶入铁路道口的轨道，FSD用户提出担忧\n美国国家航空航天局发射价值43亿美元的罗曼太空望远镜，探索宇宙最大奥秘\n分类\n世界\n印度\n解释\n观点\n体育\n板球\n科技\n娱乐\n图片故事\n生活方式\n汽车\n商业\n视频\n网络故事\nNETWORK18网站\nNews18\nMoney Control\nCNBC TV18\nForbes India\n刊登广告\n网站地图\n联系我们 隐私政策 Cookie政策 使用条款 版权所有 @ 2026。Firstpost——保留所有权利。\n首页\n视频\nFirst AI\n快速阅读\n短视频","publish_source":"firstpost.com","publish_time":"2024-11-14T15:14:26+05:30"}},{"id":"news-224","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"Adobe 与 CrowdStrike：2026 年哪只科技股更值得买入？","title_en":"Adobe vs. CrowdStrike: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool 对比 Adobe 与 CrowdStrike。Adobe 以创意与生产力软件订阅服务覆盖逾 2 万家企业客户，2025 财年营收近 238 亿美元，增长约 10.5%，净利润约 71 亿美元，并收购 Topaz Labs 强化生成式 AI 能力。CrowdStrike 通过 Falcon 平台保护身份、数据与云工作负载，2026 财年营收近 48 亿美元，增长约 21.7%，净亏损约 1.625 亿美元。文章比较估值与风险后，作者仍倾向选择 CrowdStrike。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool compares Adobe and CrowdStrike. Adobe serves over 20,000 enterprise customers with creative and productivity software subscriptions, posting FY 2025 revenue near $23.8 billion, up about 10.5%, and net income near $7.1 billion, while acquiring Topaz Labs to boost generative AI. CrowdStrike's Falcon platform protects identity, data, and cloud workloads, with FY 2026 revenue near $4.8 billion, up about 21.7%, and a net loss of roughly $162.5 million. After weighing valuation and risk, the author still favors CrowdStrike.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:32:45.128915+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/better-buy/2026/09/11/adobe-vs-crowdstrike-which-technology-stock-is-a-better-buy-in-2026","content":"Software investing often forces a choice between a stable, cash-rich giant and a high-velocity disruptor, leaving investors to wonder which path leads to better long-term outcomes in an evolving digital economy. Choosing between Adobe (ADBE +0.87%) and CrowdStrike (CRWD +1.80%) requires weighing established dominance against high-growth potential.Adobe is the creative world's standard, while CrowdStrike is a cloud-native cybersecurity defender protecting modern enterprise workloads. They are being compared because both rely on subscription models to dominate their respective fields but offer very different risk and reward profiles for retail investors.CollapseADBE & CRWD: Performance ComparisonKey Financial MetricsADBE – Adobe$252.67+0.87% (+$2.17)CRWD – CrowdStrike$245.70+1.80% (+$4.34)Market Cap$100B52wk Range$190.12 - $370.31Gross Margin88.68%P/E Ratio14.09EPS (TTM)$17.93Market Cap$252B52wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Gross Margin75.12%P/E Ratio6882.35EPS (TTM)$0.04ADBE – Adobe$252.67+0.87% (+$2.17)Market Cap$100B52wk Range$190.12 - $370.31Gross Margin88.68%P/E Ratio14.09EPS (TTM)$17.93CRWD – CrowdStrike$245.70+1.80% (+$4.34)Market Cap$252B52wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Gross Margin75.12%P/E Ratio6882.35EPS (TTM)$0.04The case for AdobeAdobe operates as a leader among tech stocks by providing creative and productivity software to more than 20,000 enterprise customers. The company uses an integrated cloud-based subscription model to serve diverse groups ranging from students to global corporations. Recent strategic moves include the acquisition of Topaz Labs to enhance content capabilities through generative and agentic artificial intelligence tools.In its latest annual report, filed for the fiscal year ended Nov. 28, 2025, revenue reached nearly $23.8 billion, representing a year over year growth rate of approximately 10.5%. This growth follows a trend of steady expansion, as revenue was roughly $21.5 billion in the previous year. The company reported a net income of close to $7.1 billion, showcasing a healthy net margin of roughly 30%.As of its November 2025 balance sheet, the debt-to-equity ratio, which compares total debt to shareholder equity, was approximately 0.6x. The current ratio, measuring the ability to cover short-term liabilities with short-term assets, stood at roughly 1.0x. Free cash flow, which is the cash a company generates after accounting for capital expenditures, reached nearly $9.9 billion during this period, indicating strong cash generation relative to its size.The case for CrowdStrikeCrowdStrike provides a cloud-native platform designed to protect identity, data, and cloud workloads for a base of nearly 4,733 customers. The company utilizes a direct sales force and an extensive network of channel partners, including a 2026 partnership with Grant Thornton Advisors. Its go-to-market strategy focuses on endpoint protection and managed detection services for both public sector entities and government agencies.In its latest annual report, filed for the fiscal year ended Jan. 31, 2026, revenue grew by approximately 21.7% to reach nearly $4.8 billion compared with the prior fiscal year. The company reported a net loss of roughly $162.5 million, resulting in a negative net margin of about 3.4%. This loss widened from the prior year, reflecting significant investments in personnel and cloud infrastructure to support the scale of its security cloud.According to its January 2026 balance sheet, the debt-to-equity ratio was roughly 0.2x, while the current ratio reached approximately 1.8x. Free cash flow totaled close to $1.3 billion in the fiscal year ended Jan. 31, 2026. Note that stock-based compensation represented roughly 68% of operating cash flow, which inflates reported cash generation since SBC is a non-cash expense added back in the cash flow statement.Risk profile comparisonAdobe faces intense competition from global software players and cloud-native entrants who may deploy resources more effectively. The rapid integration of generative AI carries risks of intellectual property infringement and shifting global regulations like the EU AI Act. Furthermore, the company faced a $150 million settlement in early 2026 regarding its online subscription cancellation practices and remains under regulatory scrutiny.CrowdStrike continues to manage the reputational and operational aftermath of the failure in its July 19, 2024, content configuration update. This incident has led to ongoing costs for customer incentives and active litigation that could affect future results. The company also faces stiff competition from established security vendors and major cloud providers like Amazon (AMZN +2.13%), which possess greater financial resources.Valuation comparisonAdobe appears significantly more conservative on a valuation basis, trading at a much lower multiple of future earnings estimates and annual sales than CrowdStrike.MetricAdobeCrowdStrikeForward P/E11.3x154.9xP/S ratio4.6x40.3xValuation metrics sourced from Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) and may differ from other data providers.Which stock would I buy in 2026?I'd go with CrowdStrike, though Adobe trading near historic lows is not something a long-term investor should dismiss without a second look. Adobe has built one of the most deeply embedded software franchises in the world, and the stock has pulled back to one of its most attractive entry points in years. Fears that AI would erode its creative software dominance are looking increasingly overblown. For a long-term investor who values predictable cash flows and a proven franchise, it is a solid choice.But CrowdStrike is outpacing Adobe on nearly every growth metric that matters right now. Annual recurring revenue just hit a record, free cash flow surged to nearly a third of total revenue, and the Falcon platform keeps consolidating more of its customers' security spending under one roof. Every major enterprise that adds an AI workload also adds a new attack surface that needs protecting, which means CrowdStrike's addressable market keeps expanding alongside the AI build-out itself.Cybersecurity is not a discretionary purchase for enterprises the way creative software can be. For a long-term investor, owning the platform that keeps growing because the problem it solves keeps getting bigger is a stronger foundation right now.Read NextSep 15, 2026 •By Scott Levine7 Best Cloud Computing Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 14, 2026 •By Parkev Tatevosian, CFAIs Adobe Stock a Buy Right Now in September?Sep 14, 2026 •By Daniel SparksWhy It May Finally Be Time to Buy Adobe StockSep 13, 2026 •By Matt DiLalloHow to Use AI to Make Money in 2026Sep 12, 2026 •By Geoffrey SeilerAdobe: After Lifting Guidance, Is the Beaten-Down Stock Ready to Break Out?Sep 11, 2026 •By Sara AppinoAdobe vs. Salesforce: Which Software Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?About the AuthorSara Appino is a contributing writer at The Motley Fool. Previously she held roles at McGraw-Hill Education, Sourcebooks, and The Field Museum of Natural History. A graduate of the University of Chicago and Northwestern University’s Medill School of Journalism, Sara also managed a surf and yoga retreat in Costa Rica for nearly a decade and helped launch a nonprofit English language program in her community there.TMFSaraASara Appino has positions in Amazon. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Adobe, Amazon, and CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool recommends the following options: long January 2028 $330 calls on Adobe and short January 2028 $340 calls on Adobe. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedAdobeNASDAQ: ADBE$252.67(+0.87%)+$2.17Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$245.70(+1.80%)+$4.34*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"软件投资往往迫使人们在一家稳定、现金充裕的巨头和一家高速发展的颠覆者之间做出选择，让投资者不禁思考，在不断演变的数字经济中，哪条道路能带来更好的长期结果。在 Adobe（ADBE +0.87%）和 CrowdStrike（CRWD +1.80%）之间进行选择，需要权衡既有的主导地位与高增长潜力。Adobe 是创意领域的行业标准，而 CrowdStrike 则是一家云原生网络安全防御商，保护现代企业工作负载。之所以将两者进行比较，是因为它们都依靠订阅模式主导各自领域，但对散户投资者而言，它们提供的风险和回报状况截然不同。\n\n收起\n\nADBE 与 CRWD：业绩比较\n\n关键财务指标\n\nADBE – Adobe\n$252.67\n+0.87%（+$2.17）\n\nCRWD – CrowdStrike\n$245.70\n+1.80%（+$4.34）\n\n市值\n$100B\n\n52周区间\n$190.12 - $370.31\n\n毛利率\n88.68%\n\n市盈率\n14.09\n\n每股收益（TTM）\n$17.93\n\n市值\n$252B\n\n52周区间\n$85.68 - $250.32\n\n毛利率\n75.12%\n\n市盈率\n6882.35\n\n每股收益（TTM）\n$0.04\n\nADBE – Adobe\n$252.67\n+0.87%（+$2.17）\n\n市值\n$100B\n\n52周区间\n$190.12 - $370.31\n\n毛利率\n88.68%\n\n市盈率\n14.09\n\n每股收益（TTM）\n$17.93\n\nCRWD – CrowdStrike\n$245.70\n+1.80%（+$4.34）\n\n市值\n$252B\n\n52周区间\n$85.68 - $250.32\n\n毛利率\n75.12%\n\n市盈率\n6882.35\n\n每股收益（TTM）\n$0.04\n\n支持 Adobe 的理由\n\nAdobe 通过向超过20,000家企业客户提供创意和生产力软件，成为科技股中的领导者。公司采用一体化的云端订阅模式，服务对象从学生到全球企业等不同群体。近期的战略举措包括收购 Topaz Labs，通过生成式和智能代理人工智能工具增强内容能力。\n\n在其最新年度报告中（提交的是截至2025年11月28日的财年），收入接近238亿美元，同比增长率约为10.5%。这一增长延续了稳定扩张的趋势，因为上一年度收入约为215亿美元。公司报告净利润接近71亿美元，显示出约30%的健康净利润率。\n\n截至2025年11月的资产负债表，负债权益比（即总负债与股东权益之比）约为0.6倍。流动比率（衡量利用短期资产偿还短期负债的能力）约为1.0倍。自由现金流（即公司在计入资本支出后产生的现金）在此期间接近99亿美元，表明相对于公司规模而言，其现金创造能力很强。\n\n支持 CrowdStrike 的理由\n\nCrowdStrike 提供一个云原生平台，旨在保护身份、数据和云工作负载，客户基础接近4,733家。公司采用直销团队和广泛的渠道合作伙伴网络，其中包括2026年与 Grant Thornton Advisors 建立的合作关系。其市场进入战略专注于为公共部门实体和政府机构提供终端保护和托管检测服务。\n\n在其最新年度报告中（提交的是截至2026年1月31日的财年），收入约增长21.7%，达到近48亿美元，而上一财年收入较低。公司报告净亏损约1.625亿美元，导致净利润率为负，约为-3.4%。这一亏损较上一年度扩大，反映出公司为支持其安全云的规模化而在人员和云基础设施方面进行了大量投资。\n\n根据其2026年1月的资产负债表，负债权益比约为\n0.2倍，而当前比率约为1.8倍。在截至2026年1月31日的财年中，自由现金流总额接近13亿美元。需要注意的是，基于股票的薪酬约占经营现金流的68%，这会夸大报告中的现金生成，因为股票薪酬是一项在现金流量表中加回的非现金支出。\n\n风险状况比较\nAdobe面临来自全球软件公司和云原生企业的激烈竞争，后者可能更有效地调配资源。生成式AI的快速整合带来了知识产权侵权风险，以及欧盟《人工智能法案》等全球监管规定变化的风险。此外，该公司在2026年初因在线订阅取消惯例支付了1.5亿美元的和解金，并且仍受到监管机构的审查。\n\nCrowdStrike仍在处理其2024年7月19日内容配置更新失败所造成的声誉和运营后果。该事件导致持续的客户激励成本和正在进行的诉讼，可能影响未来业绩。该公司还面临来自成熟安全供应商和亚马逊（AMZN +2.13%）等大型云服务提供商的激烈竞争，后者拥有更雄厚的财力。\n\n估值比较\n从估值角度看，Adobe显得明显更为保守，其未来收益预期和年度销售额的倍数都远低于CrowdStrike。\n\n指标\tAdobe\tCrowdStrike\n远期市盈率\t11.3倍\t154.9倍\n市销率\t4.6倍\t40.3倍\n\n估值指标来源于Financial Modeling Prep（FMP），可能与其他数据提供商的数据有所不同。\n\n我会在2026年买哪只股票？\n\n我会选择CrowdStrike，不过，Adobe股价接近历史低点，并非长期投资者应该不加考虑地忽视的机会。Adobe已经建立了全球最根深蒂固的软件业务之一，而其股价已回落到多年来最具吸引力的切入点之一。人们担心AI会削弱其创意软件主导地位，这种担忧正越来越显得过度。对于重视可预测现金流和成熟业务的长期投资者而言，它是一个稳健的选择。\n\n但就目前而言，CrowdStrike几乎在所有重要增长指标上都超过了Adobe。年度经常性收入刚刚创下纪录，自由现金流飙升至总收入的近三分之一，而Falcon平台不断将更多客户的安全支出集中在一个平台之下。每一家增加AI工作负载的大型企业，也都会增加一个需要保护的新攻击面，这意味着CrowdStrike的可服务市场正随着AI建设本身不断扩大。\n\n对企业而言，网络安全不像创意软件那样属于可自由裁量的采购。对于长期投资者来说，拥有一个因其所解决的问题不断扩大而持续增长的平台，目前是更坚实的基础。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月15日 •作者：Scott Levine\n2026年7大云计算股票及投资方法\n\n2026年9月14日 •作者：Parkev Tatevosian，CFA\nAdobe股票在9月目前值得买入吗？\n\n2026年9月14日 •作者：Daniel Sparks\n现在或许终于到了买入Adobe股票的时候\n\n2026年9月13日 •作者：Matt DiLallo\n如何利用AI在2026年赚钱\n\n2026年9月12日 •作者：Geoffrey Seiler\nAdobe：上调指引后，这只跌幅惨重的股票准备突破了吗？\n\n2026年9月11日 •作者：Sara Appino\nAdobe对 Salesforce：2026年哪只软件股更值得买入？\n\n关于作者\nSara Appino是《Motley Fool》的特约撰稿人。此前，她曾在McGraw-Hill Education担任职务，\nSourcebooks，以及菲尔德自然历史博物馆。Sara毕业于芝加哥大学和西北大学梅迪尔新闻学院；此外，她还在哥斯达黎加管理了一家冲浪和瑜伽度假中心，近十年之久，并帮助在那里所在的社区启动了一个非营利英语语言项目。TMFSaraASara Appino持有亚马逊的仓位。The Motley Fool持有Adobe、亚马逊和CrowdStrike的仓位并推荐这些股票。The Motley Fool推荐以下期权：买入Adobe 2028年1月到期、行权价为330美元的看涨期权，卖出Adobe 2028年1月到期、行权价为340美元的看涨期权。The Motley Fool有披露政策。提及的股票：AdobeNASDAQ: ADBE$252.67(+0.87%)+$2.17Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐可访问---%平均回报率CrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$245.70(+1.80%)+$4.34*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报率。成本基础和回报率基于前一个市场交易日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-11T16:35:44+00:00"}},{"id":"news-23","ktid":2575920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"2575920","source":"Google","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"比较卡特彼勒和霍尼韦尔工业股投资价值","title_en":"Caterpillar vs. Honeywell International: Which Industrials Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"文章比较卡特彼勒与霍尼韦尔两只工业股：卡特彼勒依托建筑、采矿和能源设备业务及全球经销商网络，2026年收购Skycatch、Monarch Tractor和RPMGlobal以增强采矿和农业技术能力；其风险包括需求受大宗商品价格和全球经济波动影响、供应链及经销商库存管理风险，以及来自小松和迪尔等竞争对手的压力。霍尼韦尔正通过剥离业务、聚焦航空航天和自动化进行重组，面临收购整合、战略剥离、法律诉讼和重组执行风险。文章认为卡特彼勒基本面强但估值较高，霍尼韦尔估值较低但仍属等待转型见效的标的。","summary_en":"The article compares Caterpillar and Honeywell as industrial stocks. Caterpillar serves construction, mining, and energy markets through a global dealer network and is pursuing acquisitions to enhance mining and agricultural technology capabilities. Its risks include cyclical machinery demand, supply-chain and dealer-inventory issues, and competition. Honeywell is refocusing on aerospace and automation while pursuing divestitures and restructuring; its risks include acquisition integration, execution of divestitures, litigation, competition, and operational disruption from reorganization. The article views Caterpillar as fundamentally strong but more highly valued, while Honeywell appears relatively cheaper and may suit value investors willing to await a turnaround.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-26T14:57:22.709782+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/better-buy/2026/09/24/caterpillar-vs-honeywell-international-which-industrials-stock-is-a-better-buy-in-2026/","content":"Investors often look to industrial giants for stability, but choosing between a machinery titan and a diversified technology leader requires looking at the data. Let's compare Caterpillar (CAT +2.03%) and Honeywell International (HON +0.36%).Caterpillar is the world's leading manufacturer of construction and mining equipment, relying on a vast global dealer network. Honeywell operates as a diversified conglomerate currently refocusing its portfolio on high-growth automation and aerospace technologies. Comparing these two involves weighing heavy equipment dominance against a technology-led transition.The case for CaterpillarCaterpillar operates as a global powerhouse among industrial stocks, primarily serving the construction, mining, and energy sectors. The company sells its heavy machinery through a massive independent dealer network, consisting of 41 dealers in the United States and 109 international dealers across 190 countries. Recent strategic moves in 2026 include the acquisitions of Skycatch, Monarch Tractor, and RPMGlobal, which are intended to boost the company's capabilities in mining and agricultural technology.ExpandNYSE: CATCaterpillarPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(2.03%) $16.33Current Price$821.58Key Data PointsMarket Cap$378BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$809.05 - $823.0052wk Range$467.46 - $1073.46Volume2MAvg Vol2.9MGross Margin32.83%Dividend Yield0.75%In FY 2025, according to its latest annual report, revenue reached nearly $67.6 billion, representing approximately 4.3% growth over the previous year. Net income for the period was roughly $8.9 billion, yielding a net margin of close to 13.1%. While revenue grew, this net margin was lower than the 16.7% achieved in FY 2024, when net income was approximately $10.8 billion.As of its December 2025 balance sheet, the debt-to-equity ratio was roughly 2.0x, calculated as total debt divided by shareholders' equity. The current ratio, which measures the ability to pay short-term obligations by dividing current assets by current liabilities, was approximately 1.4x. Free cash flow for FY 2025 reached nearly $7.5 billion, representing cash generated after paying for operating costs and equipment upgrades.The case for Honeywell InternationalAccording to its latest annual report, filed for FY 2025, Honeywell is transforming into an organization focused on independent aerospace and automation businesses. It provides advanced technology and services to building operators, energy sector partners, and defense customers. Following a strategic review, the company is divesting its Warehouse and Workflow Solutions business and has already spun off its aerospace segment, Honeywell Aerospace (HONA +0.20%).ExpandNASDAQ: HONHoneywell TechnologiesPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore66/100Today's Change(0.36%) $0.76Current Price$212.55Key Data PointsMarket Cap$67BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$210.75 - $213.6452wk Range$195.77 - $260.15Volume1.8MAvg Vol3.6MGross Margin37.84%Dividend Yield2.09%In FY 2025, revenue reached roughly $37.4 billion, which is an increase of approximately 7.8% over the previous year. Net income for the same period was close to $4.7 billion, resulting in a net margin of roughly 12.6%. This reflects a decline in net margin from FY 2024, when the company reported net income of approximately $5.7 billion and a net margin of nearly 16.4%.As of its December 2025 balance sheet, the debt-to-equity ratio was approximately 2.2x. The current ratio for the same period was roughly 1.3x, indicating the company's ability to cover its short-term liabilities with its current assets. Free cash flow, which is the cash a company generates after accounting for capital expenditures, reached nearly $5.4 billion in FY 2025.Risk profile comparisonCaterpillar faces significant cyclicality risk, as demand for its heavy machinery is highly sensitive to commodity price volatility and global economic shifts. Operational risks include potential disruptions in complex global supply chains and a reliance on dealer inventory management. The company also faces intense competition from global rivals such as Komatsu (KMTUF +8.37%) and Deere (DE -0.65%), which can lead to pricing and margin pressure.Honeywell is exposed to risks associated with integrating numerous acquisitions and executing its complex strategic divestitures. The company faces ongoing legal and litigation risks, including substantial settlements related to past commercial agreements. Additionally, it must manage competitive threats from peers such as GE Vernova (GEV +0.27%) in technology-driven markets while navigating the operational impact of its corporate reorganizations.Valuation comparisonHoneywell appears to be the more affordable option based on its P/S ratio, though Caterpillar carries a higher valuation relative to its Forward P/E and future earnings estimates.MetricCaterpillarHoneywell InternationalForward P/E29.7x24.8xP/S ratio5.5x1.7xValuation metrics sourced from Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) and may differ from other data providers.Which stock would I buy in 2026?Caterpillar and Honeywell are both titans of the industrial sector. Therefore, investors will need to dig beneath the surface to determine which stock could be the right choice for them. Here, we'll take a look at what each stock has to offer.First, there's Caterpillar. The company is an industrial mainstay and provides much of the equipment used to create global infrastructure. In recent years, Caterpillar has benefited from the artificial intelligence (AI) boom. Right now, and going forward, Caterpillar equipment will be hard at work constructing the data centers needed as AI infrastructure comes into being. What's more, Caterpillar's fundamentals are rock solid, with nearly $68 billion in revenue and close to $9 billion in net income.As for Honeywell, it is also a mainstay in the industrial sector. However, the company is undergoing a restructuring. This has resulted in some short-term turbulence, as the company must pivot operationally. The remaining corporate parent is focused on transforming into an industrial automation company. Here, it hopes to capitalize on the AI data center build-out and automate existing warehouses to improve logistics. At any rate, Honeywell stock remains a turnaround story. Shares currently trade at an affordable price-to-sales (P/S) valuation of only 1.7x. That's far below Honeywell's five-year average P/S of 3.2x.In summary, different types of investors may favor different stocks here. Caterpillar is a company firing on all cylinders. Its valuation reflects that. Honeywell, on the other hand, may appeal to value-oriented investors willing to wait for its turnaround to bear fruit. At any rate, both stocks have solid fundamentals that will appeal to long-term investors.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Catie HoganIs Caterpillar the Best Industrials Stock to Buy Right Now?Sep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCaterpillar vs. Corning: Which Industrials Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Lee SamahaWhat Higher Interest Rates Mean for Caterpillar, GE Vernova, and VertivSep 20, 2026 •By Marc GubertiThe Caterpillar Correction Shouldn't Last Much LongerSep 19, 2026 •By Rick OrfordOracle Has Committed Hundreds of Billions to AI Data Centers. These 2 Industrial Stocks Will Power Them.Sep 11, 2026 •By Matt DiLallo5 Best Industrial Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorJake Lerch is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering artificial intelligence, cloud computing, cybersecurity, e-commerce, and semiconductors. Prior to The Motley Fool, Jake worked for 12 years at Credit Suisse, an international investment bank. He holds a bachelor’s degree in business with a concentration in economics from the University of North Carolina at Wilmington.TMFRescueDogJake Lerch has positions in Caterpillar. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Caterpillar, Deere & Company , GE Vernova, Honeywell Aerospace, and Honeywell Technologies. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCaterpillarNYSE: CAT$821.58(+2.03%)+$16.33Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnHoneywell TechnologiesNASDAQ: HON$212.55(+0.36%)+$0.76*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"投资者常常将工业巨头视为稳定性的来源，但要在一家机械巨头与一家多元化技术领导者之间做出选择，需要审视数据。让我们比较卡特彼勒（CAT +2.03%）和霍尼韦尔国际（HON +0.36%）。卡特彼勒是全球领先的建筑和采矿设备制造商，依靠庞大的全球经销商网络。霍尼韦尔作为一家多元化企业集团运营，目前正将其业务组合重新聚焦于高增长的自动化和航空航天技术。比较这两家公司，需要权衡重型设备领域的主导地位与技术驱动的转型。\n\n卡特彼勒的投资理由\n\n卡特彼勒是工业股中的全球强者，主要服务于建筑、采矿和能源行业。该公司通过庞大的独立经销商网络销售其重型机械，该网络由美国的41家经销商和覆盖190个国家的109家国际经销商组成。2026年近期的战略举措包括收购Skycatch、Monarch Tractor和RPMGlobal，旨在增强公司在采矿和农业技术方面的能力。展开NYSE: CAT卡特彼勒高级功能Moneyball Superscore85/100今日变动(2.03%) $16.33当前价格$821.58关键数据点市值$378B市值仅使用已发行的公开交易股票计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。当日区间$809.05 - $823.0052周区间$467.46 - $1073.46成交量2M平均成交量2.9M毛利率32.83%股息收益率0.75%\n\n根据其最新年度报告，2025财年营收达到近676亿美元，较上一年增长约4.3%。该期间的净利润约为89亿美元，净利率接近13.1%。尽管营收增长，但这一净利率低于2024财年实现的16.7%，当时净利润约为108亿美元。\n\n截至2025年12月的资产负债表，债务权益比约为2.0倍，按总债务除以股东权益计算。衡量以流动资产除以流动负债来偿还短期债务能力的流动比率约为1.4倍。2025财年的自由现金流达到近75亿美元，代表支付运营成本和设备升级费用后产生的现金。\n\n霍尼韦尔国际的投资理由\n\n根据其为2025财年提交的最新年度报告，霍尼韦尔正在转型为一家专注于独立航空航天和自动化业务的组织。它向建筑运营商、能源行业合作伙伴和国防客户提供先进技术和服务。经过战略审查后，该公司正在剥离其Warehouse and Workflow Solutions业务，并且已经拆分其航空航天部门霍尼韦尔航空航天（HONA +0.20%）。展开NASDAQ: HON霍尼韦尔科技高级功能Moneyball Superscore66/100今日变动(0.36%) $0.76当前价格$212.55关键数据点市值$67B市值仅使用已发行的公开交易股票计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。当日区间$210.75 - $213.6452周区间$195.77 - $260.15成交量1.8M平均成交量3.6M毛利率37.84%股息收益率2.09%\n\n2025财年，营收达到约374亿美元，较上一年增长约7.8%。同期净利润接近47亿美元，产生了净\n利润率约为12.6%。这反映出净利润率较2024财年下降；当时该公司报告的净收入约为57亿美元，净利润率接近16.4%。截至2025年12月的资产负债表，其债务权益比约为2.2倍。同一时期的流动比率约为1.3倍，表明该公司能够以流动资产偿付短期负债。自由现金流，即公司扣除资本支出后产生的现金，在2025财年达到近54亿美元。\n风险概况比较\n卡特彼勒面临显著的周期性风险，因为其重型机械需求对大宗商品价格波动和全球经济变化高度敏感。运营风险包括复杂全球供应链可能中断，以及对经销商库存管理的依赖。该公司还面临来自小松（KMTUF +8.37%）和迪尔（DE -0.65%）等全球竞争对手的激烈竞争，这可能导致定价和利润率承压。\n霍尼韦尔面临与整合大量收购交易及执行其复杂战略性剥离相关的风险。该公司持续面临法律和诉讼风险，包括与过去商业协议有关的重大和解。此外，在经历企业重组带来的运营影响时，它还必须应对技术驱动型市场中来自GE Vernova（GEV +0.27%）等同行的竞争威胁。\n估值比较\n根据市销率，霍尼韦尔似乎是更便宜的选择，尽管相对于其预期市盈率和未来盈利预估，卡特彼勒的估值更高。\n指标\n卡特彼勒\n霍尼韦尔国际\n预期市盈率\n29.7倍\n24.8倍\n市销率\n5.5倍\n1.7倍\n估值指标来源于Financial Modeling Prep（FMP），可能与其他数据提供商存在差异。\n2026年我会买哪只股票？\n卡特彼勒和霍尼韦尔都是工业领域的巨头。因此，投资者需要深入分析，以确定哪只股票可能是适合自己的选择。下面，我们来看看每只股票能提供什么。\n首先是卡特彼勒。该公司是工业领域的中坚力量，并提供了建设全球基础设施所使用的大量设备。近年来，卡特彼勒受益于人工智能（AI）热潮。当前以及未来，随着AI基础设施逐步成形，卡特彼勒设备将忙于建设所需的数据中心。此外，卡特彼勒的基本面非常稳健，营收接近680亿美元，净收入接近90亿美元。\n至于霍尼韦尔，它也是工业领域的中坚力量。然而，该公司正在进行重组。这导致了一些短期波动，因为公司必须在运营上作出转变。保留的母公司正专注于转型为一家工业自动化公司。在此过程中，它希望抓住AI数据中心建设的机遇，并将现有仓库自动化以改善物流。无论如何，霍尼韦尔股票仍然是一个转型故事。该股目前的市销率（P/S）估值仅为1.7倍，较霍尼韦尔五年平均市销率3.2倍低得多。\n总之，不同类型的投资者可能会偏好这里不同的股票。卡特彼勒是一家全速运转的公司，其估值也反映了这一点。另一方面，霍尼韦尔可能会吸引那些愿意等待其\n扭亏为盈。无论如何，这两只股票都拥有扎实的基本面，将吸引长期投资者。继续阅读\n2026年9月24日 • 作者：Catie Hogan\nCaterpillar 是现在最值得买入的工业股吗？\n2026年9月24日 • 作者：Jake Lerch\nCaterpillar 与 Corning：2026年哪只工业股更值得买入？\n2026年9月21日 • 作者：Lee Samaha\n更高的利率对 Caterpillar、GE Vernova 和 Vertiv 意味着什么\n2026年9月20日 • 作者：Marc Guberti\nCaterpillar 的回调不应持续太久\n2026年9月19日 • 作者：Rick Orford\nOracle 已承诺为 AI 数据中心投入数千亿美元。这两只工业股将为其提供动力。\n2026年9月11日 • 作者：Matt DiLallo\n2026年5只最佳工业股及投资方法\n关于作者\nJake Lerch 是 Motley Fool 的特约科技分析师，负责报道人工智能、云计算、网络安全、电子商务和半导体。在加入 The Motley Fool 之前，Jake 曾在国际投资银行瑞士信贷工作12年。他拥有北卡罗来纳大学威明顿分校工商管理学士学位，主修经济学。\nTMFRescueDog\nJake Lerch 持有 Caterpillar 的头寸。The Motley Fool 持有并推荐 Caterpillar、Deere & Company、GE Vernova、Honeywell Aerospace 和 Honeywell Technologies。The Motley Fool 有一项披露政策。\n提及的股票\nCaterpillar\n纽约证券交易所：CAT\n821.58美元（+2.03%）+16.33美元\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor 的最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报\nHoneywell Technologies\n纳斯达克：HON\n212.55美元（+0.36%）+0.76美元\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报率。成本基础和回报率基于前一交易日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-24T15:45:02+00:00"}},{"id":"news-27","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike与Figma：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？","title_en":"CrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool对比CrowdStrike与Figma。CrowdStrike通过云原生Falcon平台为政府与大型企业保护端点、身份与云环境，2026财年营收近48亿美元，同比增长约21.7%，净亏损约1.625亿美元，净利率约负3.4%；股票薪酬约占经营现金流68%。文章提及2024年7月19日事件后的订阅延期与折扣、对亚马逊云基础设施的依赖及激烈竞争，认为CrowdStrike对成长型投资者更具吸引力。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool compares CrowdStrike and Figma. CrowdStrike's cloud-native Falcon platform protects endpoints, identities, and cloud environments for governments and large enterprises, with fiscal 2026 revenue near $4.8 billion, up about 21.7%, and a net loss of roughly $162.5 million, a negative 3.4% net margin; stock-based compensation was about 68% of operating cash flow. The article notes subscription extensions and discounts after the July 19, 2024 incident, reliance on Amazon's cloud infrastructure, and intense competition, concluding CrowdStrike likely appeals more to growth-oriented investors.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:47:58.591967+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/better-buy/2026/09/24/crowdstrike-vs-figma-which-technology-stock-is-a-better-buy-in-2026","content":"Choosing between high-growth technology leaders requires balancing established market dominance against emerging software platforms. In 2026, investors are weighing the cybersecurity prowess of CrowdStrike (CRWD -0.12%) against the collaborative design innovation of Figma (FIG -1.72%).CrowdStrike provides mission-critical security through its cloud-native Falcon platform, helping organizations stop breaches in real time. Figma offers a collaborative design environment that has become the standard for product teams worldwide. While both companies operate in the tech sector, they serve different enterprise needs and face unique growth hurdles.The case for CrowdStrikeCrowdStrike sells its cloud-native Falcon platform to protect endpoints, identities, and cloud environments for governments and large enterprises. The company serves a wide range of sectors, including healthcare, financial services, and utilities, among tech stocks. Following an incident on July 19, 2024, the company has focused on providing subscription extensions and discounts to maintain its customer base.In the fiscal year ended Jan. 31, 2026, revenue reached nearly $4.8 billion, representing approximately 21.7% growth over the prior fiscal year. Despite this growth, the company reported a net loss of roughly $162.5 million for the period. This resulted in a negative net margin of approximately 3.4%, which measures the percentage of revenue remaining as profit after all expenses.As of its January 2026 balance sheet, the debt-to-equity ratio was nearly 0.2x, indicating that total debt is low relative to shareholder equity. The current ratio, which measures the ability to cover short-term liabilities with current assets, was roughly 1.8x. Free cash flow for the fiscal year ended Jan. 31, 2026, reached approximately $1.3 billion. Note that stock-based compensation accounted for roughly 68% of operating cash flow, inflating reported cash generation, since SBC is a non-cash expense added back to cash flow.The case for FigmaFigma operates a design platform that allows teams to build products together using tools for prototyping, development handoff, and AI-assisted creation. The platform is highly international, with approximately 85% of its monthly active users located outside the U.S. as of its latest disclosures. To drive growth, the company uses a free starter plan to attract users before moving them to paid subscriptions.In the fiscal year ended Dec. 31, 2025, according to its latest annual report, revenue reached nearly $1.1 billion. This marked a significant increase of approximately 41% over the previous year. However, the company reported a net loss of roughly $(1.3) billion, resulting in a net margin of nearly (118.4)%.As of its December 2025 balance sheet, Figma maintained a debt-to-equity ratio of approximately 0.1x. The current ratio was nearly 2.6x, suggesting a strong position for meeting short-term financial obligations. Free cash flow for the fiscal year ended Dec. 31, 2025, was close to $246.2 million. Note that stock-based compensation represented roughly 544.2% of operating cash flow, meaning reported cash generation is heavily inflated by this non-cash add-back.Risk profile comparisonCrowdStrike faces ongoing reputational and business damage stemming from the content configuration incident that occurred on July 19, 2024. The company must also navigate intense competition from legacy antivirus providers and newer cloud security vendors. Additionally, it relies heavily on Amazon (AMZN +0.07%) for the underlying cloud infrastructure required to deliver its platform.Figma faces risks related to recent changes to its pricing and billing models, including new limits on AI credit usage. It competes against major software platforms, including Adobe (ADBE -1.08%) and other AI-driven design tools. The company also faces potential legal hurdles regarding the accuracy of AI outputs and data privacy concerns.Valuation comparisonFigma trades at a much lower P/S ratio compared to CrowdStrike.MetricCrowdStrikeFigmaP/S ratio50.3x10.5xValuation metrics sourced from Financial Modeling Prep (FMP) and may differ from other data providers.Which stock would I buy in 2026?CrowdStrike and Figma are two very different technology stocks. Particularly at this moment, with so much changing in the overall tech landscape, CrowdStrike and Figma present investors with a stark choice. Let's dig into the details to see what opportunities present themselves.First, there's CrowdStrike. The company has quickly become a backbone of the cybersecurity landscape. The stock now boasts a market cap of more than $250 billion, making it the second-largest cybersecurity stock, trailing only Palo Alto Networks' (PANW -0.14%) $320 billion market cap. CrowdStrike's products have become essential must-haves for many organizations eager to fend off cybercriminals. As a result, core metrics like revenue and free cash flow have exploded higher in recent years. Moreover, the company is positioning itself as a key player in the AI security infrastructure space.Then, there's Figma. The changing technology landscape has presented a different challenge for Figma. That's because frontier AI models could threaten Figma's core moat. The company provides collaborative canvases for designing user interfaces (UI) and user experiences (UX). Frontier AI models could disrupt this entire workflow by allowing humans to simply prompt the model to produce an application preview in one step. Figma is adapting by integrating AI features into its software, as humans will still need to collaborate and evaluate designs, but it remains to be seen how these changes will affect Figma's monetization model going forward. Right now, the company's net losses have increased to $(1.3) billion despite 40% revenue growth.In summary, CrowdStrike will likely have greater appeal among growth-oriented investors, given its solid fundamentals and broad appeal as a key cybersecurity provider to many organizations. Read NextSep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400Sep 14, 2026 •By Danny Vena, CPAWhy CrowdStrike Stock Rocketed Higher TodayAbout the AuthorJake Lerch is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering artificial intelligence, cloud computing, cybersecurity, e-commerce, and semiconductors. Prior to The Motley Fool, Jake worked for 12 years at Credit Suisse, an international investment bank. He holds a bachelor’s degree in business with a concentration in economics from the University of North Carolina at Wilmington.TMFRescueDogJake Lerch has positions in Amazon and CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Adobe, Amazon, CrowdStrike, and Figma. The Motley Fool recommends Palo Alto Networks and recommends the following options: long January 2028 $330 calls on Adobe and short January 2028 $340 calls on Adobe. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$262.95(+0.17%)+$0.46Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnFigmaNYSE: FIG$21.39(-1.72%)-$0.38*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"在高增长科技领导者之间做出选择，需要在既有的市场主导地位与新兴软件平台之间取得平衡。2026年，投资者正在权衡CrowdStrike（CRWD -0.12%）的网络安全实力与Figma（FIG -1.72%）的协作式设计创新。CrowdStrike通过其云原生Falcon平台提供任务关键型安全服务，帮助组织实时阻止安全漏洞。Figma提供协作式设计环境，已成为全球产品团队的行业标准。尽管两家公司都在科技行业运营，但它们服务于不同的企业需求，也面临独特的增长障碍。\n\nCrowdStrike的支持理由\nCrowdStrike向政府和大型企业销售其云原生Falcon平台，以保护终端、身份和云环境。在科技股公司中，该公司服务于包括医疗保健、金融服务和公用事业在内的广泛行业。继2024年7月19日发生一起事件后，公司一直专注于提供订阅延期和折扣，以维持其客户基础。\n\n在截至2026年1月31日的财年中，收入达到近48亿美元，较上一财年增长约21.7%。尽管实现了这一增长，公司在该期间仍报告净亏损约1.625亿美元。这导致净利润率为负约3.4%，该指标衡量扣除所有费用后作为利润保留下来的收入百分比。\n\n截至2026年1月的资产负债表，债务权益比接近0.2倍，表明相对于股东权益而言，总债务较低。流动比率衡量利用流动资产偿还短期负债的能力，该比率约为1.8倍。在截至2026年1月31日的财年中，自由现金流达到约13亿美元。需要注意的是，股票薪酬约占经营现金流的68%，由于股票薪酬是计入现金流加回的非现金费用，这夸大了报告中的现金生成额。\n\nFigma的支持理由\nFigma运营着一个设计平台，团队可以使用原型设计、开发交接和AI辅助创作工具共同构建产品。该平台具有高度国际化特征，根据最新披露，截至当时约85%的月活跃用户位于美国以外。为推动增长，公司采用免费入门套餐吸引用户，然后再将他们转化为付费订阅用户。\n\n根据最新年度报告，在截至2025年12月31日的财年中，收入达到近11亿美元。这较上一年大幅增加约41%。然而，公司报告净亏损约（13）亿美元，导致净利润率接近（118.4）%。\n\n截至2025年12月的资产负债表，Figma保持约0.1倍的债务权益比。流动比率接近2.6倍，表明其具备较强的能力来履行短期财务义务。在截至2025年12月31日的财年中，自由现金流接近2.462亿美元。需要注意的是，股票薪酬约占经营现金流的544.2%，这意味着报告中的现金生成额因这项非现金加回而被大幅夸大。\n\n风险状况比较\nCrowdStrike仍面临源于2024年7月19日发生的内容配置事件的持续声誉和业务损害。该公司还必须应对传统杀毒软件供应商和新兴云安全供应商的激烈竞争。此外，它\n严重依赖亚马逊（AMZN +0.07%）提供交付其平台所需的底层云基础设施。Figma面临与近期定价和计费模式变化相关的风险，包括对AI积分使用设置的新限制。它与包括Adobe（ADBE -1.08%）在内的主要软件平台以及其他AI驱动的设计工具展开竞争。公司还面临关于AI输出准确性和数据隐私问题的潜在法律障碍。\n\n估值比较\n与CrowdStrike相比，Figma的市销率（P/S）低得多。\n\n指标 | CrowdStrike | Figma\n市销率 | 50.3倍 | 10.5倍\n\n估值指标来源于Financial Modeling Prep（FMP），可能与其他数据提供商的数据不同。\n\n我会在2026年买哪只股票？\nCrowdStrike和Figma是两只截然不同的科技股。尤其是在当前这个整体科技格局变化如此之大的时刻，CrowdStrike和Figma给投资者带来了鲜明的选择。让我们深入细节，看看有哪些机会显现出来。\n\n首先是CrowdStrike。该公司已迅速成为网络安全领域的支柱。如今，公司股票对应的市值已超过2500亿美元，使其成为第二大网络安全股，仅次于市值3200亿美元的Palo Alto Networks（PANW -0.14%）。CrowdStrike的产品已成为许多急于抵御网络犯罪分子的组织不可或缺的必需品。因此，近年来，收入和自由现金流等核心指标都大幅增长。此外，公司正将自己定位为AI安全基础设施领域的关键参与者。\n\n然后是Figma。不断变化的技术格局给Figma带来了不同的挑战。这是因为前沿AI模型可能威胁到Figma的核心护城河。该公司提供用于设计用户界面（UI）和用户体验（UX）的协作画布。前沿AI模型可能通过让人类只需一步提示模型生成应用预览，颠覆整个工作流程。Figma正通过将AI功能整合进其软件来适应，因为人类仍然需要协作并评估设计，但这些变化将如何影响Figma未来的变现模式，仍有待观察。目前，尽管收入增长了40%，公司的净亏损已扩大至13亿美元。\n\n总而言之，鉴于其稳健的基本面，以及作为许多组织的关键网络安全供应商所具备的广泛吸引力，CrowdStrike可能更受偏好增长型投资者的青睐。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月23日 •作者：Adam Spatacco\n不是Palantir，也不是美光。这家价值3250亿美元的英伟达合作伙伴刚被Jim Cramer称为“必买”股票\n2026年9月22日 •作者：Pamela Kock\nCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？\n2026年9月21日 •作者：Leo Sun\n现在值得买的两只百万富翁制造机网络安全股\n2026年9月17日 •作者：Catie Hogan\n两只将在2027年称霸的网络安全股\n2026年9月15日 •作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA\n这只网络安全股可能将1000美元变成超过4400美元\n2026年9月14日 •作者：Danny Vena，CPA\nCrowdStrike股价今天为何大幅上涨\n\n关于作者\nJake Lerch是《Motley Fool》的特约科技分析师，负责报道人工智能、云计算、网络安全、电子商务和半导体。在加入《Motley Fool》之前，Jake在国际投资银行瑞士信贷工作了12年。他拥有北卡罗来纳大学的商学学士学位，主修经济学。\nWilmington.TMF救援犬 Jake Lerch 持有亚马逊和CrowdStrike的仓位。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐Adobe、亚马逊、CrowdStrike和Figma。《Motley Fool》推荐Palo Alto Networks，并推荐以下期权：做多2028年1月到期、执行价330美元的Adobe看涨期权，做空2028年1月到期、执行价340美元的Adobe看涨期权。《Motley Fool》有披露政策。提及的股票CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$262.95(+0.17%)+$0.46Motley Fool股票顾问的最新精选获取访问权限---%平均回报Figma纽约证券交易所：FIG$21.39(-1.72%)-$0.38*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-24T14:30:01+00:00"}},{"id":"news-246","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike 与 Okta：这两家网络安全巨头的营收趋势向投资者传递了什么信号","title_en":"CrowdStrike vs. OKTA: What Revenue Trends Between These Cybersecurity Giants Tell Investors | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool 对比 CrowdStrike 与 Okta 的季度营收趋势：CrowdStrike 截至2026年7月31日季度营收约15亿美元，Okta 约8.05亿美元，两者均实现环比增长。文章称人工智能加速漏洞识别与系统入侵，推升网络安全需求；CrowdStrike 为综合平台型方案，增长更快但尚未盈利，Okta 专注身份与访问管理，盈利为正、市销率更低。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool compares quarterly revenue trends for CrowdStrike and Okta. CrowdStrike reported about $1.5 billion for the quarter ended July 31, 2026, while Okta reported about $805 million, with both showing sequential growth. The article attributes demand to AI accelerating vulnerability discovery and system compromise. It notes CrowdStrike offers a broad platform with faster growth but no GAAP profit, while Okta focuses on identity and access management with positive earnings and a lower price-to-sales multiple.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:36:47.258984+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/charts/2026/09/08/crowdstrike-vs-okta-what-revenue-trends-between-these-cybersecurity-giants-tell-investors","content":"CrowdStrike: A Consistent Trajectory of Rapid Revenue ExpansionCrowdStrike (CRWD +1.80%) primarily generates revenue through recurring subscription sales of its comprehensive cloud-native cybersecurity software and protection modules.While expanding its internal research capabilities by establishing a dedicated new cybersecurity laboratory and simultaneously broadening external cloud infrastructure collaborations with major technology partners, it reported an operating margin of -2% for the quarter ended July 31, 2026.OKTA: A Reliable Pattern of Steady Revenue IncreasesOKTA (OKTA +1.01%) primarily generates revenue by selling identity and access management software subscriptions to diverse global enterprise customers.It recently introduced updated security protection tools tailored specifically for autonomous digital systems and issued formal administrative warnings to its users regarding active voice phishing campaigns, while it recorded an operating margin of 13% for the quarter ended July 31, 2026.Why Tracking Revenue Growth Matters for Long-Term InvestorsRevenue helps investors determine whether a specific business is successfully attracting and retaining paying customers over extended operational periods. This metric serves as a fundamental baseline measure of overall customer demand and business growth.Quarterly Revenue Trends for CrowdStrike and OKTACalendar quarterCrowdStrike RevenueOKTA RevenueQ3 2024$1.0 billion (quarter ended Oct. 31, 2024)$665.0 million (quarter ended Oct. 31, 2024)Q4 2024$1.1 billion (quarter ended Jan. 31, 2025)$682.0 million (quarter ended Jan. 31, 2025)Q1 2025$1.1 billion (quarter ended April 30, 2025)$688.0 million (quarter ended April 30, 2025)Q2 2025$1.2 billion (quarter ended July 31, 2025)$728.0 million (quarter ended July 31, 2025)Q3 2025$1.2 billion (quarter ended Oct. 31, 2025)$742.0 million (quarter ended Oct. 31, 2025)Q4 2025$1.3 billion (quarter ended Jan. 31, 2026)$761.0 million (quarter ended Jan. 31, 2026)Q1 2026$1.4 billion (quarter ended April 30, 2026)$765.0 million (quarter ended April 30, 2026)Q2 2026$1.5 billion (quarter ended July 31, 2026)$805.0 million (quarter ended July 31, 2026)Data source: Company filings. Data as of Sept. 8, 2026.Foolish TakeThe revenue trends for CrowdStrike and OKTA reveal several insights for investors. Both are experiencing quarter-over-quarter sales growth, an indication of the strong demand for their respective cybersecurity offerings. This is due to the rise of artificial intelligence.AI has demonstrated that it can identify security vulnerabilities and hack corporate systems at unprecedented speed. Consequently, CrowdStrike and OKTA's protections are seen as necessities, driving revenue expansion.CrowdStrike's rapid growth compared to OKTA illustrates the differences in their cybersecurity businesses. The former is a comprehensive solution, so it is able to attract a wider customer base. The latter focuses on the identity and access management markets within the digital security landscape, and this niche has led to a more steady sales growth trend.The difference in their businesses has also resulted in CrowdStrike's stock sporting a high valuation, as evidenced by its price-to-sale ratio (P/S) of 38 compared to OKTA's far more reasonable sales multiple of ten. Wall Street is expecting CrowdStrike's rapid growth to continue, but the company is not profitable. Meanwhile, OKTA's bottom line is positive and growing year over year, and with a lower P/S ratio, it's a better value for those interested in investing.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400Sep 14, 2026 •By Danny Vena, CPAWhy CrowdStrike Stock Rocketed Higher TodaySep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoCrowdStrike vs. UiPath: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoC3.ai vs. CrowdStrike: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 13, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoCybersecurity Is the Next Big Market for Artificial Intelligence (AI), According to Jensen Huang. This Super Stock-Split Stock Is the One to Own.About the AuthorRobert \"Izzy\" Izquierdo is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering information technology, consumer discretionary, consumer staples, and communication services sectors. Prior to The Motley Fool, Izzy was head of product management at Target Media Partners, developing and launching multimillion-dollar software used by businesses such as Charter Communications. Prior to that, he worked at Yahoo! and startups on software products in connected TV, AI, consumer apps, and digital advertising. He holds a bachelor’s degree in English literature from UCLA and is certified in software product management.TMFWryWriteRobert Izquierdo has positions in CrowdStrike and Okta. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike and Okta. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$245.70(+1.80%)+$4.34Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnOktaNASDAQ: OKTA$190.02(+1.01%)+$1.90*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"CrowdStrike：收入快速扩张的持续轨迹\nCrowdStrike（CRWD +1.80%）主要通过销售其全面的云原生网络安全软件和防护模块的经常性订阅来获得收入。在通过建立专门的新网络安全实验室来扩展内部研究能力的同时，并进一步扩大与主要科技合作伙伴的外部云基础设施合作，该公司报告称，截至2026年7月31日的季度营业利润率为-2%。\n\nOKTA：收入稳步增长的可靠模式\nOKTA（OKTA +1.01%）主要通过向全球各地的企业客户销售身份和访问管理软件订阅来获得收入。该公司最近推出了专门针对自主数字系统的更新版安全防护工具，并就正在进行的语音网络钓鱼活动向用户发布了正式的管理警告；截至2026年7月31日的季度，其营业利润率为13%。\n\n为什么跟踪收入增长对长期投资者很重要\n收入有助于投资者判断某项业务是否在较长的运营周期内成功吸引并留住付费客户。这一指标是衡量总体客户需求和业务增长的基本基准。\n\nCrowdStrike和OKTA的季度收入趋势\n日历季度｜CrowdStrike收入｜OKTA收入\n2024年第3季度｜10亿美元（截至2024年10月31日的季度）｜6.650亿美元（截至2024年10月31日的季度）\n2024年第4季度｜11亿美元（截至2025年1月31日的季度）｜6.820亿美元（截至2025年1月31日的季度）\n2025年第1季度｜11亿美元（截至2025年4月30日的季度）｜6.880亿美元（截至2025年4月30日的季度）\n2025年第2季度｜12亿美元（截至2025年7月31日的季度）｜7.280亿美元（截至2025年7月31日的季度）\n2025年第3季度｜12亿美元（截至2025年10月31日的季度）｜7.420亿美元（截至2025年10月31日的季度）\n2025年第4季度｜13亿美元（截至2026年1月31日的季度）｜7.610亿美元（截至2026年1月31日的季度）\n2026年第1季度｜14亿美元（截至2026年4月30日的季度）｜7.650亿美元（截至2026年4月30日的季度）\n2026年第2季度｜15亿美元（截至2026年7月31日的季度）｜8.050亿美元（截至2026年7月31日的季度）\n数据来源：公司文件。截至2026年9月8日的数据。\n\nFoolish观点\nCrowdStrike和OKTA的收入趋势为投资者揭示了若干重要信息。两家公司都在经历环比销售增长，这表明市场对各自网络安全产品的需求强劲。这是由人工智能的兴起所推动的。\n\n人工智能已经证明，它能够以前所未有的速度识别安全漏洞并入侵企业系统。因此，CrowdStrike和OKTA的防护措施被视为必需品，推动收入增长。\n\n与OKTA相比，CrowdStrike的快速增长体现了两家公司网络安全业务之间的差异。前者是一套全面解决方案，因此能够吸引更广泛的客户群。后者专注于数字安全领域中的身份和访问管理市场，而这一细分领域带来了更加稳定的销售增长趋势。\n\n两家公司业务的差异也导致CrowdStrike股票拥有较高估值，其市销率（P/S）为38，而OKTA的销售倍数合理得多，仅为10。华尔街预计CrowdStrike的快速增长将持续下去，但该公司尚未实现盈利。与此同时，OKTA的利润底线为正，并且同比增长，且市销率较低\n比率，对于有意投资的人来说，这是更高的性价比。接下来阅读2026年9月17日•作者：Catie Hogan《将在2027年称霸的2只网络安全股票》2026年9月15日•作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA《这只网络安全股票可能将1,000美元变成超过4,400美元》2026年9月14日•作者：Danny Vena，CPA《CrowdStrike股票今天为何大幅上涨》2026年9月14日•作者：Sara Appino《CrowdStrike对比UiPath：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？》2026年9月14日•作者：Sara Appino《C3.ai对比CrowdStrike：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？》2026年9月13日•作者：Adam Spatacco《据Jensen Huang所说，网络安全是人工智能（AI）的下一个大型市场。这只超级拆股股票值得持有。》关于作者Robert \"Izzy\" Izquierdo是《Motley Fool》特约股市分析师，负责报道信息技术、非必需消费品、必需消费品和通信服务行业。在加入《Motley Fool》之前，Izzy曾任Target Media Partners产品管理负责人，负责开发并推出数百万美元级的软件，供Charter Communications等企业使用。在此之前，他曾在Yahoo!和初创公司从事软件产品工作，涉及联网电视、AI、消费者应用和数字广告。他拥有加州大学洛杉矶分校英语文学学士学位，并持有软件产品管理认证。TMFWryWriteRobert Izquierdo持有CrowdStrike和Okta的仓位。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐CrowdStrike和Okta。《Motley Fool》实行披露政策。提及的股票CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$245.70（+1.80%）+$4.34Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个交易日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-08T21:32:26+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1794","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"今日股市1月20日：分析师上调评级强调AI服务器CPU增长，英特尔上涨","title_en":"Stock Market Today, Jan. 20: Intel Rises on Analyst Upgrades Highlighting AI Server CPU Growth | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"英特尔股价周二收于48.56美元，上涨3.41%，此前多家券商在第四季度财报发布前上调其评级，分析师强调AI驱动的服务器CPU增长率今年有望高达40%。成交量达1.451亿股，较三个月均值高出约56%。当日标普500下跌2.06%，纳斯达克综合指数下跌2.39%，英伟达下跌4.38%，市场整体呈避险情绪。期权市场预计英特尔财报后股价波动约8.8%。","summary_en":"Intel shares closed Tuesday at $48.56, up 3.41%, after multiple brokerages upgraded the stock ahead of its fourth-quarter earnings report, with analysts highlighting expected AI-driven server CPU growth of up to 40% this year. Trading volume reached 145.1 million shares, about 56% above its three-month average. The S&P 500 fell 2.06% and the Nasdaq Composite lost 2.39%, while Nvidia dropped 4.38% amid a broader risk-off trade. Options markets anticipate an approximately 8.8% move after Intel's Q4 report.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:42.273687+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/01/20/stock-market-today-jan-20-intel-rises-on-analyst-upgrades-highlighting-ai-server-cpu-growth","content":"ExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%Intel (INTC +7.67%), a designer and manufacturer of microprocessors and related semiconductor products, closed Tuesday at $48.56, up 3.41%. Shares moved higher after multiple brokerages upgraded the stock ahead of fourth-quarter earnings. Investors are also watching upcoming results and guidance for confirmation of improving AI-driven server central processing unit (CPU) demand.Trading volume reached 145.1 million shares, coming in about 56% above compared with its three-month average of 93 million shares. Intel IPO'd in 1980 and has grown 14,818% since going public.How the markets moved todayThe S&P 500 (^GSPC +1.14%) fell 2.06% to 6,797, while the Nasdaq Composite (^IXIC +1.69%) lost 2.39% to finish at 22,954. Among semiconductors, Advanced Micro Devices (AMD +6.36%) closed at $231.92 (+0.04%), while Nvidia (NVDA +2.54%) closed at $178.07, down 4.38%, underscoring mixed sentiment across chipmakers.What this means for investorsAnalyst upgrades drove Intel shares higher today, bucking the overall market trend. The semiconductor stock was one of the rare exceptions to today’s “risk off” trade spurred by new tariff threats from President Trump over the weekend. Several analysts highlighted expected AI-driven CPU growth rates of up to 40% this year. That gave Intel shares momentum as the company’s earnings report approaches later this week. Options markets are anticipating an approximately 8.8% move in response to Intel’s Q4 report, highlighting traders’ views that earnings and updates on its foundry strategy are pivotal turning points in the company's turnaround story.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorHoward Smith is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering technology and industrial stocks. Prior to The Motley Fool, Howard spent nearly 30 years supervising quality and operations in the steel industry, mostly with leading steel company Nucor. He holds a bachelor’s degree in metallurgical engineering from Lafayette College and a master’s degree in environmental engineering from Johns Hopkins University.TMFBuilt2LastHoward Smith has positions in Intel and Nvidia and has the following options: short February 2026 $170 calls on Nvidia and short March 2026 $26 calls on Intel. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Advanced Micro Devices, Intel, and Nvidia. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnAdvanced Micro DevicesNASDAQ: AMD$545.09(+6.36%)+$32.59NvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"展开NASDAQ：INTC英特尔高级功能Moneyball Superscore67/100今日变动(7.67%) $7.75当前价格$108.80关键数据点市值$575B市值仅按公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。当日区间$104.70 - $111.37 52周区间$28.73 - $142.35成交量4.6M平均成交量109.7M毛利率39.05%英特尔（INTC +7.67%）是一家微处理器及相关半导体产品的设计和制造商，周二收于$48.56，上涨3.41%。多家券商在第四季度财报发布前上调该股评级，推动股价走高。投资者也在关注即将公布的业绩和指引，以确认由AI推动的服务器中央处理器（CPU）需求正在改善。\n\n成交量达到1.451亿股，比其9300万股的三个月平均成交量高出约56%。英特尔于1980年上市，自上市以来已增长14,818%。\n\n今日市场走势\n标普500指数（^GSPC +1.14%）下跌2.06%，至6,797点；纳斯达克综合指数（^IXIC +1.69%）下跌2.39%，收于22,954点。在半导体股中，超威半导体（AMD +6.36%）收于$231.92（+0.04%），而英伟达（NVDA +2.54%）收于$178.07，下跌4.38%，凸显芯片制造商之间情绪不一。\n\n这对投资者意味着什么\n分析师上调评级推动英特尔股价今日上涨，逆势于整体市场走势。这只半导体股票是今日由特朗普总统周末提出的新关税威胁引发的“避险”交易中少有的例外。多位分析师强调，今年由AI驱动的CPU增长率预计最高可达40%。随着公司将在本周晚些时候发布财报，这为英特尔股价带来了动能。期权市场预计英特尔第四季度报告发布后股价将出现约8.8%的波动，这凸显交易员认为，业绩以及其晶圆代工战略的更新，是该公司扭亏故事中的关键转折点。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Johnny Rice\n英特尔股票今日为何上涨7.6%\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Emma Newbery\n今日股市，9月17日：传闻与SK海力士洽谈，英特尔飙升8%\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Joe Tenebruso\n英特尔股票今日为何上涨\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Daniel Sparks\nSK海力士正与英特尔洽谈在美国制造存储芯片。这可能对英特尔股票意味着什么。\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Howard Smith\n今日股市，9月16日：英特尔因与SK海力士洽谈制造存储芯片而上涨\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Scott Levine\n2026年6只最佳物联网股票及投资方法\n\n关于作者\nHoward Smith是Motley Fool的特约股票市场分析师，负责科技和工业股报道。加入The Motley Fool之前，Howard曾在钢铁行业监督质量和运营近30年，主要任职于领先钢铁公司Nucor。他拥有拉斐特学院冶金工程学学士学位，以及约翰斯·霍普金斯大学环境工程学硕士学位。\n\nTMFBuilt2Last\nHoward Smith持有英特尔和英伟达的头寸，并拥有以下期权：卖出英伟达2026年2月到期、行权价$170的看涨期权，以及卖出英特尔2026年3月到期、行权价$26的看涨期权。The Motley Fool持有并推荐超威半导体、英特尔和英伟达。The Motley Fool有披露政策。\n\n提及的股票\n英特尔\nNASDAQ：INTC\n$108.80\n(+7.67%)\n+$7.75\n\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报\n\n超威半导体\nNASDAQ：AMD\n$545.09\n(+6.36%)\n+$32.59\n\n英伟达\nNASDAQ：NVDA\n$219.34\n(+2.54%)\n+$5.44\n\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报按前一个交易日收盘价计算。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-01-20T22:41:46+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1704","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"今日股市1月28日：传英伟达与苹果代工合作，英特尔股价飙升","title_en":"Stock Market Today, Jan. 28: Intel Surges After Reports of Nvidia and Apple Foundry Partnerships | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"英特尔股价周三收于48.78美元，上涨11.04%，此前有报道称英伟达和苹果可能将部分2028年芯片生产转移至英特尔，同时公司CEO买入股票及分析师给出高目标价也提振了股价。成交量达2亿股，较三个月均值高出约107%。不过文章提醒，英特尔股价仍未从上周第四季度财报公布后两位数的跌幅中恢复，该财报显示3亿美元GAAP亏损及持续的供应限制。","summary_en":"Intel shares closed Wednesday at $48.78, up 11.04%, after reports that Nvidia and Apple may shift some 2028 chip production to Intel, alongside news of insider buying by the CEO and a high analyst price target. Trading volume reached 200 million shares, about 107% above its three-month average. The article notes Intel shares have still not recovered from their double-digit fall after last week's Q4 2025 earnings report, which showed a $300 million GAAP loss and ongoing supply constraints.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:19.511992+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/01/28/stock-market-today-jan-28-intel-surges-after-reports-of-nvidia-and-apple-foundry-partnerships","content":"ExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%Intel (INTC +7.67%), designs and manufactures microprocessors and related technologies, closed Wednesday at $48.78, up 11.04%. The stock moved higher after reports of prospective Nvidia and Apple foundry deals and insider buying. Investors are watching whether these partnerships can offset earlier concerns about Intel’s 2026 outlook.Trading volume reached 200 million shares, about 107% above its three-month average of 96 million shares. Intel IPO'd in 1980 and has grown 14,885% since going public.How the markets moved todayS&P 500 (^GSPC +1.14%) slipped 0.01% to 6,978, while the Nasdaq Composite (^IXIC +1.69%) rose 0.17% to 23,857. Within semiconductors, industry peers Advanced Micro Devices (AMD +6.36%) closed at $252.74 (up 0.28%) and Nvidia (NVDA +2.54%) finished at $191.52 (up 1.59%), trailing Intel’s sharper rebound.What this means for investorsIntel’s market move today can be mostly attributed to a pre-market report suggesting that Nvidia and Apple (AAPL +1.38%) may shift some of their 2028 chip production to Intel. While the highest-end chips will still be manufactured by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing Company (TSM +3.00%), any business shifting to Intel is good news for its foundry ambitions. Other news about Intel’s CEO buying stock and a high price target from an analyst likely added to the stock’s great day.Despite today’s good news, it’s worth remembering that Intel’s shares have still not recovered from their double-digit fall after last week’s Q4 2025 earnings report that showed a $300 million GAAP loss and ongoing supply constraints. Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorJeff Santoro is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering technology and consumer goods. In addition to his work with The Motley Fool, he is co-host of the Investing Unscripted podcast and serves as a public school administrator. Jeff holds both bachelor’s and master’s degrees in music education from Rutgers University.TMFMktmusician@marketmusicianJeff Santoro has positions in Apple and Nvidia. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Advanced Micro Devices, Apple, Intel, Nvidia, and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnAdvanced Micro DevicesNASDAQ: AMD$545.09(+6.36%)+$32.59NvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"展开NASDAQ: INTC英特尔高级功能Moneyball超级评分67/100今日涨跌(7.67%) $7.75当前价格$108.80关键数据点市值$575B市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权结构中的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$104.70 - $111.3752周区间$28.73 - $142.35成交量4.6M平均成交量109.7M毛利率39.05%英特尔（INTC +7.67%）设计并制造微处理器及相关技术，周三收于48.78美元，上涨11.04%。在有关英伟达和苹果潜在晶圆代工合作以及内部人士买入的报道后，该股走高。投资者正在关注这些合作能否抵消此前对英特尔2026年展望的担忧。成交量达到2亿股，比三个月平均成交量9600万股高出约107%。英特尔于1980年首次公开募股，自上市以来上涨14,885%。今日市场走势标普500指数（^GSPC +1.14%）下跌0.01%，至6,978点；纳斯达克综合指数（^IXIC +1.69%）上涨0.17%，至23,857点。在半导体行业中，同行超威半导体（AMD +6.36%）收于252.74美元（上涨0.28%），英伟达（NVDA +2.54%）收于191.52美元（上涨1.59%），均落后于英特尔更为强劲的反弹。这对投资者意味着什么英特尔今日的市场走势主要可归因于一份盘前报告，该报告称英伟达和苹果（AAPL +1.38%）可能会将部分2028年芯片生产转移给英特尔。尽管最高端芯片仍将由台积电（TSM +3.00%）制造，但任何转移给英特尔的业务都将利好其晶圆代工业务。有关英特尔首席执行官买入股票以及分析师给出高目标价的其他消息，可能也助推了该股的出色表现。尽管今日有利好消息，但值得记住的是，英特尔股价仍未从上周公布2025年第四季度财报后出现的两位数跌幅中恢复；该财报显示美国通用会计准则亏损3亿美元，并且供应限制仍在持续。接下来阅读2026年9月17日•作者：Johnny Rice英特尔股票今日为何上涨7.6%2026年9月17日•作者：Emma Newbery今日股市，9月17日：传SK海力士洽谈后英特尔飙升8%2026年9月16日•作者：Joe Tenebruso英特尔股票今日为何上涨2026年9月16日•作者：Daniel SparksSK海力士正与英特尔洽谈在美国制造存储芯片。这对英特尔股票意味着什么？2026年9月16日•作者：Howard Smith今日股市，9月16日：英特尔因SK海力士存储芯片制造洽谈而上涨2026年9月16日•作者：Scott Levine2026年值得关注的6只物联网股票及投资方法关于作者Jeff Santoro是《Motley Fool》特约股市分析师，负责科技和消费品领域。除在《Motley Fool》工作外，他还是Investing Unscripted播客的联合主持人，并担任公立学校管理人员。Jeff拥有罗格斯大学音乐教育学士和硕士学位。TMFMktmusician@marketmusicianJeff Santoro持有苹果和英伟达的仓位。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐超威半导体、苹果、英特尔、英伟达和台积电，并设有披露政策。提及的股票英特尔NASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报超威半导体NASDAQ: AMD$545.09(+6.36%)+$32.59英伟达NASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报根据前一交易日收盘价计算。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-01-28T22:03:55+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1095","ktid":5775050,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"5775050","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"今日股市4月27日：传与OpenAI合作开发智能手机芯片，高通上涨","title_en":"Stock Market Today, April 27: Qualcomm Rises on Reported OpenAI Smartphone Chip Collaboration | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"高通股价周一收于150.26美元，上涨0.95%，此前有报道称该公司正与OpenAI合作开发面向AI的智能手机处理器，凸显在移动设备上直接运行先进模型的兴趣日益增长。成交量达4160万股，较三个月均值高出约242%。文章指出，与OpenAI的合作预计影响长远，商业收益可能要到未来产品周期才会显现，高通即将发布的财报仍将取决于智能手机需求、授权收入及汽车和边缘计算领域的多元化进展。","summary_en":"Qualcomm shares closed Monday at $150.26, up 0.95%, after reports that the company is working with OpenAI on AI-focused smartphone processors, highlighting growing interest in running advanced models directly on mobile devices. Trading volume reached 41.6 million shares, roughly 242% above its three-month average. The article notes the OpenAI opportunity is expected to have a long-term impact, with commercial benefits likely in future product cycles, while Qualcomm's upcoming earnings will depend on smartphone demand, licensing revenue, and diversification in automotive and edge computing.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:23.057423+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/04/27/stock-market-today-april-27-qualcomm-rises-on-reported-openai-smartphone-chip-collaboration","content":"ExpandNASDAQ: QCOMQualcommPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore81/100Today's Change(2.09%) $3.87Current Price$188.71Key Data PointsMarket Cap$198BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$187.76 - $191.9152wk Range$121.99 - $259.92Volume90.6KAvg Vol14.2MGross Margin54.23%Dividend Yield1.92%Qualcomm (QCOM +2.09%), a developer of wireless communication technologies and semiconductors for mobile devices and networks, closed Monday at $150.26 up 0.95%. The stock moved higher after reports of a potential OpenAI smartphone-chip collaboration and during Monday’s session investors are watching how this AI opportunity could reshape Qualcomm’s growth mix ahead of its earnings release.The company’s trading volume reached 41.6 million shares, which is roughly 242% above compared with its three-month average of 12.1 million shares. Qualcomm IPO'd in 1991 and has grown 27,052% since going public.How the markets moved todayThe S&P 500 (^GSPC +1.14%) added 0.12% to finish Monday at 7,173.91, while the Nasdaq Composite (^IXIC +1.69%) gained 0.20% to close at 24,887.10. Among semiconductors, industry peers Texas Instruments (TXN -0.97%) closed at $269.50 (-2.77%) and Broadcom (AVGO +2.29%) finished at $418.20 (-1.08%), lagging Qualcomm’s AI-fueled advance.What this means for investorsQualcomm shares rose after reports that the company is working with OpenAI on AI-focused smartphone processors, a development that highlights growing interest in running advanced models directly on mobile devices. The potential shift toward on-device AI is particularly relevant for Qualcomm, whose chipsets sit at the center of the smartphone upgrade cycle and could benefit if more processing moves from the cloud to the device.However, the opportunity with OpenAI is expected to have a long-term impact, with commercial benefits likely to materialize in future product cycles rather than in the near term. Qualcomm’s upcoming earnings will remain dependent on smartphone demand, licensing revenue, and ongoing diversification efforts in automotive and edge computing. Investors will now be watching to see if Qualcomm demonstrates stable handset demand and maintains margin support while positioning its AI capabilities to drive future growth.Read NextSep 15, 2026 •By Erin KennedyApplied Materials vs. Qualcomm: Which Tech Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 14, 2026 •By David Jagielski, CPAThis Could Be the Most Underrated Artificial Intelligence Stock to Buy Right NowSep 13, 2026 •By Scott Levine12 Best 5G Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 11, 2026 •By Parkev Tatevosian, CFAAmazon Delivers Fantastic News for Qualcomm Stock InvestorsSep 11, 2026 •By Sara AppinoAdvanced Micro Devices vs. Qualcomm: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 11, 2026 •By Daniel SparksQualcomm Sold Server Chips Once Before and Quit Within a Year. History Says What Has to Be Different This Time.About the AuthorEric Trie is a Motley Fool contributing stock analyst covering technology and semiconductors, healthcare, financial services, and consumer sectors. Previously, he worked in investment analysis and financial writing. He holds a B.A. in Philosophy from Rutgers University. Eric lives in New York City and is an avid sports fan.CMFIdeaMachineEric Trie has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Broadcom, Qualcomm, and Texas Instruments. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedQualcommNASDAQ: QCOM$188.71(+2.09%)+$3.87Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnTexas InstrumentsNASDAQ: TXN$258.14(-0.97%)-$2.53BroadcomNASDAQ: AVGO$347.30(+2.29%)+$7.79*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"展开NASDAQ：QCOM 高通 高级功能 Moneyball 超级评分 81/100 今日变动（2.09%）$3.87 当前价格 $188.71 关键数据点 市值 $198B。市值仅使用公开交易的流通股计算，不包括未上市、私人持有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间 $187.76 - $191.91 52周区间 $121.99 - $259.92 成交量 90.6K 平均成交量 14.2M 毛利率 54.23% 股息率 1.92% 高通（QCOM +2.09%）是一家为移动设备和网络开发无线通信技术及半导体的公司，周一收于150.26美元，上涨0.95%。在有报道称其可能与OpenAI合作开发智能手机芯片后，股价走高；周一交易期间，投资者正关注这一人工智能机会在公司公布财报前可能如何重塑高通的增长结构。公司成交量达到4160万股，约比三个月平均成交量1210万股高242%。高通于1991年首次公开募股，自上市以来增长了27,052%。今日市场走势 标普500指数（^GSPC +1.14%）上涨0.12%，周一收于7,173.91点；纳斯达克综合指数（^IXIC +1.69%）上涨0.20%，收于24,887.10点。在半导体领域，同行德州仪器（TXN -0.97%）收于269.50美元（-2.77%），博通（AVGO +2.29%）收于418.20美元（-1.08%），表现落后于高通受人工智能推动的涨势。这对投资者意味着什么 有报道称高通正与OpenAI合作开发面向人工智能的智能手机处理器，随后高通股价上涨。这一进展凸显出人们对直接在移动设备上运行先进模型的兴趣日益增长。向设备端人工智能转移的潜在趋势与高通尤其相关，因为其芯片组处于智能手机升级周期的核心；如果更多处理从云端转移到设备端，高通可能从中受益。然而，与OpenAI的机会预计将产生长期影响，商业收益可能会在未来的产品周期中实现，而不是在近期实现。高通即将发布的财报仍将取决于智能手机需求、授权收入以及在汽车和边缘计算领域持续推进的多元化努力。投资者现在将关注高通能否证明手机需求稳定、维持利润率支撑，同时布局其人工智能能力以推动未来增长。接下来阅读 2026年9月15日 •作者：Erin Kennedy 应用材料与高通：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？ 2026年9月14日 •作者：David Jagielski，CPA 这可能是目前最被低估、值得买入的人工智能股票 2026年9月13日 •作者：Scott Levine 2026年12只最佳5G股票及投资方法 2026年9月11日 •作者：Parkev Tatevosian，CFA 亚马逊为高通股票投资者带来绝佳消息 2026年9月11日 •作者：Sara Appino 超威半导体与高通：哪只科技股更值得买？ 2026年9月11日 •作者：Daniel Sparks 高通曾经销售服务器芯片，但不到一年就退出了。历史表明这次必须有哪些不同。关于作者 Eric Trie 是《Motley Fool》的特约股票分析师，负责科技和半导体、医疗保健、金融服务及消费领域。他此前从事投资分析和财经写作，拥有罗格斯大学哲学学士学位。Eric 居住在纽约市，是一名狂热的体育迷。CMFIdeaMachine Eric Trie 未持有文中提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐博通、高通和德州仪器。《Motley Fool》有披露政策。提及的股票 高通 NASDAQ：QCOM $188.71（+2.09%）+$3.87 Motley Fool 股票顾问最新推荐 获取权限 ---% 平均回报 德州仪器 NASDAQ：TXN $258.14（-0.97%）-$2.53 博通 NASDAQ：AVGO $347.30（+2.29%）+$7.79 *自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-04-27T22:23:02+00:00"}},{"id":"news-937","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"今日股市5月18日：AI泡沫风险警告抵消早盘涨幅，英特尔收跌","title_en":"Stock Market Today, May 18: Intel Slips After AI Bubble Risk Warning Offsets Early Gains | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool报道，英特尔（INTC）周一收于108.17美元，下跌0.55%，盘中受AI泡沫风险警告与获利了结影响走低。成交量约1.439亿股，较三个月均值高约26%。同期标普500微跌0.07%，纳斯达克跌0.51%，AMD与英伟达亦承压。花旗分析师将目标价从95美元上调至130美元，Benchmark给出140美元目标价，看好AI动能延续。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reported that Intel (INTC) closed Monday at $108.17, down 0.55%, pressured by profit-taking and a fresh warning about potential AI bubble risk. Volume reached about 143.9 million shares, roughly 26% above its three-month average. The S&P 500 slipped 0.07% and the Nasdaq fell 0.51%, with AMD and Nvidia also under pressure. Citigroup raised its price target to $130 from $95, while Benchmark set a $140 target, citing continued AI momentum.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:51:05.537449+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/coverage/stock-market-today/2026/05/18/stock-market-today-may-18-intel-slips-after-ai-bubble-risk-warning-offsets-early-gains","content":"ExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.5MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%Intel (INTC +7.67%), a major PC and data center chipmaker, closed Monday at $108.17, down 0.55%. The stock slipped during the regular session as traders weighed recent earnings strength and AI-driven momentum against profit-taking after last week’s volatility and a fresh warning about potential AI “bubble risk.”Trading volume reached 143.9 million shares, coming in about 26% above its three-month average of 113.8 million shares. Intel IPO'd in 1980 and has grown 33,130% since going public.How the markets moved todayThe S&P 500 (^GSPC +1.14%) inched down 0.07% to 7,403, while the Nasdaq Composite (^IXIC +1.69%) fell 0.51% to 26,091 as growth stocks eased. Among semiconductors, Advanced Micro Devices (AMD +6.36%) closed at $420.99 (-0.73%) and Nvidia (NVDA +2.54%) finished at $222.32 (-1.33%), underscoring broad sector pressure on chipmakers.What this means for investorsIntel stock has been on a tear, nearly tripling this year, even after a recent pullback. The stock has dropped more than 15% in the past four trading sessions. It’s not surprising to see profit-taking after the stock’s massive surge even as two Wall Street analysts raised price targets today. Citigroup (C -0.19%) analyst Atif Malik raises his target share price to $130 from $95 per share, while Benchmark Equity Research analyst Cody Acree is also bullish with a new $140 price target. Both views see AI momentum continuing, giving Intel shares room for further upside. If the total market for CPUs grows by 35% annually due to demand for processors that support AI agents., as Malik thinks is possible, Intel may resume its rise soon.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorHoward Smith is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering technology and industrial stocks. Prior to The Motley Fool, Howard spent nearly 30 years supervising quality and operations in the steel industry, mostly with leading steel company Nucor. He holds a bachelor’s degree in metallurgical engineering from Lafayette College and a master’s degree in environmental engineering from Johns Hopkins University.TMFBuilt2LastCitigroup is an advertising partner of Motley Fool Money. Howard Smith has positions in Nvidia. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Advanced Micro Devices, Intel, and Nvidia. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnAdvanced Micro DevicesNASDAQ: AMD$545.09(+6.36%)+$32.59NvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"展开NASDAQ：INTC英特尔高级功能Moneyball超级评分67/100今日变动(7.67%) $7.75当前价格$108.80关键数据点市值$575B市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$104.70 - $111.3752周区间$28.73 - $142.35成交量4.5M平均成交量109.7M毛利率39.05%英特尔（INTC +7.67%）是一家主要的个人电脑和数据中心芯片制造商，周一收于$108.17，下跌0.55%。在常规交易时段，随着交易员权衡近期盈利强劲表现和人工智能驱动的势头、上周波动后获利了结的压力，以及关于潜在人工智能“泡沫风险”的最新警告，该股出现下滑。\n成交量达到1.439亿股，比三个月平均水平1.138亿股高出约26%。英特尔于1980年首次公开募股，自上市以来增长了33,130%。\n今日市场走势\n标普500指数（^GSPC +1.14%）下跌0.07%，至7,403点；纳斯达克综合指数（^IXIC +1.69%）下跌0.51%，至26,091点，因成长型股票走弱。在半导体板块中，超威半导体（AMD +6.36%）收于$420.99（-0.73%），英伟达（NVDA +2.54%）收于$222.32（-1.33%），凸显芯片制造商面临的广泛板块压力。\n这对投资者意味着什么\n英特尔股票今年一路飙升，几乎翻了三倍，即使近期出现回调。过去四个交易日，该股已下跌超过15%。尽管今天两位华尔街分析师上调了目标价，在股价大幅飙升后看到获利了结并不令人意外。花旗集团（C -0.19%）分析师 Atif Malik 将目标股价从每股$95上调至$130；Benchmark Equity Research 分析师 Cody Acree 也持乐观态度，将目标价设为$140。两种观点都认为人工智能势头将持续，这为英特尔股票进一步上涨留下空间。如果由于市场对支持人工智能代理处理器的需求，CPU总市场每年增长35%，正如 Malik 认为可能发生的那样，英特尔可能很快恢复上涨。\n继续阅读2026年9月17日 •作者：Johnny Rice英特尔股票今日为何上涨7.6%2026年9月17日 •作者：Emma Newbery今日股市，9月17日：传闻 SK 海力士谈判推动英特尔飙升8%2026年9月16日 •作者：Joe Tenebruso英特尔股票今日为何上涨2026年9月16日 •作者：Daniel SparksSK 海力士正与英特尔洽谈在美国制造内存芯片。这对英特尔股票意味着什么。2026年9月16日 •作者：Howard Smith今日股市，9月16日：SK 海力士内存芯片制造谈判推动英特尔上涨2026年9月16日 •作者：Scott Levine2026年6只最佳物联网股票及投资方法\n关于作者\nHoward Smith 是 Motley Fool 的特约股市分析师，负责科技和工业股票。在加入 Motley Fool 之前，Howard 在钢铁行业主管质量和运营近30年，主要任职于领先钢铁公司 Nucor。他拥有拉斐特学院冶金工程学士学位和约翰斯·霍普金斯大学环境工程硕士学位。\nTMFBuilt2Last\n花旗集团是 Motley Fool Money 的广告合作伙伴。Howard Smith 持有英伟达的仓位。Motley Fool 持有并推荐超威半导体、英特尔和英伟达。Motley Fool 制定了信息披露政策。\n提及的股票\n英特尔\nNASDAQ：INTC\n$108.80（+7.67%）+$7.75\nMotley Fool 股票顾问的最新推荐\n获取权限\n---%平均回报\n超威半导体\nNASDAQ：AMD\n$545.09（+6.36%）+$32.59\n英伟达\nNASDAQ：NVDA\n$219.34（+2.54%）+$5.44\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-05-18T21:14:08+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3645","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"一个惊人趋势解释了CrowdStrike股价200%的涨幅","title_en":"1 Incredible Trend Explains CrowdStrike's Amazing 200% Gain. | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章指出，CrowdStrike股价自2023年初以来上涨200%，主要受网络犯罪激增推动。2024年2月Change Healthcare遭大规模攻击，促使企业加快安全支出。CrowdStrike凭借AI驱动的安全模块，营收从2017财年5300万美元增至2023财年22亿美元，2024财年再增36%至31亿美元，超62%客户购买五个以上模块。作者认为该股仍值得买入。","summary_en":"Motley Fool notes CrowdStrike shares have risen 200% since early 2023, driven by surging cybercrime. The February 2024 Change Healthcare attack pushed organizations to boost security spending. CrowdStrike's AI-powered modules helped revenue grow from $53 million in fiscal 2017 to over $2.2 billion in fiscal 2023, then another 36% to $3.1 billion in fiscal 2024, with over 62% of customers buying five or more modules. The author considers the stock still worth buying.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:17:20.660454+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2024/03/19/1-incredible-trend-crowdstrikes-amazing-gain","content":"It's been a wonderful 15 months for CrowdStrike Holdings (CRWD -1.07%) shareholders. The company's stock has risen 200% since the beginning of 2023.\nBut the question remains: Is CrowdStrike still a buy after this incredible rally?\nI think it is. Here's why.\nThe world is teeming with cybercrime\nThe news is filled with examples of large-scale cyber attacks. The latest catastrophic case is the Feb. 2024 attack on Change Healthcare, which has disrupted claims payments for hundreds of thousands of medical providers.\nWith so many cybercriminals eager to cause chaos, organizations are having to spend quickly to upgrade their defenses. No one wants to be the next victim of a major attack.\nCrowdStrike's revenue is soaring as cyber spending ramps up\nEven before the most recent headlines, CrowdStrike had been gaining momentum thanks to its AI-powered cybersecurity modules that help its customers protect their systems, data, and endpoints.\nAs you can see in the chart below, the company's revenue has skyrocketed from $53 million in fiscal 2017 to over $2.2 billion in fiscal 2023.\nImage source: Statista.\nWhat's more, the company grew its top line another 36% in fiscal 2024 to $3.1 billion. The company's subscription-based model seems to be paying off as its customers continue to ramp up their security spending. Indeed, the company reports that over 62% of its customers purchase more than five of its security modules.\nIs CrowdStrike a buy now?\nAs organizations large and small bolster their cybersecurity defenses, industry leaders like CrowdStrike are answering the call. That demand is fueling rapid top line growth for the company, and its margins and profits are also improving.\nFor investors willing to buy and hold, CrowdStrike remains a stock worth considering.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400About the AuthorJake Lerch is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering artificial intelligence, cloud computing, cybersecurity, e-commerce, and semiconductors. Prior to The Motley Fool, Jake worked for 12 years at Credit Suisse, an international investment bank. He holds a bachelor’s degree in business with a concentration in economics from the University of North Carolina at Wilmington.TMFRescueDogJake Lerch has positions in CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$259.67(-1.07%)-$2.82Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"对于CrowdStrike Holdings（CRWD -1.07%）的股东来说，这是美妙的15个月。自2023年初以来，该公司股价已上涨200%。\n但问题仍然存在：经历这轮惊人上涨后，CrowdStrike仍值得买入吗？\n我认为值得。以下是原因。\n世界充斥着网络犯罪\n新闻中充满了大规模网络攻击的例子。最近一次灾难性事件是2024年2月对Change Healthcare的攻击，该事件扰乱了数十万家医疗服务提供商的理赔付款。\n随着如此多的网络犯罪分子急于制造混乱，各组织不得不迅速投入资金升级防御措施。没有人想成为重大攻击的下一个受害者。\n随着网络安全支出增加，CrowdStrike的收入正在飙升\n甚至在最近的新闻出现之前，CrowdStrike就已凭借其人工智能驱动的网络安全模块获得发展势头，这些模块帮助客户保护其系统、数据和终端。\n如下图所示，该公司收入已从2017财年的5,300万美元飙升至2023财年的超过22亿美元。\n图片来源：Statista。\n更重要的是，公司2024财年营收又增长36%，达到31亿美元。随着客户继续增加安全支出，该公司的订阅制模式似乎正在奏效。事实上，公司报告称，超过62%的客户购买了五个以上的安全模块。\n现在是买入CrowdStrike的时候吗？\n随着大小组织纷纷加强网络安全防御，CrowdStrike等行业领导者正在响应这一需求。这种需求推动公司营收快速增长，其利润率和利润也在改善。\n对于愿意买入并持有的投资者来说，CrowdStrike仍是一只值得考虑的股票。继续阅读2026年9月24日•作者：Jake LerchCrowdStrike对决Figma：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？2026年9月23日•作者：Adam Spatacco不是Palantir，也不是美光。Jim Cramer刚刚称这家价值3,250亿美元的英伟达合作伙伴为“必买”股票2026年9月22日•作者：Pamela KockCrowdStrike对决Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？2026年9月21日•作者：Leo Sun现在可以买入的两只百万富翁制造者网络安全股2026年9月17日•作者：Catie Hogan两只将在2027年称霸的网络安全股2026年9月15日•作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA这只网络安全股可能将1,000美元变成超过4,400美元关于作者Jake Lerch是《Motley Fool》的特约科技分析师，负责报道人工智能、云计算、网络安全、电子商务和半导体。在加入《Motley Fool》之前，Jake在国际投资银行瑞士信贷工作了12年。他拥有北卡罗来纳大学威尔明顿分校商学学士学位，专业方向为经济学。TMFRescueDogJake Lerch持有CrowdStrike的仓位。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐CrowdStrike。《Motley Fool》有披露政策。提及的股票CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$259.67（-1.07%）-$2.82《Motley Fool》股票顾问的最新推荐获取访问权限---% 平均回报*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2024-03-19T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2722","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"若六年前投资1万美元于CrowdStrike Holdings股票，如今价值几何？","title_en":"If You'd Invested $10,000 in CrowdStrike Holdings Stock 6 Years Ago, Here's How Much You'd Have Today | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章回顾，若2019年投资1万美元于CrowdStrike，如今价值超13.4万美元，总回报超1200%，年复合增长率52%，远超标普500的129%回报。公司过去12个月营收增长1560%至41亿美元，分析师预计本财年营收达48亿美元。但文章也提示估值偏高、市销率超28倍及盈利不稳定等风险，认为适合成长型投资者。","summary_en":"A Motley Fool article reviews that a $10,000 investment in CrowdStrike in 2019 would be worth over $134,000 today, a total return exceeding 1,200% and a 52% CAGR, far outpacing the S&P 500's 129% return. Revenue has grown 1,560% to $4.1 billion over the trailing 12 months, with analysts projecting $4.8 billion this fiscal year. The article also flags risks including a rich valuation above 28 times sales and inconsistent profitability, deeming it suitable for growth investors.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:16:49.124862+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2025/06/18/if-youd-invested-10000-in-crowdstrike-holdings-sto","content":"You never know how things are going to turn out in the stock market. Some stocks go up, some go down, and others move sideways for years at a time. With that in mind, I'll review how a $10,000 investment in CrowdStrike Holdings (CRWD -1.07%) stock would have changed over the last six years.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-1.07%) $-2.82Current Price$259.67Key Data PointsMarket Cap$269BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$258.53 - $263.8752wk Range$85.68 - $263.87Volume8.4MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nTo put it simply, a $10,000 investment in CrowdStrike stock in 2019 was a very smart move. After many ups and downs along the way, that initial investment would be worth over $134,000 today. That works out to a total return of more than 1,200%, or a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of 52%.\nCompare that to the performance of the benchmark, the S&P 500 (^GSPC -0.02%), which has generated a total return of 129% over six years, or a CAGR of less than 15%.\nCRWD Total Return Level data by YCharts.\nThe biggest reason for CrowdStrike's excellent stock performance is the company's skyrocketing revenue. Since 2019, the company's trailing 12-month revenue has climbed by 1,560% to a total of $4.1 billion.\nWhat's more, Wall Street analysts are predicting even more of that explosive growth for the company. According to estimates compiled by Yahoo Finance, CrowdStrike should generate $4.8 billion in revenue this fiscal year (the 12 months ending on Jan. 31, 2026) and $5.8 billion next fiscal year (ending Jan. 31, 2027).\nImage source: Getty Images.\nWhile CrowdStrike should continue to benefit from the unending demand for cybersecurity, in general, and its brand of artificial intelligence (AI)-powered cybersecurity, in particular, there are risks to owning the stock.\nFirst, it's expensive, with a price-to-sales ratio (P/S) over 28x. Second, the company has struggled to remain consistently profitable. Taken together, these traits make CrowdStrike stock a poor choice for value investors.\nNevertheless, for growth-oriented investors, the stock remains compelling, thanks to its high-octane growth and the secular trends of cybersecurity and AI-powered software. As CrowdStrike's last six years have proven, growth alone can deliver big returns for patient investors.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400About the AuthorJake Lerch is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering artificial intelligence, cloud computing, cybersecurity, e-commerce, and semiconductors. Prior to The Motley Fool, Jake worked for 12 years at Credit Suisse, an international investment bank. He holds a bachelor’s degree in business with a concentration in economics from the University of North Carolina at Wilmington.TMFRescueDogJake Lerch has positions in CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$259.67(-1.07%)-$2.82Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnS&P 500 IndexSNPINDEX: ^GSPC$7,704.13(-0.02%)-$1.90*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"你永远无法预知股市的走势。有些股票上涨，有些下跌，还有一些会连续多年横盘。基于这一点，我将回顾一下，过去六年中，对CrowdStrike Holdings（CRWD -1.07%）股票投资10,000美元会发生怎样的变化。\n展开NASDAQ：CRWD CrowdStrike 高级功能 Moneyball Superscore 85/100 今日变动（-1.07%）-$2.82 当前价格$259.67 关键数据点 市值$269B 市值仅根据已发行的公开交易股票计算。不包括未上市、私募或双重股权结构中未交易的股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。 当日区间$258.53 - $263.87 52周区间$85.68 - $263.87 成交量8.4M 平均成交量10.2M 毛利率75.12%\n简单来说，2019年对CrowdStrike股票投资10,000美元是非常明智的选择。经历一路上的多次起伏后，这笔初始投资如今价值超过134,000美元。这相当于总回报超过1,200%，或52%的复合年增长率（CAGR）。\n与基准指数标普500（^GSPC -0.02%）的表现相比，后者六年来的总回报为129%，复合年增长率不足15%。\nYCharts提供的CRWD总回报水平数据。\nCrowdStrike股票表现出色的最大原因，是公司收入的飙升。自2019年以来，公司过去12个月的收入增长了1,560%，达到总计41亿美元。\n此外，华尔街分析师预测该公司还将实现更多这种爆发式增长。根据Yahoo Finance汇编的估计，CrowdStrike应在本财年（截至2026年1月31日的12个月）产生48亿美元收入，并在下一财年（截至2027年1月31日）产生58亿美元收入。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n虽然CrowdStrike应会继续受益于对网络安全总体上永无止境的需求，尤其是对其人工智能（AI）驱动型网络安全的需求，但持有该股票仍存在风险。\n首先，它价格昂贵，市销率（P/S）超过28倍。其次，公司一直难以保持持续盈利。综合来看，这些特点使CrowdStrike股票不适合价值型投资者。\n不过，对于成长型投资者而言，得益于其强劲增长以及网络安全和AI驱动软件的长期趋势，该股票仍然具有吸引力。CrowdStrike过去六年的表现已证明，单靠增长就能为耐心的投资者带来丰厚回报。\n继续阅读\n2026年9月24日 • 作者：Jake Lerch\nCrowdStrike vs. Figma：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月23日 • 作者：Adam Spatacco\n不是Palantir，也不是Micron。Jim Cramer刚刚称为“必买”的那家市值3,250亿美元的英伟达合作伙伴\n2026年9月22日 • 作者：Pamela Kock\nCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月21日 • 作者：Leo Sun\n现在可以买入的两只造就百万富翁的网络安全股票\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Catie Hogan\n将主宰2027年的两只网络安全股票\n2026年9月15日 • 作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA\n这只网络安全股票可将1,000美元变成超过4,400美元\n关于作者\nJake Lerch是Motley Fool的特约科技分析师，报道人工智能、云计算、网络安全、电子商务和半导体。在加入The Motley Fool之前，Jake曾在国际投资银行瑞士信贷工作12年。他拥有北卡罗来纳大学威尔明顿分校工商管理学士学位，主修经济学。\nTMFRescueDog\nJake Lerch持有CrowdStrike的仓位。The Motley Fool持有并推荐CrowdStrike。The Motley Fool设有披露政策。\n提及的股票\nCrowdStrike\nNASDAQ：CRWD\n$259.67\n（-1.07%）\n-$2.82\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报\n标普500指数\nSNPINDEX：^GSPC\n$7,704.13\n（-0.02%）\n-$1.90\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2025-06-18T08:43:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2382","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike股价今日为何大涨","title_en":"Why CrowdStrike Stock Is Soaring Today | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike在Fal.Con大会期间上调2027年净新增年度经常性收入指引至至少增长20%，高于今年预期的17%，带动股价周四大涨约10%，十余名分析师上调目标价。文章回顾该公司一年前因故障更新导致股价暴跌逾40%、销售增速放缓，如今收入增速回升至21%。公司近期收购Pangea Cyber与Onum，布局云、身份与SIEM领域，并与Salesforce合作开发AI代理安全方案。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike shares jumped about 10% Thursday after the company, during its Fal.Con conference, raised guidance for net new annual recurring revenue to accelerate to at least 20% in 2027, above the 17% expected this year, prompting more than a dozen analysts to lift price targets. The article recalls the stock's over-40% plunge a year ago after a faulty update and slowing sales growth, now recovering to 21% revenue growth. Recent acquisitions of Pangea Cyber and Onum expand cloud, identity, and SIEM efforts, plus a Salesforce AI-agent security partnership.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:33:47.210867+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2025/09/18/why-crowdstrike-stock-is-soaring-today","content":"Shares of leading cloud-based cybersecurity juggernaut CrowdStrike (CRWD -3.23%) are up 10% Thursday as of noon ET, according to data provided by S&P Global Market Intelligence.\nCrowdStrike is holding its three-day Fal.Con keynote this week and has the market buzzing with optimism.\nThe key figure that may have stolen the show was updated guidance for net new annual recurring revenue (ARR) to accelerate to at least 20% in 2027 -- above the 17% expected this year.\nFollowing this announcement, more than a dozen analysts scrambled to raise their CrowdStrike price targets this morning, prompting today's soaring share price.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-3.23%) $-7.93Current Price$237.78Key Data PointsMarket Cap$252BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$234.90 - $247.5052wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Volume4.8MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nIs CrowdStrike set to rebound?\nJust over one year ago, CrowdStrike's stock plummeted over 40%, following a massive outage stemming from a faulty update.\nFollowing this outage, the company's sales growth declined from above 30% to 20%, and its free cash flow (FCF) margin dropped from above 30% to 24% within the same year. Worse yet, it wasn't initially clear how much customer trust CrowdStrike lost amid the mess.\nImage source: CrowdStrike.\nHowever, following last quarter's first reacceleration in revenue growth to 21% and management's better-than-expected guidance for 2027, it seems the company avoided the worst-case scenario.\nFurthermore, CrowdStrike recently acquired Pangea Cyber and Onum, launching it full speed ahead into three critical growth areas: next-generation cloud, identity, and security information and event management (SIEM).\nThese solutions currently account for roughly $1.6 billion in ARR and are growing by 40% annually. However, management believes the target addressable market for these growth areas could be $116 billion by 2030.\nOn top of this, CrowdStrike also recently partnered with Salesforce to create security solutions for its artificial intelligence (AI) agents -- a nascent market that could be worth $90 billion on its own by 2030, according to industry estimates.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400Sep 14, 2026 •By Danny Vena, CPAWhy CrowdStrike Stock Rocketed Higher TodaySep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoCrowdStrike vs. UiPath: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoC3.ai vs. CrowdStrike: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 13, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoCybersecurity Is the Next Big Market for Artificial Intelligence (AI), According to Jensen Huang. This Super Stock-Split Stock Is the One to Own.About the AuthorJosh Kohn-Lindquist is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering consumer goods, industrials, and technology stocks. Previously, Josh was a senior mutual fund accountant at Gemini Fund Services. He holds a bachelor’s degree in business management from the University of South Dakota.TMFJoryko@JorykoliJosh Kohn-Lindquist has positions in CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike and Salesforce. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$237.78(-3.23%)-$7.93Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"根据S&P Global Market Intelligence提供的数据，截至周四美国东部时间中午，领先的云端网络安全巨头CrowdStrike（CRWD -3.23%）股价上涨10%。\nCrowdStrike本周正在举行其为期三天的Fal.Con主题演讲，市场因此充满乐观情绪。\n可能抢尽风头的关键数据是，净新增年度经常性收入（ARR）的最新指引显示，2027年其增速将加快至至少20%——高于今年预计的17%。\n这一消息发布后，十多名分析师今早争相上调CrowdStrike的目标价，推动今日股价飙升。\n展开NASDAQ：CRWD CrowdStrike高级功能 Moneyball Superscore 85/100\n今日变动\n(-3.23%) $-7.93\n当前价格\n$237.78\n关键数据点\n市值\n$252B\n市值仅使用公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n当日区间\n$234.90 - $247.50\n52周区间\n$85.68 - $250.32\n成交量\n4.8M\n平均成交量\n10.2M\n毛利率\n75.12%\n\nCrowdStrike是否将迎来反弹？\n就在一年多前，因一次有缺陷的更新引发大规模宕机，CrowdStrike的股价暴跌逾40%。\n这次宕机后，该公司的销售增长率从30%以上降至20%，其自由现金流（FCF）利润率也在同一年内从30%以上降至24%。更糟的是，起初并不清楚CrowdStrike在这场混乱中失去了多少客户信任。\n图片来源：CrowdStrike。\n不过，在上个季度营收增速首次重新加速至21%，且管理层给出好于预期的2027年指引后，该公司似乎避免了最坏情形。\n此外，CrowdStrike最近收购了Pangea Cyber和Onum，全面进军三个关键增长领域：下一代云、身份，以及安全信息和事件管理（SIEM）。\n这些解决方案目前约占16亿美元ARR，并以每年40%的速度增长。不过，管理层认为，到2030年，这些增长领域的目标可服务市场规模可能达到1160亿美元。\n除此之外，CrowdStrike最近还与Salesforce合作，为其人工智能（AI）代理创建安全解决方案——根据行业估计，这一新兴市场到2030年自身可能价值900亿美元。\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Catie Hogan\n2只将主宰2027年的网络安全股票\n2026年9月15日 • 作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA\n这只网络安全股票可能让1,000美元变成超过4,400美元\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Danny Vena，CPA\nCrowdStrike股票今日为何大幅飙升\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Sara Appino\nCrowdStrike与UiPath：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Sara Appino\nC3.ai与CrowdStrike：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月13日 • 作者：Adam Spatacco\n据Jensen Huang称，网络安全是人工智能（AI）的下一个大市场。这只超级拆股股票才是应持有的标的。\n关于作者\nJosh Kohn-Lindquist是Motley Fool的特约股票市场分析师，覆盖消费品、工业和科技股票。此前，Josh曾任Gemini Fund Services高级共同基金会计师。他拥有南达科他大学工商管理学士学位。\nTMFJoryko@Jorykoli\nJosh Kohn-Lindquist持有CrowdStrike的仓位。Motley Fool持有并推荐CrowdStrike和Salesforce。Motley Fool设有披露政策。\n提及股票\nCrowdStrike\nNASDAQ：CRWD\n$237.78\n(-3.23%)\n-$7.93\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报*\n自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报以前一个交易日收盘价为准。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2025-09-18T17:45:19+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2307","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英特尔股价9月为何大涨","title_en":"Why Intel Rallied in September | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章称，英特尔股价9月上涨37.8%。此前美国政府将芯片法案拨款转为约9%股权，软银投资20亿美元；9月英伟达宣布向英特尔投资50亿美元，约合4%股权，并达成两项产品合作：英特尔数据中心CPU更紧密整合英伟达AI GPU服务器生态，英伟达RTX图形芯粒将集成进英特尔x86 SoC。文章还提到英特尔在亚利桑那18A工厂展示及即将发布Panther Lake等产品。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool article said Intel shares rallied 37.8% in September. Earlier, the U.S. government converted CHIPS Act grant money into roughly a 9% equity stake and SoftBank invested $2 billion; in September, Nvidia announced a $5 billion investment for about a 4% stake plus two product partnerships: tighter integration of Intel data center CPUs with Nvidia's AI GPU server ecosystem, and Nvidia RTX graphics chiplets integrated into Intel x86 SoCs. It also noted Intel's Arizona 18A fab events and upcoming Panther Lake launches.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:54.289929+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2025/10/05/why-intel-rallied-in-september","content":"Shares of Intel (INTC +7.67%) rallied 37.8% in September, according to data from S&P Global Market Intelligence.\nIntel had already experienced a momentous month in August after the U.S. government converted its CHIPS Act grant money into roughly a 9% equity stake, while Japanese tech giant Softbank invested another $2 billion.\nThose investments, while notable, were dwarfed in significance by last month's $5 billion investment from AI leader Nvidia (NVDA +2.54%), which also came along with an announcement of two key product partnerships.\nAttracting the investment of arguably the world's most important AI company sent beaten-down Intel's stock soaring in September.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nThe ins and outs of the Nvidia-Intel partnership\nThere were three major components to the Nvidia-Intel announcement: two product partnerships, along with Nvidia's $5 billion investment in Intel stock at $23.28 per share -- good for about a 4% ownership stake.\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%\nOn the product-level partnership, Intel will integrate its data center CPUs more tightly with Nvidia's leading AI GPU server ecosystem, while Nvidia will more closely integrate its graphics GPU technology with Intel's leading CPU architecture for PCs, where Intel still holds a large market share.\nIn order to make fully integrated AI servers, which still require a CPU, Nvidia has developed its own internally designed \"Grace\" CPUs based on the Arm Holdings architecture in recent years. However, Arm CPUs are generally known for their power efficiency, not performance. Meanwhile, most enterprise data center servers are still tied to the x86 CPU architecture, not Arm. As such, Intel's performance-optimized Granite Rapids Xeon 6 CPU, which came out last year, became the reference design as the \"host\" CPU in Nvidia's new DGX B300 server systems.\nThe two companies will now bring Nvidia's GPU and Intel's x86 CPU architectures even closer together, with Intel giving Nvidia the ability to customize its own CPU design on Intel's x86 CPU architecture for future AI systems.\nAnd while Nvidia dominates AI servers, Intel, despite having lost its near-monopoly from a decade ago, still commands over 76% of the consumer PC market. Nvidia already sells discrete RTX graphics chips to the high-end gaming PC market, but has been somewhat left out of a large part of the PC market that demands close integration of graphics and central processing units on the same system-on-chip (SOC).\nWhile Intel also has its own line of Arc graphics chips, Intel will now integrate Nvidia's RTX graphics chiplets directly into Intel's x86 SOCs for the part of the PC market where integrated SOCs are required. The tie-up will thus expand Nvidia's addressable market in PCs, while Nvidia's premium graphics brand and IP should help Intel win back market share.\nWhy Intel took off so much on the news\nAs was the case with the U.S. government's investment, Intel's stock took off on the news, despite the effects of shareholder dilution. This is likely due to the halo effect of being in league with Nvidia, which is currently seen as the gold standard in graphics and AI. Intel has suffered from a crisis of confidence and market share losses in recent years, so to get a vote of confidence from Nvidia at this time goes a long way.\nAnd while some analysts were skeptical there was no announcement for Nvidia to use Intel's nascent foundry manufacturing services, the lack of an announcement today doesn't mean there couldn't be a foundry deal for Nvidia chips down the road. Meanwhile, Nvidia's investment indicates confidence in Intel's technology roadmap and future, which includes its foundry efforts.\nOn that note, Intel is currently hosting tech and financial analysts at its new 18A fabs in Arizona this week, and is set to formally introduce its Panther Lake and Clearwater Forest chips on Thursday, Oct. 9. These will be the first internal products made on Intel's new 18A process node, which Intel believes could bring it back to semiconductor technology leadership once again.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorBilly Duberstein is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering semiconductors, hardware, software, and AI, as well as consumer goods. Billy loves looking at the story behind investments from an interdisciplinary point of view, with an equal appetite for high-growth disruptors and beaten-down value names. He is also CEO of Stone Oak Capital, a registered investment adviser in California. He previously worked as a technology analyst for several hedge funds and as a research assistant at Wedbush Securities. Billy holds an MBA in finance from New York University and a bachelor’s degree in music from the University of Virginia.TMFStoneOakBilly Duberstein has positions in Intel. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Intel and Nvidia. The Motley Fool recommends the following options: short November 2025 $21 puts on Intel. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnNvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44SoftBank GroupOTC: SFTBY$21.15(+7.20%)+$1.42Arm HoldingsNASDAQ: ARM$264.90(+8.57%)+$20.92*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"根据标普全球市场情报的数据，英特尔（INTC +7.67%）的股价在9月份上涨了37.8%。\n在美国政府将其《芯片法案》拨款转换为约9%的股权后，英特尔在8月份已经经历了一个意义重大的月份；与此同时，日本科技巨头软银又投资了20亿美元。\n这些投资虽然引人注目，但其重要性远不及上个月人工智能领军企业英伟达（NVDA +2.54%）的50亿美元投资，后者还伴随着两项关键产品合作的公告。\n吸引到这家可能是全球最重要的人工智能公司的投资，使英特尔这只遭受重创的股票在9月份大幅飙升。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n英伟达与英特尔合作的来龙去脉\n英伟达公告包含三个主要部分：两项产品合作，以及英伟达以每股23.28美元的价格投资英特尔股票50亿美元——相当于约4%的持股比例。\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%\n在产品层面的合作中，英特尔将把其数据中心CPU与英伟达领先的人工智能GPU服务器生态系统进行更紧密的整合，而英伟达则会将其图形GPU技术与英特尔领先的PC CPU架构进行更紧密的整合；在PC领域，英特尔仍占据很大的市场份额。\n为了制造完全集成的人工智能服务器（这类服务器仍需要CPU），英伟达近年来开发了基于安谋控股架构、内部设计的“Grace”CPU。然而，Arm CPU通常以能效著称，而非性能。与此同时，大多数企业数据中心服务器仍采用x86 CPU架构，而不是Arm。因此，英特尔于去年推出、针对性能优化的Granite Rapids Xeon 6 CPU，成为英伟达新款DGX B300服务器系统中作为“主机”CPU的参考设计。\n如今，两家公司将进一步拉近英伟达GPU与英特尔x86 CPU架构之间的距离，英特尔将赋予英伟达在英特尔x86 CPU架构上定制自身CPU设计的能力，以用于未来的人工智能系统。\n尽管英伟达主导着人工智能服务器市场，但英特尔虽然已失去十年前的近乎垄断地位，仍掌控着逾76%的消费级PC市场。英伟达已经向高端游戏PC市场销售独立的RTX图形芯片，但在很大一部分PC市场中仍有所缺席；该市场要求在同一片系统级芯片（SOC）上实现图形处理器与中央处理器的紧密整合。\n虽然英特尔也拥有自己的Arc图形芯片产品线，但现在，英特尔将把英伟达的RTX图形芯粒直接整合进英特尔的x86 SOC，用于需要集成式SOC的PC市场部分。因此，这一合作将扩大英伟达在PC领域的可服务市场，而英伟达的高端图形品牌和知识产权应能帮助英特尔夺回市场份额。\n英特尔为何因这一消息大幅上涨\n与美国政府投资的情况一样，尽管股东遭到稀释，英特尔股价仍因这一消息大幅上涨。这可能是因为与英伟达结盟所产生的光环效应；英伟达目前被视为人工智能领域的黄金标准。\n图形和人工智能。近年来，Intel一直遭遇信心危机和市场份额流失，因此此时获得Nvidia的信任支持意义重大。\n尽管一些分析师对Nvidia使用Intel尚处于起步阶段的代工制造服务持怀疑态度，并且今天没有宣布这项安排，但这并不意味着未来不会达成Nvidia芯片的代工协议。与此同时，Nvidia的投资表明其对Intel的技术路线图和未来充满信心，其中包括Intel的代工业务。\n说到这里，Intel本周正在亚利桑那州的新18A晶圆厂接待科技和金融分析师，并计划于10月9日（星期四）正式推出Panther Lake和Clearwater Forest芯片。这些将是首批采用Intel新18A制程节点制造的内部产品，Intel相信该制程有望帮助其再次夺回半导体技术领导地位。接下来阅读2026年9月17日 • 作者：Johnny Rice英特尔股价今日为何上涨7.6%2026年9月17日 • 作者：Emma Newbery今日股市，9月17日：传闻与SK Hynix谈判，英特尔飙升8%2026年9月16日 • 作者：Joe Tenebruso英特尔股价今日为何上涨2026年9月16日 • 作者：Daniel SparksSK Hynix正与Intel洽谈在美国生产存储芯片。这对英特尔股价可能意味着什么？2026年9月16日 • 作者：Howard Smith今日股市，9月16日：英特尔因与SK Hynix洽谈存储芯片制造而上涨2026年9月16日 • 作者：Scott Levine2026年6只最佳物联网股票及投资方式关于作者Billy Duberstein是Motley Fool的特约科技分析师，负责报道半导体、硬件、软件和人工智能，以及消费品。Billy喜欢从跨学科视角审视投资背后的故事，对高增长颠覆者和遭受重创的价值型股票同样感兴趣。他还是Stone Oak Capital的首席执行官，该公司是加利福尼亚州注册的投资顾问。他此前曾担任多家对冲基金的科技分析师，并在Wedbush Securities担任研究助理。Billy拥有纽约大学金融学工商管理硕士学位，以及弗吉尼亚大学音乐学学士学位。TMFStoneOakBilly Duberstein持有Intel的头寸。The Motley Fool持有Intel和Nvidia的头寸并推荐这两家公司。The Motley Fool推荐以下期权：做空2025年11月到期、执行价21美元的Intel看跌期权。The Motley Fool制定有信息披露政策。提及的股票Intel纳斯达克：INTC$108.80（+7.67%）+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---% 平均回报Nvidia纳斯达克：NVDA$219.34（+2.54%）+$5.44SoftBank Group场外交易：SFTBY$21.15（+7.20%）+$1.42Arm Holdings纳斯达克：ARM$264.90（+8.57%）+$20.92*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2025-10-05T18:04:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1891","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"最后机会：2025年结束前是否应加仓英特尔股票？","title_en":"Last Call: Should You Load Up on Intel Stock Before 2025 Ends? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"英特尔股价2025年上涨近90%，新任CEO上任，美国政府、英伟达和软银通过股权投资注入数十亿美元，同时裁员和削减成本降低了开支。2026年英特尔需为代工业务赢得大客户，并推进18A和14A制程；Panther Lake和Nova Lake PC处理器将于2026年推出。但存储芯片价格因AI需求飙升，可能推高PC价格并抑制需求，成为短期逆风。","summary_en":"Intel shares soared nearly 90% in 2025 as a new CEO took over, with the U.S. government, Nvidia, and SoftBank injecting billions through equity investments while layoffs and cost cuts reduced expenses. In 2026, Intel must secure a major foundry customer and advance its 18A and 14A process nodes, with Panther Lake and Nova Lake PC CPUs set to launch. However, soaring memory chip prices amid the AI boom could raise PC prices and hurt demand, posing a near-term headwind.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:44.325065+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2025/12/31/last-call-load-up-on-intel-stock-2025","content":"Shares of Intel (INTC +7.67%) soared nearly 90% in 2025 as a new CEO took the reins. The U.S. government, Nvidia, and SoftBank injected billions of dollars through equity investments, bolstering Intel's balance sheet, while layoffs and other cost-cutting measures reduced expenses.\nSeveral factors must align for Intel in 2026 for the stock to continue its rally, and the company will need to overcome a major headwind.\nImage source: Intel.\nFoundry, CPUs, and memory prices\nFirst and foremost, Intel needs to secure a major customer for its foundry business. Rumors have emerged that Apple is considering a version of the Intel 18A process, which would be a huge win if a deal can be worked out. Intel will also need to show tangible progress in securing customers for its upcoming Intel 14A process, which is scheduled for 2027.\nThose process nodes will also play a critical role in Intel's product business. Panther Lake and Nova Lake, two PC CPU families that will use the Intel 18A process, are set to launch in 2026. Intel has been losing market share to AMD for years, partly due to Intel's manufacturing edge evaporating. Intel's new manufacturing processes should at least close the gap with TSMC, AMD's manufacturing partner.\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%\nWorking against Intel is the current state of the memory chip market. Memory chip prices are soaring as demand outstrips supply amid the AI boom, and there's little hope for relief anytime soon. This situation will push up the price of PCs, which could hurt demand and make it difficult for Intel's PC CPU business to grow in 2026.\nFor long-term investors, it's important to remember that the memory chip headwind is temporary. Intel's foundry represents a multi-billion-dollar opportunity, particularly as custom-designed chips proliferate. While Intel stock could go either way in 2026, when you zoom out, the picture looks promising.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorTim Green is a contributing Motley Fool technology and consumer goods analyst covering companies in AI, cloud computing, retail, and other market sectors. Before The Motley Fool, Tim was in a doctoral program for computational physics. He holds a bachelor’s degree in physics from Rochester Institute of Technology.TMFTimGreenTimothy Green has positions in Intel. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Advanced Micro Devices, Apple, Intel, Nvidia, and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnAppleNASDAQ: AAPL$337.00(+1.38%)+$4.59Taiwan Semiconductor ManufacturingNYSE: TSM$430.26(+3.00%)+$12.54NvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$219.34(+2.54%)+$5.44Advanced Micro DevicesNASDAQ: AMD$545.09(+6.36%)+$32.59SoftBankOTC: SFBQF$1.63(+5.52%)+$0.09*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"英特尔（INTC +7.67%）股价在2025年飙升近90%，一位新任首席执行官走马上任。美国政府、英伟达和软银通过股权投资注入数十亿美元，增强了英特尔的资产负债表，而裁员及其他削减成本措施降低了开支。\n英特尔要想让股价在2026年继续上涨，几个因素必须协同发挥作用，而且公司还需要克服一个重大阻力。\n图片来源：英特尔。\n晶圆代工、CPU和内存价格\n首先，英特尔需要为其晶圆代工业务争取到一家大客户。有传言称苹果正在考虑采用英特尔18A工艺的一个版本，如果能够达成协议，这将是巨大胜利。英特尔还需要在为即将推出、计划于2027年推出的英特尔14A工艺争取客户方面展现切实进展。\n这些工艺节点也将在英特尔的产品业务中发挥关键作用。将采用英特尔18A工艺的Panther Lake和Nova Lake两大PC CPU系列计划于2026年推出。多年来，英特尔一直在丢失对AMD的市场份额，部分原因是英特尔的制造优势逐渐消失。英特尔的新制造工艺至少应能缩小其与台积电（AMD的制造合作伙伴）之间的差距。\n展开 NASDAQ：INTC 英特尔 高级功能 Moneyball综合评分 67/100 今日变动（7.67%） $7.75 当前价格 $108.80 关键数据点 市值 $575B 市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算，不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间 $104.70 - $111.37 52周区间 $28.73 - $142.35 成交量 4.6M 平均成交量 109.7M 毛利率 39.05%\n内存芯片市场的当前状况对英特尔不利。在人工智能热潮中，需求超过供应，内存芯片价格飙升，短期内几乎看不到缓解希望。这种情况将推高PC价格，可能损害需求，并使英特尔的PC CPU业务难以在2026年增长。\n对于长期投资者而言，重要的是要记住，内存芯片的阻力是暂时的。英特尔的晶圆代工业务代表着数十亿美元的机遇，尤其是在定制设计芯片日益普及之际。虽然英特尔股票在2026年可能走向任何一方，但拉长视角来看，前景颇为乐观。继续阅读 2026年9月17日 • 作者：Johnny Rice 为什么英特尔股价今日上涨7.6% 2026年9月17日 • 作者：Emma Newbery 今日股市，9月17日：传闻SK海力士谈判，英特尔飙升8% 2026年9月16日 • 作者：Joe Tenebruso 英特尔股价今日为何上涨 2026年9月16日 • 作者：Daniel Sparks SK海力士正与英特尔洽谈在美国制造内存芯片。这对英特尔股价可能意味着什么。 2026年9月16日 • 作者：Howard Smith 今日股市，9月16日：SK海力士内存芯片制造谈判推动英特尔上涨 2026年9月16日 • 作者：Scott Levine 2026年6只最佳物联网股票及投资方法\n关于作者 Tim Green是《Motley Fool》科技和消费品分析师，负责报道人工智能、云计算、零售及其他市场领域的公司。在加入《Motley Fool》之前，Tim曾攻读计算物理博士。他拥有罗切斯特理工学院物理学学士学位。TMFTimGreen Timothy Green持有英特尔股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐Advanced Micro Devices、苹果、英特尔、英伟达和台积电的股票。《Motley Fool》有披露政策。\n提及的股票 英特尔 NASDAQ：INTC $108.80（+7.67%）+ $7.75 Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐 获取权限——-% 平均回报 苹果 NASDAQ：AAPL $337.00（+1.38%）+ $4.59 台积电 NYSE：TSM $430.26（+3.00%）+ $12.54 英伟达 NASDAQ：NVDA $219.34（+2.54%）+ $5.44 Advanced Micro Devices NASDAQ：AMD $545.09（+6.36%）+ $32.59 软银 OTC：SFBQF $1.63（+5.52%）+ $0.09 *所有推荐自成立以来的平均回报。成本基础和回报依据前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2025-12-31T19:45:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1461","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英特尔股价2月下跌逾6%，原因何在？","title_en":"Intel Stock Dropped by More Than 6% in February. Here's What Happened. | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"英特尔股价在2025年大涨84%后，2026年2月下跌6.5%。1月第四季度财报电话会上，管理层对第一季度营收指引为117亿至127亿美元，中值122亿美元低于华尔街126亿美元的共识预期，引发投资者担忧。此外，其代工业务第四季度亏损25亿美元，CEO陈立武警告称建设代工业务需要时间和大量资源。这些担忧延续至2月，股价低迷可能持续到3月。","summary_en":"After an 84% surge in 2025, Intel shares fell 6.5% in February 2026. On its January fourth-quarter earnings call, management guided first-quarter revenue to $11.7 billion-$12.7 billion, with the $12.2 billion midpoint below Wall Street's $12.6 billion consensus, worrying investors. Its foundry business lost $2.5 billion in Q4, and CEO Lip-Bu Tan warned that building a foundry business will take time and considerable effort and resources. Those concerns followed the stock into February and the slump could continue through March.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-18T12:52:03.267826+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/03/05/intel-stock-dropped-by-more-than-6-in-february-her","content":"After years of struggle for Intel (INTC +7.67%), its 84% stock price surge in 2025 offered shareholders some confidence that a turnaround was taking shape at the chipmaker.\nInvestors were looking for signs that its momentum could carry over into 2026, but Intel's shares dropped by 6.5% in February, showing how quickly confidence can shift.\nHere's what made the market reevaluate the situation.\nSource image: Getty Images.\nThe Intel slump\nOn its fourth-quarter earnings call in January, Intel worried investors with the guidance it offered for the current quarter.\nFor Q1, management forecast that its revenue will be between $11.7 billion and $12.7 billion. The first quarter has historically been a seasonally weaker period for Intel, but as management noted, the $12.2 billion midpoint of that guidance range would be on the low side even relative to that standard.\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(7.67%) $7.75Current Price$108.80Key Data PointsMarket Cap$575BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$104.70 - $111.3752wk Range$28.73 - $142.35Volume4.6MAvg Vol109.7MGross Margin39.05%\nWhile Wall Street analysts' $12.6 billion consensus estimate fell within the guidance range, the midpoint sat below it, which contributed to investor worry.\nAnother thing that investors remain concerned about is Intel's ability to position itself as a go-to chipmaker for other companies. Its foundry business lost $2.5 billion in Q4, and CEO Lip-Bu Tan warned shareholders that it will not be an easy road ahead: \"As I have said before, building a foundry business will take time and considerable effort and resources,\" he said during the earnings conference call.\nAll of those concerns from the January earnings report followed Intel stock into February. The slump we're seeing now could continue through March as well, as it may take a piece of unexpected good news to offset shareholders' currently muted expectations and change the stock's trajectory.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Johnny RiceWhy Intel Stock Jumped 7.6% TodaySep 17, 2026 •By Emma NewberyStock Market Today, Sept. 17: Intel Surges 8% on Rumored SK Hynix TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel Stock Jumped TodaySep 16, 2026 •By Daniel SparksSK Hynix Is in Talks With Intel to Make Memory Chips in the U.S. Here's What It Could Mean for Intel Stock.Sep 16, 2026 •By Howard SmithStock Market Today, Sept. 16: Intel Jumps on SK Hynix Memory-Chip Manufacturing TalksSep 16, 2026 •By Scott Levine6 Best Internet of Things Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorJack is a seasoned content strategist with over a decade of experience in financial publishing. He's directed technology, emerging opportunities, and alternative asset publications to deliver actionable insights to investors.TMFJackDelaneyJack Delaney has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Intel. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$108.80(+7.67%)+$7.75Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"英特尔（INTC +7.67%）经历多年挣扎后，其股价在2025年上涨84%，这让股东对这家芯片制造商正在形成扭转局面的信心有所增强。\n投资者一直在寻找其势头能否延续到2026年的迹象，但英特尔股价在2月份下跌了6.5%，显示出信心转变可能有多快。\n以下是促使市场重新评估这一情况的原因。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n\n英特尔的低迷\n\n在1月份举行的第四季度业绩电话会上，英特尔就其对当前季度给出的指引令投资者感到担忧。\n对于第一季度，管理层预计营收将在117亿美元至127亿美元之间。第一季度历来是英特尔季节性较弱的时期，但正如管理层所指出的，该指引区间中位数122亿美元，即便相对于这一季节性标准而言也处于低位。\n展开NASDAQ：INTC英特尔高级功能Moneyball综合评分67/100今日变动（7.67%）7.75美元当前价格108.80美元关键数据点市值5750亿美元市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间104.70美元 - 111.37美元52周区间28.73美元 - 142.35美元成交量460万平均成交量1.097亿毛利率39.05%\n\n虽然华尔街分析师126亿美元的一致预期处于该指引区间内，但中位数低于这一预期，这加剧了投资者的担忧。\n投资者仍然担心的另一件事，是英特尔能否将自己定位为其他公司的首选芯片制造商。其代工业务在第四季度亏损25亿美元，首席执行官陈立武提醒股东，未来道路并不容易：“正如我以前所说，建立代工业务需要时间、大量努力和资源，”他在业绩电话会上说。\n\n1月份业绩报告中的所有这些担忧都伴随着英特尔股票进入2月份。我们目前看到的低迷也可能延续到3月份，因为可能需要一条出乎意料的好消息，才能抵消股东目前低迷的预期并改变股价走势。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Johnny Rice\n英特尔股价今日为何上涨7.6%\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Emma Newbery\n今日股市，9月17日：英特尔因传闻与SK海力士会谈而上涨8%\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Joe Tenebruso\n英特尔股价今日为何上涨\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Daniel Sparks\nSK海力士正与英特尔洽谈在美国制造存储芯片。这对英特尔股价可能意味着什么？\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Howard Smith\n今日股市，9月16日：英特尔因SK海力士存储芯片制造谈判而上涨\n2026年9月16日 • 作者：Scott Levine\n2026年6只最佳物联网股票及投资方法\n\n关于作者\nJack是一位经验丰富的内容策略师，在金融出版领域拥有十多年经验。他曾负责科技、新兴机遇和另类资产出版物，为投资者提供可执行的洞见。\nTMFJackDelaney\nJack Delaney未持有上述任何一只股票。Motley Fool持有英特尔的仓位并予以推荐。Motley Fool有披露政策。\n\n提及的股票\n英特尔\nNASDAQ：INTC\n108.80美元（+7.67%）\n+7.75美元\nMotley Fool股票顾问的最新推荐\n获取权限\n---%\n平均回报*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报根据前一个市场日收盘价计算。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-03-05T12:22:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1396","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike与Palo Alto Networks：哪只网络安全股将在2026年胜出？","title_en":"CrowdStrike vs. Palo Alto Networks: Which Cybersecurity Stock Will Win 2026? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool对比CrowdStrike与Palo Alto Networks两只网络安全股。过去12个月CrowdStrike上涨33%，Palo Alto下跌4%。Palo Alto以Strata、Prisma和Cortex三大平台运营并收购CyberArk；CrowdStrike则依靠云原生Falcon平台。分析师预计两者营收增速相近，但Palo Alto估值更低，作者倾向选择Palo Alto。","summary_en":"Motley Fool compares cybersecurity stocks CrowdStrike and Palo Alto Networks. Over the past 12 months CrowdStrike rose 33% while Palo Alto fell 4%. Palo Alto operates Strata, Prisma and Cortex platforms and acquired CyberArk; CrowdStrike relies on its cloud-native Falcon platform. Analysts expect similar revenue growth, but Palo Alto trades at a lower valuation, leading the author to favor Palo Alto.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:24:42.076156+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/03/13/crowdstrike-vs-palo-alto-networks-which-cybersecur","content":"CrowdStrike (CRWD -3.56%) and Palo Alto Networks (PANW -4.68%) are two of the world's largest cybersecurity companies. Both stocks have generated massive multibagger gains since their public debuts as the cybersecurity market expanded.\nBut over the past 12 months, CrowdStrike's stock has risen 33%, while Palo Alto's stock has declined 4%. Let's see why the former outperformed the latter, and if it will remain the better cybersecurity stock to buy for the rest of 2026.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nThe differences between CrowdStrike and Palo Alto Networks\nPalo Alto Networks splits its ecosystem into three main platforms: Strata, for its older on-site networking services; Prisma, for its cloud-based services; and Cortex, for its AI-powered threat detection services. Most of its recent growth has been driven by Prisma and Cortex, which it collectively refers to as its \"next-gen security\" services. It also recently acquired CyberArk, a leader in privileged access management (PAM) services, for $25 billion.\nPalo Alto's older services still need to be deployed on-site via expensive, maintenance-intensive appliances that are difficult to scale as a company grows. CrowdStrike addresses those issues with Falcon, its cloud-native endpoint security platform that doesn't require on-site appliances and locks customers in with sticky recurring subscriptions. Its customers start with a handful of trial cloud modules and add more to access additional security features.\nWhich company is growing faster?\nFrom fiscal 2020 to fiscal 2025 (which ended last July), Palo Alto's revenue grew at a 22% CAGR. It also became profitable under generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP) in fiscal 2023 and grew its net income at a 61% CAGR over the following two years.\nFrom fiscal 2025 to fiscal 2028, analysts expect Palo Alto's revenue and EPS to grow at CAGRs of 19% and 22%, respectively. That growth should be driven by its NGS services, its recent acquisition of CyberArk, and its \"platformization\" strategy of bundling more niche services into its core platforms to pull companies away from smaller cybersecurity companies.\nExpandNASDAQ: PANWPalo Alto NetworksPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore93/100Today's Change(-4.68%) $-17.56Current Price$357.50Key Data PointsMarket Cap$307BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$357.40 - $376.0152wk Range$139.57 - $398.88Volume2MAvg Vol6.6MGross Margin65.48%\nFrom fiscal 2021 to fiscal 2026 (which ended this January), CrowdStrike's revenue grew at a 41% CAGR. However, it isn't profitable by GAAP measures yet. It grew rapidly as its cloud-native services pulled more companies away from legacy cybersecurity providers, and it increased revenue per customer by selling more modules.\nFrom fiscal 2026 to fiscal 2029, analysts expect CrowdStrike's revenue to grow at a 22% CAGR. They also expect it to turn profitable in fiscal 2027, and to grow its net income at a 100% CAGR over the following two years. Its top-line growth should be driven by the expansion of its consumption-based \"Falcon Flex\" plans (which don't require rigid subscriptions or module purchases) and the use of generative AI tools to simplify its threat detection services. Its profitability should also improve as it reduces its stock-based compensation expenses.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-3.56%) $-8.74Current Price$236.96Key Data PointsMarket Cap$252BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$236.86 - $247.5052wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Volume2.9MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nBoth companies are well positioned to profit from the secular expansion of the cybersecurity market, which is generally insulated from macro headwinds because companies won't shut off their digital defenses just to save a few dollars. According to Fortune Business Insights, the global cybersecurity market could still expand at a 13.8% CAGR from 2026 to 2034.\nHowever, both companies could eventually face tougher competition from diversified tech giants like Microsoft (MSFT -0.99%), which are bundling more endpoint security services into their software, and AI-native cybersecurity companies like SentinelOne (S -2.95%).\nWhich stock is the better value?\nPalo Alto trades at 45 times its forward-adjusted (non-GAAP) earnings, while CrowdStrike has a much higher forward-adjusted price-to-earnings ratio of 91. CrowdStrike is growing only slightly faster than Palo Alto, but its cloud-native approach is attracting more growth-oriented investors.\nBoth of these stocks are still reliable cybersecurity plays. But if I had to pick one over the other, I'd buy Palo Alto because it's trading at a more reasonable valuation in this volatile market.Read NextSep 14, 2026 •By Parkev Tatevosian, CFAThe Proliferation of Agentic AI Has Been Great News for Palo Alto Stock InvestorsSep 14, 2026 •By Rich SmithWhy Palo Alto Networks Stock Popped TodaySep 8, 2026 •By Motley Fool TranscribingPalo Alto Networks (PANW) Q4 2026 Earnings Call TranscriptSep 6, 2026 •By Keith NoonanWhy Palo Alto Networks Stock Plummeted This WeekSep 4, 2026 •By Geoffrey SeilerAfter an 80% Gain on the Year, Is Palo Alto Networks Stock a Buy on Its Recent Pullback as Revenue Surges?Sep 4, 2026 •By Anthony Di PizioThis Unstoppable Stock Is Obliterating the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq-100 in 2026, but Is There Still Time to Buy?About the AuthorLeo Sun is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst who has worked with the company since 2013, covering technology, consumer goods, industrial, and financial sectors. He became a self-made millionaire by age 40 through long-term investing, crediting lessons from Warren Buffett and Peter Lynch. Leo is a regular guest on CNBC Asia providing stock analysis on Chinese technology companies, including Tencent, Baidu, and Alibaba. He previously wrote for InvestorGuide and holds a bachelor’s degree in English from the University of Texas at Austin.TMFSunLion@TMFSunLionLeo Sun has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike, Microsoft, and SentinelOne. The Motley Fool recommends Palo Alto Networks. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedPalo Alto NetworksNASDAQ: PANW$357.50(-4.68%)-$17.56Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnMicrosoftNASDAQ: MSFT$492.81(-0.99%)-$4.94CrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$236.12(-3.90%)-$9.58SentinelOneNYSE: S$22.51(-2.95%)-$0.69*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"CrowdStrike（CRWD -3.56%）和Palo Alto Networks（PANW -4.68%）是全球最大的两家网络安全公司。随着网络安全市场不断扩大，两只股票自上市以来都实现了巨大的多倍回报。\n但在过去12个月里，CrowdStrike的股价上涨了33%，而Palo Alto的股价下跌了4%。让我们看看前者为何跑赢后者，以及在2026年剩余时间里它是否仍将是更值得买入的网络安全股。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\nCrowdStrike与Palo Alto Networks之间的差异\nPalo Alto Networks将其生态系统划分为三大平台：Strata，用于其较早的本地网络服务；Prisma，用于其云端服务；以及Cortex，用于其人工智能驱动的威胁检测服务。其近期大部分增长由Prisma和Cortex推动，公司统称其为“下一代安全”服务。公司最近还以250亿美元收购了特权访问管理（PAM）服务领导者CyberArk。\nPalo Alto较老的服务仍需要通过昂贵且维护密集型的设备在本地部署，随着公司的发展，这些设备难以扩展。CrowdStrike通过其云原生端点安全平台Falcon解决了这些问题。Falcon不需要本地设备，并通过具有较强客户黏性的经常性订阅锁定客户。客户会先使用少量试用云模块，然后通过增加模块来获得更多安全功能。\n哪家公司增长更快？\n从2020财年至2025财年（截至去年7月），Palo Alto的营收以22%的复合年增长率增长。该公司还在2023财年按美国公认会计原则（GAAP）实现盈利，并在随后两年以61%的复合年增长率增长净利润。\n从2025财年至2028财年，分析师预计Palo Alto的营收和每股收益将分别以19%和22%的复合年增长率增长。这一增长应由其NGS服务、最近对CyberArk的收购，以及其“平台化”战略推动，即将更多小众服务捆绑到核心平台中，以吸引企业离开规模较小的网络安全公司。\n展开NASDAQ：PANWPalo Alto Networks高级功能Moneyball超级评分93/100今日变动（-4.68%）$-17.56当前价格$357.50关键数据点市值$307B市值仅根据公开交易的已发行股票计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$357.40 - $376.0152周区间$139.57 - $398.88成交量2M平均成交量6.6M毛利率65.48%\n从2021财年至2026财年（截至今年1月），CrowdStrike的营收以41%的复合年增长率增长。然而，按GAAP指标计算，它目前仍未实现盈利。随着其云原生服务吸引更多企业离开传统网络安全供应商，并通过销售更多模块提高每位客户的营收，公司实现了快速增长。\n从2026财年至2029财年，分析师预计CrowdStrike的营收将以22%的复合年增长率增长。他们还预计公司将在2027财年实现盈利，并在随后两年以100%的复合年增长率增长净利润。其营收增长应由基于用量的“Falcon Flex”计划扩张推动（该计划不要求严格的订阅或模块购买），以及利用生成式人工智能工具简化其威胁检测服务推动。随着公司降低基于股票的薪酬支出，其盈利能力也应有所改善。\n展开NASDAQ：CRWDCrowdStrike高级功能Moneyball\n综合评分85/100今日变动(-3.56%) $-8.74当前价格$236.96关键数据点市值$252B市值仅根据已发行的公开交易股票计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权结构中的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$236.86 - $247.5052周区间$85.68 - $250.32成交量2.9M平均成交量10.2M毛利率75.12%\n两家公司都处于有利位置，有望从网络安全市场的长期扩张中获利。该市场通常不受宏观经济阻力影响，因为企业不会仅仅为了节省几美元就关闭数字防御。根据《财富》商业洞察，全球网络安全市场在2026年至2034年期间仍可能以13.8%的复合年增长率扩张。\n然而，两家公司最终都可能面临来自多元化科技巨头（如微软（MSFT -0.99%））的更激烈竞争，后者正将更多终端安全服务捆绑到其软件中；同时还可能面临来自以人工智能为原生基础的网络安全公司（如SentinelOne（S -2.95%））的竞争。\n哪只股票更具价值？\nPalo Alto的交易价格相当于其远期调整后（非GAAP）收益的45倍，而CrowdStrike的远期调整后市盈率则高得多，达到91倍。CrowdStrike的增长速度仅略快于Palo Alto，但其云原生方式正吸引更多以增长为导向的投资者。\n这两只股票仍然都是可靠的网络安全投资标的。但如果必须二选一，我会买入Palo Alto，因为在这个波动剧烈的市场中，它的估值更加合理。继续阅读2026年9月14日 •作者：Parkev Tatevosian，CFA代理型人工智能的普及为Palo Alto股票投资者带来了极大利好2026年9月14日 •作者：Rich Smith为何Palo Alto Networks股票今日上涨2026年9月8日 •作者：Motley Fool TranscribingPalo Alto Networks（PANW）2026财年第四季度财报电话会议记录2026年9月6日 •作者：Keith Noonan为何Palo Alto Networks股票本周暴跌2026年9月4日 •作者：Geoffrey Seiler今年上涨80%之后，随着营收飙升，Palo Alto Networks股票近期回调后是否值得买入？2026年9月4日 •作者：Anthony Di Pizio这只势不可挡的股票在2026年击败标普500指数和纳斯达克100指数，但现在是否仍有买入机会？关于作者Leo Sun是《Motley Fool》特约股市分析师，自2013年起与该公司合作，负责科技、消费品、工业和金融领域的报道。他通过长期投资在40岁时成为白手起家的百万富翁，并将此归功于沃伦·巴菲特和彼得·林奇的经验教训。Leo经常作为嘉宾出现在CNBC亚洲频道，分析包括腾讯、百度和阿里巴巴在内的中国科技公司股票。他此前曾为InvestorGuide撰稿，并拥有德克萨斯大学奥斯汀分校英语学士学位。TMFSunLion@TMFSunLionLeo Sun未持有文中提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐CrowdStrike、微软和SentinelOne。《Motley Fool》推荐Palo Alto Networks。《Motley Fool》遵循信息披露政策。提及的股票Palo Alto Networks纳斯达克：PANW$357.50(-4.68%)-$17.56Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取权限---%平均回报微软纳斯达克：MSFT$492.81(-0.99%)-$4.94CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$236.12(-3.90%)-$9.58SentinelOne纽约证券交易所：S$22.51(-2.95%)-$0.69*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报率。成本基础和回报率根据前一个市场交易日收盘价计算。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-03-13T15:39:54+00:00"}},{"id":"news-931","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike的Falcon推动股价高涨，自由现金流倍数超100倍","title_en":"CrowdStrike's Falcon Has Its Shares Flying High at Over 100 Times Free Cash Flow | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章指出，CrowdStrike股价自2月低点上涨70%并创历史新高，与英伟达和Anthropic的合作增强了投资者信心。公司正从端点安全转向集成式网络安全操作系统，Falcon Flex模式允许客户按需激活模块，50%客户使用六个以上模块，美元净留存率升至115%，Flex客户ARR达17亿美元，同比增长120%。2026财年自由现金流12亿美元，利润率26%，但估值偏高，约125倍自由现金流。","summary_en":"Motley Fool notes CrowdStrike shares have climbed 70% from February lows to an all-time high, helped by partnerships with Nvidia and Anthropic. The company is shifting from endpoint security to an integrated cybersecurity operating system. Its Falcon Flex model lets customers activate modules on demand; 50% of customers use six or more modules, dollar-based net retention rose to 115%, and Flex ARR reached $1.7 billion, up 120% year over year. Fiscal 2026 free cash flow was $1.2 billion at a 26% margin, but the stock trades at roughly 125 times FCF.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:28:53.043422+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/05/19/crowdstrikes-falcon-has-shares-flying-high-at-over","content":"The market has recognized CrowdStrike (CRWD -1.07%) as a major winner in the evolving cybersecurity landscape. After some brief volatility earlier in the year, the stock has climbed 70% from its February lows and now trades at an all-time high.\nThe company's partnerships with tech leaders such as Nvidia and Anthropic helped persuade investors that its security platform will indeed be useful as AI's footprint expands across workplaces. Where the stock might go from here is tougher to gauge. Shares now trade at roughly 30 times sales even though revenue growth slowed to 22% last quarter. That valuation leaves little margin of safety for investors who buy at today's price.\nWhile CrowdStrike's role in AI will unfold over time, the current story for the cybersecurity company is about platform consolidation. Its strategy is gaining traction, driving the results that have fueled the market's optimism.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nFalcon flexes its muscles\nCrowdStrike is moving from its roots as an endpoint security vendor to an integrated cybersecurity operating system for its enterprise clients. The company's Falcon Flex model allows customers to buy credits for the entire platform and activate new security modules on demand. This removes the hassle of traditional sales cycles and has been a key driver of adoption growth.\nThe results have been strong: 50% of the company's customers now use six or more of its modules. This helped the company improve its dollar-based net retention rate by 3 percentage points to 115%. Annual recurring revenue (ARR) from Flex customers reached $1.7 billion at the end of last year, up 120% year over year.\nCrowdStrike's competitive advantage stems from its network effects and data-driven approach to cybersecurity. The company's platform collects massive amounts of data from its installed base of clients, which it uses to train its artificial intelligence (AI) models. As more businesses subscribe to the company's platform, the volume of data flowing through it increases, making it more effective at detecting and responding to threats.\nHow profitable can the business become?\nThe Falcon Flex model has proven to be a powerful tool for expanding CrowdStrike's sales to its established customers. Net new ARR reaccelerated in the second half of its fiscal 2026 (which ended Jan. 31), and management expects to add another $1.2 billion in fiscal 2027.\nThe company generates substantial cash flow. Free cash flow (FCF) reached $1.2 billion in fiscal 2026, for a margin of 26%. Management expects margins to expand to at least 30% this fiscal year. That level of profitability is impressive, but the stock is a bit rich at this stage of the game, trading at around 125 times FCF.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-1.07%) $-2.82Current Price$259.67Key Data PointsMarket Cap$269BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$258.53 - $263.8752wk Range$85.68 - $263.87Volume8.3MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nThe valuation has held up, even as revenue growth has naturally decelerated from over 50% a few years ago to the low 20% range today. CrowdStrike is a high-quality business, but interested investors should be patient and wait for a better entry point.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400About the AuthorBryan White is a contributing Stock Analyst at The Motley Fool, covering publicly traded companies across a wide range of industries and market caps. He brings more than a decade of experience as an analyst, advisor, and writer for Fool.com and several premium TMF services, including Stock Advisor, Everlasting Portfolio, Million Dollar Portfolio, and Dividend Investor Canada, where he served as lead advisor. Bryan specializes in long-term, buy-to-hold investing and enjoys making complex financial concepts approachable and engaging for individual investors. Bryan’s path to investing included entrepreneurship, which still shapes how he evaluates businesses today.TMFCaccamisiBryan White has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike and Nvidia. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$259.67(-1.07%)-$2.82Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"市场已将CrowdStrike（CRWD -1.07%）视为不断演变的网络安全领域中的大赢家。经历年初一段短暂的波动后，该股已从2月低点上涨70%，目前处于历史最高水平。\n该公司与英伟达和Anthropic等科技巨头的合作，帮助说服投资者相信，随着人工智能在工作场所的影响力不断扩大，其安全平台确实会发挥作用。至于该股从这里还能走多远，则更难判断。尽管上季度营收增速放缓至22%，该股目前的市销率仍约为30倍。对于以今日价格买入的投资者而言，这一估值几乎没有安全边际。\n虽然CrowdStrike在人工智能领域的作用还将随着时间展开，但这家网络安全公司的当前故事在于平台整合。其战略正获得发展势头，推动了支撑市场乐观情绪的业绩表现。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\nFalcon展现实力\nCrowdStrike正从端点安全供应商的根基，转型为面向企业客户的集成式网络安全操作系统。该公司的Falcon Flex模式允许客户为整个​​平台购买积分，并按需启用新的安全模块。这消除了传统销售周期的繁琐，成为推动采用率增长的关键因素。\n业绩十分强劲：目前该公司50%的客户使用其六个或更多模块。这帮助公司将美元口径净留存率提高3个百分点，达到115%。截至去年年底，Flex客户带来的年度经常性收入（ARR）达到17亿美元，同比增长120%。\nCrowdStrike的竞争优势源于其网络效应以及数据驱动的网络安全方法。该公司的平台从其客户基础中收集海量数据，并利用这些数据训练人工智能（AI）模型。随着越来越多企业订阅公司的平台，流经平台的数据量不断增加，使其在检测和应对威胁方面更加有效。\n这项业务的盈利能力能达到多高？\n事实证明，Falcon Flex模式是扩大CrowdStrike对现有客户销售额的有力工具。在截至1月31日的2026财年下半年，净新增ARR重新加速增长，而管理层预计2027财年还将新增12亿美元。\n公司产生了可观的现金流。2026财年自由现金流（FCF）达到12亿美元，利润率为26%。管理层预计本财年利润率将扩大至至少30%。这一盈利水平令人印象深刻，但现阶段该股估值略显昂贵，市盈率约为125倍自由现金流。\n展开NASDAQ：CRWD CrowdStrike高级功能Moneyball综合评分85/100今日变化（-1.07%）$-2.82当前价格$259.67关键数据点市值2690亿美元。市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算，不包括未上市、私人持有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$258.53 - $263.87过去52周区间$85.68 - $263.87成交量830万平均成交量1020万毛利率75.12%\n即使营收增速自然地从几年前超过50%放缓至如今的20%出头，这一估值仍维持稳健。CrowdStrike是一家高质量企业，但感兴趣的投资者应保持耐心，等待更好的入场点。接下来阅读2026年9月24日•作者：Jake LerchCrowdStrike对比Figma：哪只科技股更值得买入\n2026？2026年9月23日 •作者：Adam Spatacco不是Palantir。不是美光。Jim Cramer刚刚称为“必买”股票的3250亿美元英伟达合作伙伴2026年9月22日 •作者：Pamela KockCrowdStrike对比Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？2026年9月21日 •作者：Leo Sun现在值得买的两只百万富翁制造者网络安全股票2026年9月17日 •作者：Catie Hogan将在2027年称霸的两只网络安全股票2026年9月15日 •作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA这只网络安全股票可能将1000美元变成超过4400美元关于作者Bryan White是《Motley Fool》的特约股票分析师，负责涵盖各行各业、不同市值的上市公司。他拥有十多年分析师、顾问和Fool.com撰稿人经验，并曾为多项TMF高级服务担任顾问，包括Stock Advisor、Everlasting Portfolio、Million Dollar Portfolio和Dividend Investor Canada，在后者担任首席顾问。Bryan专注于长期买入并持有的投资，也喜欢让复杂的金融概念变得易于个人投资者理解且引人入胜。Bryan的投资之路始于创业经历，这段经历至今仍影响着他评估企业的方式。TMFCaccamisiBryan White不持有文中提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐CrowdStrike和英伟达。《Motley Fool》遵循信息披露政策。提及的股票CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$259.67（-1.07%）-$2.82Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报率*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报率。成本基础和回报率基于前一个交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-05-19T18:12:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-835","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike宣布1拆4股票拆分且业绩强劲，该股值得买入吗？","title_en":"CrowdStrike Just Announced a 4-for-1 Stock Split and Robust Results. Is the Stock a Buy? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"《Motley Fool》报道，CrowdStrike宣布首次股票拆分，董事会批准1拆4的前瞻性拆股，以股票股息形式实施，无需股东批准。截至2026年6月25日登记在册的股东将每股额外获得三股，7月2日起按拆股调整后交易。公司2027财年第一季度营收同比增长26%至13.9亿美元，年度经常性收入增长24%至55亿美元，调整后每股收益增长51%至1.10美元，均超预期。文章还提及公司在端点保护领域的行业地位及估值偏高的风险。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reports that CrowdStrike announced its first-ever stock split, with the board approving a 4-for-1 forward split effected as a stock dividend, requiring no shareholder approval. Shareholders of record as of June 25, 2026 will receive three additional shares per share, with split-adjusted trading beginning July 2. In fiscal 2027 Q1, revenue rose 26% year over year to $1.39 billion, annual recurring revenue grew 24% to $5.5 billion, and adjusted EPS climbed 51% to $1.10, beating estimates. The article also notes the company's industry standing in endpoint protection and its rich valuation.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:50:56.137208+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/06/03/crowdstrike-4-for-1-stock-split-stock-a-buy","content":"There's no denying the ongoing threat of cybersecurity attacks. The global average cost of a data breach in 2025 was $4.44 million, according to a report by IBM, and the threat grows with each passing year. Add to that the threat of hackers deploying artificial intelligence (AI) to gain access, and the stakes have never been higher. Cybersecurity has become a crucial consideration for every business -- and CrowdStrike Holdings (CRWD +1.80%) is one of the undisputed leaders in the field.\nThe company's track record of consistent execution and strong business performance has fueled an impressive ascent. CrowdStrike stock has gained 394% over the past three years (as of this writing), driven by strong revenue and profit growth, thanks to growing demand for its cybersecurity solutions. In fact, since CrowdStrike's initial public offering (IPO) in mid-2019, the stock has soared from a debut price of $34 to more than $747, representing gains of 2,097%.\nOn Wednesday, in conjunction with its quarterly financial report, CrowdStrike announced plans for its first-ever stock split. This revelation has prompted investors to take a fresh look at the stock. Let's take a look to see what it means for investors.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nThe fine print\nCrowdStrike announced that its board of directors had approved a 4-for-1 forward stock split, to be effected as a stock dividend -- meaning it doesn't require shareholder approval.\nStockholders of record as of June 25, 2026, will receive three additional shares of stock for each share they own after the market close on Wednesday, July 1. The stock is expected to begin trading on a split-adjusted basis on July 2.\nCrowdStrike shareholders won't need to take any further action to receive the additional shares. Investment banks and brokerage firms will handle the details behind the scenes, and the additional stock will be added to investor accounts. The timing can vary from brokerage to brokerage, so the newly issued shares may not appear immediately on July 2. Rest assured, the additional shares will appear in due course.\nThe math is relatively simple. For each share of CrowdStrike stock a shareholder owns -- currently trading for roughly $748 per share (as of this writing) -- post-split, investors will hold 4 shares worth $187 each (4 x $187 = $748).\nIs CrowdStrike stock a buy?\nWhile the stock split alone isn't reason enough to buy CrowdStrike, there are other reasons to buy the cybersecurity expert. The company's recent financial report backs up that contention.\nIn its fiscal 2027 first quarter (ended April 30), CrowdStrike reported revenue that climbed 26% year over year to $1.39 billion, fueled by record annual recurring revenue (ARR) that grew 24% to $5.5 billion. This drove adjusted earnings per share (EPS) up 51% to $1.10. Analysts' consensus estimates called for revenue of $1.36 billion and adjusted EPS of $1.07, so CrowdStrike beat on both counts.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(1.80%) $4.34Current Price$245.70Key Data PointsMarket Cap$252BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$233.19 - $250.3252wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Volume12.3MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nBeyond the financial results, CrowdStrike's bona fides are well documented. AI start-up Anthropic recently developed Claude Mythos Preview, a frontier AI model that discovered thousands of exploits hackers could use to gain access to critical systems -- including \"every major operating system and web browser.\" The company formed a coalition of big tech companies to fix these loopholes, and CrowdStrike was one of just two cybersecurity leaders initially invited to participate.\nIf you have any doubts as to CrowdStrike's pedigree, consider this. The company was rated as a leader in Gartner's 2026 Magic Quadrant for endpoint protection, marking the seventh consecutive appearance.\nEarlier this year, Forrester released a Total Economic Impact study that revealed that CrowdStrike customers achieved a 273% return on investment by \"reducing breach risk and simplifying security operations.\"\nTaken together, the company's long track record of execution, impressive share price gains, and industry accolades make CrowdStrike stock a winning investment.\nThere is the matter of the stock's valuation to consider, which will be off-putting to some investors. The surging price has led to a commensurate increase in its valuation. CrowdStrike is currently selling for 154 times forward earnings -- which is by no means cheap. However, the stock has soared 394% over the past three years, more than five times the 76% return of the S&P 500 during the same period, illustrating why it's worthy of a premium valuation.\nThe company's consistent track record makes it a great candidate for dollar-cost averaging, a strategy that lets you buy fewer shares when the price is higher and more when it's lower.\nIf you still think that CrowdStrike is too pricey right now, it certainly deserves a place on your watch list.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400Sep 14, 2026 •By Danny Vena, CPAWhy CrowdStrike Stock Rocketed Higher TodaySep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoCrowdStrike vs. UiPath: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoC3.ai vs. CrowdStrike: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 13, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoCybersecurity Is the Next Big Market for Artificial Intelligence (AI), According to Jensen Huang. This Super Stock-Split Stock Is the One to Own.About the AuthorDanny Vena, CPA, is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst specializing in artificial intelligence, cloud computing, semiconductors, software, cybersecurity, and consumer electronics. He is a Certified Public Accountant and previously worked as a controller and accountant across small and midsize businesses. Danny also served 13 years in the U.S. Army. He holds a bachelor’s degree in accounting from the University of Phoenix.TMFLifeIsGood@dannyvenaDanny Vena, CPA has positions in CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike and International Business Machines. The Motley Fool recommends Gartner. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$245.70(+1.80%)+$4.34Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnInternational Business MachinesNYSE: IBM$237.75(+0.11%)+$0.26S&P 500 IndexSNPINDEX: ^GSPC$7,637.76(+1.14%)+$85.95GartnerNYSE: IT$187.80(-1.97%)-$3.77Forrester ResearchNASDAQ: FORR$11.25(-3.18%)-$0.37*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"网络安全攻击持续构成威胁，这是毋庸置疑的。据 IBM 的一份报告，2025 年全球数据泄露的平均成本为 444 万美元，而且这一威胁逐年加剧。再加上黑客利用人工智能（AI）获取访问权限的威胁，风险从未如此之高。网络安全已成为每家企业都必须认真考虑的问题，而 CrowdStrike Holdings（CRWD +1.80%）是该领域公认的领导者之一。\n\n该公司持续稳定的执行力和强劲的业务表现推动了其令人瞩目的崛起。截至本文撰写时，CrowdStrike 股票在过去三年上涨了 394%，这得益于其网络安全解决方案需求不断增长所带来的强劲营收和利润增长。事实上，自 CrowdStrike 于 2019 年年中首次公开募股（IPO）以来，其股价已从 34 美元的发行价飙升至超过 747 美元，涨幅达到 2,097%。\n\n周三，CrowdStrike 在发布季度财报的同时，宣布计划进行首次股票拆分。这一消息促使投资者重新审视该股票。让我们看看这对投资者意味着什么。\n\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n\n细则\n\nCrowdStrike 宣布，其董事会已批准按 4 比 1 的比例进行正向股票拆分，并以股票股息的形式实施——这意味着无需获得股东批准。\n\n截至 2026 年 6 月 25 日登记在册的股东，将在 7 月 1 日（星期三）收市后，每持有一股股票额外获得三股。预计该股票将于 7 月 2 日开始按拆分调整后的价格交易。\n\nCrowdStrike 股东无需采取任何进一步行动即可获得额外股份。投资银行和经纪公司将处理幕后细节，新增股票将计入投资者账户。具体时间可能因经纪公司而异，因此新发行的股份可能不会在 7 月 2 日当天立即显示。但请放心，额外股份会在适当时候到账。\n\n计算相对简单。对于股东持有的每一股 CrowdStrike 股票——截至本文撰写时目前每股交易价格约为 748 美元——拆分后，投资者将持有 4 股、每股价值 187 美元的股票（4 × 187 美元 = 748 美元）。\n\nCrowdStrike 股票值得买吗？\n\n虽然仅凭股票拆分本身并不足以成为买入 CrowdStrike 的理由，但买入这家网络安全专家公司还有其他理由。该公司最近的财务报告支持了这一观点。\n\n在其 2027 财年第一季度（截至 4 月 30 日），CrowdStrike 报告营收同比增长 26%，达到 13.9 亿美元；年度经常性收入（ARR）创下纪录，增长 24%，达到 55 亿美元。这推动调整后每股收益（EPS）增长 51%，达到 1.10 美元。分析师共识预期营收为 13.6 亿美元、调整后每股收益为 1.07 美元，因此 CrowdStrike 两项指标均超出预期。\n\n展开NASDAQ：CRWD CrowdStrike 高级功能 Moneyball 综合评分 85/100 今日变动（1.80%）4.34 美元 当前价格 245.70 美元 关键数据点 市值 2520 亿美元 市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私募或双重股权结构中的非交易股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间 233.19 美元 - 250.32 美元 52 周区间 85.68 美元 - 250.32 美元 成交量 1230 万 平均成交量 1020 万 毛利率 75.12%\n\n除了财务业绩之外，CrowdStrike 的实力也有充分记录。人工智能初创公司 Anthropic 最近开发了 Claude Mythos Preview，这是一款前沿的\n发现数千个黑客可利用来访问关键系统的漏洞的 AI 模型——包括“每一种主要操作系统和网页浏览器”。该公司组建了一个由大型科技公司组成的联盟来修复这些漏洞，而 CrowdStrike 是最初获邀参与的仅有两家网络安全领导者之一。\n如果你对 CrowdStrike 的资历有任何疑问，不妨考虑这一点。该公司在 Gartner 2026 年端点保护魔力象限中被评为领导者，这也是其连续第七次入选。\n今年早些时候，Forrester 发布了一项总体经济影响研究，显示 CrowdStrike 客户通过“降低数据泄露风险并简化安全运营”实现了 273% 的投资回报率。\n综合来看，该公司长期稳定的执行记录、令人印象深刻的股价涨幅以及业内荣誉，使 CrowdStrike 股票成为一项成功的投资。\n还需要考虑该股的估值问题，这会让一些投资者望而却步。价格飙升也带来了估值相应的上涨。CrowdStrike 目前的预期市盈率为 154 倍——无论如何都算不上便宜。然而，该股过去三年飙升了 394%，是同期标普 500 指数 76% 回报率的五倍多，这说明它为何值得享有溢价估值。\n该公司始终如一的业绩记录使其成为定投策略的绝佳候选，这种策略允许你在价格较高时少买一些股票，在价格较低时多买一些。\n如果你仍然认为 CrowdStrike 目前太贵，它当然值得列入你的观察名单。接下来阅读2026 年 9 月 17 日 •作者：Catie Hogan2027 年将称霸的 2 只网络安全股票2026 年 9 月 15 日 •作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA这只网络安全股票可能将 1,000 美元变成超过 4,400 美元2026 年 9 月 14 日 •作者：Danny Vena，CPACrowdStrike 股价今日为何大幅上涨2026 年 9 月 14 日 •作者：Sara AppinoCrowdStrike 对比 UiPath：2026 年哪只科技股更值得买入？2026 年 9 月 14 日 •作者：Sara AppinoC3.ai 对比 CrowdStrike：2026 年哪只科技股更值得买入？2026 年 9 月 13 日 •作者：Adam Spatacco据 Jensen Huang 称，网络安全是人工智能（AI）的下一个大型市场。这只超级拆分股才是值得持有的股票。\n关于作者Danny Vena，CPA，是《Motley Fool》特约科技分析师，专门研究人工智能、云计算、半导体、软件、网络安全和消费电子。他是一名注册会计师，曾在中小型企业担任财务总监和会计师。Danny 还曾在美国陆军服役 13 年。他拥有菲尼克斯大学会计学学士学位。TMFLifeIsGood@dannyvenaDanny Vena，CPA 持有 CrowdStrike 的头寸。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐 CrowdStrike 和 International Business Machines。《Motley Fool》推荐 Gartner。《Motley Fool》遵循披露政策。\n提及的股票CrowdStrike纳斯达克：CRWD$245.70（+1.80%）+$4.34Motley Fool 股票顾问最新推荐获取访问权限---% 平均回报International Business Machines纽约证券交易所：IBM$237.75（+0.11%）+$0.26标普 500 指数SNPINDEX：^GSPC$7,637.76（+1.14%）+$85.95Gartner纽约证券交易所：IT$187.80（-1.97%）-$3.77Forrester Research纳斯达克：FORR$11.25（-3.18%）-$0.37*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报率。成本基础和回报率基于前一个市场日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-06-04T01:08:04+00:00"}},{"id":"news-643","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS + Yahoo title resolution via Reader","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"股票拆分后CrowdStrike股票是否值得买入？","title_en":"Is CrowdStrike Stock a Buy After Its Stock Split? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章称，CrowdStrike于7月2日实施1拆4股票拆分，股价降至193美元，拆分后股价一度上涨约2%至196美元。文章指出，自6月3日宣布拆分以来股价上涨约8%，公司最新季度营收增长26%至13.9亿美元，净利润2800万美元，净新增年度经常性收入增长32%。文章认为公司势头良好，但估值偏高，建议等待拆分后涨势消退再买入。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reports CrowdStrike executed a 4-for-1 stock split on July 2, lowering its share price to $193, with the stock rising about 2% to $196 after the split took effect. It notes the stock is up about 8% since the split was announced June 3, and that latest-quarter revenue rose 26% to $1.39 billion, net income was $28 million, and net new ARR jumped 32%. The article sees strong momentum but a rich valuation, suggesting waiting for the post-split spike to subside before buying.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:49:50.745717+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/07/06/is-crowdstrike-stock-a-buy-before-date","content":"On July 2, cybersecurity leader CrowdStrike (CRWD +1.80%) underwent a 4-for-1 stock split, reducing its share price to $193. The day before, the stock closed around $773 per share, and each stockholder of record received four shares for each share they held.\nThe price rose after the split took effect, up about 2% to $196 during the trading day. That's not unusual -- splits generally result in the stock price popping, both before and shortly after the split.\nSince the split was announced on June 3, CrowdStrike's stock is up about 8%. This is because investors wanted to buy in to get the split, and they anticipate it getting a lift from its new, more accessible stock price.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nBut does it really change anything for the stock beyond this short-term spike?\nCrowdStrike stock is not cheap\nThe stock has had a good year, up about 66% year to date on a split-adjusted basis.\nIt has been fueled by excellent performance. In the latest quarter, revenue rose 26% to $1.39 billion, and CrowdStrike posted net income of $28 million, up from a $104 million loss the same quarter a year ago. Its net new annual recurring revenue (ARR) jumped 32%, and it posted record free cash flow.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(1.80%) $4.34Current Price$245.70Key Data PointsMarket Cap$252BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$233.19 - $250.3252wk Range$85.68 - $250.32Volume12.3MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nManagement raised its revenue and earnings guidance for fiscal 2027 and lifted its outlook for net new ARR by 520 basis points.\nThe company has great momentum, and the stock split should make it more accessible to more investors who can now more easily buy full shares.\nBut the concern is its valuation. CrowdStrike has a sky-high price-to-earnings ratio (P/E) of 401 but a more reasonable forward P/E of 39. I do think the stock is a buy, but it might be wise to wait for the split spike to subside and buy at a lower price.Read NextSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400Sep 14, 2026 •By Danny Vena, CPAWhy CrowdStrike Stock Rocketed Higher TodaySep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoCrowdStrike vs. UiPath: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 14, 2026 •By Sara AppinoC3.ai vs. CrowdStrike: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 13, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoCybersecurity Is the Next Big Market for Artificial Intelligence (AI), According to Jensen Huang. This Super Stock-Split Stock Is the One to Own.About the AuthorDave mainly covers financials, consumer goods, and technology stocks and ETFs. He wrote for the Fool from 2019-2023 and rejoined the Fool in 2026. In the past he's covered mutual funds and institutional investments for Pensions & Investments, personal finance for S&P, money markets and bonds for Crane Data, and stocks for ValueWalk.TMFdkovaleskiDave Kovaleski has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$245.70(+1.80%)+$4.34Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"7月2日，网络安全领军企业CrowdStrike（CRWD +1.80%）进行了1拆4的股票拆分，将其股价降至193美元。前一天，该股收于每股约773美元，每位登记在册的股东每持有1股便获得4股。\n拆分生效后，股价在交易日内上涨约2%，至196美元。这并不罕见——股票拆分通常会导致股价在拆分前及拆分后不久上涨。\n自6月3日宣布拆分以来，CrowdStrike股价已上涨约8%。这是因为投资者希望买入以获得拆分后的股票，并预计其更易接近的新股价将带来提振。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n但除了这种短期飙升之外，它真的会改变这只股票的其他任何情况吗？\nCrowdStrike股票并不便宜\n该股今年表现良好，按拆分调整后计算，年初至今上涨约66%。\n这得益于出色的业绩表现。在最近一个季度，营收增长26%，至13.9亿美元；CrowdStrike实现净利润2800万美元，而上年同期为净亏损1.04亿美元。其净新增年度经常性收入（ARR）跃升32%，并创下自由现金流纪录。\n展开\nNASDAQ：CRWD\nCrowdStrike\n高级功能\nMoneyball Superscore\n85/100\n今日变动\n(1.80%) 4.34美元\n当前价格\n245.70美元\n关键数据点\n市值\n2520亿美元\n市值仅根据已发行的公开交易股票计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n当日区间\n233.19美元 - 250.32美元\n52周区间\n85.68美元 - 250.32美元\n成交量\n1230万\n平均成交量\n1020万\n毛利率\n75.12%\n管理层上调了2027财年的营收和盈利指引，并将净新增ARR的预期提高了520个基点。\n该公司势头强劲，股票拆分应使其更容易被更多投资者买入，因为他们现在可以更轻松地购买整股。\n但令人担忧的是其估值。CrowdStrike的市盈率（P/E）高达401，但预期市盈率为39，更为合理。我确实认为该股值得买入，但或许明智的做法是等待拆分带来的涨势消退后，以更低价格买入。\n继续阅读\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Catie Hogan\n两只将在2027年称霸的网络安全股票\n2026年9月15日 • 作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA\n这只网络安全股票可能将1,000美元变成超过4,400美元\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Danny Vena，CPA\n为何CrowdStrike股票今日大幅飙升\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Sara Appino\nCrowdStrike对比UiPath：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Sara Appino\nC3.ai对比CrowdStrike：2026年哪只科技股更值得买入？\n2026年9月13日 • 作者：Adam Spatacco\n据黄仁勋称，网络安全是人工智能（AI）的下一个大市场。这只超级股票拆分股是值得持有的一只。\n关于作者\nDave主要报道金融、消费品和科技股票及ETF。他在2019年至2023年间为The Fool撰稿，并于2026年重新加入The Fool。过去，他曾为Pensions & Investments报道共同基金和机构投资，为S&P报道个人理财，为Crane Data报道货币市场和债券，并为ValueWalk报道股票。\nTMFdkovaleski\nDave Kovaleski未持有文中提及的任何股票头寸。The Motley Fool持有CrowdStrike的头寸并推荐CrowdStrike。The Motley Fool设有披露政策。\n提及的股票\nCrowdStrike\nNASDAQ：CRWD\n245.70美元\n(+1.80%)\n+4.34美元\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报*\n自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报以前一交易日收盘价为准。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-07-06T08:25:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-635","ktid":2575920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"2575920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"最新分拆后霍尼韦尔已有四只股票，哪只更值得买入？","title_en":"There Are Now 4 Honeywell Stocks After This Latest Spin-Off. Which Is the Better Buy Today? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"文章梳理霍尼韦尔分拆后形成的四家上市实体：霍尼韦尔技术公司、霍尼韦尔航空航天、Solstice先进材料和Quantinuum，并逐一评估投资价值。霍尼韦尔技术公司2025年备考营收增长3.5%、每股收益增长7%，但市盈率约28倍；霍尼韦尔航空航天市盈率约27倍，估值偏高；Solstice自九个月前分拆以来股价上涨近66%，受益于数据中心冷却、半导体材料和核能需求，被视为最佳潜力股；Quantinuum上市后上涨逾24%，霍尼韦尔技术持有约48.1%股份，但该公司尚未产生实质收入。","summary_en":"The article reviews the four listed entities created by Honeywell's break-up: Honeywell Technologies, Honeywell Aerospace, Solstice Advanced Materials and Quantinuum, assessing each as an investment. Honeywell Technologies posted pro forma 2025 revenue growth of 3.5% and EPS growth of 7% but trades at about 28 times forward earnings; Honeywell Aerospace trades near 27 times forward earnings, seen as pricey; Solstice has risen nearly 66% since its spin-off nine months ago, benefiting from data center cooling, semiconductor materials and nuclear demand, and is viewed as the best-positioned contender; Quantinuum has gained over 24% since its IPO, with Honeywell Technologies owning about 48.1%, though it has yet to generate material revenue.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T17:03:40.115655+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/07/07/there-are-now-4-honeywell-stocks-after-this-latest/","content":"You may know Honeywell as one of the world's largest industrial conglomerates, but following last week's spinoff transaction, that is no longer the case. Following the spinoff of Honeywell Aerospace (HONA -1.72%) as a separate, publicly traded company, Honeywell Inc. is now Honeywell Technologies (HON -0.14%), an industrial automation pure play.\nFurthermore, the latest corporate divestiture is the culmination of other spinoff activities the company has undertaken over the past 12 months. As you may recall, last October, Honeywell spun off Solstice Advanced Materials (SOLS -2.02%), a specialty chemicals and materials company with exposure to fast-growing industries like data center cooling solutions and semiconductor materials.\nAlso, last month, prior to the aerospace spinoff, Honeywell took its quantum computing business, Quantinuum (QNT -2.65%), public, with Honeywell Technologies maintaining a large stake.\nAmong these four public entities, which one presents the greatest opportunity for investors right now? Let's take a look at each one and determine which, if any, is worthy of a buy right now.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nTread carefully with Honeywell Technologies\nOn one hand, owning Honeywell Technologies means owning the most stable of the former industrial conglomerate's disparate businesses. Long the core of Honeywell's overall business, the industrial automation segment presents the opportunity for steady profitability and growth. A look at its financials confirms this view.\nExpandNASDAQ: HONHoneywell TechnologiesPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore66/100Today's Change(-0.14%) $-0.29Current Price$212.28Key Data PointsMarket Cap$67BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$209.18 - $212.7752wk Range$195.77 - $260.15Volume695.8KAvg Vol3.6MGross Margin37.84%Dividend Yield2.09%\nBased on pro forma financials released after last week's spinoff, Honeywell Technologies experienced 3.5% revenue growth and 7% earnings per share (EPS) growth, respectively, during 2025. Better yet, as Honeywell Technologies and Honeywell Aerospace continue with margin expansion efforts initiated prior to the spinoff, management has guided for the potential for Honeywell's core to experience double-digit earnings growth.\nStill, with Honeywell Automation trading for 28 times forward earnings after the spinoff , it's easy to see why shares have pulled back. You may want to wait for further weakness before entering a long-term position at a more favorable valuation. That said, given the company's indirect exposure to the quantum computing venture Quantinuum, keep the value of this position in mind when determining whether Honeywell Technologies is undervalued or overvalued.\nThe same goes for Honeywell Aerospace\nRight out of the gate, Honeywell Aerospace has become a hot stock. Aerospace stocks have, in general, been running hot lately, so it's not all that surprising that investors have bid up this spinoff stock on the heels of the divestiture. The question now is whether this supplier of civilian and defense aerospace components and products represents a good value at current prices.\nExpandNASDAQ: HONAHoneywell AerospaceToday's Change(-1.72%) $-2.81Current Price$160.52Key Data PointsMarket Cap$52BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$159.39 - $163.9752wk Range$149.19 - $297.50Volume931.2KAvg Vol4.1M\nUnfortunately, just like its former parent's, its shares appear pricey. They're trading for around 27 times forward earnings, so once again, the market has factored in growth resurgence potential. That said, Honeywell Aerospace technically remains cheap compared to its richly valued peers like GE Aerospace, which trades for nearly 50 times forward earnings, and Boeing, which trades for over 90 times forward earnings.\nHowever, Boeing's seemingly rich valuation largely reflects a big anticipated rebound in earnings. With GE Aerospace, analysts expect the company to report nearly 15% earnings growth next year. For Honeywell Aerospace shares to experience further multiple expansion, say to a valuation well north of 30 times forward earnings, the company may have to really knock it out of the park to inspire a bullish response among investors.\nConversely, as expectations run high for a double-digit growth resurgence, any hiccup could lead to significant near-term losses. Hence, as with Honeywell Automation, tread carefully here.\nIs Solstice the dark horse contender?\nHoneywell Automation and Honeywell Aerospace may be garnering greater attention following the spinoff news, but if you're wondering which Honeywell stock to buy, Solstice Advanced Materials could be the dark horse contender. This comes even as its shares have surged nearly 66% since the spinoff from the former Honeywell nine months ago.\nSolstice's strong stock market performance isn't surprising. Not only does this stock offer exposure to industries adjacent to the artificial intelligence (AI) megatrend, like data center cooling solutions and semiconductor materials, but Solstice also manufactures uranium hexafluoride, an essential material used in nuclear power plants. This makes it a nuclear energy stock as much as its AI-related tailwinds make it an AI stock.\nExpandNASDAQ: SOLSSolstice Advanced MaterialsToday's Change(-2.02%) $-1.17Current Price$56.81Key Data PointsMarket Cap$9.2BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$56.05 - $57.1652wk Range$40.43 - $90.80Volume1.1MAvg Vol3.4MGross Margin30.62%Dividend Yield0.39%\nThat said, Solstice shares have stalled in recent months, pulling back slightly from the all-time highs following its latest earnings. The fact that Solstice did not raise guidance after last reporting earnings may have something to do with it. Still, in the quarters ahead, if AI- and nuclear-energy-related tailwinds lead to further strong growth, sentiment could swing back to bullish.\nWith shares trading for just 30 times forward earnings, against forecasted earnings growth exceeding 20%, renewed bullishness could drive a major rerating. Among the Honeywell spinoff stocks, Solstice appears the best positioned to outperform.\nThe best approach with moonshot Quantinuum\nAs mentioned earlier, Quantinuum technically isn't a Honeywell spinoff. Instead of spinning it off and distributing the newly issued stock to shareholders, Honeywell took its quantum computing venture public, raising nearly $1.7 billion. Following the IPO, Honeywell Automation owns around 48.1% of the company's outstanding shares.\nQuantinuum has rallied by over 24% since its public market debut. Given Quantinuum's $19.5 billion market cap, Honeywell Automation's stake is worth around $9.4 billion. Not too shabby, considering Honeywell Automation's current market value is around $73 billion. As with other quantum computing stocks, this one's valuation remains largely based on future potential. Quantinuum has yet to generate material revenue, with sell-side analysts estimating heavy losses in the foreseeable future.\nInstead of owning Quantinuum directly, investors bullish on its prospects may want to own Honeywell Automation instead. Again, Honeywell Automation could decide to start paring down its position, providing billions in fresh capital for growth and/or stock buybacks. At the same time, even if Quantinuum suffers a major pullback, that may have just a muted impact on Honeywell Automation's stock performance, given how most of its value comes from its automation business.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCaterpillar vs. Honeywell International: Which Industrials Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 9, 2026 •By Anders Bylund7 Best Quantum Computing Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 4, 2026 •By Reuben Gregg BrewerHoneywell Is Now Three Companies. Here's Which Piece I'd Actually Own.Sep 24, 2026 •By Prosper Junior BakinyBillionaire Bill Ackman’s Pershing Square Capital Management Has 12.7% of Its Portfolio Invested in This Beaten-Down StockSep 24, 2026 •By Todd ShriberWant Reliable Dividend Income? These 2 Industrial Stocks DeliverSep 24, 2026 •By Leo SunRivian vs. the S&P 500: Which Investment Wins Through 2030?About the AuthorThomas Niel is a contributing Analyst at The Motley Fool, covering publicly traded companies in the consumer goods and technology sectors. Prior to the Motley Fool, Thomas was a contributing Analyst for several online investing publications, including InvestorPlace, Seeking Alpha, and TipRanks. He also has past career experience in the accounting and government contracting industries. He holds a B.B.A. in Accounting from Marymount University. Thomas won his school's geography bee in the fifth grade, but retired from the professional geography bee circuit shortly thereafter.TMFThomasNielThomas Niel has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Boeing, GE Aerospace, and Honeywell Technologies. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedHoneywell TechnologiesNASDAQ: HON$211.76(-0.38%)-$0.81Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnSolstice Advanced MaterialsNASDAQ: SOLS$56.81(-2.02%)-$1.17QuantinuumNASDAQ: QNT$48.78(-2.65%)-$1.33Honeywell AerospaceNASDAQ: HONA$160.39(-1.80%)-$2.94*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"你可能知道霍尼韦尔是世界上最大的工业综合企业之一，但在上周完成分拆交易后，情况已不再如此。随着霍尼韦尔航空航天（HONA -1.72%）作为一家独立的上市公司完成分拆，霍尼韦尔公司如今成为霍尼韦尔技术（HON -0.14%），一家专注于工业自动化的公司。\n此外，最新的公司资产剥离，是该公司过去12个月开展的其他分拆活动的最终成果。正如你可能记得的那样，去年10月，霍尼韦尔分拆出了Solstice Advanced Materials（SOLS -2.02%），这是一家专用化学品和材料公司，涉足数据中心冷却解决方案、半导体材料等快速增长的行业。\n此外，上个月，在航空航天业务分拆之前，霍尼韦尔将其量子计算业务Quantinuum（QNT -2.65%）推向公众市场，同时霍尼韦尔技术仍持有其大量股份。\n在这四家上市实体中，哪一家目前为投资者提供了最大的机会？让我们逐一看看，并判断其中是否有任何一家目前值得买入。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n谨慎对待霍尼韦尔技术\n一方面，持有霍尼韦尔技术意味着持有这家前工业综合企业各项业务中最稳定的部分。工业自动化业务长期以来一直是霍尼韦尔整体业务的核心，带来了稳定盈利和增长的机会。查看其财务数据证实了这一观点。\n展开NASDAQ：HON霍尼韦尔技术高级功能Moneyball超级评分66/100今日变化（-0.14%）$-0.29当前价格$212.28关键数据点市值$67B市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$209.18 - $212.7752周区间$195.77 - $260.15成交量695.8K平均成交量3.6M毛利率37.84%股息率2.09%\n根据上周分拆后公布的备考财务数据，霍尼韦尔技术在2025年分别实现了3.5%的营收增长和7%的每股收益（EPS）增长。更好的是，随着霍尼韦尔技术和霍尼韦尔航空航天继续推进分拆前启动的利润率扩张工作，管理层已给出指引，霍尼韦尔核心业务的盈利可能实现两位数增长。\n不过，分拆后霍尼韦尔自动化业务的远期市盈率为28倍，因此很容易理解股价为何出现回落。在更有利的估值水平下建立长期仓位之前，你可能需要等待进一步走弱。话虽如此，鉴于公司间接持有量子计算企业Quantinuum的敞口，在判断霍尼韦尔技术被低估还是高估时，请将这一仓位的价值考虑在内。\n霍尼韦尔航空航天也是如此\n霍尼韦尔航空航天一上市就成为热门股票。总体而言，航空航天类股票近期表现火热，因此投资者在资产剥离后推高这只分拆股票，并不十分令人意外。现在的问题是，这家民用和国防航空航天零部件及产品供应商按当前价格是否具有良好的投资价值。\n展开NASDAQ：HONA霍尼韦尔航空航天今日变化（-1.72%）$-2.81当前价格$160.52关键数据点市值$52B市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中的非交易\n股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内波动区间$159.39 - $163.97\n52周波动区间$149.19 - $297.50\n成交量931.2K\n平均成交量4.1M\n\n遗憾的是，就像其前母公司一样，其股票似乎估值偏高。目前股价约为预期收益的27倍，因此市场再次计入了增长复苏的潜力。话虽如此，与估值高昂的同行相比，霍尼韦尔航空航天在技术上仍然便宜，例如通用电气航空航天的预期收益市盈率接近50倍，而波音则超过90倍。\n\n不过，波音看似高昂的估值，很大程度上反映了市场对其收益大幅反弹的预期。对于通用电气航空航天，分析师预计该公司明年的收益将增长近15%。如果霍尼韦尔航空航天的股票要进一步扩大估值倍数，比如升至远高于预期收益30倍的水平，那么该公司可能必须真正拿出惊艳表现，才能激发投资者的看涨反应。\n\n相反，随着市场对两位数增长复苏的预期高涨，任何小插曲都可能导致近期大幅亏损。因此，与霍尼韦尔自动化一样，在这里也要谨慎行事。\n\nSolstice是黑马竞争者吗？\n\n霍尼韦尔自动化和霍尼韦尔航空航天可能在分拆消息后获得更多关注，但如果你想知道该买哪只霍尼韦尔股票，Solstice Advanced Materials可能是黑马竞争者。即便如此，自从九个月前从原霍尼韦尔分拆出来以来，其股价已经飙升近66%。\n\nSolstice强劲的股市表现并不令人意外。这只股票不仅让投资者得以接触人工智能（AI）大趋势相关的邻近行业，例如数据中心冷却解决方案和半导体材料，而且Solstice还生产六氟化铀，这是一种核电站使用的关键材料。这使它既是一只核能股票，而其与AI相关的顺风因素也使其成为一只AI股票。\n\n展开NASDAQ: SOLS\nSolstice Advanced Materials\n今日变动(-2.02%) $-1.17\n当前价格$56.81\n关键数据点\n市值$9.2B\n市值仅根据公开交易的已发行股票计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权结构中未交易的股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n日内波动区间$56.05 - $57.16\n52周波动区间$40.43 - $90.80\n成交量1.1M\n平均成交量3.4M\n毛利率30.62%\n股息收益率0.39%\n\n话虽如此，Solstice的股价近几个月陷入停滞，在最近一次公布财报后从历史高点小幅回落。Solstice在上次公布收益后没有上调业绩指引，这一事实可能与此有关。不过，在未来几个季度，如果与AI和核能相关的顺风因素推动进一步强劲增长，市场情绪可能重新转为看涨。\n\n目前股价仅为预期收益的30倍，而预期收益增幅超过20%，市场看涨情绪重燃可能推动估值大幅重估。在霍尼韦尔分拆股票中，Solstice似乎最有希望跑赢大盘。\n\n押注Quantinuum这只潜力股的最佳方式\n\n如前所述，Quantinuum严格来说并不是霍尼韦尔的分拆公司。霍尼韦尔没有将其分拆并把新发行的股票分配给股东，而是让其量子计算业务上市，并筹集了近17亿美元。IPO之后，霍尼韦尔自动化持有该公司约48.1%的已发行股票。\n\nQuantinuum自进入公开市场以来已经上涨超过24%。鉴于Quantinuum的市值为195亿美元，霍尼韦尔\nAutomation持有的股份价值约94亿美元。考虑到Honeywell Automation目前约730亿美元的市值，这个数字相当可观。与其他量子计算股票一样，这只股票的估值仍主要基于未来潜力。Quantinuum尚未产生实质性收入，卖方分析师预计其在可预见的未来将出现巨额亏损。\n看好Quantinuum前景的投资者可能希望持有Honeywell Automation，而不是直接持有Quantinuum。同样，Honeywell Automation可能决定开始削减其持仓，为增长和/或股票回购提供数十亿美元的新资本。与此同时，即使Quantinuum遭遇大幅回调，考虑到Honeywell Automation的大部分价值来自其自动化业务，这可能也只会对其股票表现产生有限影响。接下来阅读2026年9月24日 •作者：Jake Lerch卡特彼勒 vs. 霍尼韦尔国际：2026年哪只工业股更值得买？2026年9月9日 •作者：Anders Bylund2026年7只最佳量子计算股票及投资方式2026年9月4日 •作者：Reuben Gregg Brewer霍尼韦尔现已拆分为三家公司。我真正会持有的是其中哪一部分。2026年9月24日 •作者：Prosper Junior Bakiny亿万富翁比尔·阿克曼的潘兴广场资本管理公司将其投资组合的12.7%投入了这只跌跌不休的股票2026年9月24日 •作者：Todd Shriber想要可靠的股息收入？这两只工业股可以满足需求2026年9月24日 •作者：Leo SunRivian vs. 标普500：哪项投资能赢到2030年？关于作者Thomas Niel是《Motley Fool》的特约分析师，负责报道消费品和科技行业的上市公司。在加入《Motley Fool》之前，Thomas曾为多家在线投资出版物担任特约分析师，包括InvestorPlace、Seeking Alpha和TipRanks。他还曾在会计和政府承包行业工作。他拥有玛丽蒙特大学会计学工商管理学士学位。Thomas在五年级时赢得了学校的地理知识竞赛，但不久后便退出了职业地理知识竞赛圈。TMFThomasNielThomas Niel未持有文中提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有Boeing、GE Aerospace和Honeywell Technologies的仓位，并对这些公司给予推荐。《Motley Fool》遵循披露政策。提及的股票Honeywell Technologies纳斯达克：HON211.76美元（-0.38%）-0.81美元Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报Solstice Advanced Materials纳斯达克：SOLS56.81美元（-2.02%）-1.17美元Quantinuum纳斯达克：QNT48.78美元（-2.65%）-1.33美元Honeywell Aerospace纳斯达克：HONA160.39美元（-1.80%）-2.94美元*所有推荐自成立以来的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-07-07T15:15:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-304","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike股价今日为何飙升","title_en":"Why CrowdStrike Stock Skyrocketed Today | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool报道，CrowdStrike公布2027财年第二季度财报后股价盘中一度大涨19.7%。营收14.7亿美元同比增长26%，调整后每股收益0.31美元同比增长34%，均超分析师预期；净新增年度经常性收入达3.33亿美元创纪录，同比增长51%，公司还上调全年业绩指引。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reports that CrowdStrike shares surged as much as 19.7% intraday after its fiscal 2027 Q2 results. Revenue rose 26% year over year to $1.47 billion and adjusted EPS climbed 34% to $0.31, both beating analyst estimates. Record net new annual recurring revenue reached $333 million, up 51% year over year, and management raised its full-year guidance.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:07:31.041470+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/27/why-crowdstrike-stock-skyrocketed-today","content":"Shares of CrowdStrike (CRWD -0.81%) charged sharply higher on Thursday, gaining as much as 19.7% in early trading. As of 2:42 p.m. ET, the stock was still up 19.6%.\nThe catalyst that sent the cloud-based cybersecurity specialist higher was financial results that blew past expectations.\nImage source: The Motley Fool.\nBlockbuster results\nCrowdStrike reported the results for its fiscal 2027 second quarter (ended July 31), and investors were clearly impressed. Revenue of $1.47 billion grew 26% year over year, as customers continued to expand their relationships with the platform. This forged record profits, with adjusted diluted earnings per share (EPS) of $0.31, up 34%.\nFor context, analysts' consensus estimates were calling for revenue of $1.44 billion and adjusted EPS of $0.29, so CrowdStrike easily surpassed both metrics.\nIt wasn't just the top- and bottom-line metrics that caught investors off guard. CrowdStrike added record net new annual recurring revenue (ARR) -- which measures subscription services growth -- of $333 million, up 51% year over year. This brought total ARR to $5.84 billion, up 25%. This suggests that CrowdStrike's growth spurt is far from over.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-0.81%) $-2.12Current Price$260.37Key Data PointsMarket Cap$269BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$258.53 - $263.8752wk Range$85.68 - $263.87Volume6.7MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nThe company also revealed that subscription customers continued to adopt more modules at a higher rate, with 51%, 35%, and 26% adopting six or more, seven or more, and eight or more modules, respectively.\nThis also translated to record operating cash flow and free cash flow of $530 million and $377 million, respectively.\nInvestors had other reasons to celebrate. For the full 2027 fiscal year, management lifted its outlook, calling for revenue of $6 billion and EPS of $1.25 at the midpoint of its guidance, ahead of analysts' consensus estimates, which called for revenue of $5.94 billion and EPS of $1.23.\nCrowdStrike stock isn't cheap, currently trading for 144 times next year's expected earnings and 45 times sales, but investors are rewarding the stock with a juicy premium, given its history of conservative guidance and robust results.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400About the AuthorDanny Vena, CPA, is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst specializing in artificial intelligence, cloud computing, semiconductors, software, cybersecurity, and consumer electronics. He is a Certified Public Accountant and previously worked as a controller and accountant across small and midsize businesses. Danny also served 13 years in the U.S. Army. He holds a bachelor’s degree in accounting from the University of Phoenix.TMFLifeIsGood@dannyvenaDanny Vena, CPA has positions in CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$260.03(-0.94%)-$2.46Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"CrowdStrike（CRWD -0.81%）股价周四大幅上涨，早盘一度上涨19.7%。截至美国东部时间下午2:42，该股仍上涨19.6%。\n推动这家云端网络安全专业公司的催化剂，是远超预期的财务业绩。\n图片来源：The Motley Fool。\n重磅业绩\nCrowdStrike 公布了其2027财年第二季度（截至7月31日）的业绩，投资者显然印象深刻。营收为14.7亿美元，同比增长26%，因为客户继续扩大与该平台的合作关系。这带来了创纪录的利润，调整后摊薄每股收益（EPS）为0.31美元，增长34%。\n作为参考，分析师共识预期营收为14.4亿美元、调整后每股收益为0.29美元，因此 CrowdStrike 轻松超过了这两项指标。\n吸引投资者注意的不仅是营收和利润指标。CrowdStrike 新增了创纪录的3.33亿美元年度经常性收入（ARR）——该指标衡量订阅服务增长——同比增长51%。这使总 ARR 达到58.4亿美元，增长25%。这表明 CrowdStrike 的增长势头远未结束。\n展开 NASDAQ: CRWD CrowdStrike 高级功能 Moneyball 综合评分 85/100 今日变化（-0.81%）-2.12美元 当前价格260.37美元 关键数据点 市值2690亿美元 市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算，不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权结构中的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间258.53美元-263.87美元 52周区间85.68美元-263.87美元 成交量670万 平均成交量1020万 毛利率75.12%\n公司还披露，订阅客户继续以更高的比例采用更多模块，其中51%、35%和26%的客户分别采用了六个或更多、七个或更多以及八个或更多模块。\n这也转化为创纪录的经营现金流和自由现金流，分别为5.30亿美元和3.77亿美元。\n投资者还有其他值得庆祝的理由。对于整个2027财年，管理层上调了业绩展望，预计营收为60亿美元，指引中点每股收益为1.25美元，高于分析师共识预期的营收59.4亿美元和每股收益1.23美元。\nCrowdStrike 股票并不便宜，目前按明年预期收益的144倍和销售额的45倍交易，但鉴于该公司一贯保守的指引和强劲业绩，投资者仍以丰厚溢价追捧这只股票。接下来阅读 2026年9月24日 • 作者：Jake Lerch CrowdStrike vs. Figma：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？2026年9月23日 • 作者：Adam Spatacco 不是 Palantir，也不是 Micron。吉姆·克莱默刚称为“必买”股票的3250亿美元英伟达合作伙伴 2026年9月22日 • 作者：Pamela Kock CrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？2026年9月21日 • 作者：Leo Sun 现在值得买入的两只百万富翁制造机网络安全股票 2026年9月17日 • 作者：Catie Hogan 两只将在2027年称霸的网络安全股票 2026年9月15日 • 作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA 这只网络安全股票可能将1000美元变成4400多美元 关于作者 Danny Vena，CPA，是 The Motley Fool 的特约科技分析师，专注于人工智能、云计算、半导体、软件、网络安全和消费电子。他是注册会计师，曾在中小型企业担任财务主管和会计师。Danny 还曾在美国陆军服役13年。他拥有菲尼克斯大学会计学学士学位。 TMFLifeIsGood@dannyvena Danny Vena，CPA，持有 CrowdStrike 的头寸。The Motley Fool 持有 CrowdStrike 的头寸并推荐该股。The Motley Fool 遵循披露政策。 提及的股票 CrowdStrike NASDAQ: CRWD 260.03美元（-0.94%）-2.46美元 Motley Fool Stock Advisor 最新推荐 获取权限---% 平均回报*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-08-27T18:50:18+00:00"}},{"id":"news-287","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike股价为何持续上涨","title_en":"Why CrowdStrike Stock Keeps Going Up | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool文章解释CrowdStrike股价持续上涨的原因。公司Falcon平台利用AI提供实时威胁检测、即时防护和自动修复，帮助企业保护设备和云工作负载。截至7月31日，其年度经常性收入同比增长25%至58亿美元，最近一个季度自由现金流达3.77亿美元。管理层预计可寻址市场将从2026年的1490亿美元增长至2030年的3250亿美元。公司还宣布Falcon平台已上线谷歌云基础设施和Snowflake市场，有望加速增长。","summary_en":"This Motley Fool article explains why CrowdStrike stock keeps rising. Its Falcon platform uses AI for real-time threat detection, instant protection, and automated remediation, helping companies secure devices and cloud workloads. As of July 31, annual recurring revenue rose 25% year over year to $5.8 billion, with $377 million in free cash flow in the most recent quarter. Management expects its addressable market to grow from $149 billion in 2026 to $325 billion by 2030. CrowdStrike also announced Falcon is now available on Google Cloud infrastructure and Snowflake's marketplace, which could accelerate growth.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:05:08.192697+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/08/31/why-crowdstrike-stock-keeps-going-up","content":"Shares of CrowdStrike (CRWD -0.82%) furthered their ascent on Monday, as investors' excitement about the artificial intelligence (AI)-powered cybersecurity leader's growth potential reached a fevered pitch.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nThe AI sentinel\nCrowdStrike's Falcon platform uses AI to provide real-time threat detection, instant protection, and automated remediation. Companies are increasingly using Falcon to secure their devices and cloud computing workloads to guard their most sensitive data from AI-driven attacks.\nCrowdStrike's business, in turn, is booming.\nIts annual recurring revenue (ARR) jumped 25% year over year to $5.8 billion as of July 31. The cyber guardian turns about a quarter of those sales into free cash flow, including $377 million in its most recent quarter.\n\"The Falcon is soaring,\" CEO George Kurtz said.\nExpandNASDAQ: CRWDCrowdStrikePremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore85/100Today's Change(-0.82%) $-2.16Current Price$260.33Key Data PointsMarket Cap$269BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$258.53 - $263.8752wk Range$85.68 - $263.87Volume6.6MAvg Vol10.2MGross Margin75.12%\nAI security is becoming increasingly vital\nManagement sees more gains ahead. CrowdStrike estimates that its total addressable market will grow from $149 billion in 2026 to $325 billion by 2030, fueled by soaring demand for AI cybersecurity solutions.\n\"Every enterprise will run on AI, and securing it is the largest market opportunity in our history,\" Kurtz said.\nNew partnerships should accelerate the AI guardian's growth. CrowdStrike announced on Monday that its Falcon platform is now available on Alphabet's Google Cloud infrastructure and Snowflake's marketplace. These collaborations will expand CrowdStrike's access to more potential customers and make it easier for existing clients to interact with its AI security tools.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCrowdStrike vs. Figma: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 23, 2026 •By Adam SpataccoNot Palantir. Not Micron. The $325 Billion Nvidia Partner That Jim Cramer Just Called a \"Must Buy\" StockSep 22, 2026 •By Pamela KockCrowdStrike vs. Palantir Technologies: Which Technology Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 21, 2026 •By Leo Sun2 Millionaire-Maker Cybersecurity Stocks to Buy NowSep 17, 2026 •By Catie Hogan2 Cybersecurity Stocks That Will Rule 2027Sep 15, 2026 •By Manali Pradhan, CFAThis Cybersecurity Stock Could Turn $1,000 Into More Than $4,400About the AuthorJoe Tenebruso is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst with more than 3,500 financial bylines to his name. Joe was an investment analyst for Stock Advisor, Income Investor, Crypto Society, and other top-rated investing services. He also managed Tier 1 Investments, a market-crushing real-money portfolio with 24.58% annualized returns. Joe graduated summa cum laude from Rutgers University with a Bachelor of Science in Finance.tmfguardian@Tier1InvestorJoe Tenebruso has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Alphabet, CrowdStrike, and Snowflake. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$260.37(-0.81%)-$2.12Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnAlphabetNASDAQ: GOOGL$342.10(+1.26%)+$4.27AlphabetNASDAQ: GOOG$338.18(+0.95%)+$3.20SnowflakeNYSE: SNOW$336.52(+0.51%)+$1.71*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"CrowdStrike（CRWD -0.82%）的股价周一继续攀升，投资者对这家人工智能（AI）驱动的网络安全领导者增长潜力的兴奋情绪达到狂热程度。\n\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n\nAI哨兵\nCrowdStrike的Falcon平台利用AI提供实时威胁检测、即时防护和自动修复。企业越来越多地使用Falcon保护其设备和云计算工作负载，以防范由AI驱动的攻击，守护最敏感的数据。\n\n反过来，CrowdStrike的业务正在蓬勃发展。\n截至7月31日，其年度经常性收入（ARR）同比增长25%，达到58亿美元。这位网络守护者将约四分之一的销售额转化为自由现金流，最近一个季度包括3.77亿美元。\n\n“Falcon正在腾飞，”首席执行官George Kurtz说。\n\n展开\nNASDAQ：CRWD\nCrowdStrike\n高级功能\nMoneyball综合评分：85/100\n今日变动（-0.82%）-2.16美元\n当前价格：260.33美元\n关键数据点\n市值：2690亿美元\n市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n日内区间：258.53美元–263.87美元\n52周区间：85.68美元–263.87美元\n成交量：660万\n平均成交量：1020万\n毛利率：75.12%\n\nAI安全正变得越来越重要\n管理层预计未来还会有更多增长。CrowdStrike估计，其总潜在市场规模将从2026年的1490亿美元增长到2030年的3250亿美元，动力来自对AI网络安全解决方案不断飙升的需求。\n\n“每家企业都将运行在AI之上，而保护AI是我们历史上最大的市场机遇，”Kurtz说。\n\n新的合作伙伴关系应会加速这位AI守护者的增长。CrowdStrike周一宣布，其Falcon平台现已可在Alphabet的Google Cloud基础设施和Snowflake的市场上使用。这些合作将扩大CrowdStrike接触潜在客户的范围，并让现有客户更容易使用其AI安全工具。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月24日 • 作者：Jake Lerch\nCrowdStrike对决Figma：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？\n2026年9月23日 • 作者：Adam Spatacco\n不是Palantir，也不是Micron。Jim Cramer刚刚称为“必买”股票的3250亿美元英伟达合作伙伴\n2026年9月22日 • 作者：Pamela Kock\nCrowdStrike对决Palantir Technologies：2026年哪只科技股更值得买？\n2026年9月21日 • 作者：Leo Sun\n现在可以买入的两只百万富翁制造机网络安全股\n2026年9月17日 • 作者：Catie Hogan\n两只将在2027年称霸的网络安全股\n2026年9月15日 • 作者：Manali Pradhan，CFA\n这只网络安全股可能让1000美元变成4400多美元\n\n关于作者\nJoe Tenebruso是《Motley Fool》特约股市分析师，署名发表的金融文章超过3500篇。Joe曾担任Stock Advisor、Income Investor、Crypto Society及其他顶级投资服务的投资分析师。他还管理Tier 1 Investments，这是一个年化回报率达24.58%、击败市场的实盘投资组合。Joe以优异成绩（summa cum laude）毕业于罗格斯大学，获金融学理学学士学位。\ntmfguardian@Tier1Investor\nJoe Tenebruso未持有本文提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐Alphabet、CrowdStrike和Snowflake，并制定有信息披露政策。\n\n提及的股票\nCrowdStrike\nNASDAQ：CRWD\n260.37美元（-0.81%）\n-2.12美元\n\n《Motley Fool》Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报\n\nAlphabet\nNASDAQ：GOOGL\n342.10美元（+1.26%）\n+4.27美元\n\nAlphabet\nNASDAQ：GOOG\n338.18美元（+0.95%）\n+3.20美元\n\nSnowflake\nNYSE：SNOW\n336.52美元（+0.51%）\n+1.71美元\n\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场交易日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-01T03:35:40+00:00"}},{"id":"news-253","ktid":2575920,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"2575920","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"霍尼韦尔已拆分为三家公司，哪一块最值得持有","title_en":"Honeywell Is Now Three Companies. Here's Which Piece I'd Actually Own. | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"霍尼韦尔已拆分为霍尼韦尔技术（HON）、Solstice Advanced Materials（SOLS）和霍尼韦尔航空航天（HONA）。文章比较三家公司：霍尼韦尔技术专注工业自动化，订单增长16%，积压订单200亿美元；航空航天下调有机销售增长指引；Solstice规模最小但二季度销售增长11%。作者认为主导分拆的CEO留任自动化业务，使其成为三者中最佳选择。","summary_en":"Honeywell has split into Honeywell Technologies (HON), Solstice Advanced Materials (SOLS), and Honeywell Aerospace (HONA). The article compares the three: Honeywell Technologies focuses on industrial automation with orders up 16% and $20 billion of a $38 billion backlog; Honeywell Aerospace lowered organic sales growth guidance; Solstice is the smallest but grew sales 11% year over year. The author favors the automation business, noting the CEO who led the breakup stayed to run it.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:28:54.670778+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/04/honeywell-is-now-three-companies-heres-which-piece/","content":"Wall Street goes through cycles. One that recurs with some regularity is the shift between conglomeration and corporate separations. Right now, conglomerates are separating, creating multiple businesses from one. Honeywell is a good example of this trend, with the conglomerate breaking into Honeywell Technologies (HON -1.25%), Solstice Advanced Materials (SOLS -2.67%), and Honeywell Aerospace (HONA -2.11%).\nIf you are thinking about buying one of these three companies, you may want to consider following the CEO who orchestrated the corporate split. Here's what you need to know.\nImage source: Getty Images.\nWhat is the point of a conglomerate like Honeywell?\nWhen it comes to acquisitions, there can be a fine line between a CEO who is simply trying to build an empire and one who is piecing together a coherent business. Honeywell was a large industrial company with the financial resources to support the businesses it operated. Bringing more industrial businesses under one roof could increase revenue diversification, eliminate redundant tasks (such as accounting), share technology and innovation among businesses, and enable enhanced access to capital markets.\nThose are all good things, but conglomerates also have their downsides. For example, business units often compete for funding. Bureaucracy can slow down decision-making. And sometimes small or underperforming business units get ignored, making poor performance hard to fix. When the negatives outweigh the positives, conglomerates often spin off businesses or break up, as Honeywell has done. That said, Wall Street's desire for de-conglomeration can also lead to business breakups simply to satisfy shifts in investor sentiment.\nExpandNASDAQ: HONHoneywell TechnologiesPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore66/100Today's Change(-1.25%) $-2.65Current Price$209.92Key Data PointsMarket Cap$67BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$209.18 - $212.7752wk Range$195.77 - $260.15Volume577.9KAvg Vol3.6MGross Margin37.84%Dividend Yield2.09%\nBy breaking a business into parts, each new business can focus all its energy on just one thing. That, in turn, is expected to lead to improved results for each of the newly independent businesses. Sometimes it works out, sometimes it doesn't. But it is usually worth watching to see which company the CEO who initiated the corporate split-up sticks around to manage.\nWhat is Honeywell today?\nThe company that retained the HON ticker is Honeywell Technologies, a pure-play industrial automation business. This is the company run by Vimal Kapur, the CEO who led Honeywell when it was an industrial conglomerate. That likely suggests that he believes automation is the most desirable business within Honeywell, noting that artificial intelligence (AI) is likely to be an important trend in industrial automation. When the company reported second-quarter 2026 earnings, the reason for his choice became clear.\nExpandNASDAQ: HONAHoneywell AerospaceToday's Change(-2.11%) $-3.45Current Price$159.88Key Data PointsMarket Cap$52BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$159.53 - $163.9752wk Range$149.19 - $297.50Volume700KAvg Vol4.1M\nThe spin-off of Honeywell Aerospace didn't occur until June 29. So it was still part of Honeywell for the quarter, but it will not be part of it going forward. Thus, Honeywell provided two sets of earnings, one with Honeywell Aerospace included and one without. One key number was very different. With the two businesses, orders rose 4%. If you isolate Honeywell Automation, however, orders rose 16%. Meanwhile, Honeywell Automation accounted for $20 billion of the combined business' $38 billion backlog. Adjusted earnings rose 10% year over year.\nAutomation looks like the business that is set to grow more rapidly. That's not to suggest that Honeywell Aerospace is a bad business; that's hardly true. Aviation spending is expected to remain strong as more people travel by plane. Still, when Honeywell Aviation reported second-quarter earnings, it lowered its organic sales growth guidance. It is clearly off to a bit of a rocky start.\nBut don't forget about Solstice Advanced Materials, the first business to be spun off, which reported an 11% year-over-year sales increase and a 23% jump in earnings per share in the second quarter, while increasing its full-year guidance. However, at a roughly $9.5 billion market cap, it is a relatively small business compared to Honeywell, which has a market cap of $65 billion. For reference, Honeywell Aerospace's market cap is $49 billion. If you owned Honeywell because it was a large business, Solstice Advanced Materials would be the smallest piece of the puzzle.\nExpandNASDAQ: SOLSSolstice Advanced MaterialsToday's Change(-2.67%) $-1.55Current Price$56.43Key Data PointsMarket Cap$9.2BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$56.05 - $57.1652wk Range$40.43 - $90.80Volume959.3KAvg Vol3.4MGross Margin30.62%Dividend Yield0.39%\nNo easy answers, but I'd follow the CEO\nYou can make a case for owning any of the three businesses that have come out of Honeywell. Honeywell Aerospace lowering guidance out of the box probably makes it the easiest to pass over, despite the long-term opportunity in the aviation industry. Solstice Advanced Materials, despite solid early results, is the smallest of the three companies, which could be viewed as a negative. That leaves Honeywell's automation business, which is both large and appears to be doing relatively well.\nBut the real key could be that the CEO who initiated the corporate breakup decided to oversee Honeywell's large automation operations. The business is seeing robust demand, as evidenced by a growing backlog. Second quarter earnings rose a solid 10% when the company's automation operations were separated out. And AI is likely to lead to a renewed push for industrial automation as it is used to improve corporate operations. That's a very solid story, and I think it makes Honeywell the best pick of the three. Though, to be honest, I'd probably have preferred if Honeywell had just remained a diversified conglomerate.Read NextSep 24, 2026 •By Jake LerchCaterpillar vs. Honeywell International: Which Industrials Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 9, 2026 •By Anders Bylund7 Best Quantum Computing Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 24, 2026 •By Todd ShriberWant Reliable Dividend Income? These 2 Industrial Stocks DeliverSep 24, 2026 •By Leo SunRivian vs. the S&P 500: Which Investment Wins Through 2030?Sep 24, 2026 •By Reuben Gregg BrewerNuScale Power Trades Below $10. Bargain or Value Trap?About the AuthorReuben Gregg Brewer is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst covering energy, utilities, REITs, and consumer staples. He is the former director of research at Value Line Publishing, where he rose from mutual fund analyst to equity analyst before leading all research operations. Reuben holds a bachelor’s degree in psychology from SUNY Purchase, a master’s in social work from Columbia University, and an MBA from Regis University. He has been featured as a financial expert on CNBC and in the Financial Times, Barron’s, and InvestmentNews.TMFReubenGBrewerReuben Gregg Brewer has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Honeywell Aerospace and Honeywell Technologies. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedHoneywell TechnologiesNASDAQ: HON$209.86(-1.27%)-$2.71Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnSolstice Advanced MaterialsNASDAQ: SOLS$56.41(-2.71%)-$1.57Honeywell AerospaceNASDAQ: HONA$159.88(-2.11%)-$3.45*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"华尔街经历着周期变化。其中一个较为规律地反复出现的周期，是企业集团化与公司拆分之间的转变。当前，企业集团正在拆分，由一家企业创建出多家业务公司。霍尼韦尔就是这一趋势的一个很好例子，这家企业集团正在拆分为霍尼韦尔技术公司（HON -1.25%）、Solstice Advanced Materials（SOLS -2.67%）和霍尼韦尔航空航天公司（HONA -2.11%）。\n如果你正在考虑买入这三家公司中的一家，或许可以考虑跟随那位策划了公司拆分的首席执行官。以下是你需要了解的内容。\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n\n像霍尼韦尔这样的企业集团有何意义？\n在收购方面，一位只是试图建立帝国的首席执行官，与一位正在拼凑一个连贯业务的首席执行官之间，可能只有一线之隔。霍尼韦尔是一家大型工业公司，拥有支持其所经营业务的财务资源。将更多工业业务纳入同一屋檐下，可以提高收入多元化程度，消除重复性工作（例如会计），在各业务之间共享技术和创新，并增强进入资本市场的能力。\n这些都是好处，但企业集团也有缺点。例如，各业务部门往往会争夺资金。官僚主义可能拖慢决策。有时，小型或表现不佳的业务部门会被忽视，使糟糕的表现难以改善。当负面因素超过正面因素时，企业集团往往会分拆业务或解体，霍尼韦尔就是这样做的。不过，华尔街对去集团化的渴望，也可能仅仅为了迎合投资者情绪的变化而导致企业拆分。\n展开NASDAQ：HON霍尼韦尔技术公司高级功能Moneyball综合评分66/100今日变动（-1.25%）$-2.65当前价格$209.92关键数据点市值$67B市值仅根据公开交易的已发行股票计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$209.18 - $212.7752周区间$195.77 - $260.15成交量577.9K平均成交量3.6M毛利率37.84%股息率2.09%\n通过将一家企业拆分成多个部分，每家新公司都可以将全部精力集中在一件事上。反过来，这预计会改善每家新独立公司的业绩。有时会成功，有时则不会。但通常值得关注的是，发起公司拆分的首席执行官会留下来管理哪家公司。\n\n如今的霍尼韦尔是什么样？\n保留HON股票代码的公司是霍尼韦尔技术公司，一家纯粹专注于工业自动化的企业。这家公司由维马尔·卡普尔领导，他是在霍尼韦尔还是一家工业企业集团时担任首席执行官的人。这可能表明，他认为自动化是霍尼韦尔旗下最理想的业务；同时需要注意的是，人工智能（AI）很可能成为工业自动化领域的重要趋势。当公司公布2026年第二季度财报时，他做出这一选择的原因变得清晰起来。\n展开NASDAQ：HONA霍尼韦尔航空航天公司今日变动（-2.11%）$-3.45当前价格$159.88关键数据点市值$52B市值仅根据公开交易的已发行股票计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重类别的非交易股票。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$159.53 - $163.9752周区间$149.19 - $297.50成交量700K平均成交量4.1M\n霍尼韦尔航空航天公司的分拆直到6月29日才完成。因此，它仍是……的一部分\n本季度的霍尼韦尔，但今后它将不再是其中的一部分。因此，霍尼韦尔提供了两组收益数据，一组包含霍尼韦尔航空航天业务，另一组不包含。一个关键数字差异很大。将两项业务合并计算，订单增长了4%。然而，如果单独看霍尼韦尔自动化业务，订单增长了16%。与此同时，霍尼韦尔自动化业务占合并业务380亿美元积压订单中的200亿美元。调整后收益同比增长10%。\n自动化业务看起来将增长得更快。这并不是说霍尼韦尔航空航天业务不好；事实远非如此。随着越来越多人乘飞机出行，航空支出预计将保持强劲。不过，霍尼韦尔航空航天公布第二季度收益时，下调了有机销售增长指引。它显然起步有些坎坷。\n但别忘了Solstice Advanced Materials，这是第一家被分拆的业务。该公司报告称，第二季度销售额同比增长11%，每股收益增长23%，同时上调了全年指引。然而，其市值约为95亿美元，与市值650亿美元的霍尼韦尔相比，这是一家相对较小的企业。作为参考，霍尼韦尔航空航天的市值为490亿美元。如果你持有霍尼韦尔是因为它是一家大型企业，那么Solstice Advanced Materials将是这幅拼图中最小的一块。\n展开NASDAQ：SOLS Solstice Advanced Materials今日变动（-2.67%）$-1.55当前价格$56.43关键数据点市值$9.2B市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中不可交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。日内区间$56.05 - $57.1652周区间$40.43 - $90.80成交量959.3K平均成交量3.4M毛利率30.62%股息率0.39%\n没有简单答案，但我会听从首席执行官的判断\n你可以为从霍尼韦尔分拆出来的三项业务中的任何一项提出持有理由。霍尼韦尔航空航天一开始就下调指引，尽管航空业存在长期机遇，这可能使它最容易被放弃。Solstice Advanced Materials尽管早期业绩稳健，却是三家公司中规模最小的，可能被视为负面因素。这就只剩下霍尼韦尔的自动化业务了，它规模庞大，而且表现似乎相对良好。\n但真正的关键可能在于，发起公司拆分的首席执行官决定亲自负责霍尼韦尔规模庞大的自动化业务。不断增长的积压订单证明，该业务正面临强劲需求。将公司的自动化业务单独列出后，第二季度收益稳健增长了10%。此外，随着人工智能被用于改善企业运营，它很可能推动工业自动化再次加速。这是一个非常扎实的故事，我认为这使霍尼韦尔成为三者中最值得选择的标的。不过，老实说，我可能更希望霍尼韦尔继续保持一家多元化企业集团的身份。继续阅读2026年9月24日 •作者：Jake Lerch卡特彼勒与霍尼韦尔国际：2026年哪只工业股更值得买？2026年9月9日 •作者：Anders Bylund2026年7只最佳量子计算股票及投资方式2026年9月24日 •作者：Todd Shriber想要可靠的股息收入？这两只工业股能够提供2026年9月24日 •作者：Leo SunRivian与标普500：哪项投资到2030年表现更佳？2026年9月24日 •作者：Reuben Gregg BrewerNuScale Power股价跌破10美元。是便宜货还是价值陷阱？关于作者Reuben Gregg Brewer是一名\n担任《Motley Fool》股票市场分析师，负责能源、公用事业、房地产投资信托基金（REITs）和必需消费品领域。他曾任Value Line Publishing研究主管，在此期间从共同基金分析师晋升为股票分析师，之后负责领导全部研究工作。Reuben拥有纽约州立大学普र्च斯分校（SUNY Purchase）心理学学士学位、哥伦比亚大学社会工作硕士学位，以及里吉斯大学工商管理硕士学位。他曾作为金融专家出现在CNBC以及《金融时报》、巴伦周刊和InvestmentNews上。TMFReubenGBrewerReuben Gregg Brewer不持有上述任何股票的仓位。Motley Fool持有Honeywell Aerospace和Honeywell Technologies的仓位，并推荐这两家公司。Motley Fool有披露政策。提及的股票Honeywell Technologies纳斯达克：HON$209.86(-1.27%)-$2.71Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报Solstice Advanced Materials纳斯达克：SOLS$56.41(-2.71%)-$1.57Honeywell Aerospace纳斯达克：HONA$159.88(-2.11%)-$3.45*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-05T02:15:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-248","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英特尔股价周二早盘为何上涨","title_en":"Why Intel Stock Rallied Tuesday Morning | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool报道，英特尔股价周二早盘一度上涨8.6%，截至美东时间11:20仍涨8.3%。催化剂是DigiTimes报道称英特尔可能年内第三次上调CPU价格，涨幅约10%，以改善毛利率。随后Northland Securities分析师Gus Richard将英特尔评级从持有上调至买入，目标价120美元。文章还提及英特尔代工雄心、CPU短缺带来的定价权，以及当前估值偏高。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reported that Intel shares rallied as much as 8.6% Tuesday morning and were still up 8.3% at 11:20 a.m. ET. The catalyst was a DigiTimes report that Intel may raise CPU prices by another 10% later this year, its third hike of 2026, to improve gross margin. Northland Securities analyst Gus Richard then upgraded Intel to outperform from market perform with a $120 price target, citing progress in its turnaround and foundry ambitions, while noting the stock's rich valuation.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:43:08.784813+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/08/why-intel-stock-rallied-tuesday-morning/","content":"Shares of Intel (INTC +1.49%) climbed out of the gate on Monday, rising as much as 8.6%. As of 11:20 a.m. ET, the stock was still up 8.3%.\nThe catalyst that drove the semiconductor company higher was a report that it may be raising prices, along with a corresponding upgrade from a Wall Street analyst.\nImage source: The Motley Fool.\nThird time's a charm\nA media report emerged early Tuesday that Intel may be planning another round of price increases as the company works to improve its gross margin rather than taking market share. Intel is expected to increase the price of its CPUs by another 10% later this year, according to a report that first appeared in DigiTimes.\nIf the report is accurate, this would mark the third such price increase this year, after hikes in the first quarter and again in July.\nOn the heels of this news, Northland Securities analyst Gus Richard upgraded Intel to outperform (buy), from market perform (hold), with a price target of $120. For those keeping score at home, that represents potential upside of 25% compared to Friday's closing price (ahead of the Labor Day weekend).\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(1.49%) $1.83Current Price$124.43Key Data PointsMarket Cap$648BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$119.55 - $125.9252wk Range$31.21 - $142.35Volume65.3MAvg Vol109MGross Margin39.05%\nThe analyst cited \"material progress\" in Intel's turnaround, with particular emphasis on the company's foundry ambitions. Additionally, the current CPU shortage will work to Intel's advantage, giving the chipmaker pricing power -- at least for now.\nIntel has previously announced plans to become the world's second-largest foundry by 2030, and while the company has certainly made progress, it still has work to do to achieve that goal.\nMoreover, Intel stock is pricey at 68 times forward earnings and 51 times next year's expected earnings, so there's already a lot of growth baked into today's stock price.Read NextSep 23, 2026 •By Daniel SparksPrediction: Intel Names a Major Outside Customer for Its Next Factory Process Before 2027Sep 22, 2026 •By Mike SchwenkASML vs. Intel: Which AI Chip Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 22, 2026 •By Keith Noonan5 Best GPU Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 21, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel, Arm, and Other AI Chip Stocks Soared TodaySep 21, 2026 •By Sara AppinoBroadcom vs. Intel: Which Semiconductor Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 20, 2026 •By Prosper Junior BakinyWhy I'm Avoiding This Popular AI Stock Despite Its Growth StoryAbout the AuthorDanny Vena, CPA, is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst specializing in artificial intelligence, cloud computing, semiconductors, software, cybersecurity, and consumer electronics. He is a Certified Public Accountant and previously worked as a controller and accountant across small and midsize businesses. Danny also served 13 years in the U.S. Army. He holds a bachelor’s degree in accounting from the University of Phoenix.TMFLifeIsGood@dannyvenaDanny Vena, CPA has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Intel. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$124.43(+1.49%)+$1.83Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg Return*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"英特尔（INTC +1.49%）股价周一开盘即上涨，最高涨幅达8.6%。截至美国东部时间上午11:20，该股仍上涨8.3%。\n推动这家半导体公司股价走高的催化剂，是一则称其可能提高价格的报道，以及一位华尔街分析师随后作出的评级上调。\n图片来源：The Motley Fool。\n\n事不过三\n周二早些时候出现的一则媒体报道称，英特尔可能正计划进行新一轮提价，因为该公司致力于改善毛利率，而非抢占市场份额。据最先刊登于DigiTimes的一篇报道，英特尔预计将在今年晚些时候再次将其CPU价格上调10%。\n\n如果该报道准确，这将是今年第三次此类提价，此前该公司已在第一季度提价，并于7月再次提价。\n\n在这一消息之后，Northland Securities分析师Gus Richard将英特尔评级从市场表现（持有）上调至跑赢大盘（买入），目标价为120美元。对于正在计算的人来说，这意味着相对于上周五收盘价（劳动节周末前），存在25%的潜在上涨空间。\n\n展开\n纳斯达克：INTC\n英特尔\n高级功能\nMoneyball Superscore\n67/100\n今日变动\n(1.49%) $1.83\n当前价格\n$124.43\n关键数据点\n市值\n$648B\n市值仅使用已公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私有或双重股权结构中未交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n当日区间\n$119.55 - $125.92\n52周区间\n$31.21 - $142.35\n成交量\n65.3M\n平均成交量\n109M\n毛利率\n39.05%\n\n该分析师援引英特尔扭转局面取得的“实质性进展”，尤其强调了该公司的晶圆代工雄心。此外，当前的CPU短缺将对英特尔有利，至少目前会赋予这家芯片制造商定价权。\n\n英特尔此前宣布，计划到2030年成为全球第二大晶圆代工厂；尽管公司确实取得了进展，但要实现这一目标仍有工作要做。\n\n此外，英特尔股票价格昂贵，预期市盈率为68倍、按明年预期收益计算的市盈率为51倍，因此当前股价中已计入大量增长预期。\n\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月23日 • Daniel Sparks撰文\n预测：英特尔将在2027年前为其下一代工厂制程引入一位重要的外部客户\n2026年9月22日 • Mike Schwenk撰文\nASML与英特尔：2026年哪只AI芯片股更值得买入？\n2026年9月22日 • Keith Noonan撰文\n2026年5只最佳GPU股票及其投资方法\n2026年9月21日 • Joe Tenebruso撰文\n为何英特尔、Arm及其他AI芯片股今日飙升\n2026年9月21日 • Sara Appino撰文\n博通与英特尔：2026年哪只半导体股票更值得买入？\n2026年9月20日 • Prosper Junior Bakiny撰文\n尽管有增长故事，我为何避开这只热门AI股票\n\n关于作者\nDanny Vena，注册会计师，是The Motley Fool的特约科技分析师，专注于人工智能、云计算、半导体、软件、网络安全和消费电子产品。他是注册会计师，曾在小型及中型企业担任财务总监和会计师。Danny还曾在美国陆军服役13年。他拥有菲尼克斯大学会计学学士学位。\nTMFLifeIsGood\n@dannyvena\nDanny Vena，注册会计师，未持有上述任何股票头寸。The Motley Fool持有英特尔头寸并推荐英特尔。The Motley Fool设有披露政策。\n\n提及的股票\n英特尔\n纳斯达克：INTC\n$124.43\n(+1.49%)\n+$1.83\n\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor的最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报*\n*自创立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一交易日收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-08T15:29:06+00:00"}},{"id":"news-147","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英特尔股价今日为何跳涨","title_en":"Why Intel Stock Jumped Today | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"Motley Fool报道，路透社消息称英特尔正与韩国SK海力士洽谈在美国生产存储芯片，受此消息影响英特尔股价周三上涨。文章指出，若交易达成将提振英特尔代工业务，该业务是CEO陈立武增长计划的核心。SK海力士表示目前尚未敲定具体计划，韩国贸易部则称涉及国家核心技术需依《产业技术保护法》审查。","summary_en":"The Motley Fool reported that Intel shares rose Wednesday after a Reuters report said the chipmaker is in talks with South Korea's SK Hynix to produce memory chips in the U.S. A deal would boost Intel's fledgling foundry business, a cornerstone of CEO Lip-Bu Tan's growth plan. SK Hynix said no specific plans have been finalized, while South Korea's trade ministry said any deal involving national core technology would face review under its industrial technology protection law.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:28:10.574102+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/16/why-intel-stock-jumped-today/","content":"Shares of Intel (INTC +0.01%) rose on Wednesday, following a Reuters report that the semiconductor giant is in talks with South Korean tech leader SK Hynix (SKHY -2.01%) to produce memory chips in the U.S.\nImage source: Intel.\nIntel wants to become a leading manufacturer of AI chips\nA potential deal could provide a major boost to Intel's fledgling foundry efforts. The computer processor designer has been trying to win high-profile clients for its third-party manufacturing operations, which are a cornerstone of CEO Lip-Bu Tan's growth plan.\nSK Hynix is a leading producer of high-bandwidth memory (HBM), dynamic random-access memory (DRAM), and NAND flash memory, all of which are in high demand due to the artificial intelligence (AI) boom.\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(0.01%) $0.01Current Price$122.61Key Data PointsMarket Cap$648BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$119.55 - $125.9252wk Range$31.21 - $142.35Volume59.7MAvg Vol109MGross Margin39.05%\nWhile the talks are apparently ongoing, investors should note that SK Hynix said, \"no specific plans or arrangements have been finalized at this time.\"\nThe U.S wants to boost domestic chip manufacturing\nA deal would likely have the full support of the Trump administration, which has long sought to bolster the nation's semiconductor supply chain and strengthen U.S. leadership in AI.\nHowever, it's less clear whether the South Korean government would allow SK Hynix to move production of its advanced chips to the U.S. South Korea's trade ministry told Reuters that any deal involving a \"national core technology\" would be subject to review under the country's Industrial Technology Protection Act.Read NextSep 23, 2026 •By Daniel SparksPrediction: Intel Names a Major Outside Customer for Its Next Factory Process Before 2027Sep 22, 2026 •By Mike SchwenkASML vs. Intel: Which AI Chip Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 22, 2026 •By Keith Noonan5 Best GPU Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestSep 21, 2026 •By Joe TenebrusoWhy Intel, Arm, and Other AI Chip Stocks Soared TodaySep 21, 2026 •By Sara AppinoBroadcom vs. Intel: Which Semiconductor Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 20, 2026 •By Prosper Junior BakinyWhy I'm Avoiding This Popular AI Stock Despite Its Growth StoryAbout the AuthorJoe Tenebruso is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst with more than 3,500 financial bylines to his name. Joe was an investment analyst for Stock Advisor, Income Investor, Crypto Society, and other top-rated investing services. He also managed Tier 1 Investments, a market-crushing real-money portfolio with 24.58% annualized returns. Joe graduated summa cum laude from Rutgers University with a Bachelor of Science in Finance.tmfguardian@Tier1InvestorJoe Tenebruso has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Intel. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$122.61(+0.01%)+$0.01Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnSK HynixNASDAQ: SKHY$185.28(-2.11%)-$4.00*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"英特尔（INTC +0.01%）股价周三上涨，此前路透社报道称，这家半导体巨头正与韩国科技领导者SK海力士（SKHY -2.01%）洽谈在美国生产存储芯片。\n图片来源：英特尔。\n英特尔希望成为领先的AI芯片制造商\n潜在交易可能会大幅提振英特尔尚处起步阶段的晶圆代工业务。这家计算机处理器设计商一直在努力为其第三方制造业务争取高知名度客户，而该业务是首席执行官陈立武增长计划的基石。\nSK海力士是高带宽内存（HBM）、动态随机存取存储器（DRAM）和NAND闪存的领先生产商；由于人工智能（AI）热潮，这些产品的需求都很高。\n展开\nNASDAQ：INTC\n英特尔\n高级功能\nMoneyball综合评分67/100\n今日变动（0.01%）0.01美元\n当前价格122.61美元\n关键数据点\n市值6480亿美元\n市值仅根据公开交易的流通股计算。不包括未上市、私人持有或双重股权结构中不可交易的股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n日内区间119.55美元–125.92美元\n52周区间31.21美元–142.35美元\n成交量5,970万\n平均成交量1.09亿\n毛利率39.05%\n\n尽管谈判显然仍在进行，投资者应注意，SK海力士表示：“截至目前，尚未敲定任何具体计划或安排。”\n美国希望提振国内芯片制造\n这项交易很可能得到特朗普政府的全力支持；特朗普政府长期以来一直寻求加强美国的半导体供应链并巩固美国在AI领域的领导地位。\n然而，韩国政府是否会允许SK海力士将其先进芯片的生产转移到美国，目前尚不明确。韩国贸易部告诉路透社，任何涉及“国家核心技术”的交易都将根据该国《产业技术保护法》接受审查。\n接下来阅读\n2026年9月23日 • Daniel Sparks\n预测：英特尔将在2027年前为其下一代工厂工艺确定一家主要外部客户\n2026年9月22日 • Mike Schwenk\nASML与英特尔：2026年哪只AI芯片股票更值得买？\n2026年9月22日 • Keith Noonan\n2026年5只GPU股票及投资方法\n2026年9月21日 • Joe Tenebruso\n英特尔、Arm及其他AI芯片股今日为何飙升\n2026年9月21日 • Sara Appino\n博通与英特尔：哪只半导体股票更值得买？\n2026年9月20日 • Prosper Junior Bakiny\n尽管增长故事诱人，我为何避开这只热门AI股票\n关于作者\nJoe Tenebruso是《Motley Fool》特约股市分析师，署名发表的金融文章超过3,500篇。Joe曾担任Stock Advisor、Income Investor、Crypto Society及其他顶级投资服务的投资分析师。他还管理Tier 1 Investments，这是一个年化回报率达24.58%、表现大幅跑赢市场的真实资金投资组合。Joe以优异成绩毕业于罗格斯大学，获金融学理学学士学位。\ntmfguardian@Tier1Investor\nJoe Tenebruso未持有本文提及的任何股票。《Motley Fool》持有并推荐英特尔。《Motley Fool》有披露政策。\n提及的股票\n英特尔\nNASDAQ：INTC\n122.61美元（+0.01%）\n+0.01美元\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---%\n平均回报\n自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场日的收盘价。\nSK海力士\nNASDAQ：SKHY\n185.28美元（-2.11%）\n-4.00美元\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个市场日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T21:50:51+00:00"}},{"id":"news-90","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike、Palo Alto Networks、SentinelOne等网络安全股本周为何大涨","title_en":"Why CrowdStrike, Palo Alto Networks, SentinelOne, and Other Cybersecurity Stocks Surged This Week | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"文章指出，数据泄露、内部威胁和AI驱动攻击的担忧推动投资者转向网络安全板块，CrowdStrike本周上涨15%，SentinelOne上涨14%，Palo Alto Networks上涨10%。CrowdStrike提供统一平台上的安全数据、全天候威胁狩猎、AI风险分析和自动响应；SentinelOne的机器学习自主安全智能及Wayfinder Frontier AI服务结合Anthropic的Claude Security；Palo Alto Networks则整合下一代防火墙、实时内容扫描和AI自动事件响应。","summary_en":"The article says fears of data breaches, rogue agents and AI-driven attacks pushed investors into cybersecurity stocks, with CrowdStrike up 15%, SentinelOne up 14% and Palo Alto Networks up 10% for the week. CrowdStrike offers security data, 24/7 threat hunting, AI-powered risk analysis and automated response on one platform. SentinelOne's machine-learning autonomous security intelligence and Wayfinder Frontier AI services pair advanced models, starting with Anthropic's Claude Security, with security experts. Palo Alto combines next-generation firewalls, real-time content scanning and AI-driven incident response.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:53:07.187463+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/20/why-crowdstrike-palo-alto-sentinelone-stocks-up","content":"It seems that not a day goes by without hearing about another data breach, a rogue agent, or a warning of a forthcoming artificial intelligence (AI)-driven apocalypse.\nIt's a perfect storm of fear-inducing news and predictions that's alerting investors to the dire need for effective cyber safeguards.\nSeveral cybersecurity stocks have jumped in response as investors rotated into companies poised to benefit from these trends.\nHere's how some of the top AI sentinels fared this past week:\nCrowdStrike (CRWD -0.31%), up 15%\nSentinelOne (S -0.10%), up 14%\nPalo Alto Networks (PANW -0.58%), up 10%\nImage source: Getty Images.\nAI fears could accelerate these cyber guardians' growth\nCrowdStrike provides extensive security data, 24/7 threat hunting, AI-powered risk analysis, and automated breach response on a single, unified platform. Customers rely on the cyber defense specialist to protect their devices and cloud networks from AI-driven intrusions.\nSentinelOne's machine learning-powered autonomous security intelligence helps companies stay a step ahead of would-be malicious actors. Its new Wayfinder Frontier AI services pair advanced AI models -- beginning with Anthropic's Claude Security -- with highly trained security experts to identify and deter real-world exploitation attempts.\nPalo Alto Networks combines next-generation firewalls with real-time content scanning, cloud application security, and AI-driven automated incident response. In turn, Palo Alto provides a level of cyber protection that traditional firewall-based systems simply can't match. Read NextSep 14, 2026 •By Parkev Tatevosian, CFAThe Proliferation of Agentic AI Has Been Great News for Palo Alto Stock InvestorsSep 14, 2026 •By Rich SmithWhy Palo Alto Networks Stock Popped TodaySep 8, 2026 •By Motley Fool TranscribingPalo Alto Networks (PANW) Q4 2026 Earnings Call TranscriptSep 6, 2026 •By Keith NoonanWhy Palo Alto Networks Stock Plummeted This WeekSep 4, 2026 •By Geoffrey SeilerAfter an 80% Gain on the Year, Is Palo Alto Networks Stock a Buy on Its Recent Pullback as Revenue Surges?Sep 4, 2026 •By Anthony Di PizioThis Unstoppable Stock Is Obliterating the S&P 500 and the Nasdaq-100 in 2026, but Is There Still Time to Buy?About the AuthorJoe Tenebruso is a contributing Motley Fool stock market analyst with more than 3,500 financial bylines to his name. Joe was an investment analyst for Stock Advisor, Income Investor, Crypto Society, and other top-rated investing services. He also managed Tier 1 Investments, a market-crushing real-money portfolio with 24.58% annualized returns. Joe graduated summa cum laude from Rutgers University with a Bachelor of Science in Finance.tmfguardian@Tier1InvestorJoe Tenebruso has no position in any of the stocks mentioned. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends CrowdStrike. The Motley Fool recommends Palo Alto Networks. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedPalo Alto NetworksNASDAQ: PANW$391.04(-0.58%)-$2.27Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnCrowdStrikeNASDAQ: CRWD$260.62(-0.71%)-$1.87SentinelOneNYSE: S$24.08(-0.10%)-$0.03*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"似乎没有一天不听到又一起数据泄露、一个失控智能体，或一则即将到来的人工智能（AI）驱动末日警告。\n\n这是一场充满恐惧诱因的新闻和预测的完美风暴，让投资者警觉到迫切需要有效的网络安全防护措施。\n\n随着投资者转向有望受益于这些趋势的公司，多只网络安全股票应声上涨。\n\n以下是一些顶级AI哨兵股在过去一周的表现：\n\nCrowdStrike（CRWD -0.31%），上涨15%\n\nSentinelOne（S -0.10%），上涨14%\n\nPalo Alto Networks（PANW -0.58%），上涨10%\n\n图片来源：Getty Images。\n\nAI担忧或可加速这些网络安全守护者的增长\n\nCrowdStrike在一个统一平台上提供广泛的安全数据、全天候威胁追踪、AI驱动的风险分析和自动化漏洞响应。客户依靠这家网络防御专家保护其设备和云网络免受AI驱动的入侵。\n\nSentinelOne由机器学习驱动的自主安全智能帮助企业领先潜在恶意行为者一步。其新的Wayfinder Frontier AI服务将先进AI模型——从Anthropic的Claude Security开始——与训练有素的安全专家配对，以识别并阻止现实世界中的利用企图。\n\nPalo Alto Networks将下一代防火墙与实时内容扫描、云应用安全和AI驱动的自动化事件响应相结合。因此，Palo Alto提供的网络保护水平是传统基于防火墙的系统根本无法匹敌的。\n\n继续阅读\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Parkev Tatevosian，CFA\n智能体AI的激增对Palo Alto股票投资者来说是个好消息\n\n2026年9月14日 • 作者：Rich Smith\n为何Palo Alto Networks股价今日飙升\n\n2026年9月8日 • 作者：Motley Fool文字记录团队\nPalo Alto Networks（PANW）2026财年第四季度财报电话会议记录\n\n2026年9月6日 • 作者：Keith Noonan\n为何Palo Alto Networks股价本周暴跌\n\n2026年9月4日 • 作者：Geoffrey Seiler\n年内上涨80%后，随着营收激增，Palo Alto Networks股票在近期回调后是否值得买入？\n\n2026年9月4日 • 作者：Anthony Di Pizio\n这只势不可挡的股票在2026年大幅跑赢标普500和纳斯达克100指数，但现在买入还来得及吗？\n\n关于作者\n乔·特内布鲁索是Motley Fool的特约股票市场分析师，署名财经文章超过3,500篇。乔曾担任Stock Advisor、Income Investor、Crypto Society及其他顶级投资服务的投资分析师。他还管理过Tier 1 Investments，这是一个以真实资金运作、年化回报率24.58%、大幅跑赢市场的投资组合。乔以最优等成绩毕业于罗格斯大学，获得金融学理学学士学位。\n\ntmfguardian@Tier1Investor\n\n乔·特内布鲁索未持有文中提及的任何股票。Motley Fool持有并推荐CrowdStrike。Motley Fool推荐Palo Alto Networks。Motley Fool有披露政策。\n\n提及的股票\n\nPalo Alto Networks\n纳斯达克：PANW\n391.04美元\n（-0.58%）\n-2.27美元\n\nMotley Fool Stock Advisor的最新推荐\n获取访问权限\n---% 平均回报\n\nCrowdStrike\n纳斯达克：CRWD\n260.62美元\n（-0.71%）\n-1.87美元\n\nSentinelOne\n纽约证券交易所：S\n24.08美元\n（-0.10%）\n-0.03美元\n\n*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报基于前一个交易日的收盘价。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-20T21:00:11+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"《愚人理财》讨论英特尔股价能否在2026年达到150美元","title_en":"Intel Is Up 220% in 2026. Can It Reach $150 Before 2026 Is Over? | The Motley Fool","summary_cn":"文章称，英特尔2026年股价已上涨逾220%，其数据中心和AI产品线第二季度同比增长59%。文章认为，英特尔18A工艺及美国政府和英伟达的投资可能增强其代工竞争力，且报道称苹果已同意让英特尔成为部分产品的第二供应商。但文章指出，英特尔股价已计入大量成功预期，估值高于台积电，并建议投资者卖出英特尔、转投台积电。","summary_en":"The article says Intel shares have risen more than 220% in 2026, while its data center and AI product lineup grew 59% year over year in the second quarter. It argues that Intel's 18A node and investments from the U.S. government and Nvidia could improve its foundry competitiveness, and reports that Apple agreed for Intel to become a second supplier for some products. However, it says Intel's valuation already reflects substantial expected success, is higher than TSMC's, and recommends selling Intel shares in favor of TSMC.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-26T14:57:02.410381+00:00","url":"https://www.fool.com/investing/2026/09/26/intel-is-up-220-in-2026-can-it-reach-150-before-20/","content":"Intel (INTC -3.45%) has been one of the top-performing stocks in 2026. It currently ranks as the sixth-best-performing stock in the S&P 500 (^GSPC +0.51%), rising more than 220% so far this year. That's a fantastic return in less than a year, but could it deliver even greater returns to push it to $150 per share before 2026 is over?\nLet's take a look at what it would take to get that far, and if it's even feasible considering the current state of the business.\nImage source: The Motley Fool.\nIntel's turnaround is underway\nIntel's business can be split into two parts: Intel products and a semiconductor foundry. Years ago, Intel used to advertise how powerful its processors were, but that growth segment is nearly wrapped up. There isn't a ton of growth in the consumer electronics space anymore, and considering the grim outlook for its semiconductor foundry, the stock looked doomed.\nHowever, one part of Intel's business continues to thrive: Its data center and AI product lineup. Intel makes CPUs for data centers, which have seen a huge boom in demand as AI has pushed the build-out of new data centers. This has created a great business for Intel, and this segment rose 59% year over year during the second quarter.\nThe biggest sleeping giant within Intel's business is its foundry business. There aren't a lot of semiconductor foundries out there, and the industry is pretty much dominated by Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing (TSM -0.12%). However, Intel had a fairly strong foundry business until it started to lose clients to TSMC's superior technology.\nThanks to various investments from the U.S. government and Nvidia, Intel now has the capabilities to compete with TSMC. Intel's 18A chip node is one of the most advanced available, and if the company can attract clients to its foundry business, the stock could be ready to skyrocket.\nExpandNASDAQ: INTCIntelPremium FeatureMoneyball Superscore67/100Today's Change(-3.45%) $-4.39Current Price$123.00Key Data PointsMarket Cap$650BMarket cap calculated using publicly traded shares outstanding only. Does not include unlisted, private, or dual-class non-traded shares. Implied market cap may vary.Day's Range$122.84 - $126.9352wk Range$32.89 - $142.35Volume97.7MAvg Vol108.8MGross Margin39.05%\nIntel found one of the biggest clients of all: Apple. Apple and Intel reportedly reached an agreement for Intel to become a second supplier for some of its products, which would be a huge win for its foundry business. If Intel can continue to capture new clients, then its foundry business can push the stock to new heights.\nBut will it be enough to get it to $150 per share before the year is over? I'm not sure about that.\nIntel has a lot of success baked into its stock already\nWhile Intel has done OK as a business in 2026, its stock has done even better. This has pushed the company's shares to a pretty high valuation. Intel's stock trades at 81 times this year's earnings estimates, and 59 times next year's.\nINTC PE Ratio (Forward 1y) data by YCharts\nThat's not a cheap stock price in any form, and it's far more expensive than the top company in the space. TSMC trades at 26 times this year's earnings estimates and 20 times next year's. That means Intel's profits must triple beyond what analysts are projecting for 2027 to be valued at the same level as TSMC.\nThat's a massive jump, and a very rich premium to pay. Investors are clearly excited about Intel's turnaround, but it may not be a reasonable price tag to pay for the stock.\nSo, if you're an Intel investor, I think the smart thing to do is sell shares, take your gains, and invest in the industry leader. TSMC is a far better company and doesn't have the turnaround risk that Intel does. Intel still has a lot of work to do, but the stock is already priced like it has completed a turnaround.Read NextSep 25, 2026 •By Robert IzquierdoARM vs. Intel: What Revenue Growth Trends Reveal About These Artificial Intelligence CompaniesSep 25, 2026 •By Brett SchaferWhy Intel Stock Jumped This WeekSep 25, 2026 •By Jack CaporalRanked: Semiconductor Manufacturers by Global Foundry RevenueSep 23, 2026 •By Daniel SparksPrediction: Intel Names a Major Outside Customer for Its Next Factory Process Before 2027Sep 22, 2026 •By Mike SchwenkASML vs. Intel: Which AI Chip Stock Is a Better Buy in 2026?Sep 22, 2026 •By Keith Noonan5 Best GPU Stocks for 2026 and How to InvestAbout the AuthorKeithen Drury is a contributing Motley Fool technology analyst covering AI, semiconductors, cybersecurity, and SaaS stocks. In addition to The Motley Fool, Keithen is a mechanical engineer and has held roles at Honeywell and smaller industrial companies like Brand Hydraulics and Lincoln Industries. He holds a bachelor’s degree in mechanical engineering from Dordt University.TMFTripleOptionKeithen Drury has positions in Nvidia and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing. The Motley Fool has positions in and recommends Apple, Intel, Nvidia, and Taiwan Semiconductor Manufacturing. The Motley Fool has a disclosure policy.Stocks MentionedIntelNASDAQ: INTC$123.00(-3.45%)-$4.39Motley Fool Stock Advisor’s Latest PickGet Access---% Avg ReturnS&P 500 IndexSNPINDEX: ^GSPC$7,743.41(+0.51%)+$39.28Taiwan Semiconductor ManufacturingNYSE: TSM$450.61(-0.12%)-$0.54AppleNASDAQ: AAPL$341.07(+1.53%)+$5.15NvidiaNASDAQ: NVDA$225.07(+0.22%)+$0.49*Average returns of all recommendations since inception. Cost basis and return based on previous market day close.","content_cn":"英特尔（INTC -3.45%）一直是2026年表现最佳的股票之一。目前，它在标普500指数（^GSPC +0.51%）中位列第六佳表现股，今年迄今已上涨逾220%。在不到一年内取得这样的回报非常出色，但它能否带来更高的回报，在2026年结束前将股价推升至每股150美元？\n\n让我们看看要达到这一目标需要什么条件，以及考虑到该公司目前的业务状况，这是否可行。\n\n图片来源：The Motley Fool。\n\n英特尔的复苏正在展开\n\n英特尔的业务可分为两部分：英特尔产品和半导体代工厂。多年前，英特尔曾宣传其处理器有多么强大，但这一增长板块已接近尾声。消费电子领域已没有太多增长空间，而鉴于其半导体代工业务的黯淡前景，该股看起来注定要失败。\n\n不过，英特尔业务中有一部分仍在蓬勃发展：其数据中心和AI产品线。英特尔为数据中心制造CPU，随着AI推动新数据中心的建设，这类产品的需求大幅增长。这为英特尔创造了一项出色的业务，该板块在第二季度同比增长59%。\n\n英特尔业务中最大的沉睡巨头是其代工业务。半导体代工厂并不多，而这个行业几乎由台积电（TSM -0.12%）主导。然而，在因台积电更先进的技术而开始流失客户之前，英特尔曾拥有相当强劲的代工业务。\n\n得益于美国政府和英伟达的各项投资，英特尔如今具备了与台积电竞争的能力。英特尔的18A芯片节点是目前最先进的节点之一，如果该公司能够吸引客户使用其代工业务，该股可能会准备好飙升。\n\n展开\n\n纳斯达克：INTC\n\n英特尔\n\n高级功能\n\nMoneyball Superscore\n\n67/100\n\n今日变动\n\n(-3.45%) $-4.39\n\n当前价格\n\n$123.00\n\n关键数据点\n\n市值\n\n$650B\n\n市值仅使用已发行的公开交易股份计算。不包括未上市、私有或双类别非交易股份。隐含市值可能有所不同。\n\n当日区间\n\n$122.84 - $126.93\n\n52周区间\n\n$32.89 - $142.35\n\n成交量\n\n97.7M\n\n平均成交量\n\n108.8M\n\n毛利率\n\n39.05%\n\n英特尔找到了最重要的客户之一：苹果。据报道，苹果和英特尔达成协议，英特尔将成为其部分产品的第二供应商，这将是其代工业务的重大胜利。如果英特尔能够继续争取新客户，那么其代工业务可以将该股推向新高度。\n\n但这是否足以在今年结束前使其达到每股150美元？我对此并不确定。\n\n英特尔的股票已计入许多成功预期\n\n尽管英特尔在2026年的业务表现尚可，但其股票表现得更好。这已将公司股票推至相当高的估值水平。英特尔股票的交易价格为今年盈利预估的81倍，以及明年盈利预估的59倍。\n\nYCharts提供的INTC市盈率（未来1年）数据\n\n无论从哪种角度看，这都不是一个便宜的股价，而且远比该领域的龙头公司昂贵。台积电的交易价格为今年盈利预估的26倍和明年盈利预估的20倍。这意味着，英特尔的利润必须在分析师对2027年的预测基础上增长三倍，才能获得与台积电相同的估值水平。\n\n这是一个巨大的跃升，也是需要支付的非常高的溢价。投资者显然对英特尔的复苏感到兴奋，但这可能不是为此支付的合理价格。\n股票。\n因此，如果你是英特尔投资者，我认为明智的做法是卖出股票，锁定收益，并投资于行业领导者。台积电是一家好得多的公司，而且没有英特尔所面临的转型风险。英特尔仍有大量工作要做，但其股价已经反映了它已完成转型。继续阅读2026年9月25日 • 作者：Robert IzquierdoARM vs. 英特尔：营收增长趋势揭示了这些人工智能公司的什么情况2026年9月25日 • 作者：Brett Schafer英特尔股票本周为何上涨2026年9月25日 • 作者：Jack Caporal按全球晶圆代工营收排名：半导体制造商2026年9月23日 • 作者：Daniel Sparks预测：英特尔将在2027年前为其下一代工工艺确定一家大型外部客户2026年9月22日 • 作者：Mike SchwenkASML vs. 英特尔：2026年哪只AI芯片股更值得买入？2026年9月22日 • 作者：Keith Noonan2026年5只最佳GPU股票及投资方法关于作者Keithen Drury是Motley Fool的特约科技分析师，负责报道AI、半导体、网络安全和SaaS股票。除在The Motley Fool任职外，Keithen还是一名机械工程师，曾在霍尼韦尔以及Brand Hydraulics和Lincoln Industries等较小的工业公司担任职务。他拥有多特大学机械工程学士学位。TMFTripleOptionKeithen Drury持有英伟达和台积电的仓位。The Motley Fool持有并推荐苹果、英特尔、英伟达和台积电。The Motley Fool设有披露政策。提及的股票英特尔纳斯达克：INTC$123.00(-3.45%)-$4.39Motley Fool Stock Advisor最新推荐获取访问权限---%平均回报标普500指数SNPINDEX：^GSPC$7,743.41(+0.51%)+$39.28台积电纽约证券交易所：TSM$450.61(-0.12%)-$0.54苹果纳斯达克：AAPL$341.07(+1.53%)+$5.15英伟达纳斯达克：NVDA$225.07(+0.22%)+$0.49*自成立以来所有推荐的平均回报。成本基础和回报以前一交易日收盘价为准。","publish_source":"fool.com","publish_time":"2026-09-26T09:45:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-910","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike（NASDAQ: CRWD）在AI威胁加速之际保持网络安全领导地位","title_en":"CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD) Maintains Cybersecurity Leadership as AI Threats Accelerate","summary_cn":"文章称CrowdStrike在2026年5月22日仍是机构NASDAQ投资组合中的知名标的，AI增强型威胁活动推动网络安全支出上升。其Falcon平台被视为企业端点保护、身份安全和云工作负载防护的领先云原生方案。公司已从2024年7月软件更新导致的大规模中断事件中恢复，客户和收入指标回升，Charlotte AI助手已集成至多个Falcon模块。政府和联邦业务因安全许可及FedRAMP授权保持稳健，2026年第一季度业绩强劲，年度经常性收入增长超分析师预期。","summary_en":"The article says CrowdStrike remained a prominent institutional NASDAQ holding on May 22, 2026, as AI-enhanced threats drove cybersecurity spending. Its Falcon platform is seen as a leading cloud-native solution for endpoint protection, identity security and cloud workload defence. The company has recovered from the July 2024 software update outage, with customer and revenue metrics rebounding and its Charlotte AI assistant integrated across Falcon modules. Government and federal business remains robust due to security clearances and FedRAMP authorisations, and strong Q1 2026 results showed annual recurring revenue growth exceeding analyst estimates.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:27:51.796709+00:00","url":"https://www.foreignpolicyjournal.com/2026/05/22/crowdstrike-nasdaq-crwd-maintains-cybersecurity-leadership-as-ai-threats-accelerate","content":"CrowdStrike Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: CRWD) remained a prominent name among institutional NASDAQ portfolios on Friday, May 22, as the cybersecurity sector continues to attract elevated spending driven by AI-enhanced threat activity.\nThe company’s Falcon platform is widely regarded as the leading cloud-native cybersecurity solution for enterprise endpoint protection, identity security, and cloud workload defence.\nCrowdStrike has continued to grow its customer base and expand its platform capabilities through 2026, following the significant reputational challenge posed by the July 2024 software update incident that caused widespread outages.\nThe company’s revenue and customer metrics have broadly recovered from the July 2024 event, with management indicating that the vast majority of affected customers have renewed their contracts.\nAI-powered threat detection has become one of the most important selling points for CrowdStrike, with the company’s Charlotte AI assistant now integrated across multiple Falcon platform modules.\nThe AI threat landscape has intensified in 2026, with adversarial use of large language models for phishing, social engineering, and code-generation attacks driving demand for more sophisticated defences.\nCrowdStrike’s government and federal business has remained robust, with the company holding extensive security clearances and FedRAMP authorisations that make it a preferred vendor for US government agencies.\nThe company reported strong first-quarter 2026 results, with annual recurring revenue continuing to grow at a pace that exceeded analyst estimates.\nAnalysts broadly maintain buy ratings on CRWD, with price targets that imply meaningful upside from current levels, though the stock trades at a premium to most software peers.\nCrowdStrike’s position at the intersection of AI, cloud security, and government spending makes it one of the most strategically positioned names on the NASDAQ for the second half of 2026 and beyond.\nShare:\nTags:","content_cn":"周五，5月22日，CrowdStrike Holdings Inc.（NASDAQ：CRWD）仍是机构 NASDAQ 投资组合中的突出名称；随着 AI 增强型威胁活动推动支出增加，网络安全领域持续吸引较高投入。\n该公司的 Falcon 平台被广泛认为是企业端点保护、身份安全和云工作负载防御领域领先的云原生网络安全解决方案。\n在 2024年7月软件更新事故导致大范围中断、给公司带来重大声誉挑战之后，CrowdStrike 在 2026 年期间继续扩大客户群并拓展平台功能。\n该公司的营收和客户指标已从 2024年7月事件中大体恢复，管理层表示，受影响客户中的绝大多数已续签合同。\nAI 驱动的威胁检测已成为 CrowdStrike 最重要的卖点之一，该公司的 Charlotte AI 助手现已整合至多个 Falcon 平台模块。\n2026 年，AI 威胁态势加剧；对大型语言模型的对抗性使用——用于网络钓鱼、社会工程和代码生成攻击——推动了对更复杂防御措施的需求。\nCrowdStrike 的政府及联邦业务仍保持强劲，公司拥有广泛的安全许可和 FedRAMP 授权，使其成为美国政府机构的首选供应商。\n公司公布了强劲的 2026 年第一季度业绩，年度经常性收入继续以超出分析师预期的速度增长。\n分析师总体维持对 CRWD 的买入评级，目标价显示较当前水平存在显著上涨空间，尽管该股的交易估值高于大多数软件同行。\nCrowdStrike 处于 AI、云安全和政府支出的交汇点，其定位使之成为 2026 年下半年及未来 NASDAQ 上战略定位最优越的公司之一。\n分享：\n标签：","publish_source":"foreignpolicyjournal.com","publish_time":"2026-05-22T21:59:00-04:00"}},{"id":"news-906","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike（纳斯达克：CRWD）创619美元历史收盘新高，网络安全需求保持坚挺","title_en":"CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD) Hits All-Time Closing High of $619 as Cybersecurity Demand Stays Firm","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike股价于2026年5月18日创下618.83美元的历史收盘新高，5月22日仍在纪录附近盘整。Jefferies分析师表示看好网络安全板块。公司Falcon平台在端点保护、身份安全等领域保持领先，2026年一季度业绩强劲，年度经常性收入增长超预期，AI安全威胁推动企业安全预算上升。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike Holdings (NASDAQ: CRWD) hit an all-time closing high of $618.83 on May 18, 2026, and consolidated near record levels on May 22. Jefferies analyst Brent Thill expressed strong bullishness on cybersecurity. The company's Falcon platform leads in endpoint protection and identity security, with strong Q1 2026 results and annual recurring revenue growth exceeding estimates, as AI-enhanced cyber threats drive enterprise security budgets higher.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:27:43.566615+00:00","url":"https://www.foreignpolicyjournal.com/2026/05/24/crowdstrike-nasdaq-crwd-hits-all-time-closing-high-of-619-as-cybersecurity-demand-stays-firm","content":"CrowdStrike Holdings Inc. (NASDAQ: CRWD) reached an all-time closing high of $618.83 on May 18, 2026, and was consolidating near those record levels on Friday, May 22, with the stock trading within its 52-week range of $342.72 to $634.24.\nJefferies analyst Brent Thill told CNBC on May 21 that he is very bullish on cybersecurity, a comment that reinforced positive sentiment across the sector and helped CRWD maintain ground near its historic peak heading into the Memorial Day weekend.\nThe stock has surged dramatically from its 52-week low, having more than doubled in value over the prior twelve months as enterprise security spending accelerated and investor confidence in the Falcon platform’s competitive position was restored following the July 2024 software update incident.\nCrowdStrike’s Falcon platform is the market-leading cloud-native cybersecurity solution for endpoint protection, identity security, and cloud workload defence, serving a customer base that spans enterprises, government agencies, and critical infrastructure operators globally.\nThe company reported strong first-quarter 2026 results, with annual recurring revenue continuing to grow at a pace that exceeded analyst estimates and confirmed that the post-outage recovery in customer retention and new business signings is essentially complete.\nA new wave of concern about AI-enhanced cyber threats has driven renewed enterprise security budgets in 2026, with organisations investing in more sophisticated detection and response capabilities as adversarial use of large language models for phishing and social engineering escalates.\nCrowdStrike’s Charlotte AI assistant, now integrated across multiple Falcon modules, has been positioned as the company’s primary response to the AI security challenge, offering natural language querying of threat intelligence and automated investigation workflows.\nThe consensus analyst price target for CRWD of $461.17 has been rendered obsolete by the stock’s extraordinary rally, with the current price approximately 34% above the most recently compiled consensus figure, suggesting significant upward revision is due from covering analysts.\nRetail investor sentiment on CRWD has been described as extremely bullish on social trading platforms, reflecting the combination of strong fundamental performance, record stock price, and an accelerating threat landscape that keeps enterprise security budgets elevated.\nThe next major catalyst for CRWD will be its fiscal second-quarter earnings report, which will provide fresh data on annual recurring revenue growth, new logo acquisitions, and the commercial momentum of its AI-powered security products.\nShare:\nTags:","content_cn":"CrowdStrike Holdings Inc.（纳斯达克：CRWD）于2026年5月18日达到618.83美元的历史收盘高点，并于5月22日星期五在接近这一纪录水平的位置盘整，当时该股处于342.72美元至634.24美元的52周区间内。\n杰富瑞分析师布伦特·希尔于5月21日告诉CNBC，他非常看好网络安全行业。这一评论强化了整个行业的积极情绪，并帮助CRWD在阵亡将士纪念日周末到来之际维持在历史峰值附近的水平。\n随着企业安全支出加速，该股已从52周低点大幅飙升，在此前十二个月中价值翻了一倍以上。2024年7月软件更新事件后，投资者对Falcon平台竞争地位的信心得到恢复。\nCrowdStrike的Falcon平台是市场领先的云原生网络安全解决方案，涵盖端点防护、身份安全和云工作负载防护，客户遍布全球各地的企业、政府机构和关键基础设施运营商。\n公司公布了强劲的2026年第一季度业绩，年度经常性收入继续以超过分析师预期的速度增长，并确认中断事件后的客户留存和新业务签约恢复基本完成。\n对人工智能增强型网络威胁的新一轮担忧推动了2026年企业安全预算的重新增长。随着攻击者利用大型语言模型进行网络钓鱼和社会工程的行为升级，各组织正在投资更复杂的检测和响应能力。\nCrowdStrike的Charlotte AI助手现已集成到多个Falcon模块中，被定位为公司应对人工智能安全挑战的主要方案，可通过自然语言查询威胁情报并执行自动化调查工作流。\nCRWD的分析师共识目标价为461.17美元，但该股的非凡涨势已使这一目标价过时。目前价格约比最近汇编的共识数字高出34%，这表明覆盖该股的分析师应大幅上调目标价。\n社交交易平台上的散户投资者情绪被描述为对CRWD极度看涨，这反映了强劲的基本面表现、创纪录的股价以及不断加剧的威胁环境共同促使企业安全预算保持高位。\nCRWD接下来的主要催化剂将是其财政年度第二季度业绩报告，该报告将提供有关年度经常性收入增长、新客户获取以及其人工智能驱动安全产品商业势头的新数据。\n分享：\n标签：","publish_source":"foreignpolicyjournal.com","publish_time":"2026-05-24T13:18:00-04:00"}},{"id":"news-152","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI与海岸警卫队就针对驶往得克萨斯油轮的 cyberattack 展开调查","title_en":"FBI And Coast Guard Launch Probe Into Cyberattacks Targeting Texas-Bound Oil Tankers","summary_cn":"美国海岸警卫队与联邦调查局（FBI）正联合调查上个月两艘驶往美国的油轮遭受的疑似网络攻击。两艘船均因船上网络疑似被怀有敌意的外国网络行为者入侵而被美方登船检查。调查人员正在审查伊朗或其他试图利用美伊紧张局势的行为者是否为幕后黑手。联合声明称目前没有运营中断、船只失稳、船员人身危险或环境影响的相关报告。","summary_en":"The US Coast Guard and FBI are jointly investigating suspected cyberattacks on two oil tankers bound for the United States last month. Both vessels were boarded by American authorities after indications their onboard networks had been compromised by foreign cyber actors operating with hostile intent. Investigators are examining whether Iran or another actor seeking to exploit US-Iran tensions was responsible. A joint statement said there are currently no reports of operational disruptions, vessel instability, physical danger to crews or environmental impacts.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:32:48.986032+00:00","url":"https://www.foreignpolicyjournal.com/2026/09/16/fbi-and-coast-guard-launch-probe-into-cyberattacks-targeting-texas-bound-oil-tankers","content":"The U.S. Coast Guard and FBI are jointly investigating suspected cyberattacks on two oil tankers that were bound for the United States last month.\nBoth vessels were boarded by American authorities following indications that their onboard networks had been compromised by foreign cyber actors operating with hostile intent.\nOn August 21, a foreign-flagged commercial vessel in the Gulf of Mexico was boarded by a highly specialized team of Coast Guard law enforcement officers, cyber protection members, and FBI cyber personnel.\nA joint statement from both agencies confirmed that “the measures were designed to ensure integrity of the vessel’s operational and information technology systems following indications that the vessel’s network were compromised by foreign cyber actors.”\nA second tanker that sustained a cyberattack was subsequently boarded by U.S. officials on August 24 to conduct a comparable systems assessment and security review.\nInvestigators are actively examining the possibility that Iran, or another actor seeking to exploit ongoing tensions between Tehran and Washington, was responsible for the attacks.\nThe joint Coast Guard and FBI statement noted that “currently, there are no reports of operational disruptions, vessel instability, physical danger to crews, or environmental impacts” stemming from either incident.\nOne of the vessels involved has been identified as the VL PROSPERITY, a Liberian-flagged supertanker with a capacity of 2.3 million barrels of crude oil.\nThe VL PROSPERITY was sailing from Egypt’s Sidi Kerir port toward a U.S. port when it was targeted by a major cyberattack in the Strait of Gibraltar on August 7, 2026, leaving it without communications for 30 hours.\nAccording to a crew member aboard the vessel, attackers infiltrated engine-room systems, reduced engine cooling flow, increased engine speed, and disabled fuel and engine-oil tank controls during the breach.\nThe sophistication of the attack on the VL PROSPERITY points to a well-resourced threat actor with specific knowledge of maritime operational technology systems and their vulnerabilities.\nNo group has yet claimed responsibility for either attack, and both investigations remain active as federal authorities work to attribute the incidents and assess the broader threat to maritime infrastructure.\nShare:\nTags:","content_cn":"美国海岸警卫队和联邦调查局（FBI）正在联合调查上个月两艘驶往美国的油轮遭遇的疑似网络攻击。\n\n在迹象显示其船载网络遭到带有敌意意图的外国网络行为者入侵后，两艘船均被美国当局登船检查。\n\n8月21日，一艘位于墨西哥湾、悬挂外国国旗的商船被一支高度专业化的队伍登船检查，该队伍由海岸警卫队执法人员、网络防护成员和FBI网络人员组成。\n\n两机构的联合声明确认，“在有迹象显示该船舶网络遭外国网络行为者入侵后，这些措施旨在确保船舶运营技术和信息技术系统的完整性。”\n\n8月24日，美国官员随后登上第二艘遭受网络攻击的油轮，开展类似的系统评估和安全审查。\n\n调查人员正在积极审查伊朗，或其他试图利用德黑兰与华盛顿之间持续紧张局势的行为者，是否应对这些攻击负责的可能性。\n\n海岸警卫队和FBI的联合声明指出，“目前没有报告称任何一起事件造成运营中断、船舶失稳、船员面临人身危险或环境影响。”\n\n涉事船舶之一已被确认为VL PROSPERITY号，这是一艘悬挂利比里亚国旗、可装载230万桶原油的超级油轮。\n\nVL PROSPERITY号当时正从埃及锡迪凯里尔港驶往美国港口，并于2026年8月7日在直布罗陀海峡成为一次重大网络攻击的目标，导致其30小时无法通信。\n\n据该船一名船员称，攻击者在入侵期间渗透进机舱系统，降低发动机冷却流量，提高发动机转速，并禁用了燃料和发动机油舱控制系统。\n\n针对VL PROSPERITY号攻击的复杂程度表明，威胁行为者资源充足，并对海事运营技术系统及其漏洞具有专门知识。\n\n尚无组织宣称对任一攻击负责；联邦当局正努力确定事件归因并评估对海事基础设施的更广泛威胁，两项调查仍在进行中。\n\n分享：\n标签：","publish_source":"foreignpolicyjournal.com","publish_time":"2026-09-16T16:27:00-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1392","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"开棺验尸后，FBI确认1970年无名男尸身份","title_en":"After Exhumation, FBI Restores Name of 1970 John Doe","summary_cn":"1970年3月20日，纽约州安多弗镇戴维斯山路发现一具无头无手的男性遗体，近56年来纽约州警察持续追查线索但身份不明。2022年6月7日，为采集DNA对遗体进行开棺，在联邦调查局协助下，最终确认死者为失踪时居住在宾夕法尼亚州杰纳西的35岁男子克莱德·A·科帕奇。该案调查仍在进行，警方呼吁公众提供线索。","summary_en":"On March 20, 1970, the headless, handless body of a male was found on Davis Hill Road in Andover, New York, and for nearly 56 years New York State Police pursued leads without identifying him. On June 7, 2022, the body was exhumed to collect DNA, and with assistance from the Federal Bureau of Investigation, it was identified as 35-year-old Clyde A. Coppage, who lived in Genesee, Pennsylvania at the time of his disappearance. The investigation remains open and active, and police seek public information.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:18:10.119177+00:00","url":"https://www.forensicmag.com/3594-All-News/624610-After-Exhumation-FBI-Restores-Name-of-1970-John-Doe","content":"After Exhumation, FBI Restores Name of 1970 John Doe\nWelcome Guest\nSign In\nRegister\nNews\nDigital ForensicsDNA AnalysisFingerprint AnalysisForensic AnthropologyGenetic GenealogyLaw EnforcementToxicologyEditorial FeaturesForensic Tips\nArticlesSuppliers Guide\nFeatured Products\nDNA HubResourcesWebinarsEventsRegisterSign In\nForensic®All NewsAfter Exhumation, FBI Restores Name of 1970 John Doe\nAfter Exhumation, FBI Restores Name of 1970 John Doe\nMarch 16, 2026\nSaveTweetBlueskyReddit\nEmail\nAdd On Google\nClyde A. Coppage. Credit: NYSP\nOn March 20, 1970, the body of a male was located without a head or hands on Davis Hill Road in the town of Andover. Over the course of nearly 56 years, investigating members of the New York State Police continued to track down every lead, but the identity of the male remained unknown.\nOn June 7, 2022, an exhumation of the body was conducted for the purpose of collecting DNA.  With the assistance of the Federal Bureau of Investigation, the DNA was ultimately used to determine the body to be that of 35-year-old, Clyde A. Coppage, who was living in Genessee, Pennsylvania at the time of his disappearance.  Coppage was not originally from the area and had never been reported missing. The Bureau of Criminal Investigation out of SP Amity are seeking public assistance with any information on Clyde A. Coppage.\nThe investigation into the death of Coppage remains open and active.\nAnyone with information about Coppage or his death is asked to contact the New York State Police at 585-344-6200.\nRepublished courtesy of NY State Police\nSubscribe to our e-Newsletters\nStay up to date with the latest news, articles, and products for the lab. Plus, get special offers from Forensic – all delivered right to your inbox! Sign up now!\nMore News\nRemains of Missing Tenn. Woman Found 2 Years after Hurricane Helene\nEighteen of those deaths were in Tennessee. Seventeen of those victims were recovered in the aftermath of the storm—everyone except Nancy Tucker.\nPolice to Exhume ‘Baby Boy Doe’ in Effort to ID Newborn Found in 1977\nThe Benton County Sheriff’s Office is taking a new step in a nearly 50-year-old cold case involving an unidentified newborn whose body was discovered in a wooded area of Benton County in 1977.\nPolice Seek Assistance to Identify DV Victim from 1984\nForty-two years ago, on September 14, 1984, a young Black woman was murdered during a domestic violence incident on Eppirt Street in 6, East Orange, New Jersey.\nGenealogy Identifies Woman, Police Seek Info About her Death\nIn 2023, human remains were discovered in a wooded area near South Military Trail in unincorporated Boynton Beach. For years, we didn’t know who she was.\nForensic® is powered by Labcompare, the Buyer's Guide for Laboratory Professionals.\nA publication of\nA Site by CompareNetworks\nSee our other sites »\nConnect with Us\n© 2026 CompareNetworks. All rights reserved.\nAbout Forensic®\nSubscribe eNewsletters\nAbout Us\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nRequest Personal Data Deletion\nDisclaimer\nAuthor Guidelines\nAdvertise with Us\nRequest Information\nRequest Media Kit\nEditorial Calendar\nNews\nDigital Forensics\nDNA Analysis\nFingerprint Analysis\nForensic Anthropology\nGenetic Genealogy\nLaw Enforcement\nToxicology\nResources\nEditorial Features\nWebinars\nForensic Tips\nForensic Docket","content_cn":"掘尸后，FBI恢复1970年无名男子的姓名\n欢迎访客\n登录\n注册\n新闻\n数字取证DNA分析指纹分析法医人类学遗传家谱学执法毒理学编辑专题法医提示\n文章供应商指南\n精选产品\nDNA中心资源网络研讨会活动注册登录\nForensic®所有新闻掘尸后，FBI恢复1970年无名男子的姓名\n掘尸后，FBI恢复1970年无名男子的姓名\n2026年3月16日\n保存推文BlueskyReddit\n电子邮件\n在Google上添加\nClyde A. Coppage。图片来源：纽约州警察局\n1970年3月20日，在安多弗镇Davis Hill Road发现了一具没有头部和双手的男性尸体。在近56年的时间里，纽约州警察局参与调查的人员持续追查每一条线索，但这名男子的身份始终不明。\n2022年6月7日，对尸体进行了掘尸，以采集DNA。在联邦调查局的协助下，DNA最终被用于确定该尸体属于35岁的Clyde A. Coppage；他失踪时居住在宾夕法尼亚州Genessee。Coppage原本并非当地人，也从未被报告失踪。来自SP Amity的刑事调查局正在寻求公众协助，征集有关Clyde A. Coppage的任何信息。\n对Coppage死亡事件的调查仍在进行，案件保持开放状态。\n任何掌握Coppage或其死亡信息的人，请拨打585-344-6200联系纽约州警察局。\n经纽约州警察局授权转载\n订阅我们的电子通讯\n获取实验室最新新闻、文章和产品信息。此外还有Forensic提供的特别优惠——所有内容都会直接发送到您的收件箱！立即注册！\n更多新闻\n飓风Helene过后两年，发现田纳西州失踪女子的遗骸\n其中18起死亡事件发生在田纳西州。暴风雨过后找回了其中17名受害者——除Nancy Tucker外的所有人。\n警方将掘尸寻找“无名男婴”，以确认1977年发现的新生儿身份\nBenton县警长办公室正在处理一宗近50年的悬案：1977年，人们在Benton县一片林地发现了一名身份不明的新生儿尸体，如今警方采取了新行动。\n警方寻求协助确认1984年家庭暴力受害者身份\n42年前，即1984年9月14日，一名年轻的黑人女性在新泽西州东奥兰治Eppirt Street发生的一起家庭暴力事件中被杀害。\n家谱学确认女性身份，警方寻求有关其死亡的信息\n2023年，在博因顿海滩非建制地区South Military Trail附近的一片林地发现了人类遗骸。多年来，我们不知道她是谁。\nForensic®由Labcompare提供支持，Labcompare是实验室专业人士的买家指南。\n出版方\nCompareNetworks旗下网站\n查看我们的其他网站 »\n联系我们\n© 2026 CompareNetworks。保留所有权利。\n关于Forensic®\n订阅电子通讯\n关于我们\n联系我们\n隐私政策\n申请删除个人数据\n免责声明\n作者指南\n刊登广告\n索取信息\n索取媒体资料包\n编辑日历\n新闻\n数字取证\nDNA分析\n指纹分析\n法医人类学\n遗传家谱学\n执法\n毒理学\n资源\n编辑专题\n网络研讨会\n法医提示\n法医案卷","publish_source":"forensicmag.com","publish_time":"2026-03-16T00:00:00-07:00"}},{"id":"news-3107","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI探员卷入霍皮族保留地致命枪击事件","title_en":"FBI agent involved in deadly Hopi reservation shooting | FOX 10 Phoenix","summary_cn":"据FBI和纳瓦霍警方消息，FBI探员在霍皮族保留地内的Moenkopi执行搜查令时，一名嫌疑人拔出武器，随后被开枪击毙。FBI表示没有探员或特遣队人员受伤，并称该枪击事件正由FBI检查部门审查。事件导致当地学校一度封锁，但警方称社区无持续威胁。探员和嫌疑人姓名尚未公布。","summary_en":"According to the FBI and Navajo Police, FBI agents executing a search warrant in Moenkopi on the Hopi reservation encountered a suspect who drew a weapon and was shot dead. The FBI said no agents or task force personnel were injured and that the shooting is under review by its Inspection Division. Schools were briefly locked down, but police said there was no active threat. The names of the agent and suspect have not been released.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:22:11.846450+00:00","url":"https://www.fox10phoenix.com/news/fbi-agent-involved-deadly-hopi-reservation-shooting","content":"FBI agent involved in deadly Hopi reservation shooting By Kenneth Wong FOX 10 Phoenix Crime and Public Safety Updated March 3, 2025 9:12 PM MST Published March 3, 2025 12:07 PM MST Share Copy Link Email Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Reddit Updated March 3, 2025 9:12 PM MST ▾ FBI agent-involved shooting on Hopi reservation A shooting in Moenkopi involving an FBI task force officer has resulted in a fatality. The Brief A suspect is dead following a shooting involving an FBI agent, according to the agency.The shooting happened in Moenkopi, which is located within the Hopi reservation. COCONINO COUNTY, Ariz. - Officials with both the FBI and the Navajo Police Department have released details surrounding a shooting Monday morning on the Hopi reservation that left a suspect dead. What we know: Per a statement from Navajo Police, FBI agents executed a search warrant at around 7:25 a.m. March 3 at Moenkopi when the suspect pulled out a weapon on the agents. In a separate statement, FBI officials said the suspect was shot, and has since died. \"No FBI or task force personnel were injured,\" read a portion of the FBI's statement. \"The FBI takes all shooting incidents involving our agents or task force members seriously. In accordance with FBI policy, the shooting incident is under review by the FBI’s Inspection Division.\" The incident, according to Navajo Police, resulted in schools being placed on lockdown, but they say there is no active threat to the community. What we don't know: The names of the agent and the suspect have not been released. Area where the shooting happened This story was reported on from Phoenix. The Source Information for this article was gathered from statements issued by the Navajo Police Department and the FBI. Crime and Public SafetyHopiNewsCoconino CountyPolice Shootings Breaking News Breaking news delivered fast By clicking Sign Up, I confirmthat I have read and agreeto the Privacy Policy and Terms of Service.\nJust In...\nView More 1 dead, 2 airlifted in Arizona 'Old West shootout' Dead ducks, foul smells plague park renovation Veteran rebuilds his life after Globe flooding Seen on TV: September 24 Live Now Prop 320 debate covers school budget mandate Trending All suspects in custody in Casa Grande killing Kyrsten Sinema's ex-bodyguard accused of causing $200,000 damage to her Cave Creek home Teen arrested in Phoenix 'Door Kick Challenge' Valley mansion tied to alleged Medicaid fraud; 'Home Improvement' star arrested l Morning News Brief Rain, storms and Hurricane Polo's impact on AZ\nLatest Videos\nView More video Lake renovation at Gilbert park draws concern video Election Day approaching | FOX 10 Talk video Globe flood survivor shares recovery story video Arizona man attacks son-in-law's killer in court video Golfers hit the links in Glendale for a good cause","content_cn":"参与霍皮保留地枪击事件的 FBI 特工\n作者：Kenneth Wong，FOX 10 Phoenix 犯罪与公共安全\n更新于 2025 年 3 月 3 日美国山地标准时间晚上 9:12\n发布于 2025 年 3 月 3 日美国山地标准时间中午 12:07\n分享 复制链接 电子邮件 Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Reddit\n更新于 2025 年 3 月 3 日美国山地标准时间晚上 9:12 ▾\n霍皮保留地发生涉及 FBI 特工的枪击事件\n一起发生在 Moenkopi、涉及一名 FBI 特遣队警官的枪击事件造成一人死亡。\n简报\n据该机构称，一名嫌疑人在涉及一名 FBI 特工的枪击事件后死亡。\n枪击事件发生在 Moenkopi，该地位于霍皮保留地内。\n亚利桑那州科科尼诺县——FBI 和纳瓦霍警察局官员都公布了周一早上霍皮保留地发生枪击事件的详情，一名嫌疑人在事件中死亡。\n我们知道的情况：根据纳瓦霍警方的一份声明，FBI 特工于 3 月 3 日上午约 7:25 在 Moenkopi 执行搜查令时，嫌疑人向特工掏出武器。FBI 官员在另一份声明中表示，嫌疑人中枪，随后死亡。\nFBI 声明中写道：“没有 FBI 人员或特遣队人员受伤。FBI 严肃对待所有涉及本机构特工或特遣队成员的枪击事件。根据 FBI 政策，该枪击事件正由 FBI 检查部门进行审查。”\n据纳瓦霍警方称，该事件导致学校进入封锁状态，但警方表示社区不存在持续的威胁。\n我们不知道的情况：特工和嫌疑人的姓名尚未公布。\n枪击事件发生区域\n本报道来自菲尼克斯。\n消息来源\n本文信息来自纳瓦霍警察局和 FBI 发布的声明。\n犯罪与公共安全 霍皮族 新闻 科科尼诺县 警察枪击事件\n快速送达的突发新闻\n点击“注册”即表示我确认已阅读并同意《隐私政策》和《服务条款》。\n刚刚发生……\n查看更多\n亚利桑那州“老西部枪战”中 1 人死亡、2 人被空运\n死鸭子和恶臭困扰公园翻修\n退伍军人在格洛布洪灾后重建生活\n电视上看到：9 月 24 日\n正在直播\n第 320 号提案辩论涉及学校预算规定\n热门\nCasa Grande 谋杀案中所有嫌疑人均已被拘留\nKyrsten Sinema 的前保镖被指控给她位于 Cave Creek 的住宅造成 20 万美元损失\n青少年因在菲尼克斯发起“踢门挑战”而被捕\n涉嫌医疗补助欺诈的山谷豪宅；《成长的烦恼》明星被捕\n早间新闻简报\n降雨、风暴和飓风 Polo 对亚利桑那州的影响\n最新视频\n查看更多视频\n吉尔伯特公园湖泊翻修引发担忧\n视频\n选举日临近｜FOX 10 访谈\n视频\n格洛布洪灾幸存者分享恢复经历\n视频\n亚利桑那州男子在法庭袭击女婿的杀手\n视频\n高尔夫球手在格伦代尔挥杆，为公益事业助力","publish_source":"fox10phoenix.com","publish_time":"2025-03-03T12:07:41-07:00"}},{"id":"news-2708","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部因以色列-伊朗冲突发布国家恐怖主义预警系统公告","title_en":"Department of Homeland Security issues National Terrorism Advisory System Bulletin amid Israel-Iran conflict","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆因美国卷入伊朗与以色列冲突而发布国家恐怖主义预警系统公告，指出美国面临威胁环境升高。国土安全部表示目前没有针对本土的具体可信威胁，但冲突可能带来网络攻击、暴力行为和反犹仇恨犯罪等风险。该公告将于2025年9月22日到期，公众可通过地方执法、FBI办事处或融合中心报告可疑活动。","summary_en":"Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem issued a National Terrorism Advisory System bulletin citing a heightened threat environment due to U.S. involvement in the Iran-Israel conflict. DHS said there are currently no specific credible threats against the homeland, but the conflict raises the possibility of cyberattacks, violence, and antisemitic hate crimes. The bulletin expires September 22, 2025, and the public is urged to report suspicious activity to local law enforcement, FBI field offices, or fusion centers.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:34:48.487500+00:00","url":"https://www.fox10tv.com/2025/06/22/department-homeland-security-issues-national-terrorism-advisory-system-bulletin-amid-israel-iran-conflict","content":"Department of Homeland Security issues National Terrorism Advisory System Bulletin amid Israel-Iran conflict By Robert RistaneoPublished: Jun. 22, 2025 at 4:12 PM CDTShareAdd Us On GoogleAdd as a preferred source on GoogleThe Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem issued a National Terrorism Advisory System regarding a heightened threat environment across the United States due to the United States involvement in the conflict between Iran and Israel.There are currently no specific credible threats against the homeland, according to DHS.The ongoing Israel-Iran conflict brings the possibility of increased threat to the homeland in the form of possible cyberattacks, acts of violence, and antisemitic hate crimes.Secretary Kristi NoemThe NTAS Bulletin will expire on September 22, 2025, according to a release from DHS.The public should report any suspicious activity or threats of violence to local law enforcement, FBI Field Offices, or a local Fusion Center. Read the NTAS Bulletin here. Copyright 2025 WALA. All rights reserved.","content_cn":"国土安全部发布国家恐怖主义威胁咨询系统公告，正值以色列与伊朗冲突期间\n作者：Robert Ristaneo\n发布时间：2025年6月22日下午4:12（CDT）\n分享\n在 Google 上关注我们\n在 Google 上添加为首选来源\n国土安全部长 Kristi Noem 发布了一份国家恐怖主义威胁咨询系统公告，称由于美国介入伊朗与以色列之间的冲突，全美面临较高的威胁环境。\n据国土安全部称，目前没有针对美国本土的具体可信威胁。\n持续的以色列—伊朗冲突带来了本土威胁增加的可能性，形式可能包括网络攻击、暴力行为和反犹太主义仇恨犯罪。\n国土安全部长 Kristi Noem\n据国土安全部发布的公告，该 NTAS 公告将于2025年9月22日到期。\n公众应向当地执法部门、联邦调查局外勤办公室或当地融合中心报告任何可疑活动或暴力威胁。请在此阅读 NTAS 公告。版权所有 2025 WALA。保留所有权利。","publish_source":"fox10tv.com","publish_time":"2025-06-22T21:12:21.074000+00:00"}}];
